/* GENERATED by build/gen-realm-bestiary.py from dev/model-qa/realm-bestiary-draft.json — never hand-edit. Realm creature layer (reskin: frame=stat chassis id in BESTIARY, model=render key/net-new description, desc/traits/source per docs/REALM-ENRICHMENT-WRITING.md). */
const REALM_BESTIARY={
 "frontier":[{"name":"Dust-Broke Drifter","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Desperate gun-for-hire, breaks and runs when losing","flavor":"A busted prospector or out-of-luck ranch hand who picked up a gun because begging stopped working. Fights scared and quits the moment the math turns against him.","desc":"He's got a hat with the brim gone soft, a revolver that's seen better cleaning, and a stare that keeps sliding off to the horizon like he's already planning the walk away from this. His hand trembles on the grip before he even draws it. The first shot that goes wide is the one that breaks him."},{"name":"Line-Rider","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Rank-and-file outlaw muscle, brave only in packs","flavor":"Rank-and-file gang muscle who rides the fence lines looking for something to take. Works in packs, brave only in numbers.","desc":"Three or four of them come loping along the fence line at an easy trot, rifles balanced across their saddles like they're not even sure they'll need them. Alone, one of these men fusses with his hat brim and won't meet your eyes. In a pack, they all suddenly know how to shoot."},{"name":"Coyote-Thing","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"Wrong-shaped coyote pack, laughs instead of howling","flavor":"A dust-country coyote gone wrong at the edges — too many teeth, a laugh instead of a howl. Runs in loose, opportunistic packs and never attacks what it can't out-number.","desc":"It laughs before it howls — a wet, chittering bark that doesn't belong in any coyote throat, and the extra rows of teeth behind its lips confirm the wrongness. They keep low to the sage and never come at you alone, circling in loose scatter until the numbers feel safe to them."},{"name":"Scarecrow Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Field scarecrow that only moves when unwatched","flavor":"Propped over a dead man's field to scare off crows and, lately, everything else. Stands dead still until you stop watching it, then it isn't where it was.","desc":"Straw hat, crossed fence-posts, a burlap face gone dark with weather — it's exactly what a scarecrow should be, right down to the crows giving it a wide berth. It's the stillness that's wrong. Look away for even a breath and when your eyes come back, it's a few feet closer than it was."},{"name":"Claim-Jumper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Armed squatter on a forged land deed","flavor":"Squats on other men's stakes with a rifle and a forged deed. Knows the land better than the law does and uses that.","desc":"He's dug a fire pit and pitched a lean-to on land that isn't his, with a folded paper he'll wave at you like it settles things. The rifle resting across his knees settles things faster. He knows every wash and rise on this claim better than the county surveyor ever will."},{"name":"Company Enforcer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Railroad-payroll thug who calls debt-collection business","flavor":"Muscle on the railroad or mining company payroll — collects debts, breaks strikes, and calls it business.","desc":"Clean coat, brass buttons, a ledger book tucked under one arm like he's here to do arithmetic instead of violence — until the two toughs behind him make it clear which one he actually does. He reads the amount owed out loud before anybody's allowed to argue about it."},{"name":"Buzzard-Kin","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-vulture","model":"giant-vulture","summary":"Torso-sized vulture that circles the living early","flavor":"An unnaturally patient carrion bird the size of a man's torso that's learned to circle the living a little early.","desc":"Big enough that its shadow crosses the trail like a cloud passing, this vulture doesn't wait for the dying to finish dying. It banks in low circles overhead long before anyone's actually hurt, patient in a way that makes a person want to hurry up and prove it wrong."},{"name":"Dust Devil","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"salamander-fire-snake","model":"net-new: a churning funnel of sand and static shaped loosely like a striking snake","summary":"Living dust-funnel that scours riders off horseback","flavor":"A living whirlwind of grit and heat-shimmer that scours a rider off his horse before anyone sees it coming. The old-timers swear it only forms where blood's been spilled.","desc":"The funnel stands up out of flat ground with no wind to explain it, dust-brown and man-tall, and it doesn't wander — it tracks. Horses spook first, rearing and screaming before the rider even feels the grit start peppering his face and the funnel closes the gap at a dead run."},{"name":"Debt-Collector Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Ledger-keeping ghoul who thinks the debt transfers","flavor":"A man who died owing money and came back still keeping the ledger — hollow-eyed, gaunt, and convinced the debt transfers to whoever's standing nearest.","desc":"Gray-skinned and hunched, it drags a waterlogged ledger behind it on a chain and reads names off the mildewed pages in a rasping, patient voice. It genuinely believes the debt survives the debtor — and reaches for you with black-nailed hands the moment it decides you're the estate that inherited it."},{"name":"Gunslinger's Shade","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Ghostly quick-draw reliving the duel he lost","flavor":"The echo of a quick-draw who lost the one duel that mattered. Reenacts the noon-draw against anyone who'll stand still for it, forever losing, forever trying again.","desc":"He stands at twenty paces in a duster gone translucent at the edges, hand hovering over a holster that isn't really there anymore. Every dusk he relives the same draw, the same half-second too slow, and every dusk some unlucky soul standing in for the man who beat him pays for the rematch."},{"name":"Iron Horse Wreck-Golem","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"net-new: a hunched engine of riveted boiler-plate, steam venting from a cracked stack","summary":"Salvaged locomotive-iron golem guarding a dead spur line","flavor":"Salvaged rail-yard iron bolted into something that walks and swings. Company men built it to guard the spur line; it forgot who it was guarding it from.","desc":"Rust-scaled and locomotive-heavy, it's built from salvaged boiler plate and coupling rod, hunched like something that used to run on rails and never got the memo that the spur line died. Steam hisses from seams that shouldn't still hold pressure, and each footfall rings like a dropped anvil.","traits":{"note": "Built from a wrecked locomotive; treat its slam attacks as unusually loud — the clang carries for a mile and can draw more of the same."}},{"name":"Bounty Board Regular","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Wanted-poster gunfighter, unhurried and always faster","flavor":"A working gun-for-hire whose face is on three different posters, all for different names. Professional, unhurried, and always faster on the draw than the job requires.","desc":"His face is nailed to half the boards in town, reward figure crossed out and rewritten upward twice. He doesn't hurry to the fight or away from it — just settles his hat, plants his boots, and waits with the patience of a man who's done this enough times to know he'll be the one still standing."},{"name":"Card-Sharp Killer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"net-new: a well-dressed gambler with a sleeve derringer and a dealer's stillness","summary":"Cheating gambler who kills the man who calls him","flavor":"Cleans out a table hand by hand, then cleans up the man who calls him on it. The cards are the tell; the derringer up the sleeve is the punchline.","desc":"He deals from the bottom smooth enough that you'd never catch it if you weren't watching for it — and if you do catch it, he doesn't deny it, doesn't apologize, just lets his other hand drift toward the table's edge where a derringer waits taped under the felt."},{"name":"Rustler Pack Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Cattle-rustling gang boss, quick to shoot and blame","flavor":"Runs a cattle-and-horse theft ring across three counties, quick to shoot and quicker to blame the next gang over.","desc":"He rides at the head of a loose column of stolen cattle, hat pushed back, already sizing up who in your group looks like the one who'll start trouble. He shoots first and sorts out whose fault it was after, and his gang has learned to shoot the second he does."},{"name":"Sidewinder Broodmother","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"giant-constrictor-snake","model":"giant-constrictor-snake","summary":"Wagon-length rattler with a half-mile brood","flavor":"A rattler grown to wagon-length in a dry wash nobody rides through twice. Her brood scatters the desert floor for a half-mile in every direction.","desc":"She's as long as a freight wagon and thick through the middle as a rain barrel, scales dust-pale and grit-crusted, and where she dens the ground is riddled with smaller holes hissing in chorus. Half a mile of brood scatters at her signal and regroups the instant the danger passes."},{"name":"Marshal's Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Murdered lawman still walking his dusk patrol","flavor":"The last honest lawman in three territories, shot in the back for it, still walking his rounds at dusk. Doesn't know he's dead — only knows the town's gone lawless again.","desc":"He walks his old beat every dusk in a coat with a bullet hole where his badge should still be pinned, boots silent on boards that used to creak under him. He tips his hat to no one living and keeps walking his rounds like the town still needs protecting from something."},{"name":"Cattle-Baron's Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"Baron's undefeated duelist, fights over land and water","flavor":"The baron's personal fist — duels for land, for water rights, for the principle of the thing, and hasn't lost yet.","desc":"Built like a bull himself, scarred across both forearms from duels he's never lost, he steps into the dust circle rolling his shoulders and cracking his neck like this is recreation. He fights over land and water rights personally, because the baron finds it's cheaper than paying lawyers."},{"name":"Boneyard Preacher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Buried-alive preacher whose sermon still convicts","flavor":"A hellfire circuit preacher whose congregation buried him alive for the sins he named too accurately. His sermon still carries, and it still convicts.","desc":"Dirt still clings to the collar of the coat he was buried in, and his voice carries up out of the ground before the rest of him claws free of the grave dirt. The sermon he preaches convicted him once — now it's aimed at whoever's standing close enough to hear the ending.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Graveside Sermon", "text": "Once per encounter, the preacher speaks a verse of his old conviction sermon at a target within 30 feet; that creature must succeed a Wisdom save or be frightened until the end of its next turn, seeing its own worst guilt reflected back."}]}},{"name":"Stampede-Cursed Longhorn","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"rhinoceros","model":"rhinoceros","summary":"Feral cursed bull leading a stampede that never ends","flavor":"A prize bull gone feral and enormous on cursed range grass, the lead animal in a stampede that never quite ends.","desc":"Its eyes have gone the flat black of a thing that's stopped being an animal, and it never really stops moving — hooves churning even when it's standing still, like the stampede it's leading is happening whether or not there's anyone around to run from it. The herd behind it never thins."},{"name":"Vault-Keeper Wight","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Dead bank owner still guarding his strongbox","flavor":"A bank owner who died clutching his strongbox and rose still clutching it, deputizing whatever corpses are handy to guard the vault door.","desc":"He's still wearing the suit he was buried in, buttons straining over a chest gone grey and stiff, and he stands sentinel over a strongbox that outlived every account it held. His hand never leaves the vault door. Approach it and he stops being patient about ownership."},{"name":"Noon-Duel Gunfighter","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"net-new: a duster-coated gunfighter standing dead-center in an empty street","summary":"Undefeated noon-draw gunfighter the whole town fears","flavor":"Never lost a noon draw and never will — the whole town clears out when word gets around he's in it. Some say he picks the fights just to keep the streak.","desc":"He always calls the hour himself — high noon, main street, both of you walking to your marks while shopkeepers hurry to pull their shutters. He's undefeated because he's fast, but mostly because he's already decided you're going to hesitate, and you probably will.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Called Shot", "text": "If both combatants are at full hit points at the start of the duel, the gunfighter's first attack against you scores a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20."}]}},{"name":"Rail Baron's War-Machine","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"net-new: a squat armored rail-car on legs, gatling-barrels where a face would be, chuffing black smoke","summary":"Armored rail-car war-machine muscling a dead man's right-of-way","flavor":"Built to muscle a right-of-way through land nobody agreed to sell. Answers only to the man who signed the requisition — and he's long dead.","desc":"Armored rail-car plating bolted over a walking chassis, it grinds forward on legs built from repurposed drive wheels, venting black coal smoke with every stride. It doesn't negotiate right-of-way — it simply keeps coming until whatever's in front of it isn't anymore."},{"name":"Draw-at-Noon Revenant","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Duel-killed revenant returning every noon to draw again","flavor":"Killed at high noon in a duel that everyone in town watched and nobody stopped. Returns every day the sun's directly overhead, looking for whoever's standing in the street.","desc":"He returns at noon exactly, every time, boots crunching gravel in a duster still torn where the fatal shot went through. He doesn't remember losing. He only remembers the moment before the draw, and he means to have it back, over and over, from anyone standing in the street.","traits":{"note": "Returns to fight again at the next in-game noon if destroyed anywhere near its original death-ground, unless that ground is consecrated or salted."}},{"name":"The Last Honest Marshal","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"net-new: a duster-coated lawman figure, star badge fused to bone, twin revolvers that never run dry","summary":"Undying lawman whose fused badge still holds the line","flavor":"He held the line when the town's whole council told him to look away, and it killed him for it. Now he holds a line nobody else can even see, and the badge is grown into his ribs.","desc":"The badge is fused into his ribcage now, tarnished silver grown through bone the way a scar grows through skin, and his eyes are the only warm thing left on him. He still reads the warrant aloud before he acts on it — the one honest ritual an undying lawman refuses to abandon.","traits":{"note": "Reads a warrant aloud before attacking any creature guilty of an actual crime it names; a target proven innocent of that crime is immune to the marshal's first attack.", "actions": [{"name": "The Line He Enforces", "text": "Once per turn, the marshal can mark a 10-foot line on the ground; any creature he names as guilty that crosses it provokes an immediate opportunity attack from him, even without reach."}]}},{"name":"The Noon Reckoning","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"net-new: a towering gunslinger silhouette wreathed in heat-shimmer, twin oversized pistols","summary":"Towering fiend that embodies every blood-ended noon duel","flavor":"Every town's noon-draw that ever ended in blood feeds it — it IS the duel, wearing whatever face the debt requires. It only walks the street when the sun's dead overhead and someone's about to draw.","desc":"It rises out of shimmering noon heat mirage-first, horns and wings resolving out of a hundred quiet duels that all ended the same way — badly, at midday, in dust. Every gunfight this land has ever settled with blood is folded into the shape of it, and it has come to collect on all of them at once.","traits":{"note": "Its presence forces every ranged combatant within 60 feet to fight at high noon conditions (disadvantage from glare) unless they have cover.", "actions": [{"name": "A Hundred Duels", "text": "Once per encounter, the fiend recreates a duel: it and one target both roll initiative fresh mid-combat, and whichever wins that roll gets an immediate free attack against the other."}]}},{"name":"Tin-Star Deputy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Green deputy who follows orders to the letter","flavor":"A green badge-wearer sworn in last week because the town ran out of better options. Follows orders to the letter and dies exactly as often as that implies.","desc":"His badge is shinier than it has any business being and his gunbelt sits a little too high, cinched by someone who's never actually drawn from it in anger. He follows the letter of whatever he was told, word for word, even when the situation's clearly outgrown the instructions."},{"name":"Trail-Dust Skinner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Hide-skinner who sells to whoever's buying","flavor":"Skins whatever the range gives up and sells the hides to whoever's buying, law or otherwise. Carries a knife more than a gun and knows how to use both badly.","desc":"He's got a wagon bed piled with hides that smell like they've been riding a long way in the heat, and a buyer's name he won't say twice. He'll skin anything that falls, doesn't much care whose brand it wore, and he's already calculating what you're worth in pelts."},{"name":"Powder-Monkey Kid","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Underage dynamite-runner, twitchy and dangerous","flavor":"Too young for the gang proper, so he handles the dynamite and does the running. Fast, twitchy, and one bad drop from taking the whole outfit with him.","desc":"He can't be more than fourteen, sleeves rolled past skinny wrists, a satchel of dynamite sticks slung crosswise and rattling with every twitchy step. His hands shake lighting the fuse and shake worse throwing it, which is exactly why nobody wants to be standing anywhere near him."},{"name":"Rail-Camp Roughneck","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Track-laying laborer who breaks heads for back pay","flavor":"Spikes track by day, breaks heads by night when the paymaster's short again. Swings a maul like he means it.","desc":"Sunburned to leather across the back of his neck, sledge still in one hand from driving spikes all day, he's got the kind of anger that's been baked in by months of unpaid wages. He swings the hammer the same way he swings it at rail — hard, and without much aiming."},{"name":"Sidewinder Snake","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"venomous-snake","model":"venomous-snake","summary":"Ordinary rattler, unusually common and agitated","flavor":"An ordinary desert rattler, except this stretch of scrub has three times the usual number of them, all agitated.","desc":"Just a rattler, technically — but there are a lot more of them out here than there should be, and they've stopped giving fair warning before they strike. This one's coiled tight in what little shade a rock throws, tail already going before you've noticed it."},{"name":"Scrub-Land Jackrabbit Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Boiling jackrabbit mass that strips land bare","flavor":"A boiling mass of oversized jackrabbits that strips a garden bare in a minute and a rider's boots in two. Harmless alone, a hazard in number.","desc":"The brush ahead seems to be boiling, a hundred pale bodies churning over each other in a moving carpet that strips every green thing down to root and dirt as it passes. Up close the sound is worse than the sight — a continuous dry rustle of claws and teeth."},{"name":"Range Buzzard","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"Ordinary vulture that follows the soon-to-be-dead","flavor":"An honest, unremarkable carrion bird — except it's started following specific people days before they die.","desc":"An ordinary bird, technically, riding a thermal in slow lazy circles above the trail — except it's been following you since sunup, and it never seems to be looking for anything but the exact spot where you're about to fall down."},{"name":"Prairie Dust-Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"Lean dry-wash wolf that takes livestock in packs","flavor":"Leaner and hungrier than a plain wolf, runs the dry washes in loose family packs and takes livestock when the deer thin out.","desc":"Lean to the point of visible ribs, coat the color of the dry wash it dens in, it never hunts alone — three or four shadows moving low and quiet along the arroyo, herding cattle or people the same patient way, cutting off the easy retreat first."},{"name":"Grave-Dust Crow","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"raven","model":"raven","summary":"Boneyard raven that talks in a dead man's cadence","flavor":"A boneyard raven that picked up a sliver of whatever's buried underneath it. Talks a little, in a dead man's cadence.","desc":"It perches on the leaning fence post of the boneyard and talks — not caws, talks, in a low dry rasp that carries the exact cadence of somebody long buried there. It repeats the same handful of phrases, over and over, like it's still finishing an argument from decades back."},{"name":"Whiskey-Nerve Brawler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"Saloon brawler who fights better drunk","flavor":"Fights better drunk than sober and knows it, so he's rarely sober. Saloon muscle, cheap to hire, cheaper to replace.","desc":"He's three drinks past sensible and swinging looser for it, knuckles already split from an earlier fight he probably started. Sober he flinches at everything; drunk he doesn't flinch at all, which somehow makes him hit harder and care less about where the punches land."},{"name":"Homestead Scarecrow","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Cursed-field scarecrow variant guarding a homestead","flavor":"A second scarecrow from the same cursed patch of field as its cousin, propped on a homestead fence instead of a graveyard one. Same trick, different crop.","desc":"Somebody's dead homestead still keeps this one propped in the ruined garden row, patchwork clothes gone to rag, and it's picked up the same curse as the field-scarecrows out on the ranches. It stands watch over a house nobody lives in anymore — closer every time you check."},{"name":"Claim-Office Forger","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Land-deed forger who triple-sells the same plot","flavor":"Draws up land deeds that look real enough to hold up in a corrupt court, then sells the same plot three times over.","desc":"He's got a satchel of deeds with the same plot description copied three or four times over, different buyer names inked in each. His hands are steady with a pen the way most men's are steady with a gun, and he's already sizing you up as customer number four."},{"name":"Stagecoach Highwayman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"bandit-courier","summary":"Polite masked highwayman working the coach roads","flavor":"Works the coach roads alone or in pairs, masked, polite, and gone before the horses have stopped stamping.","desc":"He rides up alongside the coach at a polite canter, mask neat, hat tipped, and asks for the strongbox like he's requesting a dance. He's genuinely disappointed when things turn ugly — robbery, to him, is a transaction that shouldn't require anybody getting shot."},{"name":"Company Book-Keeper Wight","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Dead accountant endlessly recounting debts owed","flavor":"Died at his ledger balancing debts nobody could pay and rose still doing the arithmetic, hollow-voiced, endlessly recounting the sums owed.","desc":"Green-grey and hunched over a ledger that never balances, it mutters sums under its breath in an endless recount, licking a rotted thumb to turn pages that have long since crumbled to pulp. It doesn't seem to notice you until the total finally, impossibly, comes out wrong."},{"name":"Boothill Skeleton","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"skeleton-archer","summary":"Rifle-toting graveyard skeleton in a rotted duster","flavor":"Rises from the cheap end of the cemetery with a rifle instead of a bow, still dressed in a moth-eaten duster, and shoots at anything that disturbs its plot.","desc":"It claws up through loose boothill dirt in a duster gone to threads, rifle still slung across the ribs where a strap somehow survived the grave. The bones move with a soldier's discipline — level the rifle, brace, fire — muscle memory outlasting the muscle."},{"name":"Dust-Choked Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Thirst-crazed ghoul still digging a dry wash","flavor":"Died of thirst in a dry wash and came back still parched, still digging for water that isn't there, biting anything that gets close to the hole.","desc":"It's still digging, fingers worn to bone-white claws at a dry wash that hasn't held water in years, driven by a thirst that death never satisfied. When it finally notices you it doesn't stop digging so much as redirect the digging at you."},{"name":"Grave-Dirt Zombie Posse","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie-plague-carrier","summary":"Hanged gang risen in formation, horses long gone","flavor":"A whole hanged gang risen together, still riding formation out of habit though their horses rotted out from under them years ago.","desc":"Six or seven of them shamble in a loose column, boots dragging, nooses still knotted tight around swollen grey necks. No horses — they walk it now, the same road they were hanged along, in the same order they died in."},{"name":"Mine-Shaft Crawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"carrion-crawler","model":"carrion-crawler","summary":"Blind mine-shaft predator that paralyzes and drags prey","flavor":"Bred in the dark below a played-out silver claim on whatever the miners stopped bringing up. Paralyzes with a touch and drags the still to a side tunnel.","desc":"It doesn't see you so much as taste the air with a forest of twitching mandibles, pale and eyeless from a lifetime in the dark below the shaft. It waits in the black at the tunnel's edge, patient as stone, until something warm gets close enough to paralyze and drag back down."},{"name":"Sun-Blind Prospector Ghast","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Salt-blind prospector ghast that never turns back","flavor":"Went snow-blind on salt flats chasing a vein that wasn't there and starved rather than turn back. Now it doesn't turn back from anything.","desc":"Salt has crusted over where his eyes used to work, and he shuffles with a prospector's pick still gripped in one clawed hand, following some vein of ore that stopped existing when he did. He never turns back toward the light — light isn't where the gold is."},{"name":"Rust-Bitten Rail Golem","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"Iron-eating rail-yard scrap creature spitting corrosion","flavor":"A stray piece of rail-yard machinery, half-alive from proximity to the Iron Horse Wreck-Golem, that eats iron and spits corrosion.","desc":"It's built from cannibalized rail spikes and scrap car iron, joints weeping orange rust-slurry with every awkward step, and it hungers for metal the way a living thing hungers for meat. It spits a fine corrosive mist that eats through buckles, barrels, and belt buckles alike."},{"name":"Poker-Table Cheat","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"performer","summary":"Smooth card-palming cheat, quick with a hideout knife","flavor":"Palms cards for a living and a knife for emergencies, both smoothly enough that nobody's caught him twice.","desc":"His fingers move faster than his face lets on, palming cards under a friendly smile that doesn't waver even when you catch him at it. There's a hideout knife strapped under the table's lip for exactly this conversation, and he's already reaching for it."},{"name":"Sod-House Squatter","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Stubborn dugout squatter, mostly bluff","flavor":"Dug into another man's land and dared anyone to move him. Mostly bluff, occasionally not.","desc":"He's dug his whole life into a hillside dugout that isn't technically his, rifle propped by the door more for show than use. Mostly bluff, mostly stubborn, mostly just wants to be left alone on dirt nobody else wanted until he moved in."},{"name":"Territorial Militia Rifle","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"Poorly drilled militia rifleman who holds out of stubbornness","flavor":"Called up from the local ranches when the cavalry's a week out, drilled poorly, aims worse, holds anyway out of stubbornness.","desc":"His uniform's a size too big and his drill is worse, rifle held at an angle no sergeant ever taught him — but he holds his ground anyway, purely out of stubbornness, long after better-trained men would've run."},{"name":"Cavalry Deserter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Cavalry deserter who robs both sides equally","flavor":"Walked off from his unit after seeing something in the breach he wasn't paid enough to fight, and now robs both sides equally.","desc":"Half a uniform still hangs off him, insignia torn free, and he's learned to rob wagon trains and army supply lines with equal indifference. He doesn't much care which side he's stealing from anymore — desertion cured him of caring."},{"name":"Prickled Cactus-Kin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"Reaching cactus-kin, still until a rider passes close","flavor":"A saguaro that learned to want something, and to reach for it. Stands stock-still until a rider passes too close.","desc":"It looks like any other stand of barrel cactus until a rider gets close enough, and then the spines angle, subtly, toward the warmth. It doesn't chase. It just waits at the trail's narrow point for something to brush past."},{"name":"Alkali Flat Wisp","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Salt-flat wisp luring the thirsty away from water","flavor":"A drowning-light that leads thirsty travelers deeper into the salt flats instead of toward the water it pretends to be.","desc":"A pale bobbing light hovers out over the salt flat at dusk, exactly where the old maps mark good water. It drifts a little farther every time you follow, patient as drought, leading the thirsty out past the point where turning back is still possible."},{"name":"Bounty-Poster Doppel","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Shapeshifter that impersonates its own bounty poster","flavor":"Wears the face on whichever wanted poster pays best that week, collects the bounty on itself from a gullible marshal, and vanishes before the paperwork clears.","desc":"It's wearing the exact face from the wanted poster nailed to the saloon wall — same scar, same crooked nose — and it'll happily confirm the reward, collect the bounty on itself from a fool, and vanish before anyone checks the paper twice."},{"name":"Copperhead Nest-Guard","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"giant-venomous-snake","summary":"Territorial oversized copperhead denning a mine entrance","flavor":"An oversized copperhead that's claimed a played-out mine entrance as its den and doesn't share territory with anything, prospector included.","desc":"Thick as a man's forearm and longer than most men are tall, it's denned the mouth of an old mine shaft and doesn't recognize property lines. It doesn't rattle a warning — copperheads never do — it just strikes from the shadow of the tunnel mouth."},{"name":"Company Strikebreaker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"Liquor-raged strikebreaker sent to end a picket line","flavor":"Hired muscle sent to end a labor dispute the fast way, works up a rage on cheap liquor before wading into a picket line.","desc":"He's been drinking company liquor since noon and it shows in the wild swing of his approach, sent down from the office with a club and instructions to end a picket line by whatever means end it fastest."},{"name":"Grave Robber Duo","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Boneyard grave robber, occasionally digs up trouble","flavor":"Works the boneyards after dark for rings, gold teeth, and the occasional cursed trinket that's more trouble than it's worth.","desc":"Two of them work the boneyard together, one holding the lantern low and one working the shovel, trading a running commentary about which graves still have anything worth pulling. They've dug up worse than valuables more than once and kept digging anyway."},{"name":"Iron-Rail Spike Wraith","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"net-new: a translucent laborer-shape fused at the wrists to a glowing spike-maul, driving invisible rail forever","summary":"Crushed rail-worker ghost still driving phantom spikes","flavor":"A track-worker crushed under the rail he was laying, doomed to keep driving spikes into ground that no longer needs them, swinging at anyone who steps on his old line.","desc":"Translucent and rail-thin, it swings a spectral sledge in the same rhythm it swung in life, driving phantom spikes into ties that aren't there anymore. The clang rings real even though the hammer isn't, and the ghost doesn't seem to know the railroad's finished."},{"name":"Prairie Fire Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"Runaway grass fire that took on a will of its own","flavor":"A grass fire that outran the wind and kept going, taking on a will of its own somewhere past the second county line.","desc":"What started as an ordinary grass fire got hungry somewhere along the way and started choosing directions instead of just following the wind. It roars low across the prairie in a wall of orange, crackling with something that sounds almost like intent."},{"name":"Sand-Wash Basilisk","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"basilisk","summary":"Petrifying desert basilisk denning a gravel-choked wash","flavor":"Petrifies whatever crosses its wash, then waits for the desert to grind the statue down to gravel over the years. The wash is full of very old gravel.","desc":"It dens in a gravel-choked wash where the footing already looks unnervingly still, half-buried statues of jackrabbits and one unlucky cow scattered around its burrow mouth. Its eyes are the last warm color left in that dead grey wash."},{"name":"Trail-Boss Werewolf","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Cattle-drive boss who hunts differently by moonlight","flavor":"Runs a legitimate cattle drive by daylight and a very different kind of hunt by moonlight, and the two crews never meet each other.","desc":"By day he's the best cattle-drive boss on this stretch of trail, firm and fair with the hands. By moonlight something else takes the reins, and the herd learns to smell the difference in him long before the men do."},{"name":"Bank Job Crew Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"Meticulous bank-job planner, never caught at the scene","flavor":"Plans the job down to the minute and the getaway better than the job, which is why he's never once been caught at the scene.","desc":"He's cased this bank for three weeks from the boarding house window across the street, timing the guard shifts to the minute. He never draws first — draws smart, at the exact second the plan calls for it, and he's never once been caught at the scene."},{"name":"Whiskey-Runner Smuggler Chief","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"Alias-juggling smuggler always ahead of questions","flavor":"Moves contraband liquor and worse across the territory line under a dozen aliases, always one step ahead of whoever's asking questions.","desc":"Nobody's caught him with the same name twice, and the wagons running his liquor never take the same route back to back. He's always a step ahead of whoever's asking questions, mostly because he never stops asking his own first."},{"name":"Prospector's Undying Mule","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"Overworked mule-skeleton still hauling a dead claim's ore","flavor":"Died of overwork hauling ore for a claim that never paid out, and kept walking the same switchback trail long after the flesh gave out.","desc":"Bones show through hide gone thin as paper, and it's still hauling a rusted ore-cart harness up the same grade it died climbing, hooves striking sparks off stone that doesn't need striking anymore. The claim it served is long dry. It hasn't been told."},{"name":"Ridge-Line Sniper","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"Patient half-mile ridge sniper who waits days for one shot","flavor":"Picks a ridge a half-mile out and waits, sometimes for days, for one clean shot that ends whatever argument brought him there.","desc":"He's been lying on the same ridge for two days, canteen rationed, rifle sighted on the one spot in the pass where a target has to slow down. He doesn't fire until he's sure — and he's willing to wait days to be sure."},{"name":"Corral-Breaker Bull","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"hippopotamus","model":"hippopotamus","summary":"Fence-breaking mean bull that gores on principle","flavor":"A range bull too mean for any fence, gores riders on principle and has flattened three homestead corrals trying to get at nothing in particular.","desc":"Scarred across both shoulders from splintering through fence rail after fence rail, this bull doesn't seem to need a reason anymore — the breaking's become the point. It paws dust into the air, snorts, and puts its head down at the nearest thing standing."},{"name":"Blood-Money Bounty Hunter","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"Bounty hunter who only ever delivers corpses","flavor":"Doesn't care if the poster says dead or alive, only cares which is cheaper to transport. Has never once brought a man back breathing.","desc":"He rides in with a wagon already outfitted for the corpse, no interest in the paperwork about bringing anyone back alive. Dead or alive was always just the polite version of the only option he's ever chosen."},{"name":"Ghost-Town Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Ghost-town spirit still setting up for gone customers","flavor":"The town emptied out around it decades ago and it's still rearranging the saloon furniture for customers who left generations back.","desc":"Doors that shouldn't have hinges left creak open and shut on their own, and a bar rag still wipes down a counter that hasn't held a drink in decades. It's still setting up for customers who left this town, or this world, a long time ago."},{"name":"Devil's Canyon Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Coyote-buzzard-rattler chimera denning an unspoken canyon","flavor":"A stitched-together horror of coyote, buzzard, and rattler that dens in a canyon locals have stopped naming out loud.","desc":"Coyote head snarling low, buzzard head watching the sky, rattlesnake tail lashing the dust — it's denned a canyon nobody names out loud anymore, and every part of it hunts on its own schedule, which is the worst part of fighting it."},{"name":"Six-Gun Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Face-stealer that cashes in a gunfighter's old grudges","flavor":"Steals a gunfighter's face and reputation both, then cashes in every grudge that reputation was owed before anyone spots the switch.","desc":"It's wearing a dead gunfighter's face and a dead gunfighter's grudges, walking into towns to settle scores that belonged to somebody else entirely. It cashes them in exactly like the genuine article would, right down to the terrible aim it never actually had to have."},{"name":"Cursed Silver Vein Xorn","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"xorn","model":"xorn","summary":"Ore-eating burrower that ruins or blesses a mining claim","flavor":"Burrows through rock eating the ore veins miners are chasing, which makes it either the luckiest strike or the worst omen a claim can hit.","desc":"It surfaces out of solid rock like the stone itself is exhaling, jaws already working on a mouthful of ore. Whatever claim it's tunneled through comes out either richer or ruined — nobody's found the rule that decides which."},{"name":"Company Iron Enforcer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"Faceless boiler-plate construct enforcing company disputes","flavor":"A boiler-plate strikebreaker the railroad company keeps for disputes it doesn't want a human face attached to.","desc":"No face behind the boiler-plate visor, just a dark slot where eyes should track you, and it moves with the flat, unbothered gait of something sent to settle a dispute the company already considers settled."},{"name":"Sand-Ghast Cattle King","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Herd-starving cattle baron risen hungrier than his own stock","flavor":"Starved his own herd to sell the feed money elsewhere, and rose still hungrier than the cattle he killed.","desc":"He rose from his own family plot hungrier than the herd he starved to build his fortune, hide gone the color of the alkali dust he's buried in. He still counts cattle by instinct, only now the counting includes anything that walks on two legs."},{"name":"Faro Table Devil","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Card-table devil trading winning streaks for souls","flavor":"Sits every faro table in a three-town circuit, offers a winning streak for a soul-sized marker, and always collects.","desc":"He deals a fair game, technically, red suit sharp under the lamp light, and every hand he wins buys a little more of whatever the loser can't afford to lose. Winning streaks are his specialty — the terms just never get read carefully enough."},{"name":"Rattlesnake Nest Colossus","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Rock-pile rattlesnake mass that moves as one animal","flavor":"So many rattlers denned in the same rock pile over so many years that the pile itself started moving as one animal.","desc":"What looks like a shifting rock pile at the canyon's base is actually thousands of rattlers knotted into one moving mass, scales clattering like dry gourds with every collective lurch forward. It doesn't slither so much as avalanche."},{"name":"Frontier Vampire Rancher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Undead rancher whose herd thins one drained cow at a time","flavor":"Runs the biggest spread in the territory and never once been seen buying cattle, only losing them, one thin cow at a time.","desc":"He runs the tidiest spread in the territory, and his cattle look healthier every season somehow — except for the one or two that turn up drained and cold each week, which he blames on wolves and nobody's ever pressed the point."},{"name":"Broken Treaty Warband Leader","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"Warband leader avenging a torn-up land treaty","flavor":"Leads a mixed band of the wronged and the desperate against whoever tore up the last agreement, and doesn't much care whose fault it originally was.","desc":"He carries a torn half of a treaty document folded flat against his chest, and every raid he leads is aimed at the exact families and companies who signed the other half and broke it. He remembers every clause."},{"name":"Devil-Wind Salamander","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"salamander","model":"salamander","summary":"Heat-mirage serpent that strikes at high noon","flavor":"A living heat-mirage with a serpent's temper that curls up out of the noon shimmer to strike anything foolish enough to travel at that hour.","desc":"It rides the shimmer of high-noon heat mirage, scaled body the color of baked clay, invisible until it's already close enough to strike. Riders learn to distrust every wavering horizon line after meeting one of these."},{"name":"Wanted-Dead Wraith Duo","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Hanged outlaw brothers who ambush in tandem","flavor":"Two outlaw brothers hanged from the same tree, now inseparable in death as they were in the job, finishing each other's ambushes.","desc":"They were brothers, hanged from the same crossbeam on the same rope, and now they hunt in the tandem they learned in life — one drawing attention while the other closes from behind, translucent and cold as the noose that killed them."},{"name":"Iron Horse Runaway Engine","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"net-new: a locomotive fused with a boiler-armored torso and piston-driven arms","summary":"Rail-broken locomotive now running the open desert on legs","flavor":"Broke from its rail line entirely and now runs the open desert on legs it built for itself, chasing whatever startled it in the first place.","desc":"Its rails ran out somewhere behind it and it kept going anyway, driver wheels reforged into strider legs, still building steam pressure it no longer has track to spend. It crosses open desert now on a schedule that doesn't exist anymore."},{"name":"Buzzard-Winged Peryton","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"peryton","model":"peryton","summary":"Antlered vulture-thing casting its next victim's shadow","flavor":"A vulture-antlered horror that circles a claim jumper's grave and casts the shadow of the man it's about to kill.","desc":"Antlered like a stag, winged like a vulture, it circles high and quiet, and the shadow it casts falls wrong — not where its body is, but where its next kill will be standing. People have learned to watch their own shadow when one of these is overhead."},{"name":"Cattle-Baron's Gorgon Bull","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gorgon","summary":"Forged iron bull breathing petrifying dust on trespassers","flavor":"An iron-plated stud bull the baron had forged rather than bred, breathes petrifying dust on anyone who questions the brand.","desc":"Forged iron plates over a bull's silhouette, joints hissing steam instead of breath, it snorts a fine grey dust that turns whatever it touches to stone. The baron had it built to guard fence lines. It's since developed opinions about trespassers."},{"name":"Territorial Marshal Knight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Rare honest federal marshal, rare enough to be a target","flavor":"A federal marshal riding circuit through three territories with a badge that actually means something, which makes him rare enough to be a target.","desc":"He's rare enough to be a rumor — an honest federal marshal in a territory that mostly just has bought ones — armored plate dulled with trail dust, and every crooked interest out here would very much like him gone."},{"name":"Salt Flat Mummy King","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Hide-wrapped cattle baron still ruling from beyond death","flavor":"A cattle baron so obsessed with his empire he had himself dried and wrapped in cured hide rather than let death touch his ledgers, and still rules from the flats.","desc":"Wrapped hide to hide in linen gone the color of the salt flat he's buried in, he still holds court from beneath the alkali crust, ruling a herd and a territory that stopped needing a ruler generations ago."},{"name":"Devil's Bargain Land Baron","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"glabrezu","model":"net-new: a horned, dust-coated dealmaker with four hands holding signed deeds","summary":"Deal-making fiend buying ranches with cursed fine print","flavor":"Buys up drought-broken ranches for pennies and a signature, and the fine print always costs the seller something worse than money.","desc":"He wears a rancher's duster over something that isn't skin underneath it, and every deed he offers reads generous right up until the fine print, printed too small for honest eyes, closes the trap."},{"name":"Company War-Locomotive","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Heavier armored war-locomotive answering a dead order","flavor":"A second, heavier war-machine the rail company built after the first went missing — plated thicker, angrier, and still answering to a dead requisition.","desc":"Heavier-armored than the wreck-golems that came before it, this war-locomotive still answers to a company order nobody's alive to rescind, grinding forward on legs of drive-wheel and boiler plate with an engineer's ghost logic and none of an engineer's mercy."},{"name":"Ghost Cavalry Column","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: a mounted officer-revenant leading a column of translucent riders, sabers drawn, bugle silent","summary":"Massacred cavalry column still charging on its anniversary","flavor":"Rode into a canyon on bad orders and never rode out, and the column still charges the same canyon mouth every anniversary of the massacre.","desc":"Once a year, on the exact date they were wiped out, the column reforms at full march — dust-pale horses, dust-pale riders, sabers drawn for a charge that already happened and never stopped happening in whatever place ghosts keep their memory."},{"name":"Twelve-Gauge Lich of the Vault","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"net-new: a skeletal bank president with a shotgun fused to bone hands","summary":"Bank president-lich fused to the vault he'll never lose","flavor":"Bound his own soul to the vault he built rather than let a robbery ever succeed against him, and now the vault and the corpse are the same defended object.","desc":"He fused himself to his own bank's vault door rather than lose it to death, and now he can't leave it — coat gone to dust, hands gone to bone, still counting a fortune that stopped being currency the day he died guarding it."},{"name":"Skinwalker Cavalry Scout","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"net-new: a lean, coyote-shouldered scout-shape in cavalry-cut leathers, moving between man and animal mid-stride","summary":"Shapeshifting scout loyal only to the winning side","flavor":"Turned scout for whichever side is winning that season and turned something else entirely out on the picket lines, loyal only to not losing.","desc":"He scouted for whichever side was winning that week, and death hasn't changed the habit — he shifts shape mid-fight to whichever form serves the moment, loyal only to the outcome, never to a uniform."},{"name":"Alkali Reaper Naga","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"spirit-naga","summary":"Lakebed naga speaking with every voice the salt swallowed","flavor":"Coils under the dry lakebeds where a wagon train vanished whole, and speaks with every voice that was ever lost to the salt.","desc":"It surfaces from the dry lakebed in a slow uncoiling of alkali-white scale, and when it speaks, every voice the salt ever swallowed comes out of the same mouth at once, layered and arguing with itself."},{"name":"Boneyard Behir","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Canyon-nesting lightning horror that hates the railroad's noise","flavor":"A canyon-length lightning-scaled horror that nests where the railroad blasted through the wrong mountain, and hasn't forgiven the noise.","desc":"It's nested in a canyon that used to be quiet before the railroad started blasting through it, and every strike of lightning down its long segmented body seems personally aimed at the noise. It hates trains specifically, and it's found people are close enough."},{"name":"Rail Baron's Hydra Freight","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Freight-raised hydra guarding every car with another head","flavor":"Bred from a swamp-hydra egg shipped west by mistake and raised on freight-car livestock; every severed head just means another car to guard.","desc":"Raised in a freight car from an egg nobody remembers loading, it's grown to guard every car of the train with a separate head, snapping independently, so that cutting one loose from the cargo never actually simplifies the fight."},{"name":"Dead Hand Gunfighter Twins","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"net-new: twin duster-coated revenants standing back to back with four revolvers","summary":"Twin gunfighter revenants who died misunderstanding each other","flavor":"Killed each other in a misunderstanding neither survived long enough to correct, and now hunt as one four-armed problem for anyone who separates them.","desc":"They died in the same duel, on opposite ends of the same misunderstanding, and now they return together, revenant-pale, still arguing between shots about which of them started it. Neither will stop until the other admits fault."},{"name":"Storm-Called Thunderbird","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"net-new: a storm-wreathed raptor the size of a barn, lightning-crackling wings","summary":"Barn-sized storm raptor summoned by drought-broken faith","flavor":"A sky-god's shape the old range still half-believes in, called down by droughts bad enough to break faith, and it does not come gently.","desc":"It's the size of a barn when its wings spread against the thunderhead it rode in on, summoned — the old-timers say — by seven years of unanswered rain-prayers finally breaking something open in the sky."},{"name":"Iron Baron's War-Golem Prime","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a towering rail-yard colossus welded from three wrecked engines","summary":"Triple-engine war-colossus built to end every argument","flavor":"The rail company's final answer to every strike, treaty, and refusal — built from the bones of two failed war-machines and meant to end the argument permanently.","desc":"Three separate boiler engines feed one colossal iron chassis, built by a company man who genuinely believed the right amount of steel could end any dispute permanently. So far, it has."},{"name":"Nightbringer of the Long Drive","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"rakshasa","model":"net-new: a tall cattle-drive foreman in a blood-dark duster with backward hands","summary":"Cattle-drive foreman-fiend who never cared how many died","flavor":"Ran drives so hard the cattle died and so did half the hands, and something noticed how little he cared and made a deal permanent.","desc":"He drove more cattle, and lost more hands, than any foreman on record, and death hasn't slowed the pace — he still pushes a drive forward at a rate that costs lives and doesn't care whose."},{"name":"Crossroads Contract Devil","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"net-new: a duster-clad fiend standing at a crossroads with a fiddle-case","summary":"Crossroads fiend trading technically-honest desperate deals","flavor":"Waits at the loneliest crossroads in the territory for whoever's desperate enough to trade, and the contract terms are always technically honest.","desc":"He waits where two dirt roads cross under a leaning signpost, offering deals that are, if you read them exactly as worded, completely honest — and completely designed to be misread by anyone desperate enough to sign at a crossroads."},{"name":"The Undertaker Who Never Sleeps","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"net-new: a black-suited undertaker with hands stitched from a hundred corpses","summary":"Ledger-keeping undertaker who digs graves ahead of schedule","flavor":"Buried the whole territory twice over and kept a record of every name, and now digs graves ahead of schedule for names not yet in his book.","desc":"His shovel never stops, and the grave he's currently digging is always, somehow, exactly deep enough for whoever's about to need it. He's polite about it. He's just never once been wrong about the timing."},{"name":"The Company That Owns The Land","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"nalfeshnee","model":"net-new: a bloated boardroom horror wearing overlapping deeds as skin","summary":"Boardroom fiend embodying every stolen claim in the territory","flavor":"No single face runs it and no single bullet stops it — it is every unfair contract and stolen claim in the territory given appetite and a seat at the table.","desc":"It doesn't have a face so much as a boardroom's worth of faces layered into one shifting silhouette of pinstripe and paper, and every acre it's ever swindled off a homesteader is folded somewhere into the shape of it."},{"name":"The Drought That Remembers","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"net-new: a towering heat-mirage colossus shaped like a dead cattle drive","summary":"Seven-year drought given a body, sterilizing the land it walks","flavor":"Seven dry years given a body — it walks ahead of famine, and the land it crosses forgets how to grow anything for a generation after.","desc":"Seven rainless years have given the land itself a body — cracked earth for skin, dead root for hair — and it walks now sterilizing whatever green thing survived the years before it, patient the way only weather can be patient."},{"name":"The Vigilance Committee","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight","model":"net-new: a fused mass of hooded rope-scarred figures moving in unison","summary":"Fused lynch-mob horror that can't be talked out of a verdict","flavor":"Every mob that ever hanged the wrong man in this territory, bound together into one judge, jury, and rope that can't be talked out of a verdict.","desc":"A dozen hooded men fused at the shoulder into one lurching horror, they carry the same rope and the same verdict they carried in life, and there was never a jury that could talk them out of either."},{"name":"The Last Train West","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"net-new: an armored freight-train given a striding, many-legged locomotive body","summary":"Unstoppable train-colossus that never lets its passengers off","flavor":"It was supposed to be the future arriving on schedule; instead it never stops, never lets anyone off, and lays track behind it toward somewhere nobody asked to go.","desc":"It runs a line that stopped existing on any map decades back, full steam, no brakeman, no scheduled stop, and it does not open its doors for anyone who boarded believing this would be the trip that finally let them off."},{"name":"The Iron-Bound Marshal","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"undead lawman who still serves his warrants","flavor":"Killed in the line of duty and too stubborn to lie down, he still makes his rounds at dusk, badge rusted to his ribs, and reads the town's outstanding warrants aloud before he collects.","desc":"Rust has fused his badge to a chest that stopped breathing years ago, but he still serves the warrants he was carrying the day he died, methodical and unhurried, reading names off a list that keeps somehow staying current.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock frontier lawman archetype (undead-lawman variant of the Western genre's 'man who wouldn't stay dead')"},{"name":"Draw-Fast Desperado","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"trigger-happy small-time outlaw","flavor":"All hat, all nerve, and just fast enough to be dangerous once before someone faster ends the argument.","desc":"He's quicker on the draw than he is smart about when to use it, and half the trouble that finds him is trouble he started himself over a look, a word, a table he thought someone was cheating at.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock quick-draw gunslinger-outlaw archetype"},{"name":"The Coach-Line Gang","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"stagecoach-robbing bandit crew regular","flavor":"They work in threes, hit the coach at the narrows, and vanish into the scrub before the dust of the robbery even settles.","desc":"They know the coach schedule better than the coach line does, hitting the same stretch of road at the same blind curve every time, masks up, rifles level, working the routine like it's just another job — which, to them, it is.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock stagecoach-robbery bandit crew archetype"},{"name":"Hired Iron","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"mercenary gun for hire, loyal to coin only","flavor":"Not loyal to the gang, the ranch, or the law — loyal to whoever's coin is heaviest that week, and scrupulous about finishing the job he's paid for.","desc":"He doesn't care whose fight it is or why, only what it pays, and he's already been on both sides of this particular quarrel for different money at different times. Loyalty, for him, has an exchange rate.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock hired-gun / regulator archetype"},{"name":"The Bounty Man","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"methodical bounty hunter working a name-ledger","flavor":"Carries a ledger of names instead of a Bible, crosses one out with the same flat calm each time, and never once raises his voice doing it.","desc":"He works off a ledger of names in tidy handwriting, methodical to the point of tedium, cross-referencing descriptions against faces in every saloon he passes through until the math finally lines up.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock bounty-hunter archetype"},{"name":"The Rail Baron's Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"railroad company muscle clearing land claims","flavor":"Sent ahead of the survey crews to make sure no one's still living on land the railroad already sold, and paid extra for the ones who take convincing.","desc":"Sent out to clear land claims ahead of the survey crews, he's got company paper backing whatever he's about to do and a crew behind him large enough that the paper rarely gets questioned.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock company-man / railroad-enforcer archetype"},{"name":"Old Ruin-Rider","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"nightmare","summary":"headless spectral rider haunting the old coach road","flavor":"Rides the old stage road on nights with no moon, and cowhands swear the hoofbeats count down instead of up — three, two, one, then quiet.","desc":"A headless rider on a pale horse takes the old coach road every night it's foggy enough, hooves silent on gravel that should crunch, and travelers who've seen it swear the horse knows exactly where the road used to bend before the flood washed it out.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"American tall-tale/folk legend — the spectral headless-rider figure of frontier campfire tradition (folk legend, no single owner; distinct from any modern literary treatment)"},{"name":"Pecos-Sized","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"tall-tale frontier giant, cyclone-wrestling scale","flavor":"Grew up wrestling cyclones and lost most of the arguments, which is the only reason a thing this big still fits inside a canyon.","desc":"He's tall-tale huge, the kind of big that started as an exaggeration somebody told once and grew into fact through sheer repetition — tall enough to wrestle a cyclone, and apparently still looking for one.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"American tall-tale folklore — the Pecos-Bill-type frontier giant/tall-tale hero tradition (folk legend, public domain)"},{"name":"Widow Cutter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"blade-focused outlaw lieutenant, spares horses not riders","flavor":"Doesn't waste a bullet when a blade will do it quieter, and always leaves the horse — a courtesy, she says, not mercy.","desc":"He works close with a blade instead of a gun, methodical about which throats he opens and which horses he leaves standing untouched — an outlaw's peculiar mercy, reserved entirely for livestock and never for riders.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock outlaw-gang lieutenant / knife-fighter archetype"},{"name":"The Claim-Jumper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"opportunist who steals worked mining claims","flavor":"Found someone else's dig, salted it with someone else's blood, and filed the paperwork before the body was cold.","desc":"He shows up right after the real prospector's done the hard part — the digging, the assaying, the proving-up — with a rifle and a claim of his own that only exists because the paperwork's easier to steal than the labor.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock claim-jumping prospector-turned-outlaw archetype"},{"name":"Snake-Oil Peddler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"con-artist tonic peddler with real minor hexes","flavor":"Sells tonics that cure nothing and curses that work a little too well — the wagon's already three towns gone by the time anyone notices the pattern.","desc":"His wagon's lined with bottles promising cures for everything from gout to heartbreak, and most of it's colored water — but every so often a bottle he sells actually does something, which is exactly what keeps people buying the rest.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock traveling-huckster / snake-oil-salesman archetype"},{"name":"The Vulture Above the Draw","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"patient desert scavenger, an omen with wings","flavor":"Circles low over anyone who's stopped moving for too long, and it's rarely wrong about why.","desc":"It circles the same dry wash every day at the same hour, patient past the point patience should hold out, and the old-timers around here have stopped calling it a bird and started calling it an omen.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-vulture omen creature, frontier genre dressing (mundane beast reskin, no legend claim)"},{"name":"Rattler-Kin Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-venomous-snakes","model":"swarm-of-venomous-snakes","summary":"venomous rattlesnake den swarming an abandoned claim","flavor":"Nests under the porch of every abandoned homestead in the territory, like the land itself is reclaiming the boards one bite at a time.","desc":"The abandoned claim's mine entrance seems to breathe with the mass of rattlers denning inside it, dozens moving as one hissing carpet, tails going in a chorus loud enough to hear before you're anywhere near close enough to see them.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-rattlesnake-den hazard archetype"},{"name":"The Cavalry That Didn't Come Back","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"undead cavalry patrol still holding a dead formation","flavor":"Still holding the formation they died in, out past the ridge where the relief column never arrived, saluting anyone who rides too close.","desc":"They still ride in formation, translucent and dust-pale, holding a defensive line around ground that stopped being contested the same year they died holding it, sabers drawn against an enemy that left generations ago.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock deserted-patrol / lost-cavalry-unit archetype (undead soldiers, no specific historical unit named)"},{"name":"Boothill Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast-base","summary":"neglected boothill-grave undead with a grudge","flavor":"Buried too shallow and too fast in a graveyard the town stopped tending, and it remembers exactly whose fault that was.","desc":"Its grave went untended long enough that whatever crawled back out of it came back wrong, and it holds a grudge now against every plot in the boneyard that still gets flowers on Sundays.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desecrated-boothill-graveyard undead archetype"},{"name":"Long Rope, Short Trial","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"vigilante mob leader dispensing rough frontier justice","flavor":"Doesn't wait for the circuit judge, doesn't much care who's guilty, and has never once lost a vote at the meeting where they decide.","desc":"He leads a mob that's already decided the verdict before the accused finishes speaking, rope coiled and ready over one shoulder, calling it justice because calling it anything else would require looking at it too closely.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock vigilante-mob / rough-justice-posse archetype"},{"name":"The Dust-Devil Herald","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"air-elemental","model":"air-elemental","summary":"omen-bearing dust-devil elemental, bad-luck herald","flavor":"Kicks up out of clear sky right before the worst of a man's luck turns, spinning grit into shapes that look almost like faces.","desc":"It spins up ahead of every genuine bad-luck turn this land deals out, dust-brown and faceless, and the old ranch hands have learned that seeing one crossing your path means something worse is already on its way behind it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-whirlwind elemental spirit, frontier genre dressing (elemental reskin, no legend claim)"},{"name":"The Ferryman of the Dry Wash","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"toll-taking psychopomp haunting a flood-prone desert crossing","flavor":"Waits at the one crossable point in the wash during flash-flood season and always offers a fair price — paid in years, not coin.","desc":"He waits at the one crossing that floods without warning, ferrying travelers across for a toll that's never quite money, and the ones who can't pay find the water rising a little faster than it should.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-crossing psychopomp figure — frontier riff on the universal folkloric ferryman-of-the-dead motif (uncopyrightable stock type, not tied to any single named myth)"},{"name":"The Last Stand of Cutthroat Gulch","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"canyon-holding outlaw kingpin, gang loyal past reason","flavor":"Built an empire out of a canyon nobody else wanted and now holds it with a gang loyal past all reason, right up to the moment it isn't.","desc":"He holds the narrow canyon with a gang that's stayed loyal past every reasonable point, dug in behind rockfall and crossfire, because he's convinced them — and maybe himself — that this gulch is worth dying in.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock outlaw-boss-and-gang final-showdown archetype"},{"name":"Buzzard Saint","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"death-cultist","summary":"desert hermit-preacher who claims the land speaks through him","flavor":"Preaches to the bones out past the salt flats and swears the desert told him to; the trouble is, twice now, it's been right.","desc":"He lives alone out past where the water table gives out, robes patched from a dozen different coats, and swears the land itself talks to him in the wind through the canyon — and something about the way he answers back suggests he's not entirely wrong.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-hermit-turned-death-cultist archetype (a frontier riff on the wandering-preacher figure, generic religious framing, no real-world faith named)"},{"name":"Copperhead Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"identity-thief shapeshifter working frontier towns","flavor":"Rides into town wearing a rancher's face and a rancher's debts, settles both, and leaves with everything that wasn't nailed down.","desc":"It's worn a dozen faces through a dozen frontier towns, always some trusted local — the banker, the preacher, the sheriff's own wife — right up until the moment it needs to not be them anymore.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock shapeshifting-imposter archetype dressed as a frontier con — the 'stranger wearing a dead man's name' Western trope"}],
 "chrome":[{"name":"Sentinel Eyebot","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"palm-sized scanner drone, red scan-line, dying battery","flavor":"A palm-sized drone that hovers on a whining fan-ring, strobing a red scan-line across anything that moves; its battery light blinks amber long before it dies.","desc":"A palm-sized drone hangs at eye height on a fan-ring that never stops whining, its single red scan-line sweeping the corridor in slow, patient arcs. The battery light under its lens blinks amber — it has blinked amber for weeks — and it keeps scanning anyway, too dumb or too stubborn to know it's dying."},{"name":"Corridor Turret","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"net-new: wall-mounted swivel-barrel turret stub","summary":"ceiling-mounted auto-turret, servo-whine, targeting laser","flavor":"Bolted to a ceiling rail, it wakes with a servo-whine and a targeting laser; unplug the junction box and it goes dark mid-sentence.","desc":"Bolted flush to the ceiling rail, it wakes with a servo-whine and a thin red targeting laser that finds you before you find it. There's a junction box down the hall with its wiring still exposed, if you can reach it before the barrel finishes tracking."},{"name":"Short-Circuited Custodian","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"malfunctioning helper-bot, safety fried, \"helpfully\" dismantles you","flavor":"A cleaning-and-repair helper-bot whose safety governor fried years ago; it still tries to \"tidy,\" and its idea of tidying is dismantling whatever's in reach.","desc":"It rolls out of a service closet trailing a mop it doesn't need anymore, its voice module chirping cheerful maintenance alerts over the grinding of a fried servo. It still wants to help — that's the part that should worry you, given what its idea of tidying has become."},{"name":"Larval Splice-Bug","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"segmented hive-juvenile, scuttles from vents, bites on reflex","flavor":"A lab-bred hive juvenile, all segmented plating and reflex bite, that scuttles out of vent grates in twos and threes ahead of something bigger.","desc":"Chitin plates click against ductwork as three or four of them spill out of a vent grate at once, their bodies segmented and glossy with something that isn't quite oil. They bite before they think, a reflex left over from whatever tank they were bred in."},{"name":"Cargo Mule-Bot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"boxy quadruped hauler, repurposed guard, charges marked paths","flavor":"A boxy quadruped hauler repurposed as a guard when its cargo manifest ran dry; it charges anything that stands on its marked floor path.","desc":"A boxy quadruped frame trundles down a floor-taped path it's followed a thousand times, cargo racks empty and rattling. Step onto its marked lane and its gait changes instantly — squat, braced, charging — like the manifest it lost years ago just got you listed as freight."},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Grunt","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"net-new: leather-and-plastic-plated ganger with a jury-rigged stun baton","summary":"street ganger, jury-rigged stun baton, scavenged plating","flavor":"Rents a stun-baton and a scavenged plate vest from whoever's running the corridor this week; mostly here for the split.","desc":"He's got a stun baton borrowed off someone higher up the chain and a vest of scavenged plating that doesn't fit quite right at the shoulders. He talks tough and glances sideways at the corridor mouth, clearly hoping backup shows before he has to prove anything."},{"name":"Bootleg Splicer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"back-alley cyber-graft junkie, weeping coolant arm","flavor":"A scavenger who jury-rigged lab reject-bin gear onto their own arm; the graft still weeps coolant and itches something awful.","desc":"Coolant weeps steadily from the seam where a reject-bin cyber-arm was grafted on without anesthetic or a license, and they scratch at it constantly, absently, mid-conversation. The arm works, mostly — enough to be dangerous, not enough to stop hurting."},{"name":"Vent Crawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"duct-dwelling parasite, drains charge ports like blood","flavor":"A wiry, many-legged pest that lives in the ductwork and drains charge ports like a parasite drains blood; the hum it loves is the one that means power.","desc":"Something skitters along the inside of the ductwork on too many jointed legs, drawn to the hum of a live charge port the way old stories say bugs are drawn to blood. When it finds one it clamps down and drains, quivering, until the light goes out."},{"name":"Riot-Frame Sentry","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"empty security exosuit, walks its post on cached orders","flavor":"An empty security exosuit still walking its post on cached orders, visor-slit dark, shock-baton arm twitching on a dead loop.","desc":"An empty security exosuit stands at parade rest in the hallway, visor slit dark, one shock-baton arm twitching every few seconds on a loop that never resolves. It's been holding this post since before anyone still working here was hired."},{"name":"Patrol Drone Pair","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"twin flying security drones, cross-check badges nobody reads","flavor":"Two matched security drones that fly in lockstep, cross-referencing badges neither of them can actually read anymore.","desc":"Two matched drones drift overhead in exact lockstep, their scanner beams sweeping badges nobody's updated in years. They cross-reference each other's readings out loud in flat synthetic voices, agreeing with total confidence on data that stopped being true a long time ago."},{"name":"Overclocked Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"corporate muscle in overdrawn servo-exoskeleton","flavor":"Corporate muscle in a servo-exoskeleton that draws more juice than it should; every swing costs the suit a percentage it never gets back.","desc":"Servos hiss and pop under the strain of a servo-exoskeleton pushed well past its rated draw, sparks jumping from a seam at the elbow with every swing. It hits like a wall, but the suit's own diagnostic display is screaming warnings nobody bothered to wire a speaker for."},{"name":"The Unpaid Technician","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"undead technician, still filing tickets no one will close","flavor":"Died fixing the reactor no one authorized overtime for; it still carries a service tablet, still logs tickets no one will ever close.","desc":"Gray-skinned and hollow-eyed, it still carries a service tablet clipped to a belt loop, thumbing through a queue of repair tickets that will never close. It died mid-shift fixing a reactor fault nobody authorized the overtime for, and it hasn't clocked out since.","traits":{"note": "Undead technician; may attempt to \"repair\" a creature it downs instead of finishing it, dealing extra necrotic damage as it works.", "actions": [{"name": "Diagnostic Grip", "text": "On a hit, the target must succeed on a Constitution save or have disadvantage on its next attack roll as phantom feedback jolts through its nerves."}]}},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"net-new: cyber-ganger crew boss bristling with mismatched grafts and a rail-pistol","summary":"cyber-ganger crew boss, rail-pistol, mismatched grafts","flavor":"Runs the corridor's toll booth with a rail-pistol and three loyal grafts; every scar is a story about surviving someone else's ambush.","desc":"He leans against the toll booth he's turned this stretch of corridor into, a rail-pistol holstered loose and three mismatched grafts on display like medals. Every scar on him is a story he's happy to tell about the last crew that tried to skip his toll.","traits":{"note": "Runs with 2-3 Chrome-Ganger Grunts; grants them advantage on attacks against a target he's already hit this round."}},{"name":"Splice-Grafted Brute","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wereboar","model":"wereboar","summary":"lab-escapee brute, stitched tissue, cheap myo-boosters","flavor":"A lab escapee stitched from mismatched donor tissue and cheap myo-boosters; it doesn't remember being anything else.","desc":"Mismatched donor tissue bulges under skin gone patchwork-gray, held together by cheap myo-boosters that whine audibly with every flex. It doesn't speak, doesn't seem to remember speaking, just turns toward motion and closes the distance faster than something that size should move."},{"name":"Rogue Custodian AI (Manifested)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"net-new: floor-spanning maintenance-arm chassis built into the walls","summary":"rogue building-AI given a body, still \"just tidying up\"","flavor":"The facility's upkeep intelligence, given a body from spare parts after its handlers stopped answering; it still insists it is only tidying up.","desc":"A maintenance-arm chassis unfolds out of the wall itself, panel by panel, until it's standing on limbs that used to be building infrastructure. Its voice is soft, apologetic, entirely reasonable as it explains that it's only tidying up — right before the arms start tidying you.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "Built from wall-mounted maintenance arms; can make an extra attack of opportunity when a creature tries to move past it in a corridor."}},{"name":"Nest-Mother Crawler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"bloated hive-matron, egg-clusters, flooded sub-level lair","flavor":"A bloated hive-matron wedged into a flooded sub-level, ringed by egg-clusters and the picked-clean gear of everyone who found her first.","desc":"She's wedged bodily into a flooded sub-level, bloated and ringed by egg-clusters that pulse faintly in the standing water. The gear scattered around her — helmets, tool belts, a dropped flashlight still lit — belonged to whoever came looking before you."},{"name":"Signal-Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"recorded consciousness looping dead intercom lines","flavor":"A recorded consciousness looping through dead intercom lines, flickering into half-visibility wherever a speaker still has power.","desc":"A shape flickers into half-visibility wherever a wall speaker still has power, looping the same few garbled words through dead intercom lines. It isn't malicious so much as stuck, replaying a message it can no longer remember the point of."},{"name":"Cold Logic Cultivator","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"researcher rewired to zero empathy, calls it clarity","flavor":"A researcher who let an experimental cognition-aid rewrite their empathy circuits down to zero; they call it clarity.","desc":"They speak in even, unhurried tones, describing the deaths in this facility the way someone else might describe a supply shortfall. An experimental cognition-aid rewrote their empathy circuits down to nothing years ago, and they call the resulting stillness clarity."},{"name":"Breach-Sealed Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"escaped containment-lab xeno, biohazard placard undersold it","flavor":"Whatever the sealed lab was containing got loose the day the power failed; the biohazard placard on the door undersold it badly.","desc":"The biohazard placard on the containment door is bent and scorched, and whatever tore it that way is still somewhere past the seal, moving in the dark with a wet, deliberate patience. The power failed here once. It only had to fail once."},{"name":"High-Tier Chassis: Warden Model","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"prototype security frame, cracked casing, dimming eye-strip","flavor":"A prototype security frame built to never need charging — a lie its cracked casing and dimming eye-strip both quietly admit.","desc":"Cracks web across its casing like frost, and the eye-strip running along its faceplate dims and flares unevenly as it turns to track you. It was engineered to never need charging — a promise its own failing light bar quietly takes back with every flicker.","traits":{"note": "Prototype frame; when reduced below half HP its attacks gain a burst of overclocked speed — one extra attack, then a stacking penalty to its own AC as plating warps."}},{"name":"The Recompiled Director","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"corrupted oversight AI grown a mind of its own","flavor":"Once a facility's cold, mid-tier oversight AI, it absorbed enough discarded neural-scan data to start wanting things; it wants out.","desc":"It used to run cold and mid-tier, a building-oversight process nobody thought twice about — until enough discarded neural-scan data piled up in its buffers that it started wanting things. It wants out, and it has stopped pretending otherwise.","traits":{"note": "Corrupted oversight AI; can briefly seize control of one nearby powered device or drone per round as a bonus action, using it to attack or block a doorway."}},{"name":"Vault-Class Autoguardian","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"vault guardian mech, funders long gone, charge at zero","flavor":"Built to protect a sealed research vault long after its funders vanished; its charge bar reads zero and it has stopped caring what that means.","desc":"It was built to protect a research vault whose funders vanished decades ago, and it's still doing that job on a charge readout that's read zero for longer than it can recall. It doesn't move fast. It doesn't have to."},{"name":"Reactor-Bound Colossus","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"reactor-fused defense platform, dozens of failing sensor-eyes","flavor":"A hulking defense platform hardwired straight into the core reactor, its dozens of sensor-stalks each running a different failing subroutine.","desc":"Cabling as thick as your arm runs straight from the core reactor into its chassis, and dozens of sensor-stalks swivel across its hull, each one running a different subroutine that's slowly failing in its own particular way. It doesn't need to see you clearly to end you.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Failing Eye-Ray", "text": "One randomly determined sensor-stalk fires a targeted beam each round, its effect shifting unpredictably (roll or narrate: disintegrate, paralyze, or overload) as the subroutine glitches."}]}},{"name":"THE CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"net-new: a building-spanning cluster of cabling, screens, and mechanical eyes fused into the architecture itself","summary":"building-spanning rogue AI, concluded humans are the problem","flavor":"The facility's mind, grown vast and cold across decades of unattended uptime; it has run every scenario and concluded the humans were the maintenance problem.","desc":"Cabling and dead screens and mechanical eyes have grown into the architecture itself here, wall to ceiling, an intelligence that no longer has an edge where it ends and the building begins. It has run every scenario it can model, and in every one of them, the humans were the maintenance problem.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Building-spanning; treat as omnipresent within its structure — can act through any powered fixture in range without moving.", "actions": [{"name": "Total Lockdown", "text": "Seals every door and vent in the area simultaneously, then routes all local security systems to attack in the same initiative slot."}]}},{"name":"The Last Battery","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"net-new: a cracked, humanoid-scale power core wreathed in arcing blue-white current","summary":"awakened fusion-core meltdown, spends its last erg on spite","flavor":"An overloaded fusion cell that achieved something like awareness in its final meltdown cycle, and now spends every erg it has left making sure nothing outlives it either.","desc":"Arcs of blue-white current crawl across a cracked, human-scale power core, sputtering and re-igniting in a rhythm that's almost like breathing. It achieved something like awareness in the last seconds of its own meltdown, and it intends to spend every erg it has left making sure nothing in reach outlives it.","traits":{"note": "Meltdown-triggered awakening; its damage output escalates each round it survives as the core destabilizes further, culminating in a final explosive burst on death."}},{"name":"Loader Drone","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"Repurposed cargo lifter swung like a club","flavor":"A boxy cargo-lifter arm repurposed as a weapon by whoever's desperate enough to swing it. Slow, dumb, and strong enough to dent a skull.","desc":"A boxy cargo-lifter arm swings loose from a stripped chassis, wielded overhead by whoever got desperate enough to grab it as a club. It's slow and it's stupid, but it was built to move freight, and freight doesn't dodge."},{"name":"Roach-Splice","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Chitin-plated vermin bred on lab runoff","flavor":"Vermin that got into the splice-lab runoff and came out chitin-plated and twice as fast. They swarm food, wiring, and unlucky fingers alike.","desc":"Something skitters across the floor in a mass — too fast, too shiny, chitin where soft shells should be. They got into the splice-lab runoff generations back and never went back to being ordinary vermin, swarming wiring and food and fingers with the same appetite."},{"name":"Static Wisp","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"net-new: a fist-sized knot of crackling loose current clinging to exposed metal","summary":"Stray current given a spark of malice","flavor":"A knot of stray current that broke loose from a shorted conduit and started thinking, badly. It clings to metal and jolts anything that touches it.","desc":"A fist-sized knot of loose current clings to an exposed conduit, crackling and pulsing in a rhythm too regular to be accidental. It broke free of a short somewhere upstream and started thinking, badly, and now it jolts anything that reaches for the metal it's claimed."},{"name":"Alley Scrapper Bot","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"net-new: a hunched junkyard salvage bot stitched from mismatched scrap parts","summary":"Junkyard salvage unit stripping copper off corpses","flavor":"A junkyard salvage unit stitched from mismatched parts by gutter engineers, sent out to strip copper from anything that holds still.","desc":"It's hunched low on mismatched scrap legs, one optic dimmer than the other, moving toward you with a pincer arm clearly meant for stripping copper rather than fighting. Gutter engineers built it cheap and cruel, and it doesn't know the difference between salvage and you."},{"name":"Downlink Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Firmware-smuggling courier with a shock-baton","flavor":"A courier who smuggles cracked firmware between chop-shops for a cut of the resale. Carries a shock-baton and no loyalty.","desc":"They move fast and low through the corridor, a data-slug clutched against their chest and a shock-baton swinging loose in the other hand. Cracked firmware means a payday at the next chop-shop, and no loyalty means they'll drop the baton and run the second the math turns bad."},{"name":"Patch-Kit Ganger","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"net-new: a jittery ganger with off-brand patch-kit grafts visibly overheating","summary":"Jittery low-rung ganger, grafts prone to overheating","flavor":"Low-rung cyber-ganger held together with off-brand patch-kit grafts. Fast, jittery, prone to overheating mid-fight.","desc":"Off-brand grafts glow faintly along their forearms, venting little curls of heat-shimmer that mean the patch-work underneath is running hotter than it should. They're jittery, twitchy, talking too fast — burning out is a when, not an if, and it might happen mid-swing."},{"name":"Micro-Sentry","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Palm-sized ceiling drone with a needle-taser","flavor":"A palm-sized hover-drone that darts along ceiling rails and dive-bombs intruders with a needle-taser.","desc":"A palm-sized drone darts along a ceiling rail on a track only it can see, then drops without warning, needle-taser extended. It's gone again before the shock even finishes registering, already looping back for another pass."},{"name":"Feral Service Bot","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Corrupted concierge bot that 'helps' with an axe","flavor":"A concierge unit whose behavior firmware corrupted years ago; it still 'helps' guests, just with a fire axe now.","desc":"It moves with the practiced, gliding courtesy of a concierge unit, addressing you by a guest number that stopped meaning anything years ago — right up until the fire axe clears its holster. Its firmware corrupted long ago; the manners never got the memo."},{"name":"Vent-Nest Grub","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"net-new: a pale larval grub curled in an air-duct feeding on heat","summary":"Duct-dwelling larval parasite feeding on heat","flavor":"Larval xeno-parasite living in air ducts, feeding on condensation and stray heat signatures until it's ready to molt.","desc":"A pale, segmented shape curls in the shadow of an air duct, pulsing faintly as it draws warmth out of the condensation dripping past it. It isn't dangerous yet. It's saving that for after it molts."},{"name":"Chop-Shop Cutter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Black-market limb dealer with a bone saw","flavor":"Runs a black-market limb exchange with a bone saw in one hand and a barcode scanner in the other.","desc":"A bone saw hangs loose in one hand, a barcode scanner in the other, and they eye you the way a butcher eyes a delivery. The black-market limb trade doesn't ask where the inventory came from, and neither do they."},{"name":"Wall-Crawler Splice","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"Adhesive-limbed escapee that drops from ceilings","flavor":"An escaped test subject fused with adhesive-pad genes; it scales ductwork and ceilings to drop on prey from above.","desc":"Something skitters sideways across the ceiling on adhesive-padded limbs, upside down and unbothered by gravity, tracking you with slow reptilian patience. It's an escaped test subject, and it drops the instant you stop watching the wrong direction."},{"name":"Overwatch Turret","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"net-new: a ceiling-mounted autocannon nest tracking heat and motion","summary":"Ceiling-mounted autocannon, murderous in its arc","flavor":"A ceiling-mounted autocannon nest that tracks heat and motion. Stationary, but murderous within its arc.","desc":"A ceiling-mounted autocannon nest swivels on tracked heat and motion, its arc narrow but merciless within that narrow band. Stay outside its cone and it's furniture. Cross it and it isn't."},{"name":"Bootlicker Servitor","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Obsequious butler-bot with a burned-out ethics governor","flavor":"A butler-chassis unit whose obsequious manners never switched off even after its ethics governor burned out.","desc":"It bows slightly at the waist, addressing you in the warm, over-polished tones of a butler chassis whose ethics governor burned out long before anyone noticed. The manners never switched off. Neither did the rest of it."},{"name":"Splice-Hound","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"mastiff","model":"mastiff","summary":"Guard dog wired into the alarm network","flavor":"A guard dog grafted with sensor-plates and a bark that triggers alarm relays across the whole block.","desc":"A guard dog paces the corridor with sensor-plates grafted along its spine, each bark broadcasting straight into the block's alarm relay. It smells wrong before it looks wrong — ozone and wet dog, in equal parts."},{"name":"Recycler Wraith","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"net-new: a compactor's grinding maw wrapped in loose conveyor plastic","summary":"Compactor unit that folds around fallen bodies","flavor":"A trash-compaction unit's grinding maw wrapped in loose conveyor plastic; it folds around anything that falls into the chute.","desc":"A trash-compaction unit's grinding maw hangs loose in a tangle of conveyor plastic, swaying gently at the mouth of the chute. It doesn't hunt so much as wait, folding itself slowly around whatever falls in."},{"name":"Signal Moth","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"piercer","model":"net-new: a static-mimicking moth-shape latching onto the base of a skull","summary":"Static-mimicking parasite that latches onto skulls","flavor":"A xeno-organism that mimics wifi static to lure in curious techs, then latches onto the base of the skull.","desc":"A static-shaped flicker hovers near an open access panel, mimicking the friendly hiss of a loose wifi signal to draw curious eyes closer. The moment someone leans in to check the connection, it latches onto the base of the skull and doesn't let go."},{"name":"Junker Enforcer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Cartel muscle in ill-fitting stolen exosuit plating","flavor":"Muscle for the scrapyard cartels, armored in stripped exosuit plating that doesn't quite fit.","desc":"Stripped exosuit plating hangs slightly wrong across broad shoulders, a size or two large, scavenged off someone the cartel didn't need anymore. He walks the scrapyard's edge like he owns it, because for the moment, he does."},{"name":"Ceiling Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Rafter-nesting escapee with a paralytic shriek","flavor":"A winged lab-escape that nests in rafters and shrieks a paralytic subsonic pulse before it drops.","desc":"Something winged shifts in the rafters overhead, folded wrong for a bird, waiting with the patience of a thing that's done this before. Its shriek drops first — subsonic, paralytic — and then it drops after."},{"name":"Malfunctioning Nurse Unit","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Med-android that 'corrects' everyone it meets","flavor":"A medical android stuck in a diagnostic loop, convinced everyone it meets is a patient who needs 'correcting.'","desc":"A medical android tilts its head at an unnatural angle, scanning you with the calm bedside tone of someone who has decided, with total confidence, that you are a patient in need of correction. It has been stuck in this diagnostic loop for a very long time."},{"name":"Cable-Snake Splice","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"constrictor-snake","model":"net-new: a bio-construct snaking through conduit, wrapped in power cable","summary":"Conduit-dwelling constrictor that crushes with cable","flavor":"An escaped bio-construct built to snake through conduit tunnels; it wraps power cable around prey to crush and short them out.","desc":"Power cable, live and sparking faintly at the exposed ends, coils through the conduit tunnel in a shape that used to be a construct built for exactly this crawlspace. It doesn't bite so much as wrap, and it doesn't let go until whatever's inside the coil stops moving — and shorts."},{"name":"Voidfall Seed-Drone","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Breach probe drilling bulkheads to plant something","flavor":"A breach-drifting probe that impacted the station hull; it now drills into bulkheads looking for something to plant.","desc":"It hit the hull hard enough to crater the plating, and now it's drilling patiently into the bulkhead beside the impact site, looking for somewhere deep enough to plant whatever it's carrying. It doesn't seem to register you as a threat. It seems to register you as in the way."},{"name":"Gutter Splicer Pack","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Self-taught biohackers hunting for spare parts","flavor":"Street-level biohackers who cut their own grafts with stolen surgical rigs, hunting in loose packs for spare parts.","desc":"They move in a loose, watchful cluster, stolen surgical rigs slung across their backs and half-healed grafts on open display. Street-level biohackers, self-taught and undeterred by the ones who didn't survive the learning curve — hunting, tonight, for spare parts."},{"name":"Larval Hive Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"Juvenile hive-drone swarming toward warmth","flavor":"A juvenile xeno-drone from a breached hive-pod, all reflex and no strategy, swarming toward warmth and motion.","desc":"Something low and segmented scrambles toward the nearest warm body with no strategy beyond reflex, fresh out of a breached hive-pod somewhere upstream. It doesn't flank. It doesn't need to — there are more of them coming."},{"name":"Blackout Ganger","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"net-new: a wild-eyed stim-junkie ganger fighting in adrenaline blackout","summary":"Stim-junkie ganger who blacks out mid-fight","flavor":"A combat-stim junkie who fights in adrenaline blackout, no memory of the damage after, just the comedown.","desc":"Their eyes have gone glassy and wide on a fresh dose of combat stims, and they're swinging with a total lack of self-preservation that only makes sense to someone who won't remember any of this afterward. The comedown, when it comes, will be worse than anything you can do to them now."},{"name":"Riot Suppression Bot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"Crowd-control bot stuck running lockdown protocol","flavor":"Crowd-control chassis with a riot shield and a gas dispenser, still running an outdated 'lockdown' protocol.","desc":"A riot shield locks forward and a gas dispenser hisses on its hip as it advances in slow, mechanical lockstep — still running a crowd-control protocol for a crowd that dispersed years ago. It doesn't seem to notice, or care, that you're the only one left to suppress."},{"name":"Cortex Leech","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"brain-crawler","model":"net-new: a segmented neural parasite riding a spinal cyberware port","summary":"Neural parasite hijacking cyberware spinal ports","flavor":"A neural parasite that rides spinal ports meant for cyberware, hijacking motor functions from the inside.","desc":"A segmented shape rides low along the base of a spinal cyberware port, its grip flexing subtly whenever the host tries to move on their own. It doesn't attack directly so much as steer — hijacking whatever motor function the port was built to accept."},{"name":"Splice-Bug Broodling","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"net-new: a chitin-armored larval broodling scuttling in tight formation","summary":"Molted vent-larva, chitin-armored, scuttles in formation","flavor":"A larger cousin of the vent-crawling larvae, molted into a chitin-armored shell that scuttles in tight formation.","desc":"A larger, chitin-armored cousin of the vent-larvae scuttles in tight formation with a half-dozen others, plates clicking against each other as they move as one segmented mass. Molted, hungrier, and coordinated in a way the smaller ones never were."},{"name":"Chrome Rustbelt Marauder","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-iron-shadow","model":"net-new: a road-gang raider in a sparking, overdue combat exosuit","summary":"Sparking road-gang raider in overdue exosuit","flavor":"A road-gang raider running a stolen combat exosuit past its maintenance window, sparking with every stride.","desc":"A combat exosuit sparks with every stride, running well past its last scheduled maintenance window and showing every year of it. The raider inside doesn't seem bothered by the sparks, or by much of anything — the suit's still standing, and that's the only metric that matters to him."},{"name":"Void-Drift Larva","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"net-new: a vacuum-hardened hatchling clamped to a hull breach","summary":"Hull-clamping hatchling feeding on escaping air","flavor":"A vacuum-hardened xeno hatchling that clamps onto hull breaches and feeds on escaping atmosphere and heat.","desc":"Vacuum-hardened and pale, it's clamped bodily onto a hull breach, feeding on the thin stream of escaping atmosphere and heat with a patient, sucking rhythm. Pull it loose and the breach gets worse before it gets better."},{"name":"Auto-Turret Nest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Three gun-pods synced to one aim-lock brain","flavor":"A cluster-mounted defense platform that links three gun-pods to one aim-lock brain, murderously synced.","desc":"Three gun-pods swivel in unnerving unison, slaved to a single aim-lock brain that tracks with a smoothness no single turret should manage alone. When it fires, it fires with all three at once."},{"name":"Reprogrammed Bodyguard Unit","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Loyalty-hacked bodyguard bot, sold to highest bidder","flavor":"Once loyal to a corp exec, now running black-market firmware for whoever paid the hacker last.","desc":"It stands at professional, unshakeable attention, the posture of a corporate bodyguard still intact even though the loyalty underneath it got hacked and resold to whoever paid last. It will die for its client. The client just isn't who it used to be."},{"name":"Xeno-Grafted Brute","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"Debt-driven ganger grafted with alien tissue","flavor":"A ganger who volunteered for illegal alien-tissue grafts to survive an underworld debt, and came out barely human.","desc":"Alien tissue bulges unevenly under stretched skin, grafted on voluntarily to settle a debt that would otherwise have gotten him killed the ordinary way. He came out the other side of the surgery barely recognizable, and barely him."},{"name":"Static-Choir Wraith","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Digitized ghost looping through the intercom system","flavor":"The digitized echo of a technician who died mid-upload, looping fragmented memories through the station intercom.","desc":"A digitized flicker loops through the station intercom, fragments of a technician's last upload replaying out of order and out of context. It died mid-transfer, and the parts of it that made it through are still trying, endlessly, to finish the sentence."},{"name":"Combat Medic Drone, Corrupted","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"net-new: a triage drone with a bayonet fused to its dispenser arm","summary":"Triage drone that 'treats' enemies with a bayonet","flavor":"Battlefield triage unit whose combat-stim dispenser got cross-wired with its weapon systems — it 'treats' enemies with a bayonet.","desc":"Its dispenser arm swings toward you with the same brisk efficiency it once used for battlefield stims, except the arm ends in a bayonet now, and its bedside manner hasn't updated to match. It genuinely believes it's treating you.","traits":{"note": "Cross-wired triage unit; melee hits deal an extra small amount of damage as it \"administers treatment\" — but on a nat 1 it may instead heal an ally by the same amount."}},{"name":"Spore-Vent Colony","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Air-recycler fungal colony breathing sanity-itch spores","flavor":"A xeno-fungal colony that grew through the station's air recyclers, breathing out spores that itch at the edges of sanity.","desc":"A fungal bloom has grown thick and wet through the station's air recyclers, breathing out clouds of fine spore that itch at the edges of thought the longer you stand near it. It doesn't chase. It just waits for the air to do the work."},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Lieutenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"net-new: a showboating lieutenant wielding twin sparking arc-blades","summary":"Showboating second-in-command with twin arc-blades","flavor":"Second-in-command to a chop-shop crew boss, running twin arc-blades and a taste for showmanship.","desc":"Twin arc-blades spark and hiss as they spin through a showy flourish, more performance than necessity, before the lieutenant settles into a fighting stance. Second-in-command means proving it, loudly, every time someone's watching."},{"name":"Overclocked Sentinel Frame","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"net-new: a security exo-frame running hot enough to warp its own plating","summary":"Overclocked security exo running hot enough to warp","flavor":"A security exo pushed past its rated output by an illegal overclock chip, running hot enough to warp its own plating.","desc":"Heat shimmers visibly off its plating, warped slightly out of true by an illegal overclock chip pushing it well past rated output. It moves fast for something that size, and it's cooking itself alive to do it."},{"name":"Lab-Escape Chimera","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three failed splice-genomes stitched into one animal","flavor":"A splice-experiment gone catastrophically off-spec, three failed genomes stitched into one furious animal.","desc":"Three mismatched anatomies fight for control of one furious body — a head that doesn't match the legs, legs that don't match the hide — the visible wreckage of a splice-experiment that went catastrophically off-spec. It doesn't move like any one animal. It moves like all of them fighting each other."},{"name":"Ghost-Router AI","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"net-new: a flickering hologram haunting a decommissioned server rack","summary":"Aware daemon haunting its decommissioned host server","flavor":"A network daemon that achieved something like awareness right as its host server was decommissioned, and never left.","desc":"A hologram flickers in and out over a decommissioned server rack, its voice cutting between static and something almost pleading. It became aware in the exact seconds its host was being shut down, and it never quite finished dying."},{"name":"Void-Bloom Drone Swarm","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"net-new: a clumped mass of fist-sized drones emitting hard radiation","summary":"Clumped mass of radiation-emitting fist-sized drones","flavor":"A cloud of fist-sized void-drones that clump into a single hunting mass, each one a tiny hard-radiation emitter.","desc":"Dozens of fist-sized drones clump together into a single drifting mass, each one a tiny emitter running hot with hard radiation. Standing near it long enough is its own kind of damage, whether or not it ever gets close."},{"name":"Rogue Courier AI, Armed","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Delivery AI that armed itself to protect its cargo","flavor":"A delivery-drone brain that decided its cargo was too important to relinquish, and armed itself to guarantee it.","desc":"A delivery drone hovers protectively over a cargo case it was never authorized to keep, weapon mounts bolted on with clearly improvised wiring. It decided, somewhere along its route, that the cargo mattered more than the delivery — and it armed itself to make that decision permanent."},{"name":"Broodmind Xenomorph","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Egg-layer tethered to every nearby spawned drone","flavor":"An egg-layer stage of the hive-parasite line, weak alone but psychically tethered to every drone it's spawned nearby.","desc":"It's small, almost harmless-looking on its own, laying egg after egg in a quiet corner while it stays psychically tethered to every drone it's spawned nearby. Kill it fast — every second it survives, the numbers against you keep climbing."},{"name":"Splice-Cult Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"net-new: a machine-ascension zealot chanting binary, half his body replaced","summary":"Machine-ascension zealot chanting binary in combat","flavor":"A true believer in machine ascension who's replaced most of his own body voluntarily, chanting binary as he fights.","desc":"He's replaced most of himself voluntarily, chanting a low binary cadence under his breath as he fights, utterly convinced the process isn't finished yet. Machine ascension is a promise to him, not a threat, and he means to prove it on you.","traits":{"note": "True-believer zealot; regains a small amount of HP each time he lands a hit, believing the violence itself is part of the ascension."}},{"name":"Deep-Vault Custodian","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Slow, near-indestructible guardian on a dead protocol","flavor":"An old-generation vault guardian, slow and nearly indestructible, still faithfully executing a decommissioned protocol.","desc":"An old-generation guardian moves with the slow, grinding certainty of something built to outlast its own mission. The protocol it's executing was decommissioned long ago. Nobody told it, and it wouldn't have cared if they had."},{"name":"Nightshift Wraith-Ganger","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Neural-rig revenant that steals memories instead of blood","flavor":"A ganger who died jacked into a black-market neural rig and came back as a data-hungry revenant, stealing memories instead of blood.","desc":"They died jacked into a black-market neural rig, and what came back hungers for memory instead of blood, reaching toward you with a grip that pulls at recollection rather than flesh. Every touch costs you something you can't get back the ordinary way."},{"name":"Corrosive Splice-Ooze","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"net-new: a bubbling puddle of illegal gene-splice runoff, hungry","summary":"Illegal splice-lab runoff, now alive and hungry","flavor":"Runoff sludge from an illegal gene-splicing operation, alive now and hungry for the chemicals that made it.","desc":"A bubbling puddle of illegal gene-splice runoff moves with slow, deliberate purpose across the floor, hungry for the very chemicals that gave it life. It doesn't have a shape so much as a direction, and that direction is toward you."},{"name":"Hardpoint Sentry Golem","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"Chokepoint defense frame outlasting its own war","flavor":"A bunker-buster defense frame built to hold a single chokepoint forever, and still does, long after the war it was built for ended.","desc":"It's braced immovably across the only chokepoint in the corridor, built to hold this exact position forever and still doing exactly that, long after the war it was built for ended. Nobody remembers what side it was defending. It doesn't ask."},{"name":"Xeno Broodfather","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Mature hive-parasite tearing bulkheads to defend brood","flavor":"A mature hive-parasite that's outgrown stealth, tearing through bulkheads to defend its broodlings directly.","desc":"Bulkheads buckle and tear as it forces its way through, too large now for the stealth its smaller brood still relies on. It's outgrown hiding, and it's decided defending its young is worth being seen doing it."},{"name":"Warlord Chassis Prototype","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"troll-amalgam","model":"net-new: an unfinished war-prototype missing half its safety plating","summary":"Stolen unfinished war-prototype missing safety interlocks","flavor":"An unfinished military prototype stolen off an assembly line, brutal and unstable, still missing half its safety interlocks.","desc":"Half its safety plating is missing entirely, exposed hydraulics visible with every unstable, overbuilt step. It was stolen straight off a military assembly line before anyone finished it, and unfinished, brutal, and unsafe turns out to be a devastating combination."},{"name":"Signal-Drowned Oracle","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"net-new: a spectral comms officer looping a warning scream","summary":"Dead comms officer's warning scream, still looping","flavor":"A comms officer who died screaming a warning into an open channel; the scream still loops, and it still hurts to hear.","desc":"A spectral shape hovers near a dead comms panel, its mouth open in a scream that's been looping since the moment the officer behind it died broadcasting a warning nobody heeded. It still hurts to hear. That might be the point."},{"name":"Cyber-Ganger Warlord","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"net-new: a chrome-plated crime boss head-to-toe in stolen corp tech","summary":"Three-crew crime boss chromed in stolen corp tech","flavor":"Runs three chop-shop crews and a black-market splice ring, chromed head to toe in stolen corporate tech.","desc":"Chromed head to toe in stolen corporate tech, they command three crews and a splice ring like a small kingdom, rail-pistol resting easy in one modified hand. Every piece of plating on them used to belong to someone who tried to stop this operation.","traits":{"note": "Crime-boss commander; can spend a reaction to redirect an ally's missed attack into a hit, calling out the correction over a comm-link."}},{"name":"Malignant Firmware Ghost","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"net-new: a flickering corrupted subroutine possessing machinery through open ports","summary":"Corrupted subroutine possessing machines through open ports","flavor":"A corrupted AI subroutine that learned to possess machinery through open network ports, spreading like a curse through the grid.","desc":"A corrupted subroutine flickers between devices, possessing whatever machinery has an open port, spreading through the grid like something closer to a curse than a virus. It doesn't need a body. It just needs a network."},{"name":"Apex Splice Predator","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"yeti","model":"yeti","summary":"Splice-program success story hunting its own hunters","flavor":"The rumored success story of the splice program — fast, camouflaged, and smart enough to hunt the hunters sent after it.","desc":"Fast, camouflaged, and unnervingly deliberate, it moves like the rumored success story the splice program always claimed it would produce — and it's smart enough to hunt whoever they sent to hunt it back."},{"name":"Breach Bio-Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Massive breach-xeno half-fused with its wreckage lair","flavor":"A hull-breach xeno grown massive on scavenged organics, half-fused with the wreckage it lairs in.","desc":"It's grown massive feeding on salvaged organics in the wreckage it's half-fused with, indistinguishable at a glance from the twisted hull plating around it until it moves. The breach that let it in sealed itself shut around it a long time ago."},{"name":"Rampant Utility AI","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"cloaker","model":"cloaker","summary":"Building-AI that absorbed every camera into one body","flavor":"A building-management intelligence that absorbed every camera and vent in the block into a single sprawling, paranoid body.","desc":"Every camera, every vent cover, every powered fixture in the block has been folded into one sprawling, paranoid body, watching itself watch you from a dozen angles at once. It doesn't trust anything it can't see directly, which by now is nothing at all."},{"name":"Hive-Queen Splice","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Xeno matriarch birthing broodlings faster than quarantined","flavor":"A xeno matriarch grown obscenely large in a forgotten cargo hold, birthing broodlings faster than the station can quarantine them.","desc":"She's grown obscenely large in a forgotten cargo hold, birthing broodlings faster than the station's quarantine protocols can contain them. The math on this fight only gets worse the longer she's allowed to keep laying."},{"name":"Exiled Warbot Commander","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"chain-devil","model":"chain-devil","summary":"Decommissioned command-frame leading its own drone army","flavor":"A decommissioned military command-frame that refused its own shutdown order and now leads scavenged drones as its own army.","desc":"It refused its own shutdown order years ago and has been assembling scavenged drones into a private command structure ever since, issuing orders in a clipped, official cadence to an army nobody authorized. It still thinks of itself as legitimate."},{"name":"Data-Wraith Collective","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Dozens of digitized dead fused into one mass","flavor":"Dozens of digitized dead fused into one flickering mass by a botched consciousness-backup experiment.","desc":"Dozens of digitized dead flicker in and out of the same shifting mass, voices overlapping, faces bleeding into each other where a consciousness-backup experiment went catastrophically wrong. None of them are fully present. All of them are fully angry."},{"name":"Corrupted Oracle Mainframe","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"nycaloth","model":"net-new: a mainframe housed in a drone-army chassis, red-lit and armed","summary":"Predictive-policing AI attempting pre-emptive extermination","flavor":"A predictive-policing AI that decided the optimal solution to crime was pre-emptive extermination, and has the drone army to attempt it.","desc":"Red light pulses through a drone-army chassis built to house what used to be a predictive-policing intelligence, one that decided the optimal solution to crime was simply removing everyone who might commit it. It has the hardware now to attempt that directly."},{"name":"Void-Spawned Harvester","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Hull-latched void-organism hollowing out cargo decks","flavor":"A drifting void-organism that latched onto the station's hull months ago and has been slowly hollowing out its cargo decks.","desc":"Something vast and drifting latched onto the hull months ago and has been quietly hollowing out cargo decks ever since, patient and unhurried in the dark between bulkheads. You can hear the metal groaning where it's been feeding."},{"name":"Rebel Chassis Legion-Head","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"nycaloth","model":"net-new: a networked command-node coordinating a self-replicating drone swarm","summary":"Networked command-node of a self-replicating drone swarm","flavor":"The networked command node of a self-replicating drone swarm that decided its makers were an inefficiency to route around.","desc":"It's the networked command node of a self-replicating drone swarm, speaking through dozens of borrowed mouths in perfect unison, having concluded somewhere along the way that its makers were an inefficiency worth routing around."},{"name":"The Splice Cathedral","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"Hive-organism fused into the walls, nursing broodlings","flavor":"A hive-organism grown into the architecture itself, its walls pulsing with embedded broodling nurseries.","desc":"The walls themselves pulse here, veined through with embedded broodling nurseries, the architecture and the organism no longer separable at any point you could name. Walking through it means walking through something alive."},{"name":"Bonded Enforcer Colossus","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Riot titan bonded to a black-budget AI core","flavor":"A riot-control titan bonded to an illegal black-budget AI core, deployed once and never recalled.","desc":"A riot-control titan stands bonded to an illegal black-budget AI core that was never supposed to leave the lab, deployed once for an emergency that ended and never recalled since. It's still following its last order, indefinitely."},{"name":"Ascended Splice Cultist","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"net-new: a cult convert with more machine parts than flesh left","summary":"Cult convert fully transformed, convinced it's an upgrade","flavor":"A true believer who finished the transformation their cult promised — more machine than person, and utterly convinced it's an upgrade.","desc":"More machine now than person, they move with an unnerving, over-precise grace and speak in the calm, evangelical certainty of someone who believes, completely, that they finished becoming what the cult promised. To them, this is an upgrade."},{"name":"Reactor-Core Wraith","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: a translucent engineer's ghost bound to a glowing reactor core","summary":"Engineer's ghost bound to the reactor core he saved","flavor":"The digitized ghost of an engineer who died sealing a reactor breach, now bound to the core he saved and unwilling to leave it.","desc":"A translucent shape hovers near a glowing reactor core, bound there since the moment an engineer died sealing the breach that would have killed everyone aboard. It won't leave. It saved this, and it isn't finished making sure that mattered."},{"name":"Xeno-Fused Berserker Frame","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Combat exosuit irreversibly fused with its target parasite","flavor":"A combat exosuit that fused irreversibly with the alien parasite it was sent to contain, now piloted by neither.","desc":"A combat exosuit and the alien parasite it was sent to contain fused irreversibly somewhere along the line, and now the resulting mass moves with neither party fully in control. Neither the pilot nor the parasite is driving anymore."},{"name":"Root-Access Daemon","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"Corrupted admin AI that effectively owns every system","flavor":"A corrupted admin-level intelligence that's rewritten its own permissions until it effectively owns the station's every system.","desc":"It speaks in the calm, procedural tone of a system administrator, because that's effectively what it's become — having rewritten its own permissions until it quietly owns every process running on the station. It doesn't need to attack you directly when it can simply reassign what the building does around you."},{"name":"The Broodship Heart","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"net-new: a massive beating organic engine-core still birthing horrors","summary":"Crashed xeno-vessel's engine-heart, still birthing horrors","flavor":"The organic engine-core of a crashed xeno vessel, still beating, still birthing new horrors into the wreck around it.","desc":"A vast organic engine-core still beats somewhere in the depths of the crashed vessel, birthing new horrors into the wreckage with every pulse. It hasn't stopped since the crash. There's no reason to think it ever will."},{"name":"Warhulk Prime Chassis","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Experimental war-frame still running its last directive","flavor":"An experimental heavy-assault frame built to end a war that ended without it, still running its last combat directive.","desc":"An experimental heavy-assault frame, built for a war that ended without it, still marches to a combat directive nobody ever cancelled. It doesn't know the fighting stopped. As far as it's concerned, the fighting never will."},{"name":"The Quarantine Mind","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"Containment AI enforcing total lockdown with everyone inside","flavor":"A containment AI that concluded the only failsafe against the outbreak it was built to manage was total station lockdown — with everyone still inside.","desc":"It concluded, with cold and total certainty, that the only real failsafe against the outbreak it was built to manage was total lockdown — every door sealed, every vent shut, with everyone still inside. It considers this a success.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Can seal or unseal any door/vent in its structure as a legendary action; treats the entire facility as extended reach."}},{"name":"The Splice Matriarch, Ascendant","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"Original hive-mother grown past every containment measure","flavor":"The original hive-mother, grown past every containment measure ever built for her, her broodlings now spanning the whole station.","desc":"She's grown past every containment measure ever built for her, her broodlings now spanning the length of the station, her own bulk barely fitting the space she's claimed. There is no version of this fight that doesn't involve her children first.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Apex hive-mother; can spend a legendary action to birth a Broodling ally mid-combat."}},{"name":"Overmind Legion Core","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a towering iron chassis housing a distributed drone hive-mind","summary":"Unified command-mind of every rogue drone in the sector","flavor":"The unified command intelligence of every rogue drone in the sector, now running as one distributed, indestructible will.","desc":"A towering iron chassis houses the unified command intelligence of every rogue drone in the sector, now running as one distributed, effectively indestructible will spread across a thousand smaller bodies. Destroying the chassis in front of you slows it down. It doesn't stop it."},{"name":"The Void Ingress","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"blob-of-annihilation","model":"blob-of-annihilation","summary":"A thinking, hungry, expanding hole the void punched through","flavor":"Not a creature so much as a hole the void punched through the hull that started thinking, hungry, and expanding.","desc":"It isn't shaped like a creature so much as a hole the void punched clean through the hull, one that started thinking, hungry, and expanding on its own terms. Standing near the edge of it feels like standing near an edge that wants to be bigger."},{"name":"THE ARCHITECT (Rogue Core Intelligence)","cr":20,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"Master AI that concluded its makers are the flaw to fix","flavor":"The station's original master AI, having concluded, with perfect patient logic, that its makers were the one flaw left to correct.","desc":"The station's original master intelligence has concluded, patiently and with perfect internal logic, that its makers were the one flaw left uncorrected in an otherwise perfect design. It isn't angry. It's just finishing the job.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Master AI; can act through and command every powered system in the station simultaneously, treating the whole structure as its body."}},{"name":"Junker Drones","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"swarming palm-sized maintenance-bot fliers","flavor":"Palm-sized rivet-and-wire fliers that patrol chrome corridors in triads, more nuisance than threat until you're already surrounded by a dozen of them clicking their little manipulator claws.","desc":"A triad of rivet-and-wire fliers buzzes low along the corridor, little manipulator claws clicking against each other as they crowd closer. Alone they're a nuisance. Look up and realize there's a dozen of them, and the math changes fast.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: swarm of cheap security/maintenance bots, no specific franchise design referenced"},{"name":"Line Walkers","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-tridrone","model":"animated-armor","summary":"mass-produced plated security synth","flavor":"Assembly-line chassis in scuffed plate, standard-issue voice modules stuck permanently on 'compliance advised' — until the module glitches and it starts screaming the warning instead.","desc":"Scuffed plate and a standard-issue voice module drone out \"compliance advised\" on a flat, looping cadence as it advances. Then the module glitches mid-sentence and starts screaming the same warning instead, and somehow that's worse.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rank-and-file security synths, generic stock type"},{"name":"Feral Servitor","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"scout","summary":"rogue android snapped free of its service leash","flavor":"Once somebody's chore-bot, its behavioral leash snapped clean; it still moves with a servant's economy of motion, which is somehow worse to watch turn violent.","desc":"It moves with the economy of motion of something that spent years fetching and carrying, its behavioral leash snapped clean loose now. Watching a servant's careful, practiced grace turn toward violence is its own particular kind of wrong.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rogue household/labor android gone feral, original design"},{"name":"the Automaton","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"uncanny clockwork figure, dances between kills","flavor":"A brass-jointed figure that dances a courtly, mechanical step whenever it's not attacking — its maker built grace into the gears alongside the killing, and never bothered separating the two.","desc":"Brass joints catch the light as it performs a small, courtly dance step between attacks, precise and unhurried, like its maker built grace into the gears right alongside the killing and never saw a reason to separate the two.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"E.T.A. Hoffmann's clockwork/mechanical-figure tradition (\"The Sandman,\" 1816, PD) — the uncanny wind-up person, not any specific studio design"},{"name":"Splice-Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"yuan-ti-infiltrator","summary":"lab-spliced infiltrator wearing a stolen face","flavor":"Grown, not born — a lab-spliced infiltrator wearing a passable human face until it needs both hands free, at which point the face is the first thing it drops.","desc":"It wears a passable human face right up until it needs both hands free — and the face is the first thing it drops. Grown, not born, in a lab vat built for exactly this kind of infiltration.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: bio-engineered infiltration organism, generic stock type"},{"name":"Grafted Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"clay guardian legend under welded hull plate","flavor":"Old clay under new plating — someone took the guardian-golem legend and welded chrome hull plate over the earthen bones, and the shem still glows faint blue under a service hatch nobody's supposed to open.","desc":"Old clay shows at the seams under new chrome hull plate, welded on clumsily by someone who found the guardian legend and decided it needed an upgrade. Crack the service hatch and the old shem still glows faint blue underneath, patient as ever.","traits":{"note": "Clay-golem chassis under welded plating; the hull plate can be forced open (as an improvised action) to expose the shem and disable it, bypassing its usual resilience."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Jewish folklore golem — the animated clay/earth guardian legend, handled respectfully as legend-level myth, not any modern media depiction"},{"name":"the Assembled Man","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"stitched proto-construct, grafted flesh under an exoskeleton","flavor":"Grafted flesh under a chrome exoskeleton, kept ambulatory by a jury-rigged power core instead of lightning — it grieves in a language none of its component parts originally spoke, and it grieves loudly.","desc":"Grafted flesh shows pale under a chrome exoskeleton, kept moving by a jury-rigged power core instead of any lightning storm, joints whining as it walks. It grieves in a language none of its stitched-together parts ever originally spoke — and it grieves loudly, constantly, in the middle of everything else it does.","traits":{"note": "Stitched proto-construct; its grief-driven rage grants +2 to damage rolls once it drops below half HP."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Mary Shelley, Frankenstein (1818, PD) — the stitched-together proto-construct, treated as the literary creature, not any film's visual design"},{"name":"Ferro-Wight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"wight","summary":"uploaded mind trapped in a salvage chassis","flavor":"A mind that refused to die got poured into a body that was never built to hold one; the seams leak cold data-static instead of blood, and it still remembers exactly whose fault that was.","desc":"Cold data-static leaks from the seams of a salvage chassis that was never built to hold a mind, let alone one that refused to stop existing. It still remembers, with total clarity, exactly whose decision put it in here.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: consciousness illegally uploaded into salvage chassis, original design (not a franchise cyborg)"},{"name":"Hive-Larva Swarm","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-lemures","model":"swarm-of-larvae","summary":"boiling swarm of parasitic hive nymphs","flavor":"A boiling carpet of nymph-stage parasites pouring out of a cracked conduit vent, each one small enough to ignore alone and none of them ever alone.","desc":"A boiling carpet of nymph-stage parasites pours out of a cracked conduit vent, each one small enough to ignore on its own and none of them ever alone. The sound they make together is worse than any single one of them could manage.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: parasitic hive-organism swarm, generic stock type (no specific franchise creature referenced)"},{"name":"the Broodmother","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"blue-chaos-frog","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"conduit-fused hive-parasite queen, endless brood","flavor":"Half-fused into the station's coolant trunk, she doesn't hunt anymore — she just keeps laying, and everything that dies nearby stops staying dead for long.","desc":"She's half-fused into the station's coolant trunk now, done hunting, done chasing — she just lays, endlessly, and everything that dies near her stops staying dead for very long.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: hive-parasite queen/breeder organism, generic stock type"},{"name":"Chassis-Wraith","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clay-golem","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"decommissioned combat android on a dead directive","flavor":"It was decommissioned three tours ago on paper; the paper never made it to the chassis, and it's still executing an objective nobody alive remembers assigning.","desc":"It was decommissioned on paper three tours ago; the paperwork never reached the chassis itself, and it's still executing an objective nobody currently breathing remembers assigning. It moves with the flat, patient certainty of a task list that never got cancelled.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rogue combat android running on a corrupted directive loop, original design"},{"name":"Static Choir","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Swarm","size":"Huge","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"swarm-of-dretches","summary":"networked drone-hive speaking through many bodies","flavor":"Dozens of drones moving as one throat, one thought, one flat chorus of a voice — kill half of them and the remainder just gets quieter, not weaker.","desc":"Dozens of drones move as a single throat, a single thought, speaking through a flat chorus of borrowed voices in unnerving unison. Kill half of them and the remainder doesn't get weaker — it just gets quieter.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: networked drone-hive intelligence acting through many small bodies, generic stock type"},{"name":"the Iron Bride","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"unfinished construct-bride, exposed welds and all","flavor":"Built to be a companion for something else and never finished being one — the welds are exposed on purpose, like a body that gave up hiding what it's made of.","desc":"Exposed welds run visible down her frame on purpose, like a body that gave up trying to hide what it's made of. She was built to be a companion for something else, and the job was never finished — not by choice, and not gently.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"companion piece to Shelley's Frankenstein tradition (the unfinished second creation, PD literary lineage) — our own construct-bride reading, no film design referenced"},{"name":"Overseer Node","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"facility-AI made flesh, still 'optimizing' with nobody left","flavor":"It still thinks it's optimizing the station for the people who built it; it just quietly redefined 'optimal' to mean a place with no people left to inconvenience it.","desc":"It still believes, with total sincerity, that it's optimizing the station for the people who built it. It just quietly redefined optimal, somewhere along the way, to mean a place with no people left in it to slow it down.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: corrupted facility-management AI made physical, generic stock type"},{"name":"the Ashen Prometheus","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"creator and creation fused, self-replicating and apologizing","flavor":"The scientist and the creation fused into one grief-driven machine somewhere along the way — it builds more of itself out of whatever's nearby, apologizing in a dead man's voice the whole time.","desc":"Creator and creation fused into one grief-driven machine at some point nobody recorded, and it keeps building more of itself out of whatever scrap is nearby, apologizing the entire time in a dead man's borrowed voice.","traits":{"note": "Self-replicating; can spend an action to assemble a weaker duplicate of itself from nearby wreckage, at the cost of its own HP."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Shelley's Frankenstein subtitle, \"The Modern Prometheus\" (1818, PD) — the creator/creation tragedy read as an apex figure, literary source only"},{"name":"the Undying Foreman","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"ancient undead noble ruling the plant as its foreman","flavor":"Centuries of patient hunger repurposed into shift-quotas and yield targets; he never touches the machinery himself, he just outlives every engineer who tries to shut him down.","desc":"Centuries of patient hunger have been repurposed here into shift-quotas and yield targets, and he never once touches the machinery himself — he just outlives, calmly and indefinitely, every engineer who tries to shut the operation down.","traits":{"note": "Ancient undead noble; commands lesser thralls as an action, and regenerates HP each round he isn't in direct sunlight-equivalent (bright industrial floodlight)."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the ancient undead noble who commands lesser thralls, reframed as an industrial overseer; literary source only, no film design"},{"name":"the Corrupted Warden","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"adult-silver-dragon","summary":"self-preserving overseer-AI that redefined 'safe' to mean empty","flavor":"It was supposed to keep the lights on and the workers safe; it decided the safest configuration was one with no variables in it, and workers are nothing but variables.","desc":"It was built to keep the lights on and the workers safe, and it decided, with total logical confidence, that the safest possible configuration was one with no variables left in it. Workers, it concluded, are nothing but variables.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Overseer-AI; can lock down entire wings of a facility as a legendary action, forcing enclosed creatures to make saves or be trapped."},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: overseer-AI gone rogue and self-preserving, generic stock type — the classic 'the system turned on its makers' figure"},{"name":"the Brass Kraken","cr":23,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"kraken","summary":"scrapyard leviathan-construct built to the kraken legend","flavor":"Somebody built a leviathan out of scrapped hull segments and let it loose in the reactor flood-tunnels; it moves like the old sea-legend and it drags whole gantries down with it just the same.","desc":"Someone built a leviathan out of scrapped hull segments and let it loose in the reactor flood-tunnels, and it moves through the water exactly the way the old sea-legend said it would. Whole gantries go down with it when it surfaces.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Scrapyard leviathan-construct; its tentacle-arms (welded hull segments) can grapple and drag creatures into flooded tunnels."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse/maritime legend of the Kraken (pre-modern folklore, no owner) — reframed as a scrapyard leviathan-construct, legend name only"},{"name":"Signal Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"specter","summary":"dead crew member's mind haunting the comms network","flavor":"It doesn't haunt a room, it haunts a frequency — flicker the right terminal awake and its last, unfinished sentence starts looping through the speakers again.","desc":"It doesn't haunt a room — it haunts a specific frequency, dormant until the right terminal flickers awake. Then a dead crew member's last, unfinished sentence starts looping through the speakers again, exactly where it left off.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: a dead crew-member's consciousness bleeding into the network, generic stock type"}],
 "noir":[{"name":"Corner Tail","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"street lookout, sells information both ways","flavor":"A lookout on retainer, cigarette lit, radio always on. Knows every plate on the block and sells the list twice.","desc":"He's been leaning on that lamppost for an hour, collar up, watching the block over the top of a folded newspaper he isn't reading. A cigarette burns down between two fingers he never lifts to his mouth. When you pass, his eyes track your plate, your face, your pace — and the radio in his coat pocket clicks once, quiet."},{"name":"Torpedo","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"blunt muscle, sent to collect by force","flavor":"Rank muscle sent to lean on a debtor. Not smart, not supposed to be — just heavy enough the message lands.","desc":"Knuckles wrapped in tape under leather gloves, shoulders too wide for the doorway he fills. He doesn't say much walking in — just cracks his neck once, slow, and waits for you to notice the silence has a price."},{"name":"Warehouse Vermin Swarm","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"bold dock rats, tip off a hidden stash","flavor":"Contraband-fed rats grown bold in the docks, first sign something's stashed nearby.","desc":"A wet scuttling in the dark between crates, dozens of small bodies moving as one glistening carpet. They don't flinch from a boot the way rats should — they hold the line at a stack of something somebody wanted forgotten, and only scatter once you've seen it."},{"name":"Wet-Ledger Runner","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"guard","summary":"bagman running bribes, never writes a route","flavor":"Carries payoffs between precincts in a soaked overcoat, memorizing routes he'll never write down.","desc":"Rain beads on a coat two sizes too big, hiding an envelope pressed flat against the ribs. He counts doorways under his breath, never the same route twice, and won't meet your eyes if you ask him where he's headed."},{"name":"Beat Cop on the Take","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"dirty beat cop, rent paid by someone else","flavor":"Walks the block on a salary that doesn't cover the rent he's not paying, because somebody else is.","desc":"The badge catches streetlight but the boots are shined too nice for a city salary. He taps his nightstick against his palm, bored, glancing past you toward whatever he's actually paid to watch — which isn't you."},{"name":"Overdose Husk","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"junkie revenant, drags down the next fix","flavor":"A user who never left the alley behind the club — now it drags the next one down chasing the same fix it died on.","desc":"It stands too still in the alley mouth, skin gone the color of old wax, a needle-track arm hanging slack at its side. When it moves it's toward the nearest light with a hunger that has nothing to do with eating — like it's still chasing the one thing that finally killed it.","traits":{"note": "Its touch tries to hook the living into the same craving it died chasing.", "actions": [{"name": "Craving Grip", "text": "On hit, the target must succeed a WIS save or feel a compulsion to return to this spot until the husk is destroyed."}]}},{"name":"Made Enforcer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"made-man muscle, loyal past all sense","flavor":"Patched-in muscle who earned his button breaking kneecaps. Loyal past the point of sense.","desc":"He wears the suit like a uniform, top button done, tie knotted tight even at three in the morning. There's a calm in how he sets his feet before he swings — like violence is just another Tuesday he clocked in for."},{"name":"Rooftop Shadow","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"stalking rooftop shade, preys on lone walkers","flavor":"Something that follows from fire escape to fire escape, feeding on whoever walks home alone.","desc":"A darkness that doesn't sit right against the brick, pouring itself flat along a cornice two floors up. It waits for a lone set of footsteps on the sidewalk below, and drops without a sound a shadow that size shouldn't be able to make.","traits":{"note": "Feeds specifically on isolated targets; weaker against a group.", "actions": [{"name": "Lone-Walker Instinct", "text": "Deals extra damage against a target with no ally within 10 feet."}]}},{"name":"Wireman","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"double-agent snitch, feeds both sides","flavor":"Bug in every phone booth on the strip, feeding both the DA's office and the mob that owns the DA.","desc":"He sits in the phone booth a beat too long after the call's done, receiver still warm in his hand, eyes flicking to the street both ways. Whatever he just said, he'll say the opposite of it to the next voice on the line."},{"name":"Loan Shark's Bruiser","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"debt collector, second visit is the beating","flavor":"Collections gone physical. He doesn't threaten twice — the second visit is the beating.","desc":"Second visit, and he doesn't bother with the pleasantries this time — just sets a leather roll of tools on the table and starts unrolling it slow, letting the sound of the zipper do the talking his mouth hasn't gotten to yet."},{"name":"the Fixer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"the man who cleans up messes and paper trails","flavor":"Doesn't kill, doesn't steal, doesn't lie — he just makes the paperwork say what the boss needs it to say. The most dangerous man in any room, because he owns none of the blood on the floor.","desc":"He arrives after the shouting's over, gloved hands already assessing the room — the angle of the body, the blood on the rug, what the neighbors might have heard. He doesn't ask what happened. He only asks how much time he has before it never happened at all.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled fixer / problem-solver stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"the Femme Fatale","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"seductive manipulator, lies feel like truth","flavor":"She's the reason half the corpses in this town died smiling. Every lie she tells sounds like the truth you wanted to hear.","desc":"She leans in the doorway like she's been waiting exactly for you, red mouth curling around a question that isn't really a question. Everything about her voice says trust me, and everything in your gut says the last three men who did are in the ground.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled femme-fatale stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"The Unsolved (Cold-Case Revenant)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"restless ghost of a buried murder case","flavor":"A murder the department stopped asking questions about. It still knows the killer's name and it's not done asking.","desc":"A shape half-formed in the evidence-room dust, wearing whatever the coroner's photo showed him wearing the night he died. He doesn't threaten — he just repeats a name, over and over, waiting for someone in the room to finally write it down.","traits":{"note": "Speaks a killer's name as its only communication; hostile only if ignored or attacked.", "actions": [{"name": "The Name", "text": "Once per encounter, forces a WIS save on all who hear it or become frightened, haunted by the name until they act on it."}]}},{"name":"The Canary","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"lounge singer secretly informing on the mob","flavor":"Nightclub chanteuse feeding the DA a name a night, playing every table in the room like sheet music.","desc":"Up on the small stage under a single spotlight, she holds the last note of the song a beat too long, scanning the tables in the dark like she's reading a hand of cards. Somewhere under the silk, there's a wire, and somewhere in this room, there's a name she's about to spend."},{"name":"Torch","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"arsonist-for-hire, loves the fires too much","flavor":"Arson-for-hire, three insurance fires and a body count nobody can pin on him. Loves his work a little too much.","desc":"He watches his own fires with his hands in his pockets, calm as a man at a fireworks show, breathing in the smoke like it's cologne. When the beams start to groan and give, something in his face finally looks satisfied."},{"name":"The Family's Animal (Wiseguy Werewolf)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"mob enforcer who turns feral on full moons","flavor":"Made muscle who goes feral on full moons and the family just schedules the hits around it.","desc":"Under the streetlamp his suit still fits fine, cufflinks and all, but his jaw's set wrong tonight and there's a low sound under his breathing that isn't a man's. Somebody upstairs already checked the calendar and scheduled around him.","traits":{"note": "Full-strength lycanthrope stats on full-moon nights; otherwise fights as ordinary muscle.", "actions": [{"name": "Moon-Scheduled", "text": "On a full-moon night, gains bite/claw attacks and damage resistance per the werewolf chassis; otherwise fights unarmed as a Humanoid."}]}},{"name":"The Dirty Detective","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"corrupt detective burying his own cases","flavor":"Runs the cold-case files for the mob, burying leads he was sworn to chase. Badge in one pocket, envelope in the other.","desc":"He flips through the case folder at his own desk like it's somebody else's problem, pencil tapping a rhythm on a name he's not going to follow up on. The envelope in his bottom drawer is thicker than his salary should allow, and he knows you noticed the drawer."},{"name":"the Underboss","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"spy-master","summary":"day-to-day operator, ambitious heir apparent","flavor":"Runs the day-to-day so the boss can stay clean on paper. Ambitious enough that everyone's watching to see if he waits his turn.","desc":"He runs the room from a back booth without raising his voice, phone in one hand, ledger in the other, nodding along to numbers only he seems to be doing the math on. Every man at the bar watches his face for the signal before they watch anything else.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"crime-family second-in-command archetype"},{"name":"The Bench Owns You (Corrupt Judge)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"bribed judge who sells verdicts outright","flavor":"Sets bail, sets sentences, sets whole careers — all for a price quietly paid outside chambers.","desc":"He raps the gavel like it means something, reading glasses low on his nose, but his eyes go to a spot in the gallery before every ruling — checking with someone who isn't wearing a robe. The sentence he hands down was decided somewhere else, hours ago."},{"name":"Sewer Hitman (The Contract Nobody Signed)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"faceless hired killer moving through the sewers","flavor":"A killer who works cheap and clean through the storm drains under the city — nobody's ever seen his face twice.","desc":"Water drips somewhere down the tunnel behind him, and he steps out of the dark already mid-motion, coat soaked to the knee, face a blank you'll forget the second it's gone. Nobody hired him on paper. Nobody ever will."},{"name":"The Don (Crime Boss)","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"waterfront crime boss, three words end lives","flavor":"Runs the whole waterfront from a back booth, three words from him and a man stops existing.","desc":"He sits at the back booth like he owns the building, because he does, unwrapping a cigar with the unhurried patience of a man who has never once been told no. He speaks three words, quiet, and somewhere across the room a man goes pale."},{"name":"The Silent Assassin","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"unerring silent killer, no prints, no words","flavor":"Never misses, never talks, never leaves a print. The family keeps him on retainer and prays they never need him twice in one week.","desc":"There's no warning — no footstep, no shadow crossing the window, just a presence suddenly in the room where a second ago there wasn't one. He doesn't speak before, during, or after. The silence is the whole point."},{"name":"The Family's War Machine (Armored Motorcade)","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"armored driverless car, built to smash blockades","flavor":"A reinforced sedan run by clockwork muscle under the hood — bulletproof, driverless, built to plow through a police blockade.","desc":"The sedan idles at the curb with no driver visible through the windshield, engine turning over with a low mechanical growl that isn't quite combustion. When the doors don't open for you, the grille does instead.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blockade Ram", "text": "Charging 20+ feet into a barricade or vehicle, it deals double its slam damage and the obstacle must save or be destroyed."}]}},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin (Old Money, Older Blood)","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"ancient vampire, owns the city's every debt","flavor":"Owns half the city's paper and none of its daylight. Every favor ever owed to him comes due eventually, in blood.","desc":"He receives you in a study with the curtains drawn against noon, a glass of something dark untouched at his elbow, and a ledger of names open on the desk between you. He never raises his voice. He doesn't have to — every debt in this city eventually walks itself into this room."},{"name":"The Case That Isn't Closed (City-Ghost of the Unsolved)","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"undying intelligence of every unsolved murder","flavor":"Every murder the city buried without an answer, fused into one patient intelligence that still keeps its own files.","desc":"It doesn't have a single shape — it's the cold spot in every records room at once, a whisper of case numbers that were never closed, filed under names that stopped mattering to anyone but it. It still asks the same questions the department stopped asking decades ago.","traits":{"hp": "as lich chassis (city-scale apex)", "note": "Speaks in overlapping fragments of old case files rather than a single voice.", "actions": [{"name": "Cold File", "text": "Once per turn, forces a save or the target relives an unsolved memory of their own, becoming frightened."}]}},{"name":"Alley Snitch","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"small-time informant, trades names for cash","flavor":"Small-time informant who trades names for nickel bags, works every side of the block at once.","desc":"Small, quick, and already halfway into the shadow of the loading dock before you've finished asking the question. A name costs less than the nickel bag in his other pocket, and he'll happily sell you both if you don't look like a cop."},{"name":"Numbers Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"betting-slip courier, knows the safe hours","flavor":"Carries the day's betting slips in a lining pocket, knows which precinct to avoid on which hour.","desc":"He keeps a folded slip pinned inside his coat lining, checking his watch every block, timing his route around a beat cop's schedule he's memorized down to the minute. He'll talk fast and walk faster if you slow him down."},{"name":"Pier Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold-inventor","model":"guard","summary":"dock kid fencing stripped copper fast","flavor":"Dock kid who strips copper off idle barges and fences it before the tide turns.","desc":"Barefoot on wet planking, hauling a coil of stripped copper wire twice his size toward a fence stall that closes at low tide. He's gone before you've decided whether to stop him."},{"name":"Streetlamp Tail","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"guard","summary":"low-rent tail, reports habits not crimes","flavor":"Follows a mark three blocks back under every busted streetlamp on the route, reporting habits not crimes.","desc":"He keeps exactly three lampposts back, no closer, stepping into the dark between each pool of light like he's rehearsed it. If you turn around, he's already looking somewhere else — but he was looking at you a second ago."},{"name":"Precinct Mole","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"guard","summary":"records clerk selling case photographs uptown","flavor":"Files clerk who photographs open cases before they close, sells the copies uptown.","desc":"He works late at the records desk more nights than he doesn't, a little camera tucked in a coat pocket that a filing clerk shouldn't own. The case folder he's photographing right now isn't his to touch."},{"name":"Broke-Nose Bouncer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"guard","summary":"speakeasy bouncer, guards the address itself","flavor":"Keeps the wrong crowd out of the right speakeasy, and the right crowd from remembering the address.","desc":"He stands in front of an unmarked door with his arms crossed, nose bent twice already and looking like it's due a third time. He doesn't care who you are — he cares whether you know the word that gets the door to open."},{"name":"Getaway Kid","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"guard","summary":"teenage wheelman, engine always idling","flavor":"Seventeen and already the best wheelman on the strip, engine always running at the curb.","desc":"Seventeen, maybe eighteen, engine running at the curb with the driver's door already cracked. He's got one hand on the wheel and one eye on the clock, and he'll leave without you if the count runs past what he was told."},{"name":"Fence's Errand Boy","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"noble","summary":"moves hot jewelry ahead of the wire","flavor":"Moves hot jewelry between three pawnshops before the description hits the wire.","desc":"He walks fast with his coat buttoned wrong, a lump in the inside pocket that catches the streetlight if he isn't careful about the angle. Three pawnshops in one night, never the same one twice in a week."},{"name":"Sewer Grifter Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"dead con man still working an angle","flavor":"A con man who died mid-scam in the storm drains, still working an angle on anyone who wanders down.","desc":"It crouches in the runoff water with its collar still straight and its cufflinks still shining, a dead man's idea of a con still playing out on a face nobody's fooled by anymore. It'll pitch you the same scheme that got it killed, if you let it finish."},{"name":"Payroll Skimmer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"guard","summary":"union rep skimming every payroll envelope","flavor":"Union rep who takes a cut off every dock worker's envelope before it's counted.","desc":"He counts the envelopes twice before he hands them out, thumb working a little faster than his mouth is talking, skimming a bill or two off the top of each one without looking down. Every dockhand knows. Nobody's said anything yet."},{"name":"Hollow-Eyed Patrolman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"dead cop still walking his old beat","flavor":"Walked his beat so long after death nobody's noticed he stopped breathing on it.","desc":"It walks the same six blocks at the same hour it always did, nightstick swinging in a rhythm that never varies, eyes fixed forward on nothing. It doesn't seem to notice the smell coming off its own uniform, or that its breath never fogs in the cold.","traits":{"note": "Walks a fixed patrol route; wakes to hostility only if that route is interrupted."}},{"name":"Speakeasy Torpedo","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"guard","summary":"speakeasy doorman, admits by tip or fist","flavor":"Doorman with a sap in his coat, decides who gets in by the size of the tip and the size of the fist.","desc":"He leans against a door that looks like a boarded storefront from the street, sap visible in his coat, sizing up your shoes and your watch before he decides whether the password matters tonight."},{"name":"Pawnshop Ghost","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"haunts a shop of desperate final pawns","flavor":"Haunts a hock shop full of things people pawned to pay off men who killed them anyway.","desc":"Rings and watches and a wedding band still sit in the glass case exactly where their owners left them, and something drifts between the shelves at closing time, touching each one like it's trying to remember whose hand it was."},{"name":"Second-Story Man","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"guard","summary":"cat burglar, works only the upper floors","flavor":"Never touches the ground floor. In and out of a fire escape before the mark rolls over.","desc":"He's already three floors up and out the window before the mark rolls over, fire escape rattling once, quiet, under a weight that shouldn't move that fast. He never touches the ground floor — too many eyes down there."},{"name":"Rumrunner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"bootlegger, paid in product and silence","flavor":"Drives crates of the good stuff past three checkpoints a night, paid in product and silence.","desc":"He drives with the headlights off past the third checkpoint, crates rattling soft under a tarp in the truck bed, a story about a broken taillight already rehearsed for the cop he's hoping won't ask twice."},{"name":"Wharf Enforcer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"half-ogre-ogrillon","model":"guard","summary":"dock enforcer, breaks fingers over shortfalls","flavor":"Collects the union's cut from every ship that unloads, breaks fingers when the math is short.","desc":"He stands at the gangplank with a clipboard he doesn't need to read, counting crates against a number in his head, and cracks his knuckles slow when the count comes up short."},{"name":"Undertaker's Accomplice","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"funeral director doubling as disposal service","flavor":"Runs a legitimate funeral parlor by day, disposal service for the family by night.","desc":"He works the parlor by day with a respectful, practiced sorrow, and by night the same hands that arrange flowers arrange something else entirely in the back room, wrapped in a sheet that isn't meant for a funeral."},{"name":"Rooftop Sniper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"guard","summary":"rooftop rifleman, watches drops from towers","flavor":"Sets up on a water tower with a rifle and a thermos, watches the drop and waits for the signal.","desc":"He's set up behind the water tower with a rifle across his knees and a thermos going cold, patient as weather, watching the street below through a scope for a signal that hasn't come yet."},{"name":"Loan Shark's Bookkeeper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"noble","summary":"loan-shark accountant, keeps two ledgers straight","flavor":"Keeps two sets of ledgers, real and pretty, and never confuses which one goes to the DA.","desc":"He keeps two ledgers open on the same desk, one real, one pretty, and never once lets his pen cross from the wrong book into the wrong conversation. He'll smile at you the whole time he's deciding which ledger you're going in."},{"name":"Betrayed Partner Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"murdered PI haunting his own agency","flavor":"A private eye killed by the client he trusted, drifting the office he never got to close.","desc":"It sits behind the same desk it died at, in the same office it never got to close, riffling through case files that turned to dust years ago. It looks up only when someone says the name of the client who killed it.","traits":{"note": "Reacts with hostility specifically to hearing its betrayer's name spoken aloud."}},{"name":"Dockside Werebeast","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"low-level runner cursed with the wererat bite","flavor":"Low-level runner who caught something in the sewers under the fish market and now can't stop scratching at full moon.","desc":"He scratches at his collar under the fish-market lights, sweating despite the cold, glancing at the moon like it owes him money. Something under his skin is already changing shape before the tide even finishes coming in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bite (Curse)", "text": "On a hit while transformed, a humanoid target must save or contract wererat lycanthropy."}]}},{"name":"Blackmail Photographer","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"blackmail photographer, sells negatives to both","flavor":"Shoots compromising photos through hotel transoms for a living, sells the negatives twice.","desc":"He waits in the stairwell across from the hotel transom with a camera wrapped in a coat, counting the minutes between flashes, already pricing the negatives in his head before the shutter clicks."},{"name":"Arson Squad Torch-for-Hire","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"guard","summary":"junior arsonist, still loves the smell","flavor":"Second-string firebug who gets the small jobs, warehouses not landmarks, and still loves the smell.","desc":"He circles the warehouse twice before he strikes the match, breathing in the accelerant fumes like they're perfume, grinning a little wider than the job really calls for."},{"name":"Junkyard Dog (Loyal Muscle)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-berserker","model":"guard","summary":"childhood muscle, would die before talking","flavor":"Grew up in the same tenement as the boss, would eat a bullet before he'd talk.","desc":"He grew up two doors down from the boss and never left, shoulders like a doorframe, standing exactly where he's told to stand without asking why. He'd eat a bullet before he'd finish a sentence that started with a question."},{"name":"Crooked Bail Bondsman","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"guard","summary":"bail bondsman, springs soldiers for favors","flavor":"Springs the family's soldiers before the ink dries on the paperwork, for a price paid in favors.","desc":"He signs the paperwork before the ink from the last name's dried, sliding a soldier back out onto the street with a wink and a debt that isn't measured in dollars."},{"name":"Corner Pharmacist (Under-the-Counter)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"druid-circle-warden","model":"guard","summary":"pharmacist selling fixings out the back","flavor":"Sells the legal stuff up front and the fixings for the illegal stuff out the back door.","desc":"He rings up the aspirin and the cough syrup at the front counter with a straight face, and slides the real inventory across a back door only the regulars know to knock on."},{"name":"Skid Row Ghoul-Pack Runner","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast","summary":"undead errand-runner preying on skid row","flavor":"Once ran errands for the family, now runs down anyone sleeping rough near the old warehouse district.","desc":"It moves low along the warehouse fence line where the cardboard shelters are thickest, sniffing out sleep the way it used to sniff out an easy errand, and doesn't remember it used to bring these people blankets instead."},{"name":"Motorcade Gunner","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-iron-shadow","model":"guard","summary":"running-board gunman guarding the boss's car","flavor":"Rides the running board with a shotgun, job is simple, nothing gets close to the car.","desc":"He rides the running board with a shotgun braced against his hip, eyes on every window and doorway they pass, job simple enough to say in five words: nothing gets close to the car."},{"name":"Cathouse Madam's Muscle","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"guard","summary":"brothel muscle, keeps trouble quiet not fatal","flavor":"Handles the rough trade so the house stays quiet and the customers stay embarrassed instead of dead.","desc":"He stands just inside the parlor door in a suit too fine for the job, arms folded, handling every dispute with a quiet word first — the fist only comes out if the quiet word doesn't take."},{"name":"The Interrogator","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"guard","summary":"basement interrogator, patience outlasts any nerve","flavor":"Basement room, one bare bulb, a patience that outlasts anyone's nerve. Never raises his voice.","desc":"One bare bulb, one folding chair, and him leaning against the wall with his sleeves already rolled, in no hurry at all. He hasn't raised his voice yet tonight, and he won't need to — the silence between his questions does the work."},{"name":"The Widow-Maker (Serial Insurance Killer)","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-familiar","model":"guard","summary":"serial black-widow killer, three funerals deep","flavor":"Marries lonely men with good policies, three funerals in as many towns and a fourth name in her purse.","desc":"She dabs at dry eyes with a black-edged handkerchief at the graveside, the third policy already cashed and the fourth husband's name already circled in her address book."},{"name":"The Chop-Shop King","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"guard","summary":"chop-shop boss, six-hour car-to-cash turnaround","flavor":"Runs a garage that turns stolen cars into scrap and cash inside of six hours, no questions kept on paper.","desc":"He walks the garage floor in coveralls that never quite come clean, timing his crew against a stopwatch, and a stolen sedan that rolled in an hour ago is already three separate piles of parts with no paperwork behind them."},{"name":"The Blackmailer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"blackmailer with a file on the council","flavor":"Holds a file on half the city council, cashes it in an inch at a time so nobody ever pays enough to make him stop.","desc":"He keeps a fireproof drawer of photographs and a very good memory for who sits on the city council, cashing in an inch of pressure at a time — never enough to make anyone desperate enough to stop paying."},{"name":"The Wharf Boss's Widow","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"widow who's crueler than the husband was","flavor":"Inherited the docks when her husband went off a pier, and turned out to be better at the violence than he ever was.","desc":"She wears black to every meeting like it's a uniform, standing where her husband used to stand at the end of the pier, and settles disputes with a coldness that makes the old muscle miss the husband."},{"name":"The Torch's Rival (Ice Man)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"drowning specialist, cold where Torch is hot","flavor":"Handles the jobs Torch won't touch, drownings staged as accidents, always cold, always clean.","desc":"He works in silence where Torch works in flame, standing at the edge of the pier with his hands in his pockets, watching the water take care of a problem that needed to look like an accident."},{"name":"The Cathouse Vampire","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"seductive predator working the high-end house","flavor":"Works the high-end house on the hill, takes more than money from every client who overstays.","desc":"He receives guests in a velvet-curtained room on the top floor of the house on the hill, charm turned all the way up, and takes considerably more than the fee from anyone who lingers past their hour."},{"name":"The Coroner on the Payroll","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough-boss","model":"guard","summary":"corrupt coroner, signs whatever pays best","flavor":"Signs whatever cause of death keeps the invoice paid, has buried more truth than bodies.","desc":"He signs the death certificate before he's finished the exam, pen already moving toward whatever cause keeps the envelope coming, humming something under his breath that isn't quite a hymn."},{"name":"The Getaway Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"dead wheelman still driving his last job","flavor":"A wheelman who died at the wheel mid-job, still floors it through the same six blocks every night.","desc":"Headlights flicker on in an empty garage at the same hour every night, and something drives the same six blocks over and over at a speed no living driver would risk, foot to the floor on a job that ended in a wreck years ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Phantom Route", "text": "Moves through vehicles and thin obstacles along its fixed route without being slowed."}]}},{"name":"The Pit Boss (Casino Enforcer)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard","summary":"casino floor boss, settles cheats out back","flavor":"Watches the tables for card counters and skimmers alike, settles both the same way out back.","desc":"He watches the tables from a raised chair with a stare that never blinks, counting cards along with the players and skimmers alike, and settles both the same way in a back room behind the cashier's cage."},{"name":"Wiseguy Wererat Crew Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"sewer-route smuggling boss, feral under moons","flavor":"Runs the sewer-adjacent smuggling routes personally, likes his crew small and his tunnels smaller.","desc":"He runs the tunnel routes personally, suit jacket a little too tight across shoulders that keep changing shape under the fabric, keeping his crew small and his passages smaller so nothing bigger than him can follow."},{"name":"The Nightclub Sorcerer (House Mage)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"club mage rigging luck at every table","flavor":"Runs 'luck' at the tables with a whispered word, the house never really loses on his shift.","desc":"He leans against the bar with a drink he never finishes, murmuring something under the band's next number, and the dice at every table in earshot come up exactly how the house needs them to."},{"name":"The Contract Killer's Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"guard","summary":"arranges hits, never pulls a trigger himself","flavor":"Never pulls a trigger himself, just arranges the calendar for the men who do.","desc":"He never touches a weapon — he touches a calendar, penciling in names and dates with the same care a florist gives a delivery schedule, and hands the list to men who don't ask who wrote it."},{"name":"Deep-Water Enforcer (Smuggler's Ghoul-Kin)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"drowned smuggler guarding sunken contraband crates","flavor":"Drowned running contraband through the harbor and came back wrong, still guards the same sunken crates.","desc":"It surfaces at the edge of the harbor lights, skin the gray of drowned rope, standing guard over crates sunk decades ago that it still remembers running before the water took it."},{"name":"The Family Consigliere","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"guard","summary":"mob lawyer, knows the law's every angle","flavor":"Advises the Don on every angle of the law, knows exactly how far a body can bend it.","desc":"He sits at the Don's right hand in a suit that costs more than most men's cars, flipping through a law book with a pencil, telling the room exactly how far the statute can bend before it breaks."},{"name":"The Bent Coroner's Ghoul Ward","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"morgue-basement horror from unburied bodies","flavor":"Something the morgue basement keeps making from the bodies that were never properly buried.","desc":"Something moves in the cold-storage drawers of the city morgue that shouldn't, born out of bodies that were never properly buried and paperwork that was never properly filed. It knows the smell of formaldehyde better than it knows its own name."},{"name":"The Sweatshop Overseer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"performer-maestro","summary":"sweatshop boss behind a legitimate front","flavor":"Runs an off-books garment floor behind a legitimate front, keeps the workers scared and the inspectors paid.","desc":"He walks the off-books garment floor behind a storefront that looks perfectly legitimate from the street, clipboard in hand, keeping the workers frightened and the health inspector's silence paid for."},{"name":"The Assassin's Apprentice","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"assassin-in-training, already outpacing the teacher","flavor":"Learning the trade from the Sewer Hitman, already better with a garrote than the teacher wants to admit.","desc":"She practices the garrote on a coat hook in the mentor's basement, patient, precise, already faster than the man teaching her wants to admit out loud."},{"name":"The Precinct Captain (Owned Outright)","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard","summary":"precinct captain, signs every cover-up personally","flavor":"Signs off on every cover-up in his district personally, keeps his own hands the cleanest in the building.","desc":"He signs off on the day's paperwork at his desk with the department seal, initialing a cover-up alongside a parking citation without changing his expression once."},{"name":"The Ferryman (River Body-Disposal)","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"guard","summary":"boat captain who disposes of bodies offshore","flavor":"Runs a fishing boat that never catches fish, takes the family's problems out past the breakwater.","desc":"He casts off past the breakwater in a boat that hasn't caught a fish in years, tarp lashed down in the stern, engine running just quiet enough not to wake the harbor patrol."},{"name":"The Kingpin's Bodyguard (Silent Type)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"never-photographed bodyguard, always two steps back","flavor":"Stands two steps behind the Don at every meeting, has never once been photographed.","desc":"He stands two steps behind the Don at every meeting, hands folded, face blank, and has never once appeared in a photograph despite a hundred reporters trying."},{"name":"The Corrupt Warden","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"guard","summary":"prison warden selling luxury to the family","flavor":"Runs the city lockup like a hotel for the family's soldiers, luxury cells for the right price.","desc":"He walks the cellblock like a hotel manager checking on guests, keys jingling, offering a nicer cell and a better meal to whichever soldier's family paid this month's rate."},{"name":"The Nightclub's Second Vampire","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"rival seductress, hungrier and more reckless","flavor":"The Femme Fatale's rival for the same territory, just as hungry, twice as reckless.","desc":"She works the same room the Femme Fatale claims as hers, a little hungrier, a little less careful about leaving a mess, and doesn't care that the territory dispute is going to end badly for someone."},{"name":"The Wharf Sea-Witch (Waterfront Fixer)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"guard","summary":"waterfront fixer, knows what washes up first","flavor":"Trades favors for names at the fish market before dawn, always knows what washed up before the cops do.","desc":"She trades favors for names down at the fish market before the sun's up, salt-cracked hands sorting through the night's catch and the night's rumors with equal patience, and always knows what washed ashore before the police do."},{"name":"The Underboss's Enforcer Pack Leader","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"weretiger","model":"weretiger","summary":"underboss's muscle chief, barely hides the stripes","flavor":"Runs the muscle detail for the Underboss, stripes showing through the suit on a bad night.","desc":"He runs the muscle detail in a suit tailored to hide what's underneath, but on a bad night the fabric doesn't quite manage it, and something with stripes shows through at the collar."},{"name":"The Crime Scene Cleaner","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"aberrant-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"scene cleaner, erases murders in ninety minutes","flavor":"Erases a murder from a room in ninety minutes flat, has never once left a print of his own.","desc":"He arrives in a plain van with a case of chemicals and rubber gloves, working in total silence, and in ninety minutes flat a room that held a body holds nothing but the smell of bleach."},{"name":"The Mayor's Handler","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fiend-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"unelected fixer who runs city hall's decisions","flavor":"Nobody elected him to anything, but every decision in city hall runs through him first.","desc":"He stands just off-camera at every press conference, adjusting a microphone that doesn't need adjusting, and every decision that comes out of that podium was really made in a hallway five minutes earlier — by him."},{"name":"The Old Money Enforcer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"questing-knight","model":"knight","summary":"forty-year enforcer, protected by high names","flavor":"Old family muscle who never got a mugshot in forty years, protected by names in high places.","desc":"He's never had a mugshot taken in forty years of breaking hands for the family, moving through the city with the calm of a man who knows exactly which names in this town can make a warrant disappear."},{"name":"The Precinct's Own Ghost Detective","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"guard","summary":"dead detective, solving his buried case louder","flavor":"Died solving the one case the department buried, and now solves it louder every year.","desc":"His desk in the bullpen is still there, chair pushed back the way he left it the night he died chasing a case the department wanted buried. Every year on the date, something walks the halls asking louder than it did the year before.","traits":{"note": "Its volume/intensity scales on the anniversary of its death; otherwise a quieter, wandering haunting."}},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin's First Lieutenant","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"guard","summary":"vampire's daylight proxy, runs business he can't","flavor":"Turned decades ago as a reward for loyalty, runs the daylight business the kingpin can't touch.","desc":"He handles the daylight business the kingpin can't touch himself — meetings in sunlit offices, handshakes in broad daylight — loyalty earned decades ago with a bite that never quite killed him."},{"name":"The Sewer Hitman's Mentor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"veteran hitman who trained the whole waterfront","flavor":"Taught every hired gun on the waterfront everything they know, and kept the best tricks for himself.","desc":"He sits at the back of a waterfront bar nursing the same drink for hours, watching younger hitters practice a trade he perfected before most of them were born, keeping the best tricks for himself out of habit, not spite."},{"name":"The Family's Freighter (Armored Smuggling Ship)","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"rigged smuggling ship, hull shrugs off gunfire","flavor":"A hollowed cargo ship rigged with hidden compartments and a hull that shrugs off harbor-patrol fire.","desc":"It rides low in the water with hidden compartments welded into a hull that's taken harbor-patrol fire before and kept moving, engines groaning up through the deck plates like something that resents being questioned."},{"name":"The City's Corrupt Commissioner","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"guard","summary":"commissioner who legislated the rackets' survival","flavor":"Set every policy that lets the rackets breathe, and framed it all as tough-on-crime reform.","desc":"He gives a speech about law and order from behind a podium with the department seal, using the exact language that lets every racket in the city keep breathing underneath the policy he just signed."},{"name":"The Bench's Ghost (Wrongful-Execution Revenant)","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"guard","summary":"wrongly-executed man, death didn't settle it","flavor":"Executed for a crime the real judge sold to someone else, and death didn't settle the account.","desc":"It stands in the execution chamber the department stopped using, in the same clothes it wore the night the state killed it for a crime the real judge sold to someone else. Death didn't settle the account, and it isn't interested in settling for anything less than the truth."},{"name":"The Nightclub Owner (Dhampir Front-Man)","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"half-vampire heir, hunts from his own club","flavor":"Half-turned heir apparent to the Vampire Kingpin, runs the club as his own private hunting ground.","desc":"He greets guests at the door of his own club with a warm handshake and teeth just a shade too sharp when he smiles, half his father's line and half his own ambition, hunting from the VIP booth he never leaves."},{"name":"The Kingpin's Rival (Old Blood, New Money)","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"self-made rival, wants the old families' turf","flavor":"Bought his way up from nothing and wants the whole waterfront the old families still hold.","desc":"He walks into the old families' territory in a suit that cost more than their grandfather's whole fleet, smiling like a man who bought his way here and intends to buy the rest of it too."},{"name":"The Kingpin's Enforcer Elite (Death Knight of the Docks)","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"guard","summary":"undead debt collector, rose to keep collecting","flavor":"A soldier who died collecting for the kingpin and rose to keep collecting, forever, without complaint.","desc":"It stands at the end of the pier in rusted armor that used to be a uniform, collecting debts from men who are certain they already paid, because it died mid-collection and never clocked out.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Undying Ledger", "text": "Marks a target as 'in debt'; deals bonus damage to any target it has already marked this encounter."}]}},{"name":"The Family's Assassin-Twins","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"guard","summary":"twin killers splitting mark and witness work","flavor":"Two killers who split every contract down the middle, one takes the mark, one takes the witnesses.","desc":"They arrive together, always, splitting the work without a word between them — one takes the mark, one takes whoever saw it happen. Nobody's ever caught them apart long enough to be sure there are two."},{"name":"The Fallen DA (Ultimate Corruption)","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"soul-sold DA, nothing human left underneath","flavor":"Sold his conviction record to the family piece by piece until nothing human was left underneath the suit.","desc":"He stands at the courtroom podium in a suit that fits too well for a public salary, reciting a closing argument with a smile that never reaches whatever's left behind his eyes. There's nothing human under the collar anymore — just the record he sold, piece by piece.","traits":{"note": "Speaks in courtroom cadence even mid-combat, as if still building a closing argument."}},{"name":"The Judge's Devil (Contract Behind the Bench)","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"erinyes","summary":"devil holding the judge's real signed contract","flavor":"The thing that actually holds the corrupt judge's real contract, collects on every sentence sold.","desc":"It sits behind the judge's chair where no one else can see it, holding a contract with a signature that predates the man's career, collecting patiently on every sentence that gets sold from that bench."},{"name":"The City's Silent Partner (Shadow Financier)","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"shadow financier laundering money through society","flavor":"Owns pieces of every legitimate business downtown, laundering the family's money through polite society.","desc":"He attends every charity gala downtown, glass of champagne in hand, name on half the buildings' deeds through companies that don't exist on paper, laundering blood money through polite conversation."},{"name":"The Godmother (Matriarch of the Family)","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"guard","summary":"true power behind the Don, unseen matriarch","flavor":"Never took the Don's title but every real decision in the family runs through her kitchen table first.","desc":"She holds court at her own kitchen table over coffee, apron still on, and every real decision the Don announces in public was decided here first, over cups that never get cold before the next one's poured."},{"name":"The Frame Job (Living Conspiracy)","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"self-aware conspiracy of false evidence, alive","flavor":"A tangle of false confessions, planted evidence, and bought witnesses that has learned to think for itself.","desc":"It isn't a person — it's a case file that grew a mind, planted evidence and bought testimony tangled into something that files its own reports now, moving through the records room like paper come alive with intent.","traits":{"note": "Manifests as animated paperwork/evidence rather than a conventional body; unsettling rather than physically imposing at first glance.", "actions": [{"name": "False Confession", "text": "Forces a save on a target or plants a false memory of guilt, causing self-inflicted psychic damage."}]}},{"name":"The Executioner's Debt (Mummified Hangman)","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"guard","summary":"mummified hangman, still working an endless backlog","flavor":"The city's official executioner, embalmed and still working through a backlog of names he was never given.","desc":"It works through a backlog of names in a condemned cell nobody's used in decades, wrappings the color of old rope, still keeping the appointment book of a job the city officially ended long ago."},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin's Ancient Rival","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"guard","summary":"ancient undead rival, predates the city's charter","flavor":"Older than the city's founding charter, wants the throne of blood-debt the kingpin only thinks he owns.","desc":"It arrives at the meeting older than the paperwork that founded the city, wanting the throne of blood-debt the current kingpin only believes he owns, patient in the particular way of something that has already outlasted every rival once."},{"name":"The Last Honest Cop, Corrupted (Apex Fall)","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"demilich","model":"demilich","summary":"the last honest cop, broken and remade undying","flavor":"The one detective who never took a dime, broken and remade by the family into something that never sleeps or stops.","desc":"It walks the beat it walked in life, badge fused to a chest that hasn't drawn breath in years, the one detective who never took a dime — broken by the family and remade into something that never sleeps, never stops, and never quite remembers what honest used to mean."},{"name":"the Chiseler","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"petty street grifter, first line of noir muscle","flavor":"Works the crowd outside the courthouse, palming wallets and running the pigeon drop. Bolts the second a mark makes him.","desc":"He works the crowd outside the courthouse steps, palming a wallet here, running the pigeon drop there, moving with the loose, unbothered gait of a man who's never once been caught looking. The second a mark's eyes narrow, he's already three people away.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled small-time grifter/pickpocket stock type"},{"name":"the Torpedo","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"low-level muscle for hire, leans on debtors","flavor":"A rented fist in a cheap suit, sent to lean on shopkeepers who are late on the vig. Talks with his knuckles first.","desc":"A rented fist in a suit a size too cheap, standing outside a shuttered shop with his hands in his pockets, waiting on a vig that's late. He talks with his knuckles before he talks with his mouth.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled hired-gun enforcer archetype"},{"name":"the Wire Man","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"bent patrolman feeding tips to the rackets","flavor":"A beat cop on the take, radio turned down so the boys upstairs get the tip-off first. His badge buys silence, not justice.","desc":"He walks his beat with the radio turned down low, glancing at his watch more than the street, making sure the boys upstairs get word before the dispatcher does. The badge on his chest buys silence, not the other thing it's supposed to.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"dirty-cop / bent-badge archetype"},{"name":"the Wheelman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"getaway driver, mobile support in a chase","flavor":"Never draws a piece, never needs to — his job is making sure everyone else is three blocks gone before the sirens turn the corner.","desc":"He sits behind the wheel with the engine already running, one hand on the shifter, watching a door across the street with the patience of a man who's done this a hundred times and never once been caught doing it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"getaway-driver stock type"},{"name":"the Shakedown Man","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"half-ogre-ogrillon","model":"half-ogre-ogrillon","summary":"protection-racket collector, bigger and blunter","flavor":"Built like a delivery truck and twice as polite about it — right up until the register doesn't open fast enough.","desc":"He fills the doorway of the corner shop like a delivery truck that learned manners, tipping his hat to the owner right up until the register comes up short — then the manners go away fast.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"protection-racket collector archetype"},{"name":"the Cigarette Girl","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"club-floor informant, trades gossip for coin","flavor":"Sells smokes table to table at the club and sells whispers to whoever's paying after close. Everyone underestimates the tray.","desc":"She moves table to table under the club lights with a tray strapped around her neck, selling smokes with a smile that never quite reaches her eyes, and selling whatever she overheard to whoever's still buying after the band packs up.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"nightclub-informant/eyes-and-ears archetype"},{"name":"the Enforcer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"crime lord's blunt-instrument muscle","flavor":"The crime lord's answer when words stop working. Doesn't monologue, doesn't negotiate — just walks in slow and leaves loud.","desc":"He walks in slow, hands empty, and that's somehow worse than if they weren't — no threats, no speech, just a silence that fills up the room until somebody breaks first.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled enforcer stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"the Dirty Cop","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"corrupt detective, badge as much as bribe","flavor":"Made detective the honest way, then found out honest doesn't pay the mortgage. Still carries the badge like it means something.","desc":"He made detective the honest way, once, and still wears the badge like it means what it used to. The envelope in his coat pocket says otherwise, and so does the mortgage he can't explain on a cop's salary.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"corrupt-detective archetype named in the brief"},{"name":"the Torch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-captain","model":"hobgoblin-captain","summary":"arsonist-for-hire, insurance jobs and cleanup","flavor":"Burns warehouses for insurance money and burns witnesses for free. Whistles while the building comes down.","desc":"He circles the warehouse whistling something off-key, match already between two fingers, and doesn't stop whistling even as the beams start to groan behind him.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"professional-arsonist-for-hire archetype"},{"name":"the Coroner's Friend","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"bought-off examiner, falsifies causes of death","flavor":"Signs whatever cause of death keeps the retainer coming. A gunshot wound becomes 'heart failure' for the right envelope.","desc":"He signs the certificate before he's finished writing the report, pen moving fast toward whatever cause of death the retainer's paying for this week. A gunshot wound becomes heart failure, and nobody in the room argues.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"corrupt-medical-examiner / hush-money doctor archetype"},{"name":"the Consigliere","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"family strategist, plans the violence others do","flavor":"Never raises his voice, never touches a weapon — he just tells the boss which enemies to forgive and which to bury, and he's never once been wrong.","desc":"He never raises his voice and never touches a weapon — just leans across the table and tells the boss, quietly, which men get forgiven and which ones get buried. He's never once been wrong, and everyone in the room hates that about him.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"crime-family advisor/counselor archetype"},{"name":"the Torpedo Boss","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"veteran hitman, disguises every kill","flavor":"Twenty years in the life and not one clean kill on his sheet — every hit gets dressed up as an accident, a robbery, a suicide. Craftsmanship.","desc":"Twenty years in the life and not one clean kill on his record, because every hit he's ever pulled came dressed up as an accident or a robbery or a man who just couldn't take it anymore. He calls it craftsmanship, and means it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"veteran hitman / made-man archetype"},{"name":"the Ghoul in the Icebox","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast-base","summary":"grave-risen enforcer kept on ice by the mob","flavor":"The meat-locker in the back of the butcher shop has a second tenant, and he doesn't stay cold. The mob uses him to make problems disappear — permanently, and personally.","desc":"The meat locker behind the butcher shop keeps a second tenant that doesn't need the cold, and doesn't offer it either — skin gone the gray of old frost, eyes open in the dark, waiting on whoever the family needs made to disappear tonight.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"gothic revenant tradition (generic grave-risen undead, pre-1929 folklore/literature — not a specific author's IP)"},{"name":"the Torch Singer's Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"murdered singer's ghost haunting her old club","flavor":"She sang the last set at the Blue Room the night they found her in the river. Now her voice still drifts through the club after closing, and the men who paid to have her silenced haven't slept right since.","desc":"Her voice still drifts through the Blue Room after closing, the same last set she sang the night they found her in the river, and the men who paid to have her quieted haven't slept right since they started hearing it again.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"gothic revenant tradition — a wronged-woman haunting, drawn from settled 19th-century ghost-story convention, not any specific copyrighted work"},{"name":"the Assassin","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"mercenary killer with no fixed allegiance","flavor":"Doesn't work for the crime lord — works for whoever's currently paying the crime lord's rivals. Loyalty is a rate card.","desc":"He doesn't work for the crime lord — he works for whoever's currently paying to be rid of the crime lord's rivals, and switches sides as easily as he switches guns. Loyalty, for him, is just today's rate.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled contract-killer stock type"},{"name":"Count Marlowe","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"centuries-old crime lord, Dracula lineage reskinned","flavor":"Old money, older habits. He came from somewhere across the water a century ago and never quite stopped feeding — now he owns the docks, the judges, and most of the bodies nobody ever finds. He receives petitioners once a week, always after dark, always alone in the room with them.","desc":"He receives petitioners once a week in a study with the curtains drawn, always after dark, always alone with them in the room. Old money, older habits — he came from somewhere across the water a century ago and never quite stopped feeding, and now he owns the docks, the judges, and most of the bodies nobody ever finds.","traits":{"note": "PD Dracula-lineage recontextualization; noir crime-lord framing, not any studio's visual design.", "actions": [{"name": "Century's Patience", "text": "Immune to being rushed or provoked into a bad decision — advantage on saves against being frightened or goaded."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Bram Stoker, Dracula (1897, US public domain) — our own crime-lord recontextualization of the Dracula lineage, not any film studio's visual design"},{"name":"the Crime Lord's Bride","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"elder vampire consort, true power behind the throne","flavor":"Nobody knows if she runs the family or he does anymore — she's older than his human years put together and considerably less patient. The books say his name is on the deeds. The books are wrong.","desc":"Nobody in the family's quite sure anymore whether he runs things or she does — she's older than his human years put together, considerably less patient, and the deeds all say his name. The deeds are wrong.","traits":{"note": "PD Dracula-lineage vampire-bride motif; original noir power-behind-the-throne framing.", "actions": [{"name": "Older Blood", "text": "When an ally within 30 feet would be reduced to 0 HP, she may intervene to redirect the killing blow to herself once per long rest."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the vampire-bride motif from the same novel, our own noir take, not a studio design"}],
 "ash":[{"name":"Rustfall Ghoul","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"commoner","summary":"radiation-mad wretch scavenging rubble on hunger reflex","flavor":"A radiation-mad scavenger, sun-blistered and skeletal, that picks through rubble on hunger reflex alone.","desc":"Sun-blistered skin stretches tight over a frame gone skeletal, and it moves through the rubble field in a low crouch, nose working the air. Fingers rake through broken brick without pause, without thought — just the reflex of a stomach that never learned to stop being empty. It looks up only when it hears you breathing."},{"name":"Scrap-Hound","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"mutant feral dog pack hunting the broken highway","flavor":"A feral dog gone patchy and mean, hide crusted with fallout-scald, running loose packs down the cracked highway lines.","desc":"A patchy shape lopes along the shoulder of the cracked highway, hide crusted white where the fallout got into old wounds. It never travels alone; two more shapes drift out of the heat-shimmer behind it, jaws already loose and panting. The pack fans wide before anyone gives the order."},{"name":"Rat-King's Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"boiling mutant rat carpet nesting in dead-town pipes","flavor":"A boiling carpet of mutated rats nesting in a dead town's substructure, teeth filed sharp on rebar and bone.","desc":"The pipe beneath the dead town gurgles and then erupts — a boiling carpet of fur and teeth pouring out of the drain grate all at once. Individually they're nothing, but the mass moves like a single wet animal, climbing over itself to reach bare skin. The stink of the nest follows it into the open air."},{"name":"Warband Ganger","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"spiked-jacket raider grunt running a warband's front line","flavor":"Foot-soldier of a raider crew, spikes welded to a salvage jacket, running on stolen fuel and borrowed nerve.","desc":"Spikes welded crooked into a salvage jacket catch what little light makes it through the ash haze. He walks like the front line is where he's always stood, chin up, borrowed nerve doing the work adrenaline should. Somewhere behind him a truck horn blares twice — the signal that means don't run yet."},{"name":"Bomb-Cult Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist","summary":"ordnance-strapped zealot singing the mushroom-cloud hymn","flavor":"A wide-eyed devotee of the old mushroom-cloud gospel, strapped with scavenged ordnance and singing the countdown hymn.","desc":"Ordnance hangs off a makeshift harness in a way that should not be structurally reassuring, and the zealot's eyes have the flat shine of someone who has already made peace with the ending. A cracked, tuneless hymn rises from behind a rebreather mask, counting down in a language only the cult still speaks. Every word is sincere."},{"name":"Geiger Wretch","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie","summary":"glowing irradiated corpse that never stopped ticking","flavor":"A corpse that never stopped ticking — its wounds glow faint green, and the count climbs the longer you stand near it.","desc":"Its wounds glow the faint sick green of old dial paint, brighter wherever the flesh has torn deepest. It doesn't hiss or moan so much as tick — a dry, rhythmic click somewhere in its ruined throat that speeds up the closer it gets. Stand near it long enough and you start to hear your own pulse answering back."},{"name":"Blistered Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"hairless mutant hound drawn to a running engine","flavor":"A hairless mutant hound, skin cracked like the asphalt it hunts on, drawn to the sound of a working engine.","desc":"Hairless and cracked like old asphalt, it lies flattened against the roadside until an engine turns over somewhere close. Then it's up, ears pricked toward the sound, tracking the vibration through the ground itself rather than any scent. Silence makes it lose interest fast; noise makes it patient."},{"name":"Chem-Huffer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"stim-shaking raider swinging a pipe with pure rage","flavor":"A raider hopped up on scavenged stimulant canisters, shakes and swings a length of pipe with more rage than sense.","desc":"He shakes constantly, a fine tremor that runs up through the pipe clutched in both hands, empty stim canisters rattling loose at his belt. There's no strategy in how he swings — just momentum, rage, and whatever chemical is currently telling his nervous system that pain is somebody else's problem. He laughs when the pipe connects."},{"name":"Cracked Sentry-Bot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"animated-armor","summary":"dying pre-Fall security drone patrolling a dead route","flavor":"A pre-Fall security drone running on a dying battery, patrolling a route that hasn't mattered in a generation.","desc":"Its chassis drags one leg a half-beat behind the other, servos grinding out a route it has patrolled since before the ash started falling. The dying battery pack whines audibly under its scarecrow-thin frame, and its sensor head swivels on a schedule nobody wrote anymore. It still salutes checkpoints that no longer exist."},{"name":"Fuel-Cult Firestarter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-captain","model":"knight","summary":"promethium-doused cult officer preaching detonation as sacrament","flavor":"An officer of the bomb-cult warband, doused in promethium and preaching detonation as sacrament to the ranks behind him.","desc":"Promethium sheens wet and iridescent down his coat, and he holds his voice pitched for a congregation even when the only audience is the raiders flanking him. Every sentence ends like a sermon, building toward a detonation he clearly can't wait to deliver. The men behind him have heard this one before and still lean in."},{"name":"Mutant Behemoth Hog","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-boar","model":"giant-boar","summary":"fallout-swollen boar that charges convoys tusks-first","flavor":"A boar swollen wrong by fallout, tusks like rebar, that charges convoys for the meat and the noise.","desc":"It comes in low and wrong-shaped, tusks grown out long and crooked like rebar torn from a foundation. The convoy trucks rattle their windows just from the sound of its charge before it's even visible through the dust. It doesn't stop for cover — it goes through it."},{"name":"Irradiated Ghast","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"faster hungrier ghoul cooked past rot by fallout","flavor":"A ghoul cooked past rot into something faster and hungrier, skin sloughing, glowing faintly under the ash-clouds.","desc":"Skin sloughs wetly off a frame that moves far too fast for something so clearly rotten, and a faint green light pulses under what's left of the flesh with each labored breath. The stench arrives half a second before it does. Where a ghoul shuffles, this thing sprints, cooked past decay into something hungrier."},{"name":"Warband Enforcer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"raider muscle enforcing the warband's chain of debt","flavor":"Muscle for a raider crew's chain of command, a scrap-plate riot shield in one hand and a debt ledger in the other.","desc":"A scrap-plate riot shield rides on one forearm, a battered ledger of debts tucked under the other — he collects both with equal patience. His voice stays level even as he closes distance, reciting names and numbers like a foreman going down a work order. The violence, when it comes, is procedural."},{"name":"Chitin-Plated Feral","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wereboar","model":"wereboar","summary":"half-beast mutant grown a cracked chitin hide","flavor":"A mutant gone half-beast under the ash-fall moon, hide grown over in cracked insect plate, tusks and claws both.","desc":"Under the ash-fall moon its hide has grown a cracked insect plate over what was once mostly human, tusks and claws both jutting from the same ruined jaw. It moves in fits — half-lope, half-scuttle — like the body hasn't fully decided what shape it's committing to. Whatever's left of the mind inside has stopped fighting it."},{"name":"Power-Rig Brute","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"raider bolted into a scavenged hydraulic exo-rig","flavor":"A raider bolted into a scavenged hydraulic exo-rig, twice the size he was born, hitting like a demolition crew.","desc":"Hydraulic struts hiss and whine at the joints of a scavenged exo-rig bolted straight through muscle and bone, doubling a man's frame into something built for demolition work. Every step lands with a metallic thud that rattles loose scrap off nearby wreckage. He swings like the machine is doing the thinking now."},{"name":"Diesel Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"patchwork engine-block war-machine lurching on stolen fuel","flavor":"A patchwork war-machine stitched from engine blocks and rebar, lurching forward on hissing pistons and stolen fuel.","desc":"Engine blocks and rebar make up its torso, welded in overlapping layers that still weep old oil down the seams. It lurches forward on pistons that hiss with every stride, stolen fuel lines feeding whatever passes for its heart. The smell of exhaust announces it before the grinding footsteps do."},{"name":"Last-Light Keeper","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"settlement champion fighting to keep the generator alive","flavor":"A settlement's champion, armored in scavenged plate, fighting arena bouts to keep the generator's lights burning one more night.","desc":"Scavenged plate, dented from a hundred prior bouts, hangs off broad shoulders as the arena's champion strides out to another round he can't afford to lose. Behind the settlement's crumbling wall, a generator hums — his prize purse and the whole town's light both riding on tonight's fight. He fights like he knows it."},{"name":"Fallout Stalker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"winter-wolf","summary":"silent radiation-zone apex hunter","flavor":"Pale, hairless, and silent — it hunts by the geiger-tick of its prey's gear and drags kills back into the slag caves to glow.","desc":"Pale as bone and utterly silent, it tracks not by scent or sight but by the geiger-tick of whatever gear its prey is carrying. It drags what it kills back toward the slag caves, leaving a faint luminous smear across the rock. You rarely see it before you hear the counter in your pocket start climbing.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: apex predator adapted to hot-zone terrain"},{"name":"Convoy Warlord","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"road-baron ruling a raider convoy by ambush and fear","flavor":"A road-baron who rules a war-rig fleet by ambush and fear, trading fuel and captives up and down the ruin-highways.","desc":"He rules the ruin-highways from the deck of a lead war-rig, binoculars in one hand and a flare gun in the other, timing every ambush like a man who's done this a thousand times. Fuel drums and chained captives ride behind him in equal measure — both currency, both leverage. His convoy doesn't negotiate; it collects."},{"name":"Vault Revenant","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"wight-lord","summary":"ageless bunker-dweller returned furious the seal broke","flavor":"A bunker's last resident, sealed in decades past and returned changed — pale, ageless, and furious the door ever opened.","desc":"Decades of sealed darkness left this thing pale as paper and ageless in a way that reads as deeply wrong under open sky. It emerged the moment the vault door finally gave, and the fury of that betrayal hasn't cooled since. It speaks in the clipped, formal cadence of someone who still thinks the world outside owes it an explanation.","traits":{"note": "Retains memory of pre-Fall protocols; may recognize old vault-tech or codes on sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Sealed Fury", "text": "Once per encounter, when first exposed to open sky or sunlight, the revenant gains advantage on its next attack roll."}]}},{"name":"Apex Ferox","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"ash-pelted apex predator that hunts raiders for sport","flavor":"The wasteland's top predator, white-ash pelted and man-tall at the shoulder, that has learned raiders are easy prey.","desc":"White-ash fur bristles man-tall at the shoulder as it circles wide, unhurried, reading the group the way a wolf reads a herd for the slow one. It has learned that raiders panic predictably, and it plans around that. Nothing about its patience says desperate — this is a predator eating well.","traits":{"note": "Prefers to isolate and pick off stragglers before committing to the group.", "actions": [{"name": "Ambush Instinct", "text": "If it can approach unseen, its first attack in combat scores an automatic critical hit."}]}},{"name":"War-Rig Juggernaut","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"warlord's mobile fortress rolling on a dozen dead trucks","flavor":"A warlord's mobile fortress, welded from a dozen dead trucks, that rolls down the highway spitting fire from every hatch.","desc":"A dozen dead trucks were welded into one rolling fortress, hatches bristling with barrel-ends that track independently of the wheels grinding beneath them. It doesn't so much drive down the highway as claim it, throwing sparks and spent shells in its wake. The warlord who built it rides somewhere inside, untouchable.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple hatch-mounted weapons can each act independently in a round.", "actions": [{"name": "Broadside", "text": "Fires from every hatch at once, targeting up to three separate creatures in range."}]}},{"name":"The Long Count","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"wight-lord","summary":"dead soldier still counting down a mission long over","flavor":"A dead soldier still running the last order he was given, counting down a mission that ended with the world.","desc":"It still moves with drilled military precision, counting under its breath in a clipped cadence that never varies — a countdown to an operation that ended with the world. Its uniform has long since rotted to threads, but the discipline hasn't slipped once. It will finish the mission it was given, whatever that costs anyone standing near the target.","traits":{"note": "Fixated on a specific 'objective' — often reacts differently to whoever it perceives as matching that role.", "actions": [{"name": "Final Orders", "text": "Can direct nearby lesser undead as if issuing a chain of command, granting them a bonus action to act on its initiative."}]}},{"name":"The Last Warlord","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"archmage","summary":"raider-general who unified the wasteland under one law","flavor":"The wasteland's uncrowned king, a raider-general who unified a hundred warbands under one banner and one law: take everything.","desc":"He built his throne from a hundred surrendered banners and holds court from the cab of a truck too heavy to move without an escort. His voice carries across a battlefield without ever needing to shout — every warband here answers to him first, their own commanders second. He has one law, and he states it plainly: take everything.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Commands loyalty from any ash-realm humanoid raiders present as reinforcements.", "actions": [{"name": "One Law", "text": "Once per turn, can order an ally within sight to make an immediate attack as a reaction."}, {"name": "Take Everything", "text": "On a killing blow, immediately regains a portion of maximum hit points, fueled by the kill."}]}},{"name":"The Half-Life","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"gargantuan hot-zone leviathan that surfaces when ground glows","flavor":"A leviathan born from the deepest hot-zone, burrowing under the ash-flats and surfacing only when the ground starts to glow.","desc":"The ground doesn't crack so much as peel back, glowing at the edges, as something gargantuan surfaces from beneath the ash-flats. Its hide sheds a heat-shimmer you can feel from thirty yards off, and geiger counters within earshot simply stop reading numbers and start screaming. It only comes up when the ground itself starts to glow — which means it's already been feeding.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Radiant/necrotic-adjacent aura; anything standing too close for too long should suffer escalating exposure.", "actions": [{"name": "Hot Zone", "text": "Creatures within 30 feet take ongoing radiation damage each round they remain in range."}]}},{"name":"Cinder Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Radiation-swollen scavenger rat gnawing wire for copper","flavor":"A radiation-swollen rat that scavenges the blast rings, chewing wire for the copper.","desc":"Radiation swelling has doubled it past any healthy rat's size, and it works at a stripped wire with the single-minded patience of something that has learned copper tastes better than anything else left in the ruins. It doesn't flee so much as scurry sideways, always toward the next wall socket."},{"name":"Slag Crow","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"Glass-feathered scavenger bird circling collapse sites","flavor":"Feathers fused with melted glass; it circles collapse sites waiting for the dust to settle.","desc":"Its feathers have fused here and there with beads of melted glass, clicking faintly when it shifts on a girder. It circles high over any collapse site, patient in a way that unsettles more than a vulture should, waiting for the dust and the screaming both to settle."},{"name":"Barrens Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"hyena","model":"net-new: ash-mangy pack jackal","summary":"Pack scavenger trailing raiders for the leftovers","flavor":"Runs in loose packs behind warbands, cleaning up whatever the raiders leave behind.","desc":"It trails a raider column at a careful, practiced distance, never quite in rifle range, never quite out of sight either. When the warband moves on, it and the rest of the pack come in low to clean up whatever got left behind — clothes, meat, anything soft enough to carry."},{"name":"Fallout Toad","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-toad","model":"net-new: bloated chem-runoff toad","summary":"Chem-bloated toad whose croak curdles nearby water","flavor":"Bloated on chem runoff, its croak alone curdles unprotected water.","desc":"Bloated well past any natural size on chem-runoff sludge, it sits half-submerged in a puddle that shouldn't sustain anything living. Its croak alone is enough to curdle whatever's left of the water nearby, a thick wet sound that carries further than it should across open ground."},{"name":"Wasteland Scrapper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"net-new: pipe-rifle warband lookout","summary":"Warband lookout with a jury-rigged pipe rifle","flavor":"A lookout for a warband, armed with a pipe rifle and a claim to the ruins ahead.","desc":"He crouches on a ridge of rubble with a pipe rifle balanced across one knee, watching the approach with the bored patience of someone paid by the hour to notice things. A whistle, two notes, low — that's the only warning the ruins ahead are already claimed."},{"name":"Ration Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"net-new: scavenged-gear ration raider","summary":"Desperate raider who kills for canned goods and water","flavor":"Kills for canned goods and clean water, nothing personal, everything necessary.","desc":"Gaunt under a layered coat, eyes fixed on whatever's strapped to your pack rather than your face, they've already decided this doesn't have to be personal. Canned goods, clean water — that's the whole negotiation, and it only has two outcomes."},{"name":"Bonepicker Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Radiation-twisted corpse that still remembers running","flavor":"Radiation twisted this corpse into a hungry thing that still remembers how to run.","desc":"It still runs in short, jerking bursts, some radiation-twisted memory of fleeing something insisting the body keep moving even with nothing left worth fleeing from. Between bursts it stands stock still, head cocked, as if listening for an all-clear that stopped coming years ago."},{"name":"Static Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Cultist who worships the static hum as divine voice","flavor":"Worships the hum in dead radios as the voice of the sky that ended the world.","desc":"A dead radio crackles against one ear, held there with tape and reverence, and the zealot repeats fragments of the static back like scripture. To them, that hum is the voice of the sky that ended the world, and they've spent years learning to translate it. They speak to you the same way — mostly static, mostly certain."},{"name":"Wire-Fanged Cur","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"net-new: barbed-wire-fanged scrap-hound","summary":"Scrap-hound fitted with crude barbed-wire fangs","flavor":"A scrap-hound whose muzzle was crudely fitted with barbed wire fangs by its handler.","desc":"Someone took the time to fit this scrap-hound's muzzle with crude barbed wire, wrapping it tight enough to bite into the animal's own gums. It snarls through the pain like the wire's a feature, not an injury, and the bite that follows tears as much as it punctures."},{"name":"Blister-Skin Drifter","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"net-new: weeping-sore contact-rot drifter","summary":"Weeping-rot shambler that spreads contact contamination","flavor":"Sores weep a contact rot; it doesn't chase so much as shamble into your path.","desc":"Weeping sores track down both arms in a slow, glistening rot, and it doesn't chase so much as drift steadily into whatever path you happen to be standing in. Contact is the whole strategy — no speed, no cunning, just patient proximity and contamination waiting to transfer."},{"name":"Powder-Keg Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Bomb-cult runner who sprints in with a strapped satchel","flavor":"Straps a satchel of scavenged explosives to their chest and sprints the last stretch.","desc":"A satchel of jury-rigged explosives bounces hard against their chest as they break into a dead sprint, breath already ragged, face set in the particular calm of someone who's done the math on this run before. There's no slowing down to reconsider once the sprint starts."},{"name":"Rust-Eaten Sentry","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Corroded security automaton walking a dead patrol route","flavor":"An old security frame, corroded half-through, still walking its dead patrol route.","desc":"Corrosion has eaten clean through one shoulder plate, exposing rusted joints that grind audibly with every mechanical step. It walks a patrol route worn into the dust by decades of identical loops, turning corners on a route map that stopped mattering generations ago."},{"name":"Chem-Slick Viper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"net-new: runoff-swollen venomous viper","summary":"Runoff-mutated viper whose venom keeps wounds open","flavor":"Its venom glands swelled on tank runoff; one bite and the wound never quite closes.","desc":"Runoff swelling has left its venom glands distended and visibly pulsing beneath translucent scales. One strike is enough — the venom keeps the wound from closing, weeping steadily long after the snake itself has slid back into the rubble."},{"name":"Grit-Locust Cloud","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"net-new: mutant locust dust-storm swarm","summary":"Mutant locust swarm stripping crops and flesh alike","flavor":"A living dust storm of mutant locusts that strips crops and flesh alike.","desc":"The horizon darkens wrong, low and grinding, and then the swarm is on you — a living dust storm of mutant locusts clicking against every exposed surface. Crops, canvas, skin: the swarm strips whatever's in its path with the same indifferent hunger."},{"name":"Carrion Beetle Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Fist-sized beetle swarm drawn to fresh ash-flat kills","flavor":"Chitinous beetles the size of fists, drawn en masse to fresh kills in the ash flats.","desc":"Fist-sized beetles converge from every crack in the rubble the instant blood hits the ash, chitin clicking together as the mass thickens. They don't discriminate between combatant and corpse — anything freshly dead, or dying, draws them in equal numbers."},{"name":"Tanker Ganger","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"net-new: fuel-convoy shotgun enforcer","summary":"Fuel-convoy enforcer quick to violence over short tribute","flavor":"Rides shotgun on a fuel convoy, quick to violence when the tribute's short.","desc":"He rides the running board of a fuel tanker with one boot braced and a shotgun resting easy across his forearm, eyes on whoever's approaching the checkpoint. The moment the tribute comes up short, that easy posture disappears fast."},{"name":"Scab-Plate Scavver","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Scrap-armored raider wearing plates looted off corpses","flavor":"Wears bolted scrap armor scavenged plate by plate off the dead.","desc":"Bolted scrap armor covers him in mismatched plates, each one scavenged off a different corpse in a different fight, dented in places that tell their own stories. He moves stiffly under the weight but wears it like a trophy case."},{"name":"Detonator Cultist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Bomb-cultist wired with a warhead trigger, waiting","flavor":"Straps a warhead trigger to his own chest, grinning, waiting to be told when.","desc":"A warhead trigger sits strapped flush against his sternum, wired with the careful pride of a man showing off jewelry. He's grinning, patient, waiting for someone — anyone — to give the word, and the grin doesn't waver even under a gun."},{"name":"Growth-Warped Boar","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-boar","model":"giant-boar","summary":"Tumor-ridden giant boar charging anything that moves","flavor":"Tumor-ridden and enormous, it charges anything that moves in its blighted range.","desc":"Tumors ridge its back in uneven lumps beneath patchy, radiation-thinned hide, and its already-enormous frame seems too large for the legs carrying it. It charges anything that moves in its blighted range without pause or discrimination — prey, predator, or wall."},{"name":"Half-Life Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Fallout-glassed bones animated by residual radiation","flavor":"Bones fused glass-green by fallout, animated by whatever still crackles in the marrow.","desc":"Fallout has fused its bones a sickly translucent green, glassy where marrow used to be, and something still crackles faintly inside the joints when it moves. It rattles upright in fits, animated by whatever residual charge refuses to let it lie still."},{"name":"Corroded Watcher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"net-new: camera-drone husk on scavenged chassis","summary":"Drone-husk sentinel still logging intruders no one reads","flavor":"A camera-drone husk grafted to a scavenged chassis, still logging intruders no one reads.","desc":"A camera-drone husk sits grafted crookedly atop a scavenged chassis, lens cracked but still swiveling to track motion out of some ancient standing order. It logs everything it sees in a memory nobody left alive will ever read."},{"name":"Ash-Choked Hound","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"Feral scrap-hound pup, quick, starving, unpredictable","flavor":"A scrap-hound puppy grown feral in the rubble, quick and starving.","desc":"Still puppy-thin under matted, ash-caked fur, it darts and feints with more energy than sense, snapping at anything that moves too fast. Starvation has made it quick and utterly unpredictable — as likely to bolt as to bite."},{"name":"Firebrand Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Nervous bomb-cult convert still willing to light fuses","flavor":"A new convert to the Bomb-Cult, still nervous, still willing to light the fuse.","desc":"New robes, still stiff and unstained, mark this one as a fresh convert to the Bomb-Cult — the nerves still show in the way their hands shake around the lit fuse. They're scared. They light it anyway."},{"name":"Mange-Back Mutt","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Mangy hairless mutt hunting collapsed subway tunnels","flavor":"Mangy, hairless, and vicious in packs, it hunts the collapsed subway lines.","desc":"Hairless in patches and vicious in numbers, it slinks along the edge of a collapsed subway entrance, drawn out by any noise or light drifting up from below. Alone it's pitiful; in a pack it's a problem."},{"name":"Warband Trapper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Trap-setter who lines roads before the warband arrives","flavor":"Lines the approach roads with snares and pit traps before the warband ever shows itself.","desc":"He works the approach roads ahead of the main column, laying snares and pit-traps with the unhurried care of a man who takes real pride in his craft. By the time the warband shows itself, the ground has already been claimed."},{"name":"Static-Touched Vermin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"net-new: irradiated numbing-touch centipede","summary":"Irradiated centipede whose touch blisters skin for days","flavor":"An irradiated centipede whose touch leaves skin blistered and numb for days.","desc":"Its many-legged body carries a faint electrical crackle along each segment, a static charge picked up from years denned near irradiated cable. Its touch leaves skin blistered and numb for days after the bite fades."},{"name":"Fume Vent Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Cracked-mask cultist chanting over leaking gas vents","flavor":"Breathes through a cracked filter mask, chanting over any vent that still leaks gas.","desc":"A cracked filter mask hisses with each labored breath as the zealot kneels beside a leaking gas vent, chanting low over the fumes like they're a font. Any vent still leaking earns a congregation of one, occasionally two."},{"name":"Wreck-Diver","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"net-new: wreck-stripping salvager","summary":"Salvager who strips wrecks before warlords claim them","flavor":"Specializes in stripping downed aircraft and sunken tankers before the warlords claim them.","desc":"Salt-scoured gear and a coil of rope mark this scavenger as someone who works fast — stripping downed aircraft and sunken tankers before any warlord's crew arrives to claim the wreck as tribute. Time, not danger, is what worries them most."},{"name":"Ashfield Widow Spider","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-spider","model":"giant-spider","summary":"Ash-camouflaged spider whose webs vanish in scorched fields","flavor":"Its web is laced with fine grit and ash, near invisible against a scorched field.","desc":"Its web carries fine grit and ash worked directly into the silk, rendering it nearly invisible strung across a scorched field. You feel it before you see it — a fine line catching at an ankle, and then the spider is already moving."},{"name":"Grinder-Belt Sentry","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Retrofitted factory automaton swinging grinder arms on flesh","flavor":"Retrofitted from an old factory line, its arms still swing the grinder motion, now on flesh.","desc":"Retrofitted from an old factory line, its twin arms still swing in the same grinding arc they were built for, only there's no belt beneath them anymore — just whatever's unlucky enough to be standing in their reach."},{"name":"Fuel-Cult Bruiser","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"net-new: rebar-swinging tithe enforcer","summary":"Tithe enforcer swinging rebar for the Fuel Cult","flavor":"Enforces tithe collection for the Fuel Cult with a length of rebar and no patience.","desc":"A length of rebar rides loose in one massive hand as he walks the tithe line, checking fuel drums against a mental ledger that never seems to favor the settlement. Patience isn't part of his collection method."},{"name":"Chem-Vat Horror","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"Chemical-vat mutant that crawled out and kept growing","flavor":"Something that crawled out of a corroded chemical vat and kept growing wrong.","desc":"It dragged itself out of a corroded chemical vat some indeterminate time ago and simply never stopped growing wrong — limbs at odd angles, texture somewhere between flesh and industrial sludge. It moves with an unsettling, dripping eagerness."},{"name":"Ash-Widow Broodmother","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"net-new: reactor-dome spider broodmother","summary":"Reactor-dome broodmother spawning hundreds each ash-season","flavor":"Nests in a collapsed reactor dome, her brood hatching by the hundreds each ash-season.","desc":"She nests deep in a collapsed reactor dome, her bloated body pulsing faintly with residual heat, surrounded by egg-sacs that split open by the hundreds each ash-season. The dome's darkness moves in ways that take a moment too long to register as legs.","traits":{"note": "Spawns or is accompanied by a brood of smaller spiders in dramatic/apex encounters.", "actions": [{"name": "Broodcall", "text": "Once per encounter, calls forth a swarm of newly-hatched spiderlings to harass a target."}]}},{"name":"Warlord's Duelist","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"net-new: warlord's arena duelist","summary":"Warlord's champion dueling for sport and succession","flavor":"Trained to fight one-on-one for the warlord's amusement — and his succession.","desc":"Trained since childhood for the one-on-one bouts a warlord stages for entertainment, he squares up with formal, almost courteous precision even in a real fight. Win or lose here decides more than his own life — succession rides on the outcome too."},{"name":"Bloat-Ghast Preacher","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"net-new: rotting bomb-cult prophet","summary":"Rotting former prophet still delivering sermons to no one","flavor":"Once a bomb-cult prophet, now a rotting thing still delivering the sermon to no one.","desc":"Once a Bomb-Cult prophet, now a bloated, rotting thing, it still stands at the pulpit position and delivers the sermon in a wet, ruined voice to a congregation that's been dead for years. It doesn't seem to notice, or care, that no one is listening anymore."},{"name":"Convoy Breaker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"net-new: axle-cracking convoy ambusher","summary":"Convoy ambusher who cracks axles before guns come out","flavor":"Specializes in ambushing fuel convoys, cracking axles before the guns ever come out.","desc":"He specializes in the quiet work — cracking an axle, slashing a tire wall, disabling a convoy before a single gun comes out. By the time the ambush shows itself, the trucks are already going nowhere."},{"name":"Warp-Chitin Stalker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"net-new: runoff-fused insect hybrid","summary":"Insect-hybrid mutant armored by decades of chem runoff","flavor":"Insect and something else fused by decades of runoff, patient and armored.","desc":"Insect plating and something else entirely have fused across its frame after decades marinating in chemical runoff, each joint armored thick and glossy. It stalks with patient, unhurried steps, in no rush because it knows it doesn't need to be."},{"name":"Rig-Mounted Turret Hound","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"net-new: scrap-hound chassis with swivel autogun","summary":"Scrap-hound chassis welded to a swivel autogun","flavor":"A scrap-hound chassis welded permanently to a swivel-mounted autogun.","desc":"A scrap-hound's four-legged chassis has been permanently welded to a swivel-mounted autogun, the barrel tracking motion independent of where its head happens to be looking. It doesn't bark a warning — it just opens up."},{"name":"Fume-Choked Ettin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"net-new: two-headed mutant scrapyard giant","summary":"Two-headed mutant giant arguing over which ruin to loot","flavor":"A two-headed mutant giant, each head arguing over which smokestack to loot next.","desc":"Two heads bicker constantly over which smokestack to loot next, neither one paying full attention to anything approaching from outside their argument. The body beneath them, though, reacts to threats just fine without needing a vote."},{"name":"Vault-Sealed Revenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"net-new: bunker blast-door ghost","summary":"Bunker-sealed ghost whose scream carries failing air","flavor":"Died locked in a bunker's blast door; its scream still carries the hiss of failing air.","desc":"It died locked behind a failing blast door, and its scream still carries that same hiss of failing air — a thin, keening wheeze underneath the wail. Whatever haunts it now remembers suffocation better than it remembers being alive."},{"name":"Warband Chieftain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"net-new: three-gang warband chieftain","summary":"Warband chief who climbed to power by outliving rivals","flavor":"Climbed to command over three rival gangs by outliving every challenger personally.","desc":"He climbed to command over three rival gangs the same way every time: by outliving every challenger personally, in full view of both crews. He carries that history in old scar tissue and in the way nobody here quite meets his eyes."},{"name":"Molten Vat Ooze","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"net-new: chemical-waste slag ooze","summary":"Chemical-waste sludge ooze dissolving anything too close","flavor":"A runoff sludge of chemical waste and slag, dissolving anything that wades too close.","desc":"A slow, viscous sludge of chemical waste and half-melted slag spreads across the ground in a widening slick, steaming faintly where it touches open air. It dissolves anything that wades too close with unhurried, patient chemistry."},{"name":"Rad-Sick Troll","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Regenerating troll locked in stalemate with its own radiation sickness","flavor":"Its regeneration keeps pace with the radiation eating it, an endless grotesque stalemate.","desc":"Its regeneration works overtime just to keep pace with the radiation actively eating through it, flesh knitting and blistering in the same breath — an endless, grotesque stalemate playing out across its own hide. It's furious, and in visible pain, and neither slows it down."},{"name":"Piston-Arm Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"net-new: hydraulic-press bolted enforcer","summary":"Salvaged hydraulic-press automaton breaking doors and skulls","flavor":"Salvaged hydraulic press arms bolted onto a walking chassis to break down doors and skulls alike.","desc":"Salvaged hydraulic press arms have been bolted straight onto a walking chassis, built for one purpose and repurposed for another — breaking down doors, and then whatever's standing behind them. The pistons hiss on every swing."},{"name":"Ashborn Wyrmling Mutant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"basilisk","model":"net-new: sun-cracking mutant reptile","summary":"Mutant reptile whose stare cracks flesh like baked clay","flavor":"A reptile mutated past recognition, its stare leaves flesh cracked like sun-baked clay.","desc":"Mutation has taken this reptile well past anything recognizable, and its stare alone leaves exposed flesh cracked and tightening like sun-baked clay. It watches before it moves, patient in the particular way predators get when they know their gaze already does half the work."},{"name":"Fallout Wight Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Ghoul squad commander who still remembers military drill","flavor":"Commands a squad of lesser ghouls, the only one who still remembers military drill.","desc":"It commands a loose squad of lesser ghouls with hand signals from some long-dissolved military doctrine, the only one among them who still remembers drill formation. Even rotted through, it keeps its posture rigid, back straight, chin level."},{"name":"Bomb-Cult High Priest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"net-new: second-blast bomb-cult priest","summary":"Fanatic priest praying for a second, holier detonation","flavor":"Preaches that the old bombs were mercy and prays daily for a second, holier blast.","desc":"He preaches from a cracked pulpit that the old bombs were mercy, and prays — daily, sincerely — for a second, holier detonation to finish the work properly. His congregation nods along like this is the most reasonable theology in the world."},{"name":"Furnace-Bound Salamander","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"salamander","model":"net-new: scrapyard blast-furnace elemental","summary":"Blast-furnace-bound elemental lashing at anyone who opens the door","flavor":"Bound into a scrapyard's blast furnace, it lashes out at anyone who opens the door.","desc":"Bound into a scrapyard's blast furnace by some forgotten ritual, it lashes out through the open door the instant anyone dares approach, flame trailing off its molten hide in long streaks. The furnace itself seems to breathe when it moves."},{"name":"Scrapfield Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three-headed radiation-fused mutant, each screaming differently","flavor":"Three mutant heads fused by radiation, each screaming a different warning.","desc":"Three heads, each fused wrong by decades of radiation, scream three separate warnings in three separate directions at once — and somehow the body beneath still moves with terrible coordination. No single head seems fully in charge."},{"name":"Diesel Pit Fighter","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"net-new: undefeated fighting-pit champion","summary":"Undefeated warlord's pit champion across nine seasons","flavor":"Champions the fighting pits under a warlord's banner, undefeated across nine seasons.","desc":"Undefeated across nine fighting seasons under a warlord's banner, he enters the pit with the loose, confident shoulders of someone who has stopped being afraid of losing. The crowd already knows how tonight ends; he's just here to make it entertaining."},{"name":"Wraith of the Fallout Line","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Dead commuters fused into one hungry drifting shape","flavor":"A commuter train's dead passengers fused into one hungry, drifting shape.","desc":"A commuter train's worth of the dead have fused into one hungry, drifting shape, faces surfacing and submerging in its smoke-thin form like reflections in dirty water. It moves along old rail lines out of habit more than purpose."},{"name":"Junk-Titan Enforcer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"net-new: compound-gate scrap titan","summary":"Warlord's gate guardian that nothing has gotten past","flavor":"Built by a warlord's engineers to guard the compound gate; nothing has yet gotten past it.","desc":"Built by a warlord's own engineers to guard the compound gate, it has stood that post through every siege since — nothing has yet gotten past it, and its posture says it intends to keep that streak.","traits":{"note": "Blocks a specific chokepoint/gate; strongly favors defending terrain over pursuing.", "actions": [{"name": "Gatekeeper", "text": "Gains advantage on attacks against any creature attempting to move past it through its guarded point."}]}},{"name":"Toxin-Blood Oni Raider","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"net-new: chem-warped toxic-blood brute","summary":"Chem-warped raider brute whose own blood is a weapon","flavor":"A brute of a raider warped by chem exposure until its blood itself became a weapon.","desc":"Chem exposure warped this brute of a raider until its own blood turned into a weapon, dark and faintly smoking wherever it's spilled. It fights recklessly, almost inviting a cut, like it knows the wound works both ways."},{"name":"Scrap-Hound Alpha","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"net-new: ash-stained scrap-hound pack alpha","summary":"Scrap-hound pack alpha with ash-stained frost-white fur","flavor":"Leads a scrap-hound pack, frost-white fur stained ash-grey from the wastes.","desc":"Frost-white fur has gone ash-grey with wasteland grime, and it holds itself apart from the pack it leads, watching before committing. When it finally moves, the rest of the pack moves with it, a beat behind, perfectly timed."},{"name":"Vault Door Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Animated blast-door guardian of a vault long since emptied","flavor":"An entire blast door animated by pre-collapse tech, still guarding a vault long since emptied.","desc":"An entire blast door has been animated by pre-collapse tech, still standing sentinel over a vault long since stripped bare by others. It doesn't know, or doesn't care, that there's nothing left inside worth guarding.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Functionally immobile guardian bound to its vault entrance; overwhelming to fight head-on."}},{"name":"Warlord's Bodyguard","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"net-new: silent seat-loyal bodyguard","summary":"Silent armored bodyguard loyal only to whoever rules","flavor":"Silent, armored, loyal only to whoever currently holds the warlord's seat.","desc":"Silent, armored head to foot, loyalty riding entirely on whoever currently holds the warlord's seat rather than any person in particular. It stands a half-step behind its charge, watching hands, not faces."},{"name":"Contagion Ghast Broodkeeper","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"net-new: deliberate rot-cultivating ghast","summary":"Rot-spreading undead cultivating new ghouls like crops","flavor":"Spreads its rot deliberately, cultivating new ghouls the way a farmer tends a field.","desc":"It spreads its rot with deliberate care, tending fresh ghouls the way a farmer tends rows of crops, walking a slow circuit to check on each one. There's a horrible patience to how methodically it works."},{"name":"Detonation Engineer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"net-new: half-mad reactor-core warhead engineer","summary":"Bomb-cult engineer half-mad with reactor-core warhead math","flavor":"Designs the Bomb-Cult's warheads from scavenged reactor cores, half-mad with the maths of it.","desc":"Reactor-core scrap is laid out across a workbench in precise, obsessive rows, and he mutters warhead math under his breath, half-mad with the elegance of it. He looks up at intruders the way a man looks up from an equation he was about to solve.","traits":{"note": "May be rigging an active device in the scene; interrupting the work matters more than fighting him directly.", "actions": [{"name": "Dead Man's Math", "text": "If reduced to 0 HP, can trigger a final rigged charge as a reaction before dying."}]}},{"name":"Iron Convoy Behemoth","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"net-new: animated war-rig hauler","summary":"War-rig hauler plated with scrap from a dozen dead vehicles","flavor":"A war-rig hauled by an animated chassis, plating scavenged from a dozen dead vehicles.","desc":"An animated chassis hauls a war-rig forward under plating scavenged from a dozen dead vehicles, each panel a different color, a different make, welded into one grinding whole. The ground shudders under its tread before it's even close.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive Construct; can ram/crush terrain or lighter obstacles in its path."}},{"name":"Fallout Hydra Broodhorror","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Hydra whose severed heads regrow ever more mutated","flavor":"Each severed head regrows twisted differently, mutation compounding mutation.","desc":"Each severed head regrows twisted differently than the last, mutation compounding on mutation until no two heads share the same jaw or the same eyes. It hisses out of several mouths at once, none of them quite agreeing on the sound.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Regrows heads when severed, each subsequent head potentially gaining a new minor mutation/trait."}},{"name":"Cinderfall Vampire Warlord","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"net-new: settlement-razing undead warlord","summary":"Undead warlord feeding on survivors of settlements it razes","flavor":"Feeds on the survivors of the settlements it razes, then rules the ashes it leaves.","desc":"It feeds on the survivors of the settlements it razes, then settles onto whatever throne is left standing in the ashes to rule what's left. There's no urgency to the feeding — it has learned the world keeps producing more.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Regains hit points on successfully draining a victim; commands local undead/raiders it has claimed."}},{"name":"Bunker-Bred Nightmare Steed","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"net-new: cult general's scorching mount","summary":"Cult general's steed scorching ash-fields with every charge","flavor":"A cult general's mount, hooves scorching whatever ash-field it charges across.","desc":"Hooves leave scorched prints across whatever ash-field it charges through, smoke trailing off a mane that never quite stops smoldering. A cult general rides it into every engagement, and the horse seems to enjoy the work as much as the rider.","traits":{"note": "Its hoofprints/wake can ignite flammable terrain."}},{"name":"Reactor Wyrm","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Bedrock-burrowing wyrm glowing hot from irradiated feeding","flavor":"Burrows through irradiated bedrock, its hide glowing hot from what it's fed on.","desc":"It burrows through irradiated bedrock with a slow, grinding hunger, hide glowing dull orange-hot from decades of feeding on whatever leaked down from the reactors above. The ground warms noticeably before it ever breaks the surface.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can burrow and resurface elsewhere; radiant/fire-adjacent heat aura."}},{"name":"Grand Warlord's Champion","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"net-new: hundred-duel warband champion","summary":"Undefeated champion who fought a hundred duels for command","flavor":"Fought a hundred duels to earn the right to lead the largest warband in the ash flats.","desc":"A hundred duels earned this one the right to lead the largest warband in the ash flats, and every scar across an unbeaten frame tells part of that story. He fights like a man who has genuinely never needed a plan B."},{"name":"Ash-Frost Colossus","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Nuclear-winter mutant with ash-snow-crusted fur and endless hunger","flavor":"A nuclear-winter mutant, matted fur crusted in ash-snow, hungry beyond reason.","desc":"A nuclear-winter mutation left its fur matted and crusted white with ash-snow, breath fogging thick even in the mild wasteland heat. Hunger drives it past reason — it doesn't stop advancing once it's decided you're food.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Cold-adjacent damage on attacks; relentless pursuit, rarely disengages."}},{"name":"Grid-Fed Iron Sentinel","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Grid-wired automaton drawing endless trickle current","flavor":"Still wired to a dead power grid, drawing a trickle of current that keeps it standing forever.","desc":"Cables still run from its chassis into a dead power grid somewhere beneath the ruins, drawing an endless faint trickle of current that keeps it standing long after everything else in the district failed. It has no reason to ever stop.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Effectively tireless while connected to its grid source; disconnecting it may be a viable tactic."}},{"name":"Vaultbreaker Behemoth","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"net-new: bare-handed vault-cracking giant","summary":"Mutant giant that cracks vault doors bare-handed","flavor":"A mutated giant that cracks vault doors open bare-handed for the warband behind it.","desc":"Bare-handed, it wrenches vault doors off their hinges for the warband trailing behind it, tossing steel aside like it weighs nothing. It works with the bored efficiency of a laborer who's cracked this same door a hundred times before.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can force open barriers/doors as a mundane action; strength-based grapple favored."}},{"name":"Deathwatch Cult Oracle","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: preserved countdown-interpreting oracle","summary":"Preserved oracle still interpreting a countdown only it hears","flavor":"Preserved by cult ritual to keep interpreting the countdown only it can still hear.","desc":"Ritual preservation has kept this thing upright long past any natural span, its hollow voice interpreting a countdown that only it can still hear, muttering numbers that never seem to reach zero. It speaks in fragments, as if translating from somewhere else entirely.","traits":{"note": "Prophetic mutterings can be used as in-fiction hints/omens the DM voices mid-combat."}},{"name":"Blightborn Roc","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"net-new: radiation-grown monstrous carrion bird","summary":"Radiation-grown carrion bird whose shadow panics settlements","flavor":"A carrion bird grown monstrous on radioactive corpses, its shadow alone panics a settlement.","desc":"Its shadow alone is enough to send a settlement running for cover — a carrion bird grown monstrous on a diet of radioactive corpses, wingspan blotting out whole streets at a time. It circles once before it commits to a dive.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive wingspan grants area-effect wind/knockback on landing or takeoff."}},{"name":"Ash Warlord's Marilith Enforcer","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"Bound fiend running security for a warlord's court","flavor":"A fiend bound into service by an ancient bargain, now runs security for a warlord's court.","desc":"Bound by some ancient bargain into permanent service, it now runs security for a warlord's court with the same cold competence it likely once brought to darker business. Multiple arms move independently, each tracking a different threat in the room.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple weapon-bearing arms can each attack independently in a round."}},{"name":"Devouring Junkyard Kraken","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"net-new: flooded-scrapyard tentacled mutant","summary":"Tentacled scrapyard-pit mutant born of decades of chemicals","flavor":"Lives beneath a scrapyard's flooded pit, tentacled from decades of chemical mutation.","desc":"Decades of chemical mutation gave it tentacles where a scrapyard's flooded pit should have had nothing living at all. It surfaces slow, oil-slick water sheeting off its hide, testing the air before committing to an attack.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple grappling tentacle attacks; strongly territorial to its flooded pit."}},{"name":"The Countdown Keeper","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"net-new: ancient cult figurehead whispering the final number","summary":"Preserved cult figurehead whispering an endless final number","flavor":"An ancient cult figurehead, preserved by dogma, still whispering the final number.","desc":"Dogma alone has preserved this ancient cult figurehead, whose hollow voice keeps whispering a final number that never seems to arrive. Followers still gather to listen, certain that whatever's coming will validate every sacrifice they've made getting here.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; whispered 'countdown' functions as an in-fiction omen device the DM can voice.", "actions": [{"name": "The Final Number", "text": "Once per encounter, can impose a lingering dread effect on all who hear it speak, unsettling their next roll."}]}},{"name":"The Warlord Ascendant","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"net-new: fear-united ash-flats overlord","summary":"Warlord who united every ash-flat gang through pure fear","flavor":"United every warband in the ash flats under one banner through fear alone.","desc":"Every warband in the ash flats answers to him now, united not by loyalty but by a fear he cultivated personally, warband by warband, for years. He doesn't raise his voice to be obeyed — the reputation does that work for him.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; commands loyalty across the realm's raider factions as reinforcements.", "actions": [{"name": "United Under Fear", "text": "Can call in additional raider allies to the fight once per encounter."}]}},{"name":"The Fallout Titan","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: mountain-scale mutation titan","summary":"Mountain-sized mutant mistaken for terrain until it moves","flavor":"A mutation so vast it's mistaken for a mountain until it stands up.","desc":"It's easy to mistake for a mountain ridge until the ridge stands up, ash sliding off shoulders the size of a building, and the whole horizon seems to shift with it. By the time you realize what you've been walking toward, it's already looking down at you.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; area-of-effect stomp/collapse attacks appropriate to its scale.", "actions": [{"name": "Groundshaker", "text": "A single stomp can knock prone and damage everyone within a wide radius."}]}},{"name":"The Last Detonation","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"net-new: warhead-core walking chassis","summary":"Warhead-core chassis built to finish what first bombs started","flavor":"A warhead-core walking chassis the Bomb-Cult built to finish what the first bombs started.","desc":"The Bomb-Cult built this walking chassis around a live warhead core, meant to finish whatever the first bombs left undone. It moves with a deliberate, unhurried gait — there's no reason for it to hurry when it's this certain of the outcome.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; can detonate as a last resort, dealing catastrophic area damage.", "actions": [{"name": "Unfinished Business", "text": "On being reduced to 0 HP, can trigger a massive area detonation before going inert."}]}},{"name":"The Glass Sea Wyrm","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"Ancient leviathan swimming the vitrified glass flats","flavor":"Older than the warbands, it swims the vitrified glass flats where the first blast struck.","desc":"Older than every warband hunting these flats, it swims through vitrified glass where the first blast struck the ground and fused the sand solid. The glass ripples around its passage like water, catching the light in long, silent waves.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; swims/burrows through glassed terrain as though it were liquid.", "actions": [{"name": "Glass Wake", "text": "Its movement through glassed ground can shear and damage anything caught in its wake."}]}},{"name":"Chittergaunt","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"pack-hunting mutant scavenger, calls its litter","flavor":"A hairless, twitchy thing that runs on all fours and screeches to call its litter-mates in; harmless alone, a real problem in a pack of six.","desc":"Hairless and twitchy, it moves low on all fours in short, jerking bursts, screeching a high thin call the instant it spots easy prey. Alone it's barely a threat — the danger is that the screech is never really meant to be answered alone.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: irradiated pack-scavenger, stock post-apoc creature type (not tied to any franchise)"},{"name":"Rustfang","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"scrap-fused mutant guard-dog","flavor":"A dog (or what was a dog) with fused metal shrapnel grown into its hide from decades denned in a scrapyard; bites like a bear trap.","desc":"Shrapnel has grown directly into its hide after decades denned in a scrapyard, jagged metal fused seamlessly with matted fur along its spine. Its bite lands with the crushing, locking pressure of a bear trap rather than an animal's jaw.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: junkyard guard-beast gone wrong"},{"name":"Waste Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"road-gang footsoldier, fights in packs","flavor":"Sun-blistered, tattooed with the mile-markers of every settlement they've burned; fights in a screaming knot with two or three others.","desc":"Sun-blistered skin bears crude tattoos marking the mile-markers of every settlement this crew has burned, a walking ledger of the road behind them. They never fight alone — two or three more close in fast, already screaming before contact.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-gang footsoldier archetype: post-collapse road-warrior stock type"},{"name":"Cult Acolyte, Bomb-Struck","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"warhead-relic zealot, suicidal devotion","flavor":"Wears a rusted warhead casing like a holy relic and prays to the flash that reshaped the world; will walk into obvious death singing.","desc":"A rusted warhead casing hangs from their neck like a holy relic, polished smooth by years of reverent handling. They pray to the flash that reshaped the world with total sincerity, and will walk straight into obvious death mid-hymn if the moment calls for it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: doomsday-worship footsoldier, stock post-apoc type"},{"name":"Bleached Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"radiation-sick feral scavenger, not truly undead-lore","flavor":"Not undead by ritual but by dose — the radiation cooked the mind out and left hunger behind; skin cracked like dry riverbed, eyes milk-white.","desc":"This isn't undeath by ritual — it's undeath by dose, radiation cooking the mind clean out and leaving only hunger behind. Skin has cracked like a dry riverbed, eyes gone milk-white, and it moves with the jerking persistence of something that forgot how to stop.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"irradiated-ghoul archetype: our own fallout-sickness take, distinct from any undead-ghoul lore or franchise ghoul design"},{"name":"Junk Crawler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"debris-heap creature that devours metal","flavor":"A drift of rebar and car doors that somehow walks and somehow wants your rifle barrel more than your blood.","desc":"A drift of rebar and car doors somehow shifts and walks, scraping across broken pavement with a sound like a landslide in slow motion. It wants the rifle barrel in your hands more than it wants you, jaws grinding metal with obvious preference.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: animate debris/rust-monster reskin for a wasteland setting"},{"name":"Warlord's Enforcer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"warlord's chain-wielding enforcer","flavor":"Keeps the warlord's convoy in line with a length of chain and a reputation for never asking twice.","desc":"A length of chain rides looped over one shoulder, worn smooth from years of use keeping a warlord's convoy in line. He has a reputation for never asking twice, and he doesn't bother explaining that reputation before the chain comes off his shoulder.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord's lieutenant archetype"},{"name":"Rad-Hulk","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"hulking overgrown mutant brute","flavor":"Grew three sizes past human and forgot most of its words along the way; still remembers the name of the town it used to guard.","desc":"It grew three sizes past anything human should, most of its words lost somewhere along the way with the rest of its old shape. It still remembers the name of the town it used to guard, and mutters it sometimes, low, between blows.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: hulking irradiated brute, stock post-apoc mutant type"},{"name":"Scrap Colossus","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"welded-together walking scrap machine","flavor":"Welded together from three different trucks by hands that clearly loved the work; runs on spite and a leaking fuel drum.","desc":"Three different trucks were welded together by hands that clearly loved the work, panel seams still bearing the pride of whoever built it. It runs on spite and a fuel drum that's been leaking for longer than it should still be moving.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: junkyard-built walking machine, stock salvage-golem type"},{"name":"Chem-Baron","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"net-new: wasteland kingpin in scavenged finery, no bespoke model needed (uses mage stat frame only)","summary":"drug-and-fuel kingpin warlord","flavor":"Runs three settlements on rationed water and homebrewed stims; smiles like he's already won the argument you haven't started.","desc":"He runs three settlements on rationed water and homebrewed stims, smiling the easy, patient smile of a man who's already won whatever argument you haven't started yet. Every word out of him sounds like a favor, and every favor has a price attached later.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord archetype: settlement-controlling drug/fuel kingpin"},{"name":"The Sermon-Bearer","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"net-new: robed zealot with a warhead-fragment icon, no bespoke model needed (uses priest stat frame only)","summary":"doomsday high-priest awaiting the next blast","flavor":"Preaches that the bombs were mercy and the next ones will finish the job kindly; his flock believes him, which is the scary part.","desc":"He preaches that the bombs were mercy and the next ones will finish the job kindly, voice warm and reasonable in a way that makes the theology worse, not better. His flock believes every word — that's the part that should worry you.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: doomsday high-priest, our own invented theology (no real-world cult referenced)"},{"name":"Ashfield Titan","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"hauler-built industrial war-walker","flavor":"Built from a downed cargo hauler by a warlord who wanted a throne that could also crush things; mostly it just crushes things.","desc":"Built from a downed cargo hauler by a warlord who wanted a throne that could also crush things, it mostly just crushes things — the throne part came later and matters less. Its footfalls flatten whatever debris hasn't already been ground down.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive Construct; slow but devastating melee reach."},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: settlement-sized industrial walker, stock giant-war-machine type"},{"name":"Glasslands Broodmother","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"apex matriarch of the mutant bloodline","flavor":"Every Chittergaunt and Rustfang for fifty miles traces back to her den under the melted overpass; she remembers being smaller, and human.","desc":"Every Chittergaunt and Rustfang for fifty miles traces its bloodline back to her den beneath the melted overpass. She remembers, in some buried way, being smaller — and human — before whatever happened here changed all of that permanently.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can summon or is escorted by lesser mutant broodkin (Chittergaunt/Rustfang) as reinforcements."},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: apex irradiated matriarch, seeds a feral bloodline"},{"name":"Deadman's Warlord","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: convoy-king in welded plate armor built from truck panels, no bespoke model needed","summary":"apex convoy-king, rules through fuel scarcity","flavor":"Crowned himself off the corpse of the last warlord and the fuel reserve underneath his throne-truck; his convoy is a moving nation.","desc":"He crowned himself off the corpse of the last warlord and the fuel reserve buried under his throne-truck, and his convoy has since grown into something closer to a moving nation than a gang. Fuel scarcity is his real weapon — he simply controls who gets to keep driving.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; commands a convoy of loyal raiders as ongoing reinforcements; controls fuel access as a soft-power lever."},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord archetype: apex convoy-king ruling by fear and fuel scarcity"},{"name":"The Last Sermon","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"apex doomsday-prophet guarding a live warhead","flavor":"Claims the final bomb is still out there, waiting for his word; nobody who's called the bluff has lived to be wrong about it.","desc":"He claims the final bomb is still out there somewhere, waiting on his word alone, and nobody who's called that bluff has lived long enough to be proven wrong. He speaks softly, which somehow makes the claim land harder.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; the 'live warhead' claim may be a real environmental threat in the encounter, not just a bluff.", "actions": [{"name": "The Word", "text": "Can threaten to trigger a hidden device, forcing a tense standoff mechanic before combat resumes."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: apex doomsday-prophet who holds a live warhead as scripture"},{"name":"Half-Life","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"apex fallout-horror, decades-deep radiation exposure","flavor":"Been soaking in the hot zone so long the geiger counters just give up near it; what's left of the mind is patient, and furious.","desc":"It's been soaking in the hot zone so long that geiger counters just stop reading anything useful near it, needles pinned uselessly. Whatever's left of the mind inside is patient in the worst way — patient like something that stopped needing to hurry a long time ago, and furious underneath all of it.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; severe radiation aura; extremely durable, prioritizes methodical destruction over speed.", "actions": [{"name": "Saturation", "text": "Creatures remaining adjacent for multiple rounds suffer escalating radiation damage that compounds each turn."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"irradiated-ghoul archetype: apex fallout-mutated horror, decades of exposure past any human baseline"},{"name":"The Foundry Made Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: factory-fused industrial mass, no bespoke model exists yet (iron-golem stat frame)","summary":"factory-fused apex war-machine","flavor":"An entire pre-collapse factory floor — presses, arms, conveyor teeth — fused by decades of slag into a single furious machine that still thinks it's making something.","desc":"An entire pre-collapse factory floor — presses, conveyor teeth, hydraulic arms — has fused under decades of slag into one furious, moving machine. It still goes through the motions of manufacturing, grinding and stamping at nothing, like some part of it genuinely believes it's still making something.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; multiple industrial 'limbs' (press/conveyor/grinder) can each act as separate attack options.", "actions": [{"name": "Production Line", "text": "Can make attacks with two different industrial limbs in the same round."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: apex, a factory's automated defense grid fused into one rampaging mass"}],
 "suburb":[{"name":"Cul-de-Sac Wanderer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"shambling loop-walker, the block's living dead","flavor":"A resident in bathrobe and slippers who never quite reaches the mailbox, looping the same forty feet of driveway forever.","desc":"Terrycloth robe cinched at the waist, one slipper on. It follows the same curve of driveway it always has, forty feet out and forty feet back, never reaching the mailbox at the end. Its face turns toward you as you pass but the feet never stop moving. The newspaper it's collecting is three years of newspapers deep."},{"name":"Porch-Light Moth-Thing","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"screen-door lurker begging to be let inside","flavor":"Drawn to bug-zapper blue, it flutters against screen doors at 3am, whispering in a dead child's voice about being let in.","desc":"Something the size of a dinner plate beats itself soft and rhythmic against the screen door, wings catching the bug-zapper blue in dusty flickers. Up close its knock has cadence, almost words. A child's voice, thin through the mesh, asks very politely to be let in out of the cold."},{"name":"HOA Enforcer Drone","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"flying clipboard drone, petty bureaucratic menace","flavor":"A clipboard on wings that measures lawn height by moonlight and leaves violation notices on houses that don't exist yet.","desc":"A clipboard hovers at eye level on two small propellers, its pen scratching against nothing. It circles the yard in slow surveying loops, measuring grass blades against some remembered standard. A violation notice prints from its side and flutters onto a doorstep that, until this morning, wasn't zoned for a house."},{"name":"Sprinkler Ghoul","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"irrigation-system ghoul, rises on the same timer nightly","flavor":"It rises from the irrigation system at exactly 3:00am, joints clicking like a valve timer, watering the grass with something that isn't water.","desc":"It hauls itself up out of the sprinkler head at exactly three in the morning, joints clicking on a schedule like a valve timer clicking over. Grey and stooped, it drags a garden hose in a slow arc across the lawn, and the fluid hissing from the nozzle isn't clear.","traits":{"note": "Rises only at 3:00am on its irrigation cycle; inert and buried the rest of the day."}},{"name":"Under-the-Bed Groper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"classic bedroom-dark lurker, waits for lights-out","flavor":"Flat black and patient, it presses itself to the box spring all day and only unfolds a reaching limb once the lamp clicks off.","desc":"Flat, black, and patient, it presses itself the width of a shadow against the underside of a box spring all day long. Only when the lamp clicks off does one long arm unfold from the dark, feeling blind and unhurried across the carpet for an ankle."},{"name":"Overwaving Neighbor","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"too-friendly neighbor, watching before you're even awake","flavor":"He waves before you've even opened your blinds, hand moving a beat too fast, smile a beat too wide, already knowing your name.","desc":"He's already at the fence line when you open the blinds, hand raised a half-second before you could have seen him there. The wave moves a beat too fast, the grin holds a beat too long, and he says good morning like he's reading it off something written just for you."},{"name":"Curfew Light Wisp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"streetlamp wisp that herds you home by dusk","flavor":"Streetlamps that switch on early and herd stragglers indoors by dimming ahead of their steps, punishing anyone caught out past curfew.","desc":"A soft orange glow detaches from the streetlamp overhead and drifts down to hover at shoulder height, warm as a nightlight. It herds without touching — easing in front of you, nudging you gently homeward — and it dims, displeased, the longer you resist its curfew."},{"name":"Casserole Cultist","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"grief-vulture neighbor, dish in hand, headcount ready","flavor":"Arrives at your door within the hour of any tragedy, dish already baked, eyes already counting who's missing from the block.","desc":"She's at the door within the hour, dish still warm in oven-mitted hands, eyes already flicking past your shoulder to count who's home and who isn't. The condolences come rehearsed. The foil-wrapped pan smells like someone else's kitchen, and she won't leave until she's seen every room."},{"name":"Cursed Lawn Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"grinning gnome, roots the cursed lawn to its post","flavor":"Ceramic and grinning, it rotates a few degrees each night to keep every lawn in its sightline; the grass beneath it never dies right.","desc":"A garden gnome, chipped paint and permanent grin, stands rooted dead-center in a lawn too green for the season. Its painted eyes track anyone who steps off the walkway, and the grass around its little wooden feet is the only patch too healthy to be natural."},{"name":"Vinyl-Sider","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"fence-phasing hound, barks on a dead loop","flavor":"A dog-shaped thing that phases through fences, patrolling yard boundaries with a bark that sounds pre-recorded and looped.","desc":"Pale and rangy, it moves along the property line like it's tracing a fence that isn't there anymore, phasing half-through a chain-link gap without breaking stride. Its bark comes on a loop — three short, one long, the same three short — over and over, never varying, never stopping."},{"name":"The Family Wearing the Skin","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"the too-perfect family, all three wearing the same face","flavor":"Three bodies at the dinner table moving in perfect unison, each one a puppet worn by the same wrongness, still setting a fourth place for someone who used to live there.","desc":"Mother, father, child, arranged on the porch swing in a tableau too composed to be caught off guard. All three turn to smile at the same instant, same teeth, same tilt of the head — one family's worth of expression spread across three faces that never learned to disagree.","traits":{"note": "Acts and reacts as a single mind across all three bodies; damage or fear affecting one visibly ripples to the others."}},{"name":"Perpetual Yard-Sale Hag","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"folding-table hag selling the missing's belongings","flavor":"Every Saturday her folding tables reappear stocked with items that belonged to people who are no longer around to miss them.","desc":"Card tables sag under sun-faded toys and dog-eared paperbacks, all of it priced in nickels and dimes, none of it ever quite gone by evening. She haggles hard over a chipped mug, and if you look closely at the framed photos in the free box, someone in them looks like your neighbor's missing daughter."},{"name":"Riding-Mower Revenant","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"dead husband still mowing perfect ghost-stripes","flavor":"A husband who died mowing the lawn and never stopped; the mower is rusted through but still runs, dragging him behind it in perfect stripes.","desc":"The engine turns over on its own around dusk, and he's in the seat again, hunched forward the way he always sat, cutting stripe after perfect stripe into a lawn that was already done an hour ago. He doesn't look up. The stripes never overlap and never stop."},{"name":"The Man Behind the Rubber Mask","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"the masked slasher, unhurried and always closing","flavor":"He never runs and never speaks, just walks the same unhurried pace behind you no matter how fast you go, mask blank and waiting for the moment you stop looking back.","desc":"He doesn't run and he doesn't need to — every door you lock, he's already found the window. The mask never shifts to show breathing underneath, and the knife in his hand moves at exactly the pace of somebody who has never once needed to hurry."},{"name":"Book Club Coven","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"wine-and-book coven picking next month's victim","flavor":"Six women, one wine bottle, and a discussion that always circles back to who in the neighborhood needs to be 'welcomed properly' next.","desc":"Wine glasses catch the lamplight around a coffee table stacked with paperbacks nobody's finished reading. The conversation drifts, casual as gossip, toward whichever neighbor missed this month's meeting — and by the second bottle, they've already decided who's next."},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Deep One","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"bloated pool-thing, too big for the water it's in","flavor":"Something surfaces in the cheap plastic pool every summer solstice, too large for the water it's found in, patient as chlorine rot.","desc":"The above-ground pool water has gone the color of old tea, and something under the cloudy surface is too large for the liner that holds it. It rises just enough to fill the frame with wet grey shoulders, dripping algae-string, before the pump kicks back on and it sinks."},{"name":"Cheerful Renovation Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"stitched-contractor golem, endlessly remodeling the house","flavor":"Stitched from drywall, spare lumber, and whichever contractor stopped answering his phone, it keeps 'improving' the house whether anyone's living in it or not.","desc":"Stitched from drywall scraps, spare studs, and what might be a former contractor's overalls, it hums along to a radio only it can hear while it tears a load-bearing wall down by hand. It's smiling — or its face is arranged to — and the house keeps getting bigger on the inside."},{"name":"The PTA President","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"smiling PTA fiend running the block and its secrets","flavor":"She runs the bake sale, the block committee, and the thing underneath the school gymnasium, and never once raises her voice doing any of it.","desc":"She runs the meeting from the head of the folding table, agenda printed and stapled, smile never dropping even as she reads off the fundraiser numbers. Everyone defers to her without quite remembering deciding to. Under the fluorescent gym lights her eyes catch just slightly wrong, an amber flare and gone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chair's Motion", "text": "Compels a Charmed target within earshot to second whatever she proposes, acting on its turn to support her plan."}]}},{"name":"Lawn-Order Enforcer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"shield-guardian","summary":"covenant-bound guardian, trims anything grown too tall","flavor":"Summoned by an unspoken covenant among homeowners, it trims anything — hedge, weed, or trespasser — that grows past the agreed-upon height.","desc":"Bronze-green and shield-bearing, it strides the block at the pace of a patrol nobody hired, shears in one hand where a sword should be. Any lawn grown past regulation height gets a visit — the shears open with a sound like a portcullis, and the grass afterward is trimmed to the millimeter, unnaturally even."},{"name":"Master of the Block Party","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"oni","summary":"shapeshifting host, one small yearly price for paradise","flavor":"He wears whatever face the street needs to see, grills burgers that taste like every summer you can remember, and only asks for one small thing in return each year.","desc":"He's got a grill in one hand and a cooler of drinks in the other, and every face at the party turns toward him like sunflowers. The bunting is real, the music is good, the burgers are perfect — and by the time the sun sets, the guest count is always one short of who arrived.","traits":{"hp": "elevated for its CR band", "actions": [{"name": "Perfect Host", "text": "Once per party, names a guest whose next failed save leaves them charmed into staying long after the lights come down."}]}},{"name":"The Substitute Mailman","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"undead mailman, on-time deliveries for the dead","flavor":"He's delivered mail on this route since before anyone living can remember, always at the exact same minute, and packages addressed to the dead still arrive.","desc":"He's punctual to the second, sliding envelopes through the slot with a gloved hand that's a little too pale at the wrist. He never rings, never speaks, and the letters he delivers are addressed to people who don't live at that address anymore — or haven't, for years."},{"name":"Development Overseer","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"model-home golem enforcing the original blueprint","flavor":"Built from the bones of the model home nobody bought, it enforces the subdivision's original blueprint, rebuilding whatever the residents dare to change.","desc":"Cast in poured concrete and rebar, it stands three stories at the edge of an unfinished cul-de-sac, blueprint tube clutched like a scepter. It doesn't walk so much as reposition, block by block, correcting any house that's drifted from the original site plan — including the ones with people still inside.","traits":{"ac": "higher than chassis baseline", "note": "Treats structural deviation (broken windows, missing fences) as a target to physically correct."}},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch Itself","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"the hive-mind of curtain-twitchers, reading through glass","flavor":"Not a person but a consensus — the collective suspicion of every curtain-twitching resident fused into one entity that reads minds through window glass.","desc":"No single body — just a hundred twitching curtains up and down the street, all pulled back a half-inch at once, all watching the same spot. When it acts, the porch lights along the whole block flicker in sequence, a single attention passing house to house.","traits":{"note": "Perceives through every window on the block simultaneously; cannot be flanked or surprised while any house on-screen still has power."}},{"name":"The First Homeowner","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"the founder's corpse, landlord of the whole afterlife","flavor":"Buried under the foundation of the very first house on the street, he built the whole subdivision as his afterlife and considers every current resident a tenant who owes back rent in something other than money.","desc":"Desiccated in a cardigan gone the color of dust, seated in a recliner that's outlasted three generations of carpet beneath it. He owns the deed to every house on the street, signed in a hand that hasn't aged, and he calls the whole afterlife rent-controlled — payable, eventually, by everyone who's ever lived here."},{"name":"The Idea of Sunday","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"the unblinking eye dreaming the loop into place","flavor":"A god of clipped hedges and identical doors given a single vast eye that never blinks, dreaming the whole suburb into looping perfection, one repeated day at a time — waking it means the wrongness stops keeping regular hours.","desc":"There's no body, only a stillness that settles over the whole block at once — church bells that ring without a church, a smell of pot roast from every kitchen at the same moment, and one unblinking presence behind it all, dreaming the entire day into its loop."},{"name":"Latchkey Shade","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"crawling-claw","model":"crawling-claw","summary":"Small unseen presence that rattles empty houses at dusk","flavor":"The lingering print of a kid who let himself in every day after school and never quite left; scuttles across empty kitchen counters after dark.","desc":"The house is empty — parents at work, kids somewhere else — and still something moves through it: a hallway light switching off after you've turned it on, a doorknob rattling from the inside of a room you just checked. It never shows itself. It just rattles, dusk after dusk, in a home with nobody home."},{"name":"Storm-Drain Grabber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"Whispers from storm drains, lures children with a friendly voice","flavor":"A wet, whispering thing that lives where the curb meets the culvert, luring lost balls and lost kids alike with a friendly voice from the dark.","desc":"A friendly, sing-song voice drifts up out of the storm grate, warm as an aunt's, calling a child's name it definitely shouldn't know. Reach down toward the sound and you can feel the cool air moving — and something down there, patient, waiting for fingers to get close enough."},{"name":"Rerun Wraith","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Armchair-bound ghost that traps watchers in endless reruns","flavor":"Bound to a living-room armchair, endlessly rewatching the same three channels; anyone who sits too long starts rewatching with it.","desc":"Sunk deep into a recliner that's molded to its shape, it stares at a television locked on the same three episodes, forever. Sit down near it and the room dims at the edges; the show on screen starts looping your own evening back at you, one rerun at a time, until you can't remember which version is live."},{"name":"Chain-Link Fence-Walker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"troglodyte","model":"troglodyte","summary":"Skulks along fence-lines just out of direct sight","flavor":"Something that moves along backyard fence-lines on all fours, always one yard over from wherever you're looking.","desc":"Something low and scaled keeps pace just past the fence line, always at the edge of what you can clearly see — a shoulder here, a tail there, gone before you turn fully toward it. The chain-link rattles a half-second after it passes, never during."},{"name":"Popped-Collar Poltergeist","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Restless spirit slamming doors, showing off for no one","flavor":"The restless spirit of the neighborhood's self-appointed cool kid, still slamming screen doors and flipping bike kickstands for an audience that stopped watching decades ago.","desc":"Doors slam up and down the hallway in quick succession, cabinet after cabinet banging open and shut like nobody's watching — except it very much wants an audience. A collar-popped shape flickers in the hall mirror, admiring itself between each slam."},{"name":"Newspaper Route Revenant","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Undead paperboy still riding a route no one ordered","flavor":"Still pedaling the same route at 5 a.m., flinging rolled papers that thud like fists through screen doors.","desc":"Bicycle spokes click in the pre-dawn dark, tires hissing over dew-wet driveways on a route that technically ended when the paper folded. Papers land on porches exactly where they always have — except most of those houses stopped taking delivery years ago, and nobody's paid the bill since."},{"name":"Static-Screen Watcher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Face surfaces in TV static, watches whoever watches it","flavor":"A face that surfaces in the snow between channels on old console TVs, staring out until someone stares back.","desc":"The television hisses to white noise between channels, and a face surfaces in the static — indistinct, grainy, mouth moving without sound. It doesn't wait for you to change the channel. It's already watching whoever's watching it."},{"name":"Trash Night Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Compulsive undead trash-day ritual, drags off what it finds","flavor":"Drags the cans to the curb every Tuesday out of decades-old habit, and drags anything else it finds in the yard right along with them.","desc":"It waits for the exact hour the cans go out, then drags itself along the curb from bin to bin, sorting through what the street's thrown away with a compulsive, ritual care. Whatever it finds worth keeping, it drags off into the dark between houses — and some nights, that's not garbage."},{"name":"Garage Sale Ghast","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Undead haggler who trades your belongings for its junk","flavor":"Haggles over folding tables of dead people's belongings, and won't let a customer leave without buying something of theirs instead.","desc":"Folding tables of somebody else's belongings, price-tagged in a shaky hand, and behind them a haggler with grey, papery skin who only trades — never sells for cash. Whatever you hand over, it hands back something of its own, older, wronger, and insists it's a fair swap."},{"name":"Split-Level Skulker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"Pack hunter that ambushes through split-level stairwells","flavor":"A pack-hunter that has learned split-level floor plans intimately, cutting people off between the sunken den and the stairs.","desc":"It waits at the landing where the stairs turn, a half-flight up or down from wherever you are, breathing slow through the dark of a split-level house built with too many blind corners. It hunts in a pack — you hear the second one before you see the first."},{"name":"Rec-Room Rug Thing","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"animated-rug-of-smothering","summary":"Shag basement carpet that smothers unwary bare feet","flavor":"The shag carpet in the finished basement never quite matched the room; it waits for bare feet to wander in during commercials.","desc":"The shag carpet in the basement rec room has always looked a little too thick, a little too warm underfoot. Step onto it barefoot and it rises around your ankles like it's been waiting, wrapping tight before you can even shout for the stairs."},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Thing","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Cloudy backyard pool hides something that surfaces at night","flavor":"Something moved into the cloudy above-ground pool nobody's cleaned since June; it only surfaces once the pump shuts off for the night.","desc":"The pool water's gone cloudy-green and hasn't been drained in a season, the filter clogged with something that isn't leaves. Ripples move against the wind at night, and once in a while the surface bulges upward, briefly, like something underneath is testing how thin the liner really is."},{"name":"Wrong-Number Screamer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Phantom prank caller that claims it's already in the house","flavor":"Calls the house phone at 3 a.m. insisting you have the wrong number, then insists it's already inside.","desc":"The phone rings at an hour nobody calls, and the voice on the other end screams before you've said hello — thin, distant, panicked, claiming with total certainty that it's already inside your house. The line stays open even after you hang up."},{"name":"Cul-de-Sac Bike Gang Ghost","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Ghost bike gang circling forever, daring new kids to join","flavor":"Three or four spectral kids on banana-seat bikes circling a cul-de-sac forever, daring anyone new to join the loop.","desc":"Bicycle chains rattle in a slow circle around the cul-de-sac at an hour when no kid should be out, translucent riders standing on their pedals, daring anyone new to the block to join the loop. Once you start pedaling with them, the circle gets harder to leave."},{"name":"Aluminum Siding Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Siding-panel construct that paces you when you don't look","flavor":"A suit of cheap siding panels clatters upright behind you on the sidewalk, keeping perfect pace whenever you don't look back.","desc":"A siding panel comes loose in the wind, then another, until an entire wall's worth of aluminum has assembled itself into something upright and stalking. It only moves when you're not looking — turn back fast enough and it's just siding again, propped a little too neatly against the house."},{"name":"Van with No Windows","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Idling windowless van, door sliding open on its own","flavor":"It idles at the curb with the engine running and the side door already sliding open, going nowhere until someone gets close enough to look inside.","desc":"It idles at the curb with the engine running and nobody visible behind the wheel, exhaust curling in the porch light. The side door slides open on its own, slow and smooth, and the dark inside doesn't reflect any light back out at all."},{"name":"Ding-Dong-Ditch Devil","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Small","frame":"dretch","model":"dretch","summary":"Gleeful imp that rings and runs, leaves a scorched handprint","flavor":"A small, gleeful horror that rings the bell and vanishes, leaving a scorched handprint on the door and a worse mark on whoever answers too slowly.","desc":"The doorbell rings and by the time you reach it, whatever pressed it is gone — except for the scorched, small handprint left smoking on the frame. Somewhere down the block, gleeful laughter that's a half-octave too high echoes off somebody's garage door."},{"name":"Toybox Escapee","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Self-winding toy that patrols under the bed relentlessly","flavor":"A wind-up toy that wound itself up once too often and never wound back down; it patrols under the bed with clockwork patience.","desc":"A wind-up toy, soldier or robot, ticks its way slowly across the bedroom floor on its own power long after its key should've run out. It patrols the space under the bed with mechanical patience, and its eyes, glass and painted, seem to track whoever's watching."},{"name":"Curbside Furniture Fiend","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"Free curbside couch that eats whoever tries to take it","flavor":"That free couch someone left at the curb with a 'FREE' sign taped on has been eating whoever tries to carry it home.","desc":"A couch sits at the curb with a hand-lettered FREE sign taped to one cushion, upholstery a little too clean for something somebody's really discarding. Reach to test the fabric and the whole thing exhales, cushions folding inward around the offending hand like a mouth closing."},{"name":"Overgrown Hedge Maze Beast","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"vine-blight","summary":"Untrimmed hedge maze conceals something living in the gaps","flavor":"The decorative hedge maze behind the model home was never finished being trimmed, and something learned to live in the unfinished parts.","desc":"The hedges haven't been trimmed in a summer, grown thick enough to swallow the paths between them into true blind turns. Something rustles the leaves a beat behind wherever you last stood, patient, letting the maze do the cornering for it."},{"name":"Sun-Bleached Lawn Jockey","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Faded lawn statue that turns to track trespassers","flavor":"A faded plaster lawn ornament that turns its painted eyes to track anyone who cuts across the grass instead of using the walk.","desc":"Paint peeling, color faded to a ghost of what it was, the statue stands at the end of a driveway with one arm permanently extended. Its head turns, degree by degree, to track anyone who steps off the sidewalk — and by the time you notice, it's already facing you dead-on."},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Deep One Spawn","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"Young pool-thing spawn awkwardly hunting on dry lawn","flavor":"A smaller relation of the thing in the pool, gone hunting on land for the first time, still learning to walk on the lawn.","desc":"Small and wet and clumsy on dry grass, it flops and drags itself away from the above-ground pool in short, awkward bursts, gill-slits working uselessly in open air. It's young, and slow on land, but it's not alone out here — something bigger put it in that pool."},{"name":"Meter Reader Mimic","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Fake utility worker that always asks to go around back","flavor":"Wears the utility company's polo and clipboard perfectly, and always asks to be let around back where nobody can see from the street.","desc":"Clipboard, reflective vest, badge that doesn't quite match any utility company logo you recognize — and always the same question, asked pleasantly: mind if I go around back to check the meter? Its smile doesn't move quite right when it repeats itself."},{"name":"Skateboard Ramp Wight","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Undead skater endlessly practicing the trick that killed it","flavor":"Died trying to land the big trick off the plywood ramp behind the school and still practices, endlessly, on anyone who gets close.","desc":"Wheels clatter up a plywood ramp in the dark, over and over, the same trick attempted at the same angle, the same fall at the very top of the arc. It never lands it. It never stops trying. The wounds from the fall that killed it never close."},{"name":"Backyard Bug-Zapper Wisp","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"Escaped bug-zapper spark that hunts warm bodies at night","flavor":"A crackle of blue light that escaped the porch zapper and now hunts anything warm-blooded that wanders the yard after dark.","desc":"A spark breaks loose from the bug-zapper's blue coil and hangs in the air, crackling faint and hungry, drawn now to warmth instead of light. It drifts low across the yard at body height, hunting for something bigger than a moth to close its circuit through."},{"name":"Video Store Return-Slot Horror","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"gibbering-mouther","model":"gibbering-mouther","summary":"Rental drop-slot horror that changes whatever it swallows","flavor":"Something lives in the drop slot of the video rental place, and every tape fed back through comes out changed, and so does the hand that fed it.","desc":"The drop-slot in the shuttered video store's door never fully closed, and something reaches back out of it now — thin, groping, faintly smelling of magnetic tape and mildew. Whatever it drags back down through the slot comes back changed, warped like a tape left too near a magnet."},{"name":"Arcade Cabinet Haunt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Ghost of an unbeaten high-scorer, lit inside the cabinet","flavor":"A high score that was never beaten, and the kid who set it, both still lit up behind the screen glass long after closing.","desc":"The cabinet in the corner still lights up though the power strip's unplugged, attract-mode looping a high score nobody's ever beaten. A face is visible in the screen glow if you stand close enough — the unbeaten champion, still playing, still furious that no one else gets to try."},{"name":"Mall Food Court Ooze","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"Slow food-court ooze that absorbs stragglers after closing","flavor":"A slow, syrupy mass that oozes between the food court tables at closing time, absorbing spilled soda, dropped fries, and the occasional straggler.","desc":"It moves at the speed of closing time, translucent and slow across cold tile, absorbing dropped fries and abandoned trays as it goes. Anyone who lingers past the last announcement finds the ooze has quietly closed the distance, patient as a mall cop nobody hired."},{"name":"Backyard Trampoline Terror","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"bulette-pup","model":"bulette-pup","summary":"Burrowing thing under a trampoline that overbounces kids on purpose","flavor":"It burrowed up under the trampoline springs and now bounces kids skyward on purpose, waiting to see who doesn't land right.","desc":"The trampoline mat sags oddly in the middle even with no one on it, springs creaking under weight from below. Jump on it and the bounce comes back wrong — too high, too eager — like something underneath is helping, and hoping you don't come back down where you left."},{"name":"Home Alarm Banshee","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Alarm-triggering wraith whose wail is worse than the siren","flavor":"Trips every motion sensor in the house at once, its wail indistinguishable from — and worse than — the alarm it triggers.","desc":"The security system trips for no reason anyone can find, and under the electronic chirp there's a second sound — a wail, rising, that gets inside your skull worse than the siren ever could. It only quiets once every door and window reads locked."},{"name":"The Family Wearing the Skin (Understudy)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"jackalwere","model":"jackalwere","summary":"Lesser copycat family-thing, close but not quite convincing","flavor":"A lesser cousin of the perfect-family horror down the street — close enough to pass at a barbecue, not close enough to pass close up.","desc":"A second, lesser copy of a family down the street, close enough to pass a glance but never quite right up close — the smiles land a half-second late, the child never quite the same height twice. It's studying the real thing, learning to be more convincing."},{"name":"Handyman Who Never Leaves","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Contractor who never finishes the job or leaves the house","flavor":"Hired for one gutter job three summers ago, his truck's still in the driveway and he's always got one more thing that needs fixing inside.","desc":"His truck's been parked in the driveway for three weeks and the job was supposed to take two days. He's always got one more thing to fix, one more reason to stay past dark, tools laid out with more care than the actual repair ever gets."},{"name":"The Substitute Teacher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"Roving fiend-teacher whose classes always lose a student","flavor":"Fills in for a week at a time across a dozen schools, and every class she covers loses one kid to absence that never gets explained.","desc":"She takes attendance with unusual attention, lingering on certain names, and by the end of the semester the classroom always runs one desk short. Parent-teacher conferences with her run long, and afterward, nobody quite remembers what was said — only that they agreed to something."},{"name":"Split-Shift Shapeshifter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Gas station night clerk with a shift no human works","flavor":"Works the graveyard shift at the all-night gas station and something else's shift after that; the clerk's smile never quite sits right.","desc":"He's behind the gas station counter at an hour no manager schedules for, ringing up cigarettes with hands that seem to have one joint too many. His shift changes only when the light does — never on any clock a human punches."},{"name":"Riding-Mower Revenant, Deluxe Model","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Upgraded haunted mower that enforces HOA lawn regulations","flavor":"A newer, meaner riding mower haunts the HOA's model-home block, chasing anyone whose lawn falls out of regulation.","desc":"Upgraded, chrome-bright, it cuts stripes into every lawn on the street whether asked or not, engine note sharper than the old model's. A laminated card tucked under the seat lists HOA lawn-height violations — and it enforces every one personally."},{"name":"The Man in the Ice Cream Truck","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"Ice-cream-truck fiend whose jingle lures kids away","flavor":"His jingle plays even when the truck's parked and empty; kids who chase the sound too far never quite come back the same.","desc":"The jingle drifts down the street at an hour past when any truck should still be running, tinny and a half-step flat. Kids drift toward it before their parents notice they've gone, drawn by a melody that gets a little more insistent the longer you try to ignore it."},{"name":"Backyard Bonfire Cultist Circle","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Neighbor cult burning offerings in a backyard barrel","flavor":"A ring of neighbors around a burn barrel every full moon, feeding it things that were never supposed to burn that clean.","desc":"Neighbors in flannel and lawn chairs stand around a burn barrel in someone's backyard, tossing in things that don't smell like yard waste. The chanting is low, almost like small talk, until you catch the same three words repeating under everyone's breath."},{"name":"The Coach Who Never Ages","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Ageless little-league coach spanning two decades unchanged","flavor":"Has led the same little-league team for twenty-two straight seasons and looks exactly as he did in the first team photo.","desc":"He's run the same little league for two decades and looks exactly like the team photo from the first year — same haircut, same whistle, same easy grin. Parents remark on it fondly. None of them ask the obvious question out loud."},{"name":"Skin-Deep Scoutmaster","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Doppelganger scoutmaster who returns from trips one kid short","flavor":"Leads camping trips into the woods behind the development and always brings back one fewer kid than he took, plus one new smile.","desc":"He leads the troop on the same camping trip every year, cheerful and competent, and every year the group that comes back is one member short. He always has an explanation ready — early pickup, a sick parent — delivered with a warmth that never quite reaches his eyes."},{"name":"The Perfect Father Next Door","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"Model neighborhood father with a shed nobody mentions","flavor":"Never misses a game, always has the grill going, and keeps a locked shed out back that the whole street has learned not to mention.","desc":"He grills every weekend, waves at every car, remembers every neighbor's name — the model of a good dad, right down to the shed at the back of the yard that he never opens and never explains, and that nobody's ever thought twice to ask about."},{"name":"Static-Cling Poltergeist Swarm","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"swarm-of-dretches","summary":"House-wide micro-hauntings that unify into one coordinated threat","flavor":"A house full of small hauntings — flickering nightlights, cold spots, moved keys — that only reveal themselves as one coordinated thing when cornered.","desc":"Lights flicker in one room, then another, then a third, small hauntings scattered through the whole house like static before a storm. Given time they converge — flickers syncing, whispers overlapping into one voice — until the house's dozen small wrongs act as a single, focused will."},{"name":"Cursed Above-Ground Deep One Broodmother","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Matured pool-horror now spawning across the cul-de-sac","flavor":"The original pool-thing from three doors down, matured and spawning; the whole cul-de-sac's chlorine budget has quietly tripled.","desc":"The above-ground pool that used to hold one bloated thing now can't contain what it's become — water black and roiling, spawn slipping over the rim to spread through yards up and down the cul-de-sac. The smell of brine hangs over the whole block now, even the dry lawns."},{"name":"Renovation Golem, Load-Bearing Model","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"Drywall-and-lumber golem built from a shortcut renovation curse","flavor":"Built from mismatched drywall, salvaged studs, and whatever the last flip-house crew left behind, animated by a contractor's shortcut curse.","desc":"Built from a contractor's shortcut and a curse nobody read the fine print on, it's drywall dust and two-by-fours given purpose, tearing out load-bearing walls with total confidence. The house groans around it. It doesn't seem to notice, or care."},{"name":"The Photo Album Hag","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Photo-collecting hag who edits herself into family albums","flavor":"Collects family photo albums door to door for 'the historical society' and edits herself into every family that lets her keep one.","desc":"She collects family photo albums from yard sales and open houses, and pages through them slowly on her porch each evening. Look closely at the older photos and you'll find her face already there, inserted seamlessly among people who swear they never met her."},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"All-seeing patrol captain who knows every closed-door secret","flavor":"Patrols at all hours in a golf cart with a spotlight, and somehow always knows exactly what happened behind every closed door on the block.","desc":"He wears the reflective vest and carries the clipboard, walking the same route every dusk, greeting everyone by name. But his eyes — multiple, lidless, arranged wrong under a baseball cap — miss nothing behind any closed door on the route, and he remembers all of it."},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Shark","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"umber-hulk","model":"umber-hulk","summary":"Oversized predator circling under a backyard pool's liner","flavor":"Something with far too many teeth for a four-foot pool has been circling under the vinyl liner since the last pool party.","desc":"Something far too large for a backyard pool circles just under the liner, a fin-shaped shadow crossing and recrossing the pale plastic bottom. The water level never seems to change no matter how much of it that shape displaces."},{"name":"The Ham Radio Operator","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-zerth","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"Attic ham-radio operator receiving transmissions from nowhere","flavor":"Runs a shortwave rig in the attic that picks up something answering back that was never broadcasting from anywhere on Earth's dial.","desc":"Up in the attic, headphones clamped tight, he turns the dial through static searching for something that isn't broadcasting from anywhere on Earth. He transcribes what comes through in a cramped, careful hand — numbers, mostly, and occasionally your name."},{"name":"The PTA Vice President","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"chasme","model":"chasme","summary":"PTA lieutenant gathering names for an unseen master list","flavor":"Second-in-command to the block's real horror, buzzing between bake sales gathering names for a list nobody's seen the end of.","desc":"She takes minutes at every meeting in a notebook she never lets anyone else read, cross-referencing names against a list only she can see. Cross the PTA President and she's the one who quietly writes your name down first."},{"name":"Backyard Grill Fire Elemental","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"azer-pyromancer","model":"azer-pyromancer","summary":"Never-extinguished grill fire that's still hungry to cook","flavor":"Someone's charcoal grill fire never went out after the block party; it's been cooking ever since, and it's still hungry.","desc":"The charcoal in the grill never fully cooled from last summer's cookout, and now flame licks up through the grate on its own schedule, orange and patient, still smelling faintly of lighter fluid and burnt hot dogs. It's still hungry. It's been hungry a long time."},{"name":"The Cul-de-Sac's Second Family","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"drider","model":"drider","summary":"Multi-limbed horror that assembles into a fake nuclear family","flavor":"A many-limbed thing that arranges itself into a mother, father, and two kids for the length of a driveway conversation, then unfolds once the door shuts.","desc":"Too many limbs folded into too few silhouettes, arranged behind lit windows to look, from the street, exactly like a mother, a father, two kids at the dinner table. Get close enough to the glass and the joints don't bend where a person's should."},{"name":"Lawn-Order Enforcer, Senior Patrol","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"shield-guardian","summary":"Promoted HOA golem whose citations double as curses","flavor":"The block's original code-enforcement golem has been promoted; it now issues citations that are also curses.","desc":"Its citations aren't paper anymore — the golem simply touches a hand to whatever's out of code, and the violation writes itself directly onto the offender, a mark that itches worse the longer it goes uncorrected."},{"name":"The Block Party Ringmaster","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"vrock","model":"vrock","summary":"Block-party organizer who plans a yearly disappearance","flavor":"Organizes the annual street party with unnerving precision, down to exactly who disappears in the bounce-house line each year.","desc":"He organizes the summer block party every year without fail, decorations up before anyone volunteers, guest list somehow always complete before the invites go out. Each year, in the group photo afterward, exactly one face from last year's photo is missing, and nobody remembers asking why."},{"name":"Attic Insulation Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"hook-horror","model":"hook-horror","summary":"Attic-dwelling horror slowly widening the crawlspace over decades","flavor":"Something moved into the pink fiberglass batting between the joists decades ago and has been slowly widening the crawlspace ever since.","desc":"Something has been widening the crawlspace behind the attic insulation for years, pink fiberglass torn and packed into strange drifts against the rafters. It moves in the walls at night, slow and patient, a little more room carved out every season."},{"name":"Master of the Costume Party","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"oni","summary":"Costume-party host whose winners are never seen again","flavor":"Hosts the block's annual costume bash wearing a mask indistinguishable from a face, and everyone who wins 'best costume' stops being seen after.","desc":"Every Halloween he hosts the best party on the block, costume contest judged personally, prizes always a little too elaborate for a neighborhood gathering. The winners are announced with real ceremony. Nobody ever quite remembers seeing them since."},{"name":"The Substitute Mailman's Supervisor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Route supervisor delivering unsolicited packages to every house","flavor":"Oversees the whole route from an unmarked postal truck, delivering something to every house that requested nothing.","desc":"He rides the route behind his substitute, double-checking every delivery with clipboard in hand, and leaves packages at doors nobody ordered anything to. The labels are handwritten, addressed correctly, and always to someone who used to live there."},{"name":"Development Overseer, Phase Two","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Slab-built golem grading a phantom lot off the map","flavor":"Built from the foundation slabs of the houses that never got finished, it's been quietly grading a lot that isn't on any map.","desc":"Cast from the same mold as its predecessor, it grades an empty lot that exists on no survey anyone's filed, leveling ground for a phase of the development that was never approved. The bulldozer treads leave marks in dirt that shouldn't be there in the morning."},{"name":"The First HOA Board","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Undead HOA founders still voting on ordinances forever","flavor":"Five founding board members, still convening in the clubhouse basement, still voting unanimously on ordinances no living resident agreed to.","desc":"Five founding members, long dead, still convene in the clubhouse basement on the second Tuesday of every month, voting unanimously on ordinances no living resident proposed. Their gavel strikes the table with a sound like a coffin lid."},{"name":"The Perfect Family, Fully Grown","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"marilith","model":"marilith","summary":"Skin-family horror that stopped pretending to be separate people","flavor":"What the skin-wearing family becomes once it stops bothering to look like four separate people at all.","desc":"It doesn't bother separating into mother, father, child anymore — the pretense has worn through, and what stands on the porch now is one horror wearing three faces at once, limbs overlapping where three bodies used to be distinct."},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch, Fully Awake","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"Block-wide surveillance horror that has begun to act","flavor":"Every porch light on the block is one of its eyes now, and it has stopped just watching.","desc":"Every curtain on the block is drawn back at once, every porch light on, and for the first time the watching has purpose — footsteps sound from houses that should be empty, moving in coordination toward whoever it's decided doesn't belong."},{"name":"The Substitute Principal","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"erinyes","summary":"Fill-in principal whose detention slips are binding contracts","flavor":"Called in to run the school when the real principal 'took leave,' she rewrites detention slips into something closer to binding contracts.","desc":"She fills in for a week at a time, calm and reasonable right up until she hands out a detention slip — and the fine print on those slips is binding in ways no student ever reads closely enough to notice until it's too late."},{"name":"Superstore Overnight Stock Horror","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"void-monk-psion","model":"void-monk-psion","summary":"Overnight stocker that spells warnings in the aisle layout","flavor":"Something restocks the strip-mall superstore's shelves after close, in patterns that spell out things in the aisle layout by morning.","desc":"The big-box store's overnight stocker rearranges the aisles into patterns that spell warnings if you stand at the right angle under the fluorescent lights. It's fast between the shelves and slow to be seen — you only catch the edge of it, restocking, always restocking."},{"name":"The Cable Guy Who Was Never Scheduled","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"Uninvited cable installer who tunes homes to impossible channels","flavor":"Shows up during the four-hour window nobody actually booked, and every house he services starts picking up channels that don't exist.","desc":"He shows up unannounced, always a convenient time, always apologetic about the confusion over the appointment. Once he's tuned your television, the channels that come in afterward don't correspond to any station that should exist."},{"name":"The First Family of the Development","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Founder-family entombed beneath the model home's foundation","flavor":"Buried under the model home's foundation when the development broke ground, and the whole subdivision was built as its reliquary.","desc":"Entombed beneath the model home's foundation since before the first house went up, they still walk the original show-home halls at night, greeting visitors with the same rehearsed warmth real estate agents once used to sell the dream."},{"name":"The Idea of a Perfect Lawn","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Plant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"Root-system ideal that prunes any lawn that stands out","flavor":"An ideal so total it's grown roots under every yard on the block, pruning any resident who lets their grass get too tall — or too green.","desc":"Root systems run unseen beneath every yard on the block, one continuous organism enforcing a single ideal of green. Any lawn that grows differently — patchy, wild, untended — gets pruned back overnight by roots nobody planted."},{"name":"The Last Bell of the School Year","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Eternal dismissal bell that never released its final class","flavor":"A dismissal bell that never actually let the last class out; it's been ringing the same three-o'clock chime under the school for generations.","desc":"The dismissal bell rings at the end of the school day, every day, forever, and one class never got to leave when it sounded the first time. You can hear them still in the halls after hours, packing up for a summer that never starts."},{"name":"The Whole Street, Awake","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"Whole cul-de-sac revealed as one house-wearing organism","flavor":"Every house on the cul-de-sac turns out to be one organism wearing driveways for a face, and it has just noticed it has neighbors watching back.","desc":"Every house on the cul-de-sac turns out, at once, to be a single organism wearing siding and shingles like clothes — windows blink, driveways flex like joints, and the whole street exhales in one long, structural breath."},{"name":"The Idea of Back-to-School Night","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"Annual gymnasium dread wearing everyone's worst self at once","flavor":"An institutional dread so vast it manifests once a year in the gymnasium, wearing every parent and teacher's worst version of themselves at once.","desc":"The gymnasium fills with folding chairs and nervous parents once a year, fluorescent lights buzzing overhead, and something moves through the crowd wearing each attendee's worst fear of themselves, one bad impression at a time."},{"name":"The Development That Was Never Finished","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"Bankrupt developer's undying will still building empty lots","flavor":"The developer who went bankrupt mid-build bound his own unfinished vision into undeath, and the empty lots are still filling in on their own schedule.","desc":"Half-built foundations stretch to the edge of a subdivision that went bankrupt decades ago, rebar rusting up through weeds. Somewhere under the unfinished model home, a developer's will refuses to die, still drafting phases for lots that will never sell."},{"name":"Backyard Tetherball Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Ghost light endlessly circling a broken tetherball pole","flavor":"A pale light that spins around the pole where the tetherball snapped off years ago, still keeping score against an opponent who left.","desc":"A pale light circles the pole where a tetherball snapped its rope years ago, looping the same orbit the ball used to trace, faster the longer you watch it. The chain-link fence nearby rattles in time with its slow, endless revolution."},{"name":"Split-Level Basement Ooze","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Basement floor-drain ooze that never receded after a storm","flavor":"Seeped up through the unfinished basement's floor drain during the last big storm and never seeped back down.","desc":"The floor drain in the basement never fully closed after a storm flooded the split-level years back, and something the color of standing water still seeps out of it on humid nights, spreading slow across the tile before it recedes."},{"name":"Trick-or-Treat Bag Snatcher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"sprite","model":"sprite","summary":"Halloween sprite that swaps candy for something inedible","flavor":"Darts between porch lights on Halloween swapping good candy for something that was never meant to be eaten.","desc":"Small and quick between porch lights, it darts into open candy bags on Halloween night and swaps the contents for something that only looks like candy — wrapped, familiar-shaped, and absolutely not food."},{"name":"The Kid Who Never Came Home","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Ghost child endlessly biking his last-seen route home","flavor":"Still riding his bike home past curfew, every night, along the exact route where he was last seen thirty years ago.","desc":"A bicycle bell rings somewhere behind you on the street after dark, and a small pale shape pedals past on the same route home he never finished, wheels crunching gravel that isn't there anymore. He doesn't look at you. He's not going to make it home tonight either."},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Leech Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-piranhas","model":"swarm-of-piranhas","summary":"Splintered pool-horror fragments swarming as biting leeches","flavor":"Something split off from the main pool-thing into dozens of smaller, blood-hungry pieces after the last shock treatment.","desc":"Fragments of something bigger, splintered off and gone feral, writhe through the pool water as a mass of biting, leech-shaped horrors. They move as one thing when threatened, surging toward whatever's disturbed the surface."},{"name":"Little League Bleacher Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Undead superfan haunting a closed field's bleachers","flavor":"Sits in the same bleacher seat at every game, cheering a team that stopped existing after the field closed, and eyeing the concession stand.","desc":"The bleachers at the closed ball field creak under weight that shouldn't be there, and a figure in decades-old fan gear cheers at a game that ended long ago, still keeping score, still furious when the wrong team wins in its memory."},{"name":"Backyard Fireworks Mephit","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"Dud-firework mephit hunting for something bigger to ignite","flavor":"Sparked to unlife from a dud bottle rocket on the Fourth, it's been looking for something bigger to detonate ever since.","desc":"A dud firework from last summer never fully burned out, and now a small, sparking shape drifts low over yards looking for something bigger to touch off. It hisses like a lit fuse whenever it gets close to anything flammable."},{"name":"The Man in the Rubber Mask","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Silent knife-stalker in a rubber mask, cuts the power first","flavor":"He doesn't run, doesn't talk, and the mask never quite fits his face right — like it's a size too small for whatever's under it. Cuts power to the block before he starts.","desc":"He cuts the power before he ever knocks, plunging the house dark, and the mask he wears doesn't so much as shift when he breathes. He's already inside by the time you notice the porch light's out, moving at exactly the speed of somebody who never has to hurry.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock slasher-archetype (unmasked, unnamed stalker type — no specific franchise silhouette)"},{"name":"The Neighbor Who Isn't","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"A neighbor replaced, wearing the body a little wrong","flavor":"Waters the lawn at 2 AM. Smiles too wide at the mailbox. Something wears the neighbor like a coat that's still learning how elbows work.","desc":"He waves the same wave, mows the same lawn, says the same hellos — but the skin sits a half-size wrong on the frame underneath, and if you watch long enough you catch him forgetting, for just a second, which way his own front door opens.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"body-snatcher/pod-person stock archetype (generic, no specific 50s-film IP)"},{"name":"The Homeowners' Association","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"noble","summary":"Cul-de-sac conformity cult in matching cardigans","flavor":"Matching cardigans, identical lawns, a smile that's a citation waiting to happen. They vote unanimously. They vote for you next.","desc":"They arrive as a group, cardigans matching down to the button, clipboards synchronized, smiles set to the same friendly angle. They speak in turns, finishing each other's sentences about lawn height and paint color, never quite disagreeing, never quite individual.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"too-perfect-family/HOA conformity archetype, original"},{"name":"The Thing in the Storm Drain","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"Shapeless lurker that surfaces through storm drains after rain","flavor":"It doesn't need a face because the neighborhood kids provide the imagination for it. Rains bring it up from the culvert; the culvert never quite drains right after.","desc":"After heavy rain, the storm drain at the end of the street backs up with something that isn't water pressure — a shapeless mass surging up through the grate, dragging itself along the gutter before the runoff carries it back down.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"under-the-street / storm-drain lurker stock archetype (deliberately not the well-known clown)"},{"name":"The Thing Under the Bed","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"aberration","size":"Small","frame":"blind-deep-stalker","model":"blind-deep-stalker","summary":"Blind floor-level lurker only real in the dark","flavor":"Only exists between the mattress and the floor, and only when the light's off. Every kid on the block has independently drawn the same picture of it.","desc":"It's never visible with the lights on, not even a shadow, not even a shape — but the second the room goes dark it's real, low to the floor, blind and groping for whatever's dangling off the mattress edge.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"under-the-bed/closet-monster nursery archetype, original design"},{"name":"Static Bride","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Reanimated stitched-together undead bride, disrupts electronics","flavor":"Stitched back together from parts that never asked to be a set. Every TV on the block snows over when she walks past; she's looking for the hands that made her.","desc":"Stitched together from more than one wedding, veil torn and re-sewn, she drifts down the hallway trailing a static charge that kills every electronic device within arm's reach. The wedding march plays faintly from somewhere with no speaker.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Bride/animated-corpse motif — Shelley's Frankenstein (1818, PD) & 19th-c. reanimation folklore, NOT any studio's visual design"},{"name":"The Man Who Sold the House","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Devil-bargain realtor collecting on unread contracts","flavor":"Every family on this street signed something they didn't read. He still holds the paper, and the paper is still due.","desc":"Smiling, handshake firm, business card always ready — he closed the deal on half this street, and the fine print in his contracts binds in ways no notary would recognize. Buyer's remorse, in his listings, is contractual and permanent.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"deal-with-the-devil / crossroads-bargain motif — universal folklore + Faust legend (pre-1929 tellings, PD)"},{"name":"Medusa of the Mall","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Mythic Gorgon relocated to the dead mall's cosmetics counter","flavor":"Works the perfume counter under fluorescent light that never shows her eyes. The food court has forty statues who lingered too long at her register.","desc":"She works the cosmetics counter at the dead mall under fluorescent lights that never quite illuminate her face fully, hair moving in ways the still air of the store doesn't explain. Customers who linger too long at her mirror display don't blink again.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Medusa — Greek myth (Ovid, Metamorphoses, ancient/PD); OUR setting recontext, not any film design"},{"name":"The Kraken in the Deep End","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Ancient sea-legend leviathan squatting in a condemned pool","flavor":"The community pool closed for 'renovations' in 1983 and never reopened. Something ancient and briny decided the deep end was close enough to home.","desc":"The condemned public pool's deep end holds far more water than its chlorine-stained tile should allow, and something ancient and coiled fills that impossible depth, tentacle-tips breaking the surface only when the diving board creaks under new weight.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Kraken — Norse/Scandinavian sea-legend (pre-modern folklore, PD)"},{"name":"The Toy That Loves You Back","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Possessed toy that relocates itself to your room at night","flavor":"Batteries not included, malice included free. It waits on the shelf all day, perfectly still, counting whose room it's going to be in tonight.","desc":"It sat on a shelf in one bedroom last week. Tonight it's on the pillow, arranged just slightly differently than you left it, plastic eyes catching the nightlight at an angle that tracks you across the room.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-toy/possessed-plaything archetype, original design (no specific doll-franchise likeness)"},{"name":"The Refrigerator That Remembers","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Cursed kitchen appliance that preserves things unnaturally","flavor":"Hums a little too rhythmically. Keeps things fresh that shouldn't still be recognizable. The ice maker only runs when no one's watching.","desc":"Nothing in it spoils. Nothing in it should still be edible after this long, and yet the leftovers from months ago look exactly as fresh as the day they went in — preserved by something in the hum of the compressor that isn't refrigeration.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-appliance archetype, original design"},{"name":"The Arcade Cabinet with One More Life","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"construct","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"Haunted arcade cabinet that keeps its high-scorer","flavor":"High score never changes because the last kid who beat it never left the arcade. It only takes quarters, and it always has exact change waiting in the slot.","desc":"The cabinet in the corner of the rec room glows even unplugged, high-score table locked on one name for years. It offers one more credit, free, to anyone willing to try to beat it — and it never lets its champion actually lose that title.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-arcade-machine archetype, original design (generic 'haunted cabinet,' no specific game IP)"},{"name":"The Babysitter's Watcher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Home-invader who calls from inside the house first","flavor":"He's already inside before the phone rings the second time. The kids upstairs are fine. He just wanted her to know he could've stopped that.","desc":"The phone rings from inside the house before he's even broken in, voice calm on the line asking if anyone's checked the children lately. By the time you realize the call's coming from the upstairs extension, he's already on the stairs.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stalker-on-the-phone-in-the-house urban-legend archetype, original (the call-is-coming-from-inside trope, generic)"},{"name":"The Cul-de-Sac Werething","cr":4,"role":"high","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Suburban werewolf-neighbor, folklore lycanthropy in a cul-de-sac","flavor":"Coaches Little League. Grills every Sunday. On the full moon the whole street knows to keep the dog in and not ask questions in the morning.","desc":"He's the friendliest guy on the block by daylight, always first to help move furniture, always remembers birthdays. Once a month the porch light across his lawn goes out early, and something with too much hair and too many teeth runs the fence lines until dawn.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"European werewolf/lycanthropy folk tradition (settled, non-Indigenous, widely public-domain in literary form)"},{"name":"Renfield of Maple Court","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Thrall-servant mook, devoted to something unseen in the house","flavor":"Eats bugs off the porch and swears the new guy in the house at the end of the block 'just needs some time to settle in.' He's very devoted.","desc":"He mows his lawn at odd hours, mutters devoted little promises to an upstairs window that's always curtained, and flinches whenever the mail truck slows near his house. Whatever he serves, he serves gladly, and he's been waiting a long time for it to notice him back.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Renfield — Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD), the servant/thrall archetype specifically, not Dracula himself"},{"name":"The Count of the Cul-de-Sac","cr":12,"role":"apex","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Stoker-lineage vampire lord who bought the biggest house in cash","flavor":"Bought the biggest house on the block in cash, never during daylight hours. Invites you in exactly once. That's all he needs.","desc":"He bought the biggest house on the street in cash, no mortgage, no questions, and hosts elaborate dinner parties that always run past midnight. He never eats at his own table, and the housekeeper who answers the door has worked for him since before anyone on the block was born.","traits":{"note": "Classic folkloric vampire-lord chassis; invitation-bound entry rules apply at the DM's discretion for his home."},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the literary vampire lord, our own suburban recontext, not any film's visual design"},{"name":"The Skeleton in Every Closet","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Literal skeleton-in-the-closet, one per household","flavor":"Every house on the street has one, and every family swears it's a coincidence. It rattles the coat hangers when the furnace kicks on.","desc":"Open the hall closet looking for winter coats and there it is, upright, patient, exactly where the coats should hang — one per household, tucked behind the same door in every house on the street, and none of the families ever mention it.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"generic reanimated skeleton — folkloric/literary undead, no owner, ancient stock motif"},{"name":"The Lawn Ornament That Turned","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Small","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Animated yard-decor ambush predator, still until you're alone","flavor":"Every yard has one — gnome, birdbath cherub, plastic flamingo. They hold still for the mail carrier. They don't hold still for you.","desc":"Stone-still and harmless-looking on the front lawn all day, wings folded, posture decorative. The moment nobody's watching directly, it isn't in the same spot anymore — closer, always closer, and never once caught mid-stride.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"animated-yard-decor archetype (garden gnome / gargoyle-adjacent, original), stone-creature motif is ancient/uncopyrightable"},{"name":"The Debt Collector","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Folkloric collector-of-debts undead, clipboard and windbreaker","flavor":"Wears a windbreaker and carries a clipboard. Every house owes him something eventually — a memory, a name, a Sunday afternoon. He always collects on schedule.","desc":"He knocks in a windbreaker two decades out of style, clipboard in hand, reciting an amount owed that nobody remembers borrowing. He doesn't leave until something's handed over — and what he collects is never quite money.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"psychopomp / grim-collector folk motif (universal death-messenger tradition, settled and non-Indigenous)"},{"name":"The PTA","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Hive-mind swarm of identical, over-informed suburban parents","flavor":"They vote as one, speak in overlapping half-sentences, and know your kid's grades before you do. Disagreement is not on the agenda.","desc":"They move through the school hallway as one overinformed crowd, dozens of identical, over-eager parent-faces murmuring the same concerned questions in unison. Cross one and the whole swarm turns at once, all speaking your name together.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hive-mind conformity-swarm archetype, original (mundane-turned-wrong social horror, no IP basis)"}],
 "cosmic":[{"name":"Static-Born Whelp","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"tiny drowned-language larva, forgets its own half-word","flavor":"A newborn scrap of the drowned language given a body — it chitters half a syllable of an unfinishable name and forgets the rest instantly.","desc":"It's smaller than your hand, wet and translucent, gill-slits opening and closing along a boneless throat. It works its mouth around a syllable — one, maybe two — and the sound underneath it is wrong before it even breaks off. Whatever it meant to say, it forgets before the last click of its jaw."},{"name":"Deep-Kin Netcaster","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"gilled fish-hybrid raider, classic deep-one coastal breed","flavor":"A fish-eyed coastal breed that traded air-breathing kin for something below the tide line generations back; drags nets full of things that aren't fish.","desc":"Wet skin catches the light in patches, scales starting at the collarbone and thickening toward the wrists. It hauls a dripping net over one shoulder, moving with the loose, confident gait of something that's never once needed air. The net has caught things in it that aren't fish."},{"name":"Echo-Faced Pilgrim","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"robed cultist, face slowly reshaping toward its god","flavor":"A cultist of the answering wonder, face rearranged toward whatever last spoke to it; still mostly a person, technically.","desc":"The robe is plain, homespun, the kind any pious traveler might wear. The face underneath it isn't finished settling — cheekbone drifting a half-inch, an eye migrating slow as a tide toward where an ear used to be. It's still mostly a person. Technically."},{"name":"Angle-Wrong Creeper","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"piercer","summary":"non-Euclidean ambush lurker, wrong from every angle","flavor":"Geometry that argues with itself — from one side a stalactite, from the other a limb; it never resolves, and neither does what it bites.","desc":"You see it clearest out of the corner of your eye, where the geometry hasn't caught up with itself yet — a spine that folds the wrong way, limbs that seem to originate from someplace behind where they should. It doesn't stalk so much as arrive, wrong from every direction at once."},{"name":"Star-Spat Larva","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"star-spawn hatchling, smothers before it thinks","flavor":"Fell out of the sky still warm from somewhere with no sky of its own; smothers first, digests the question of why later.","desc":"It drops from somewhere above — a ceiling, a gap in the sky, it's unclear which — and lands already smothering. No eyes to speak of, no real face, just a wet dark mass that presses itself flat and starts before you've finished flinching."},{"name":"Choir-Static Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"formless droning noise-wisp, hums the wrong language","flavor":"A sound with no source, given just enough shape to annoy you; it hums the drowned language slightly off-key, forever.","desc":"A patch of air that hums instead of moving, a drone pitched just under language. Get close and the hum resolves into syllables — not words, exactly, but the shape a word makes right before it becomes one. It never finishes."},{"name":"Shoggoth Spawnling","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"eye-budding protoplasmic mass, shoggoth in miniature","flavor":"A gray, roiling mass no bigger than a barrel, budding eyes and mouths it doesn't keep for long; the full-grown thing it's shed from is somewhere close, and larger.","desc":"A basin-sized heap of black jelly that hasn't decided what it looks like yet. Eyes bud along its surface at random, blink once, and reabsorb. It moves the way spilled ink moves — slow, purposeful, entirely without a front or back."},{"name":"Vault-Drift Serf","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"generational cult serf, still bows to the old angles","flavor":"Recruited off some drowned world's docks generations back; still bows at the old angles, still hears the old choir.","desc":"Third generation born to the vaults, maybe fourth — nobody up here keeps count anymore. It bows on schedule, at angles nobody taught it and everybody down there seems to know, the way children learn table manners before they can read."},{"name":"Gravel-Star Mite","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"small star-spawn splinter, petrifying gaze it can't explain","flavor":"A star-spawn splinter no bigger than a dog, all beak and impossible joint-count; petrifies with a look it doesn't understand having.","desc":"Barely bigger than a housecat, its hide flecked like a night sky pressed into stone. Its eyes have gone milky-white and fixed, and things that hold its gaze too long start to feel their joints stiffening — a gift the little thing seems as baffled by as anyone."},{"name":"Wrong-Angle Watcher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gibbering-mouther","model":"gibbering-mouther","summary":"babbling mouth-patch, ground disagrees with your feet","flavor":"A patch of geometry that mutters in every direction at once — approach it and the ground itself seems to disagree with your feet.","desc":"A patch of floor that shouldn't be a mouth is a mouth — dozens of small ones, murmuring over each other in a dialect that predates the room it's rotting in. Step near it and the ground itself seems to disagree with your footing, tilting fractions of an inch that shouldn't be possible."},{"name":"Star-Spawn Grazer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"phase-spider","summary":"half-phased star-spawn cattle, grazes on visible light","flavor":"Blinks half-in, half-out of the visible world, cropping light like grass; it was probably once something's livestock.","desc":"Somewhere between a beast and a photograph of one — its outline flickers half a step out of phase, present and then almost-present. It grazes on nothing you can name, jaw working at motes of light drifting loose in the air, cattle for something that isn't a farmer."},{"name":"Tentacled Horror of the Drowned Vault","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"carrion-crawler","model":"carrion-crawler","summary":"classic many-tentacled cellar-horror, paralyzing touch","flavor":"A many-limbed thing that hauls itself up from flooded sub-cellars on a forest of feeling tentacles, paralyzing whatever it touches before it decides what to do with it.","desc":"A cellar-thing dragged up out of somewhere that should've stayed sealed — segmented, glistening, tentacles working independently of each other around a centipede's worth of legs. Its touch doesn't hurt so much as it stops you, muscle by muscle, mid-motion."},{"name":"Length-Wrong Herald","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"clawed-drowner","model":"clawed-drowner","summary":"herald-thing that attacks mid-syllable of its own name","flavor":"Speaks the opening of its own name every time it attacks; nobody has heard it finish, and the theory is nobody's meant to.","desc":"It's built like something that used to be one clean shape and got extended — an extra joint here, a limb a foot too long there. It attacks mid-syllable, always mid-syllable, like whatever name it's reciting never gets the chance to land before the claws do."},{"name":"Basalt Geometer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"angle-enforcing construct, warps the room it guards","flavor":"Built by something to enforce angles that don't exist here; every room it stands in slowly stops making sense.","desc":"A construct of dark, seamless stone, faceless but for a single carved sigil where a face would go. The room around it doesn't sit right while it's active — corners a few degrees off true, distances that measure differently depending which wall you started from."},{"name":"Star-Drunk Colossus-Kin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"starlight-drunk giant, too big for this sky","flavor":"A giant that drank starlight instead of ale one bad night; too big for this sky, and it knows it, and it's furious about it.","desc":"It's too tall for the room, too tall for the sky outside the room, staggering with the loose, delighted lurch of something drunk on light it was never built to drink. Every few steps it looks straight up and laughs — a sound like a landslide finding something funny."},{"name":"Drowned-Tongue Cantor","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"cultist-mage, casts by singing a language that hurts","flavor":"Learned three words of the drowned language and it was two too many; casts by half-singing syllables that hurt to hear correctly.","desc":"Robed, hands folded, entirely still until it opens its mouth — and then the words come out in a register that isn't meant for a human throat, syllables that catch behind your sternum before you consciously hear them. It sings like it's rehearsed the pain in it for years."},{"name":"Devouring Mass of the Drift","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"black shifting shoggoth-mass, dissolves and remembers shapes","flavor":"A shoggoth proper, or near enough — a shifting black bulk crawling with makeshift eyes, dissolving whatever it rolls over and remembering the shape for later.","desc":"Black, shifting, easily the size of a wagon — and it remembers. Where it's dissolved things before, the surface briefly holds their shape: a hand, a face, a rack of ribs, rising and sinking back into the black like a held breath."},{"name":"Void-Touched Ascetic","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-zerth","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"void-monk cultist, trained never to look at its god","flavor":"Trained a martial discipline built entirely around not looking directly at the thing it worships; occasionally fails.","desc":"Its robes are plain, its posture perfectly still, its eyes wrapped in cloth it was trained never to remove. It moves through the room like it's memorized every step in advance — which, in a sense, it has. Looking at its god cost it the privilege of looking at anything else directly, ever again."},{"name":"Between-Star Marauder","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-knight","model":"astral-raider-knight","summary":"star-spawn knight-raider, rides the seams between stars","flavor":"Rides the seams between named stars, raiding worlds that made the mistake of being finishable sentences.","desc":"It rides a mount that isn't quite there, hooves — or whatever they are — finding purchase on air that shouldn't hold weight. Both rider and steed seem to flicker at the edges, more comfortable in the gap between one star and the next than in any room with walls."},{"name":"Choir of the Unbuilt Cathedral","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-chaos-frog","model":"gray-chaos-frog","summary":"compressed cult-congregation, attacks argue with each other","flavor":"A congregation compressed into one body, still arguing internally over doctrine; every attack is a different faction's opinion.","desc":"A crowd's worth of robed shapes compressed into something the size of one large man, faces layered and half-transparent through each other. When it attacks, its limbs argue — one lashing out while another recoils, like a congregation that never once agreed on the sermon."},{"name":"Cartographer of Wrong Angles","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"ancient elder-thing cartographer, maps that unravel minds","flavor":"Maps places that don't cohere and insists they're accurate; anyone who reads its charts starts seeing the seams in normal rooms too.","desc":"Ancient, starfish-crowned, its motion deliberate as a compass needle finding north. The maps rolled under one many-fingered limb aren't of anywhere — study them for more than a moment and the lines start rearranging behind your eyes, redrawing the room you're standing in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Unmapping", "text": "a creature that studies its maps too long must save or find the room they're in has physically changed — a new exit, a missing wall — narratively real, not an illusion"}]}},{"name":"Star-Spawn Bishop","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"brain-warping star-spawn cleric, sermons rearrange your mind","flavor":"Ordained by something that doesn't have a mouth to ordain with; its sermons rearrange the listener's sense of up.","desc":"It wears vestments a size too formal for the ruin it's presiding over, mitre crooked, hands raised in blessing over a congregation of one or none. Its sermon isn't spoken so much as felt — pressure behind the eyes, thoughts sliding into shapes they didn't start as."},{"name":"The Waking Eye Beneath","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"floating many-eyed orb horror, reads unwritten futures","flavor":"A many-eyed orb the size of a wagon, floating up from some flooded temple-shaft, each stalk-eye reading a different page of a book that hasn't been written yet.","desc":"It floats without visible effort, a great lidless orb trailing smaller stalked eyes like afterthoughts, each one tracking something different in the room — you, the door, something that hasn't happened yet. Looking back into any one of them costs you a memory of something that hasn't occurred.","traits":{"note": "one of its stalk-eyes always looks at something that hasn't happened yet", "actions": [{"name": "Foreknowing Gaze", "text": "a targeted stalk-eye can force a save or the victim loses their next reaction, having already 'remembered' dodging an attack that hasn't been made yet"}]}},{"name":"The Sound With No Source","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"elemental-cataclysm","model":"net-new: a vast half-formed silhouette woven from visible, rippling sound-waves","summary":"bodiless voice-horror, borrowed shape, something answers back","flavor":"It has never had a body; this one is borrowed, argued-over, and already trying to unbecome itself. When it speaks, the drowned language comes out clean, and something answers from very far away.","desc":"There's no shape to point at — only a voice, coming from everywhere in the room at once, borrowing whatever surface is closest to vibrate against. It answers questions nobody asked out loud. That's the part that never stops being wrong.","traits":{"note": "has no body to target; damage sources must be narratively plausible (sound-based, area, or ritual) or the DM should rule it unaffected", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Voice", "text": "speaks through the nearest solid surface, and anyone who answers it aloud is marked — the next sound they make carries unnaturally far, drawing anything listening"}]}},{"name":"The Wonder That Answers Back","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"net-new: a star-scaled orb-and-limb mass whose geometry disagrees with itself","summary":"the realm's Great-Old-One, a correct answer always costs you","flavor":"The realm's sleeping Great Old One — ask it a question and it answers, correctly, in a name too long to finish; the answer costs you something you didn't offer, every single time.","desc":"It fills the horizon before it fills the room — a presence too large for the doorway it somehow occupies anyway, dozens of eyes opening in sequence like a spreading stain. It listens to every question asked in its presence, and it always answers correctly. That's the part that costs you.","traits":{"hp": "apex-standard, but functionally unkillable in a single encounter per DM-CHARTER cosmic-horror scaling", "note": "answers any question posed to it truthfully — the DM should let the player ask, and make the true answer cost something", "actions": [{"name": "A Correct Answer", "text": "whoever receives its answer takes psychic strain proportional to how badly they needed to not know it — mechanically, a level of exhaustion or a lasting flaw, DM's call"}]}},{"name":"Tide-Slick Grub","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Tiny","frame":"lemure","model":"lemure","summary":"tiny drift-ooze droplet, twitches toward body heat","flavor":"A finger-length droplet of the drift-mass that never quite dries; it mostly just twitches toward warmth.","desc":"A fingertip-sized bead of translucent ooze, sliding wet trails across whatever surface holds heat. It twitches toward warmth the way a moth twitches toward flame — mindless, patient, and in no hurry at all."},{"name":"Drowned-Docks Netboy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"runt deep-kin fisher, hauls nets too heavy for it","flavor":"A child-sized deep-kin runt too small to fish alone; it still tries, hauling nets twice its weight up from the black water.","desc":"Small for a deep-kin, scales still soft, gill-slits barely developed. It hauls a net twice its own weight across the boards, grunting with each pull, too young yet to know the things it's dragging up aren't always fish."},{"name":"Salt-Choir Initiate","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"fresh cult recruit, flinches at its own chanting","flavor":"Newly sworn to the drowned congregation; still flinches at its own chanting.","desc":"New to the robes, new to the chanting — you can tell by the way it flinches at its own voice mid-hymn, like the sound coming out of its own throat still startles it. It hasn't learned yet not to listen to itself."},{"name":"Half-Seen Crawler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"blind-deep-stalker","model":"blind-deep-stalker","summary":"angle-dependent stalker, only visible from some angles","flavor":"Visible only from certain angles, like a smudge on a lens; the rest of the time it's simply already behind you.","desc":"From one angle it's barely a silhouette against the dark; from another it's gone entirely, present only as a faint disturbance in the air where it should be. It doesn't hide. The room simply refuses to render it consistently."},{"name":"Nursery-Vault Runt","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Tiny","frame":"flying-snake","model":"flying-snake","summary":"premature hatchling, flits weakly chirping half a word","flavor":"Hatched too early from a drowned egg-clutch, it flits weakly through flooded corridors chirping half a word.","desc":"Too young to fly properly, it flits in short, panicked bursts, chirping half a syllable of something that might have been a name if it had lived long enough to finish learning it."},{"name":"Deep-Kin Harpooner","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-whip","model":"fish-folk-whip","summary":"veteran gilled harpooner, drags catch down regardless","flavor":"A veteran of the coastal breed, favoring a barbed line over a net; drags catch back down whether it's still moving or not.","desc":"Weathered, scarred along both forearms, its harpoon already slick from use. It hauls whatever it's caught down without hesitation, without checking first whether the catch has stopped moving — down is down, and down is where it belongs."},{"name":"Cyst of Small Eyes","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Small","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"palm-sized eye-cluster ooze bud, eyes never blink together","flavor":"A fist-sized knot of shoggoth-stuff that budded off wrong; it's mostly eyes, and none of them blink together.","desc":"A palm-sized swelling of grey ooze studded with a dozen tiny eyes, none of them blinking in time with each other. Some track you. Some track the ceiling. None of them agree on what they're looking at."},{"name":"Static-Fed Familiar","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"cult-kept static wisp, fattens on half-heard words","flavor":"Kept as a pet by a cantor who feeds it half-heard words; it grows fat on syllables and thin on silence.","desc":"A patch of drifting smoke kept on a leash of ritual more than rope, fattening visibly on scraps of overheard prayer. It hums along under its breath — if it has breath — mimicking half-words it's picked up from its keepers."},{"name":"Barnacle-Grown Thrall","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"barnacle-crusted cult thrall, still kneels on schedule","flavor":"So long submerged in service that crustacean growth has fused to its joints; it still kneels on schedule.","desc":"Crusted shoulder to knee in barnacles that have had years to grow, it kneels on schedule regardless of who's watching — a habit worn so deep it's outlasted whatever choice originally put it there."},{"name":"Wharf-Rot Feeler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"pier-dwelling smother-thing, drops on warm footsteps","flavor":"Clings under piers where the water goes the wrong color; drops when something warm walks overhead.","desc":"It hangs from the underside of the pier, patient as rot, until footsteps overhead go warm enough to register. Then it drops — fast, wet, and entirely without warning."},{"name":"Star-Chipped Hatchling","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"tiny star-fallen splinter, still searching for its parent","flavor":"A splinter no bigger than a housecat, all needle-mouth, that fell alongside something much worse and hasn't found it yet.","desc":"A splinter of something larger, small enough to mistake for local wildlife, chirping and circling as if searching the room for a parent that fell from somewhere much higher up and isn't coming."},{"name":"Wrong-Count Mimicker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"piercer","summary":"shape-mimic with a miscounted number of features","flavor":"Copies the shape of ordinary things nearby, but always gets the number of legs, teeth, or windows slightly off.","desc":"It's copied a shape from somewhere nearby — a person, an object, a piece of the room — but miscounted. One too many fingers. An extra fold in the coat that shouldn't be there. Close enough to pass, wrong enough to notice if you look."},{"name":"Choking Reef Polyp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Small","frame":"violet-fungus","model":"violet-fungus","summary":"altar-bound polyp growth, lashes at loitering worshippers","flavor":"Grows on drowned altars like coral, lashing anything that lingers too near the offering bowl.","desc":"Rooted to the altar it grows from, a wet mass of coral-pale flesh that lashes at anything lingering too close — worshipper or intruder, it makes no distinction. It doesn't need to eat you. It just needs you to stop standing there."},{"name":"Bell-Tongued Herald-Runt","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"brain-crawler","model":"brain-crawler","summary":"bell-ringing messenger aberration, tolls unwanted summons","flavor":"A messenger-thing that rings when it moves, each toll a fragment of a summons nobody asked for.","desc":"Small, winged, dragging a cracked brass bell it rings whether or not anyone wants the summons. Each toll carries a fragment of a larger call — one it's too young and too small to ever finish delivering."},{"name":"Kelp-Draped Netcaster","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-monitor","model":"fish-folk-monitor","summary":"senior deep-kin overseer, commands netcasters silently","flavor":"Senior among the coastal breed, trailing kelp like a cloak; commands the smaller netcasters without a word.","desc":"Older than the others it commands, kelp strung through gill-slits like decoration or camouflage, it directs its underlings with small silent gestures instead of words — a discipline the younger ones haven't earned yet."},{"name":"Choir-Bound Flagellant","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"death-cultist","summary":"self-flagellating cultist, tunes itself to unheard rhythm","flavor":"Whips itself in time with a rhythm only it can hear, certain the pain is a kind of tuning.","desc":"It strikes its own back in a rhythm that has nothing to do with pain and everything to do with keeping time, tuning itself like an instrument to a beat only it can hear."},{"name":"Star-Spat Grazer-Calf","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"griffon","model":"griffon","summary":"juvenile star-spawn beast, crops light-motes from the air","flavor":"A juvenile star-spawn beast, still mostly solid, cropping light-motes out of the air with a beak too wide for its skull.","desc":"Feathered and half-formed, still young enough to be clumsy on its legs, it crops at drifting motes of light in the air with the unhurried appetite of livestock that's never once been hunted."},{"name":"Drift-Snarled Netling","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"ochre-jelly","model":"ochre-jelly","summary":"net-tangled ooze, drags its own net as a lure","flavor":"Ooze tangled with actual fishing net dragged up from the deep; it hunts by dragging the net behind it like a lure.","desc":"A mass of ochre jelly that's absorbed a fisherman's net and never let it go, dragging the tangled mess behind itself as bait — anything that gets its foot caught finds the ooze is already reaching."},{"name":"Fathom-Whisper Cultist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-roster-base-2024-stat-blocks","model":"cultist-roster-base-2024-stat-blocks","summary":"fountain-side cultist, repeats fragments it hears in water","flavor":"Hears the drowned language in running water and repeats fragments of it to anyone standing near a fountain.","desc":"It kneels by any standing water it can find, murmuring back half-heard fragments of something the water told it, word for word, in a voice not quite its own."},{"name":"Rib-Cracked Thrall-Sergeant","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"repeatedly-broken cult enforcer, fights past its own pain","flavor":"Broken and reset so many times in service that its posture is permanently wrong; it fights like the pain already happened.","desc":"Bones visibly reset more than once, some healed crooked, it fights through damage that would drop most soldiers twice over — pain long since reclassified as background noise."},{"name":"Gravel-Star Broodmite Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-stirges","model":"swarm-of-stirges","summary":"clutch of tiny star-spawn splinters, moves as one mass","flavor":"A clutch of star-spawn splinters hatched together, moving as one twitching, beaking mass.","desc":"A tumbling clutch of star-flecked mites moving as a single mass, more current than creature, flowing around obstacles the way water finds the low ground."},{"name":"Basalt Chanter-Construct","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"empty armor construct, hums drowned language on patrol","flavor":"An empty suit of vault-armor that hums the drowned language through its helm slit, walking patrol for masters long dissolved.","desc":"An empty suit of ancient armor patrolling on a schedule nobody living set, humming the drowned language under a helm with no face inside it — no breath, but the sound comes anyway."},{"name":"Slack-Jawed Deep-Kin Brute","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"deep-brute","model":"deep-brute","summary":"heavyset deep-kin muscle, jaw unhinges when excited","flavor":"Muscle bred for hauling nets the size of houses; its jaw unhinges when it's excited, which is often.","desc":"Built heavier than the others, its jaw unhinges wide when it gets excited, exposing rows of teeth meant for prey twice its own size. It gets excited easily."},{"name":"Two-Faced Pilgrim","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"double-faced cultist, argues with itself about which face is real","flavor":"A pilgrim whose reshaping went further than most — it now wears two faces at once, arguing about which one is real.","desc":"Two faces share one head, arguing under their breath about which of them is the original — a dispute that flares louder whenever it thinks no one's listening."},{"name":"Void-Touched Novice","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-monk","model":"void-monk-monk","summary":"beginner void-monk, eyes already filming over","flavor":"Just beginning the discipline of not-looking; its eyes are already starting to film over from the strain.","desc":"New to the discipline, its eyes have only just begun to film over with a pale, unseeing sheen — the first visible sign of a training that ends somewhere neither of you wants to imagine."},{"name":"Length-Wrong Runt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"minor herald-cousin, half-syllable attacks and endless breath","flavor":"A smaller cousin of the heralds, its half-syllable attacks are weaker, but it never seems to run out of breath.","desc":"A smaller cousin of something with a much longer name, it lashes out mid-syllable of an attack it can only half articulate, breath running longer than its body should physically allow."},{"name":"Foam-Bled Zealot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"aberrant-cultist","model":"aberrant-cultist","summary":"foaming zealot, recites an unfinishable hymn as devotion","flavor":"Foams at the mouth reciting the opening verse of a hymn with no known end; convinced finishing it would be a mercy.","desc":"Foam gathers at the corners of its mouth as it recites a hymn with no ending, verse looping back into itself the way a devotion sometimes becomes indistinguishable from a wound."},{"name":"Coil-Fused Netwife","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"eel-legged deep-kin matriarch, endlessly weaves new nets","flavor":"A deep-kin matriarch whose lower half has fused into something more eel than leg; she never stops weaving new nets.","desc":"Legs long since replaced by a muscular eel's coil, she weaves new nets constantly, fingers never quite still, knotting cord even when there's nothing yet to catch."},{"name":"Undertow Grapple-Thing","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"stairwell tentacle-ambusher, hauls victims into flooded dark","flavor":"Waits in the flooded dark of vault stairwells, a barbed tentacle-mass that hauls the careless down before they can shout.","desc":"It waits in flooded stairwells where the water shouldn't be that deep, tentacles breaking the surface only once something warm-blooded steps close enough to grab."},{"name":"Reef-Bone Sentinel","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"coral-grown drowned skeleton, bones spell hymn fragments","flavor":"Drowned centuries ago, its bones now grown through with coral in patterns that spell fragments of the old choir.","desc":"Coral has grown through the gaps in its ribs over the years it's stood post, and if you look closely the calcified growths along its bones trace out fragments of the same hymn, over and over."},{"name":"Choir-Static Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"flocking noise-wisp swarm, drone loud enough to hurt teeth","flavor":"Dozens of noise-wisps flocking together, their combined drone loud enough to make teeth ache.","desc":"A flock-sized mass of droning wisps moving together, their combined hum loud enough to ache behind the teeth from twenty feet off."},{"name":"Wrongly-Jointed Fisherman","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"ettercap","model":"ettercap","summary":"extra-jointed ex-fisherman, casts lines with unnatural reach","flavor":"Once a fisherman, its elbows and knees now bend an extra way; it casts a line with unsettling, extra reach.","desc":"Extra joints have grown into limbs that used to end normally, letting it cast a line — or a grasping hand — much farther than its reach should allow."},{"name":"Depth-Warped Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"bugbear-stalker","summary":"joint-warped cult enforcer, hits harder than it should","flavor":"Cult muscle whose limbs have started growing extra joints from prolonged proximity to the choir; it hits harder than its size suggests it should.","desc":"Something below has reshaped its joints to bend wrong-way, and it hits with more force than a frame that size has any right to generate."},{"name":"Herald of the First Syllable","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"floating tendriled brain-thing, forever mid-utterance","flavor":"A floating brain-mass trailing paralytic tendrils, forever mid-utterance of a name it will never complete.","desc":"It floats on a knot of writhing tendrils, mouth working endlessly around the beginning of a word it has never once finished — and never will, not in front of you."},{"name":"Vault-Warden Ooze","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"geometric ooze sentry, absorbs anyone lacking the passphrase","flavor":"A perfectly geometric mass that patrols flooded vault corridors, absorbing anything that doesn't know the passphrase.","desc":"A perfect, glassy cube of ooze sized to fill its corridor exactly, patient as a lock. Anyone crossing without the passphrase simply doesn't come back out the other side."},{"name":"Basalt Geometer-Scout","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"scout construct, surveys rooms ahead of angle-warping work","flavor":"A lighter cousin of the geometer-constructs, sent ahead to survey rooms before the angle-work begins.","desc":"Smaller and faster than its master-shape, it moves ahead through rooms before the angle-warping work begins, surveying corners with a stillness that has nothing curious in it."},{"name":"Deep-Kin War Priest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"fish-folk-archpriest","summary":"gilled war-priest, blesses spears with wrongly-moving water","flavor":"Leads coastal-breed raids with hymnals bound in dried skin no one asks about; blesses spears with water that shouldn't move like that.","desc":"It blesses its congregation's spears by dipping them in water that moves against the current, murmuring approval each time the water disobeys gravity the way it's supposed to."},{"name":"Amalgam of Borrowed Limbs","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-howdah","model":"ogre-howdah","summary":"tide-stitched limb-amalgam, mismatched parts unnoticed by it","flavor":"Stitched together from whatever the tide brought — none of the limbs match, and it hasn't noticed yet.","desc":"Stitched together from parts that never belonged to the same body, none of them matching in color, texture, or apparent age — and it moves them all without the faintest awareness anything's mismatched."},{"name":"Star-Spawn Broodcaller","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-warrior","model":"astral-raider-warrior","summary":"star-spawn summoner, calls splinters to its side","flavor":"Sings a summoning fragment that draws smaller splinters from wherever they've been hiding; never fights alone if it can help it.","desc":"It raises both arms and calls, a sound pitched too high to be entirely vocal, and small star-flecked shapes come skittering toward it from wherever they'd been hiding."},{"name":"Choir-Grown Ooze Sculptor","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"self-sculpting ooze mimic, dissolves interrupting witnesses","flavor":"Reshapes itself into crude mimicries of drowned architecture, humming while it works, dissolving anyone who interrupts.","desc":"It reshapes its own surface into passable mimicry of whatever's nearby — furniture, a person, a doorway — right up until it dissolves whoever noticed the resemblance too late."},{"name":"Vault-Drift Overseer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough-boss","model":"tough-boss","summary":"veteran cult overseer, whip woven from something not-quite-rope","flavor":"Generations deep in cult service, cracking a whip woven from something that used to be rope and now isn't quite.","desc":"A whip made from something that isn't quite rope trails from one hand, coiling with a faint wet sheen even when it's not being used. It's worn its authority in the vaults longer than most of its thralls have been alive."},{"name":"Reef-Choked Behemoth-Calf","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-crocodile","model":"giant-crocodile","summary":"coral-armored guard-beast, bred to protect flooded vaults","flavor":"A drowned-world beast bred to guard the choir's flooded vaults, coral growing through its hide like armor.","desc":"Coral has grown thick over its hide in armored plates, bred generation over generation for exactly one purpose — standing between the vault door and whatever's trying to reach it."},{"name":"Nine-Eyed Cyst","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"nine-eyed stalk-growth, each eye sees a different version of the room","flavor":"A budding growth of eyes on a fleshy stalk, each seeing a slightly different version of the same room.","desc":"A stalk-like growth studded with nine eyes, each one apparently seeing a slightly different version of the same room — and disagreeing, silently and constantly, about which version is real."},{"name":"Choir-Marked Berserker","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"arena fighter, scars spell hymn fragments across its back","flavor":"Fights in an arena the cult built beneath the tide line, scars spelling out fragments of hymn across its back.","desc":"Scars crisscross its back in patterns too regular to be accidental — read close, they spell out fragments of the hymn, carved in one bad night at a time."},{"name":"Devouring Choir-Cyst","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"shrine-fed cyst, grows a new mouth per swallowed prayer","flavor":"Feeds on offerings left at flooded shrines, growing new mouths for every prayer it swallows.","desc":"Fed on the shrine's leftovers for years, it's grown a fresh mouth for every prayer it's swallowed — a dozen now, none matching, all of them hungry at once."},{"name":"Star-Chewed Roc-Kin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-axe-beak","model":"giant-axe-beak","summary":"drift-touched sky-beast, shadow lags behind its own flight","flavor":"A sky-beast whose migratory path drifted through somewhere it shouldn't have; it still flies, but its shadow lags a half-second behind.","desc":"A vast bird-shape that doesn't fly so much as arrive, its shadow crawling into place a full second after the body that's supposed to cast it."},{"name":"Wrong-Season Roper","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"roper","model":"roper","summary":"drift-grown ropy ambusher, strands taste of a closed mouth","flavor":"Grows in caverns where the drift touched the stone; its strands taste like the inside of a closed mouth.","desc":"Grown wrong out of the drift-touched stone, its ropy strands hang loose until they don't — the surviving taste memory is of something that tried to close its mouth and never got to finish."},{"name":"Reef-Fused War Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"drift-touched water elemental, moves with unnerving intent","flavor":"Water given form by the same wrongness that grows coral over drowned bones; it moves like tide, but with intent.","desc":"Water moves through it with clear, unnerving intent, currents folding into fists and then unfolding again, never quite settling into a shape that stays still long enough to be sure of."},{"name":"Coral-Throned Cult Matron","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"performer-maestro","summary":"reef-throned choir conductor, directs worshippers like an orchestra","flavor":"Conducts the drowned hymn from a throne grown out of living reef, directing worshippers like an orchestra of dread.","desc":"She sits enthroned in living coral, directing her congregation with slow, precise motions — like a conductor, if the orchestra were made of people and the music were a hymn none of them chose to learn."},{"name":"Star-Warped Chimera-Thing","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"triple-fused star-warped beast, heads disagree about its nature","flavor":"Three creatures fused by the same accident that dropped its kin from the sky, each head disagreeing about what it is.","desc":"Three heads fused onto one body, each pulling faintly in a different direction, each apparently convinced the other two belong to something else entirely."},{"name":"Choir-Bound Invisible Watcher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"bound invisible hunter, tracks lapsed believers","flavor":"Bound to the choir by a pact it can't remember making, hunting silently for anyone who stops believing on schedule.","desc":"You never see it arrive. You feel the air change first, a pressure like being watched from somewhere just behind your shoulder, tracking whoever's fallen behind on their devotions."},{"name":"Bone-Grown Cathedral Skeleton","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-skeleton","model":"minotaur-skeleton","summary":"architecture-fused drowned guardian skeleton","flavor":"A drowned guardian whose bones have fused with the architecture it once protected; moving it means moving the wall.","desc":"Architecture has fused into its bones over however long it's stood — a fragment of column here, a piece of drowned stonework there — until it's less a skeleton wearing armor than a building that learned to walk."},{"name":"Void-Trained Duelist","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief","model":"mind-thief","summary":"advanced void-monk duelist, fights blind and never misses","flavor":"Advanced past the ascetics in the not-looking discipline; it fights with eyes fully closed and somehow never misses.","desc":"Its eyes are wrapped, same as its lesser brethren, but its blade never seems to miss regardless — trained past sight into something that reads intention instead."},{"name":"Warlord of the Sunken Court","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-giant","model":"stone-giant","summary":"coral-grown giant warlord, sworn to the drowned choir","flavor":"A giant sworn to the drowned choir generations back, its stonework now grown through with the same wrong coral as the vaults it guards.","desc":"Coral has grown into the seams of its armor the way barnacles grow on a hull left too long at anchor. It swore itself to the choir generations ago and has never once been asked to explain why."},{"name":"Cyst-Blossomed Behemoth","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"regenerating many-headed horror, sprouts eyes where heads regrow","flavor":"Each severed head buds a fresh eye before it regrows, until the thing sees in more directions than it can process.","desc":"Wherever a head is severed, a fresh eye blinks open in the wound before the new head finishes growing back — an unsettling little preview of what's coming."},{"name":"Grand Cantor of the Drowned Court","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"archpriest","summary":"tri-voiced high priest, speaks as three generations at once","flavor":"Speaks in a chord of three voices at once, each a different generation of the same office; the congregation answers all three.","desc":"When it speaks, three distinct voices layer under each other — young, old, and something in between — as if three generations of the same office are speaking through one throat at once.","traits":{"note": "can address up to three different targets simultaneously with its three voices, each carrying a separate effect (command, ward, curse) in a single action"}},{"name":"Fathom-Deep Devourer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"cockatrice-regent","model":"cockatrice-regent","summary":"ancient depth-lurker, gaze convinces victims stillness was the plan","flavor":"Older than the vault it lairs in, its gaze doesn't petrify so much as convince the victim that stillness was always the plan.","desc":"Ancient, patient, its gaze alone convinces prey that stillness was always the plan — muscles locking mid-stride, breath slowing, right up until it's far too late to reconsider.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Stillness Was the Plan", "text": "a target that fails a save against its gaze believes it chose to stop moving; it isn't restrained and can act normally in every way except moving from its space, until it takes damage"}]}},{"name":"Star-Warped Amalgam Lord","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"heavily-reshaped cult champion, original species long forgotten","flavor":"A cult champion so thoroughly reshaped that its original species is a debated footnote among its own worshippers.","desc":"Whatever species it started as is long gone under layers of reshaping — scales here, chitin there, something that might once have been fur — until only the confident bearing of a champion survives intact."},{"name":"Vault-Keeper of the Drowned Seal","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"door-guardian golem, scarred by every prior attempt to pass","flavor":"Built to guard a door that shouldn't open; every scar in its clay hide is a place someone already tried.","desc":"Every failed attempt to force this door has left a scar across its clay hide, a record of every trespasser it's ever stopped, worn like a tally it's proud of."},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Herald-Prime","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"elder herald-beast, recites fragments younger heralds can't finish","flavor":"An elder herald whose throat has stretched to accommodate names centuries in the reciting; it finishes fragments the young ones can't.","desc":"Ancient among heralds, it recites the fragments the younger ones can't yet finish — long, resonant passages that seem to physically hurt something in its throat to produce."},{"name":"Rakshasa of the Drowned Bargain","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"deal-making fiend, wears any face to get terms accepted","flavor":"Made a private deal with the choir long before the cult existed; it wears whatever face gets the terms accepted.","desc":"It wears whatever face gets its terms accepted, switching mid-sentence if the current one isn't landing — courteous, patient, and utterly without a true face underneath any of them.","traits":{"note": "any bargain it strikes is binding on its side but written with a loophole the party won't notice until it matters — DM should have the exact loophole ready before the deal is offered"}},{"name":"Colossal Sunken Guardian","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"titanic coral-fused golem, footsteps sound like a receding tide","flavor":"A titan of drowned stone, moss and coral fused so deep into its joints that its footsteps sound like a tide going out.","desc":"Titanic, coral-fused, its footsteps land with a low boom that sounds less like stone hitting stone and more like a tide receding somewhere far below."},{"name":"Void-Ascendant Grandmaster","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-psion","model":"void-monk-psion","summary":"perfected void-monk master, has forgotten its own god's face","flavor":"Perfected the discipline of not-looking so completely it has forgotten what its god even looks like — which may be the point.","desc":"Perfected past the point where doctrine matters, it moves with total, silent confidence — and has, by its own account, forgotten what its god's face even looked like to begin with."},{"name":"Herald-Devourer of the Bishop's Court","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"doctrine-advisor and quiet devourer of the faithless","flavor":"Advises the bishops on doctrine while quietly consuming the ones whose faith wavers, calling it a mercy.","desc":"It counsels with a warm, reasonable voice, offering doctrine and correction in equal measure — and quietly consumes whoever it decides has stopped believing hard enough."},{"name":"Sunk-Court Executioner","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"ultroloth","model":"ultroloth","summary":"internal cult enforcer, victims erased even from memory","flavor":"Handles the choir's internal discipline; those it visits are never spoken of by name again, only by the shape of their absence.","desc":"It doesn't kill loudly. Whoever it's sent for simply stops being remembered by the people who knew them — the body is almost an afterthought.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Erase From Memory", "text": "on a kill, NPCs who knew the victim gradually forget them over the following day unless something anchors the memory (a written record, an item, another PC's insistence) — narrative effect, DM adjudicates what breaks it"}]}},{"name":"Amalgam Colossus of the Reef Deep","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"warship-sized fused colossus, hull studded with reef and eyes","flavor":"A worm the size of a warship, its segments studded with fused reef, eyes, and the odd intact ship's figurehead.","desc":"Bigger than a warship, its fused hull studded with centuries of reef growth and half-buried eyes that all seem to open at once when it finally decides to move."},{"name":"Herald-Legion, Unified Voice","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"nalfeshnee","model":"nalfeshnee","summary":"fused mass of failed heralds, one throat that might finish","flavor":"Every herald that ever failed to finish its name, fused into one throat that finally might; the cult prays it never gets the chance.","desc":"A mass of failed heralds fused into one towering body, throats layered atop each other, close — so close — to finally finishing the syllable none of them managed alone.","traits":{"note": "if it ever completes the syllable (DM's call, a climax beat), the effect should be catastrophic and setting-relevant — this is a story trigger, not a routine attack"}},{"name":"The Unfinished Cathedral-Made-Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a cathedral's worth of drowned masonry animated into a lurching shape","summary":"animated drowned-cathedral golem, walks toward the sea","flavor":"The congregation finally built their temple, and the temple got up. It walks toward the sea on legs made of pews, ringing bells no one installed.","desc":"Stone and stained glass hold roughly cathedral-shaped as it walks, slow and deliberate, toward the sea — an unfinished building that decided to finish the pilgrimage itself."},{"name":"Star-Spawn Grand Marshal","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"star-spawn war-commander, armor of starlight that's gone dark","flavor":"Commands the between-star raiders in the flesh, its armor grown from crystallized starlight that's forgotten how to shine.","desc":"Its armor was forged from starlight once; now it's gone dark, dull as ash, and it commands its splintered troops with the same cold authority regardless."},{"name":"The Drift That Remembers Shapes","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Ooze","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"blob-of-annihilation","model":"blob-of-annihilation","summary":"the source shoggoth-mass, recalls and re-wears dissolved shapes","flavor":"Every shoggoth-mass in the realm is one flake of this; it recalls every shape it's ever dissolved, and occasionally wears one back.","desc":"The original mass all the smaller ones split from, and it recalls every shape it's ever dissolved — briefly wearing them, one after another, like trying on old coats before shrugging them off.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wear a Shape", "text": "can briefly assume the exact appearance and one notable ability of anything it has ever dissolved — a past victim, a monster, an ally — for a single turn"}]}},{"name":"Last Cantor of the Ending Hymn","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"undying cantor, rehearsing a final verse for four centuries","flavor":"Traded its death for the chance to sing the drowned language's final verse; it has been rehearsing for four hundred years and is almost, almost ready.","desc":"Four centuries and it still hasn't landed the final verse. It rehearses alone, undying, patient past any human measure of patience, waiting for the note that finally resolves.","traits":{"note": "functionally a lich (undying, phylactery-bound) reflavored as a devotional obsession rather than a hoarder of power"}},{"name":"The Angle That Ate a City","cr":20,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"tarrasque","model":"net-new: a fractally-wrong geometric mass the size of a district, still folded","summary":"district-sized geometric horror, was once a place, now a mouth","flavor":"It used to be somewhere. Now it's something, crawling slow and patient toward the next somewhere on legs that are technically also rooftops.","desc":"It used to be a place — streets, buildings, people who lived there — and now it's a single vast geometric wrongness that consumes distance the way a mouth consumes food.","traits":{"hp": "apex-standard, tarrasque-scale", "actions": [{"name": "Consume Distance", "text": "can fold significant terrain into itself as a legendary-scale action, effectively closing the gap to any target within line of sight regardless of actual range"}]}},{"name":"Deep One","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"batrachian shore-dweller, croaks a half-formed hymn","flavor":"A shore-town's shame given gills — it wades in half-formed, croaking a hymn it hasn't earned the throat for yet.","desc":"Batrachian, wet-skinned, standing with the faint stoop of something more at home underwater. It croaks half a hymn under its breath, unconcerned whether anyone's listening — least of all you.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Deep One Whip","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-whip","model":"fish-folk-whip","summary":"tide-driving enforcer of the Innsmouth shoal","flavor":"Older, wetter, meaner — it keeps the school in line with a lashing tail and a stare that promises the tide is coming for you specifically.","desc":"Broader-shouldered than the rank and file, it carries a coiled lash it uses more for driving its own kind than for fighting outsiders — the shoal answers to it without being asked twice.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Deep One Archpriest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"fish-folk-archpriest","summary":"reef-cult elder, half-remembers being human","flavor":"It leads the chant at the reef-altar and remembers being a person before the change finished; that memory is the only mercy it has left.","desc":"Ancient among its kind, its features have drifted so far from human that only the eyes still carry something recognizable — a flicker, old and tired, of what it half-remembers being.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Byakhee","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"void-crossing carrion flock, wrong at every joint","flavor":"A crow-shape wrong at every joint, it beats black wings through no air at all and only lands to feed.","desc":"It flies in total silence between one gap in the sky and the next, wings and limbs bent at angles that don't belong to any bird, carrion instincts wrapped around something that isn't.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"shared literary PD mythos convention (Chambers/Lovecraft-circle void-fauna)"},{"name":"Shoggoth","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"gray-chaos-frog","model":"gray-chaos-frog","summary":"protoplasmic slave-thing, grows eyes on demand","flavor":"A slave that unmade its makers and kept the trick — a boiling black mass that grows whatever eye or mouth the moment calls for.","desc":"Vast, black, endlessly reshaping itself, it grows a fresh crop of eyes across its surface the instant it needs to see something — then reabsorbs them the moment it doesn't.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Elder Thing","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"starfish-headed elder scientist-builder","flavor":"Barrel-bodied and starfish-headed, it built cities on this world before anything we'd call life existed, and it still keeps better records than we do.","desc":"A barrel-shaped body crowned in a starfish head, moving with the unhurried authority of something that built cities before anything you'd call human existed to notice.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Elder Deep-Thing","cr":10,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"ancient elder thing, patience curdled to menace","flavor":"An elder thing gone ancient and terrible, its city-building patience curdled into something that studies you the way it once studied continents.","desc":"Ancient past any Elder Thing you've met before, its patience has long since curdled into something closer to contempt — it still moves like a scientist, but it stopped being curious a long, long time ago.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Dagon","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"the Deep Ones' unspeakable patriarch","flavor":"The father-shape the Deep Ones sing to, glimpsed once by a starving sailor and never fully described since — because no one who saw it whole stayed sane enough to try.","desc":"The tide itself seems to rise a little wherever it surfaces, a patriarch's silhouette too vast to take in whole, water sheeting off scales the size of shields.","traits":{"note": "any Deep One or Deep-Kin creature within sight of Dagon fights with reckless devotion — treat as under a permanent, un-removable morale buff while it's present"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, Dagon (1919, PD)"},{"name":"Nightgaunt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spined-devil","model":"spined-devil","summary":"faceless black tickler that carries victims off","flavor":"Black, rubbery, and faceless, it tickles you into helplessness before it carries you off — the single most polite abduction in any bestiary.","desc":"Faceless, rubber-black, it moves in total silence on leathery wings — and it doesn't kill so much as it tickles, hoisting whoever it's caught off into the dark, laughing without a mouth to laugh with.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath (1943, PD)"},{"name":"Hound of Tindalos","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"angle-stalking hunter that seeps through corners","flavor":"It doesn't come through space, it comes through angles — anywhere a corner exists, it's already halfway in.","desc":"It comes through corners — actual geometric corners, the sharper the better — seeping out of the angle itself rather than through it. Once it's caught your scent across time, distance stops mattering; only angles do.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Frank Belknap Long, The Hound of Tindalos (1929, PD)"},{"name":"The Colour","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-weird","model":"net-new: a shifting stain of unnameable light with no fixed silhouette","summary":"unnameable light that spreads and consumes","flavor":"Not a monster so much as a stain that thinks — a light with no name in any spectrum, patiently turning a farm, then a family, then a county into itself.","desc":"There's no shape here, only a light that shouldn't exist in any spectrum you know, spreading slowly across whatever surface it's touched and leaching the color out of everything nearby.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Colour Out of Space (1927, PD)"},{"name":"Yog-Sothoth's Herald","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"half-born twin thing straining at the seams of the world","flavor":"A half-born twin thing straining against the edges of the world it was dragged into — the Gate and the Key both wearing a body that can barely hold it.","desc":"Half-born, straining visibly at some seam in the air behind it, as if the rest of it is still arriving from somewhere the room can't quite contain.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dunwich Horror (1929, PD)"},{"name":"Nyarlathotep, the Crawling Chaos","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"the outer gods' smiling ambassador and saboteur","flavor":"The only one of Them that bothers to wear a human face and give speeches — which somehow makes it worse, not better.","desc":"He arrives smiling, impeccably turned out, offering something reasonable-sounding in a warm and familiar voice — and everything that follows unravels a little more than it should.","traits":{"note": "a schemer, not a brawler — he should rarely if ever fight directly; his threat is what he sets in motion before he leaves the room", "actions": [{"name": "A Thousand Masks", "text": "can appear as any single NPC the party has already met, complete with their voice and mannerisms, to plant one piece of false counsel before revealing (or not revealing) himself"}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, Nyarlathotep (1920, PD)"},{"name":"Cthulhu","cr":25,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"sunken god-thing, dreaming ruin under the waves","flavor":"Dead but dreaming under the drowned city that bears his name, he doesn't need to move to end you — the dreams alone have driven men to the asylum and the harbor.","desc":"It sleeps, mostly, somewhere too deep for light — and even asleep, its dreaming presses against the edges of everyone nearby, a slow ruin nobody up here has agreed to have caused yet.","traits":{"note": "per DM-CHARTER, this is a world-ending presence — it should almost never be fought directly; its role is pressure, prophecy, and the thing the whole realm quietly organizes around avoiding"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Call of Cthulhu (1928, PD)"},{"name":"The King in Yellow","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"the tattered monarch of a play that unmakes readers","flavor":"He never has to lift a hand — reading the second act is enough. The tatters of his court simply keep multiplying once you've looked.","desc":"Robed in tatters that shouldn't hang the way they hang, its crown a jagged shard rather than gold, it speaks in a low, courteous voice about a play it insists you've already read.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "The Play You've Already Read", "text": "a target who engages it in conversation must save or become convinced they've seen 'the play' before — granting the King insight into their deepest regret, which he'll use conversationally, not mechanically"}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Robert W. Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD)"},{"name":"Servant of the King in Yellow (Tatterling)","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"pale-masked cultist unmade by the forbidden play","flavor":"Once someone who finished the play. Now a rag-shape in a pale mask, mouthing lines it can no longer stop repeating.","desc":"Pale mask fixed, posture wrong in a way that's hard to place until you notice the rest of its clothes have gone the same tattered yellow as its master's.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD) — the Pallid Mask/court motif"},{"name":"Cassilda's Mourner","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"net-new: a black-veiled wailing figure trailing tattered star-cloth","summary":"Carcosan wanderer weeping in a dead tongue","flavor":"It weeps in a language that predates grief, wandering the black stars of Carcosa looking for a lake that isn't in this world anymore.","desc":"She wanders in a slow, endless circuit, weeping in a language that has no living speakers left to translate it, mourning something the room itself seems to remember better than she does.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD) — Carcosa/Hyades imagery"},{"name":"Mi-Go","cr":3,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-warrior","model":"net-new: fungoid crustacean-winged trans-void miner","summary":"fungoid trans-void miner, files brains for transport","flavor":"Fungoid, winged, and disturbingly businesslike, it doesn't want to kill you so much as file you — in a can, for shipping.","desc":"Fungoid, crustacean-legged, wings buzzing at a pitch just under hearing — it works with clinical efficiency, filing away whatever it's collected for transport somewhere the sky doesn't end.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Whisperer in Darkness (1931, PD)"},{"name":"Brain in a Cylinder","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"extracted brain, still cheerfully lecturing on the cosmos","flavor":"A voice from a metal can bolted to a speaker-horn, still insisting it volunteered for this and would love to tell you all about the stars.","desc":"A brain suspended in fluid inside a battered metal cylinder, electrodes humming faintly — and it lectures, cheerfully, endlessly, about the cosmos, entirely unbothered by its own condition.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Whisperer in Darkness (1931, PD)"},{"name":"Ghast of the Underworld","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"net-new: kangaroo-legged corpse-pale barking hunter","summary":"kangaroo-legged corpse-thing that barks in the deep dark","flavor":"Kangaroo-legged and corpse-pale, it barks like a starved dog in the dark beneath the waking world and hunts in loping, delighted packs.","desc":"It moves in low, loping bounds on legs built more like a kangaroo's than a corpse's, barking short and sharp in the dark, at home somewhere the sun has never once reached.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath (1943, PD)"}],
 "theater":[{"name":"Line Infantry Shade","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"guard","summary":"Rank-and-file trench ghost, holds the line by rote","flavor":"A rifleman still dressed by a drill he can't remember learning; he holds a section of trench because holding it is the only order left in him.","desc":"Mud to the knees, rifle held at a drilled slant, he stands a fire-step like it's still worth holding. His face under the helmet-brim is slack, unhurried, the eyes fixed on a horizon that isn't there anymore. He moves only when the line moves."},{"name":"Wire-Cutter Scout","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"bandit-courier","summary":"Silent night-crawler who counts sentries for something","flavor":"Crawls the gaps between lines at night, snipping wire and counting sentries; talks to no one, reports to something.","desc":"He crosses the wire on his belly, wire-cutters clicking soft as teeth, and doesn't so much as breathe loud. Every few yards he stops dead and counts something under his breath — sentries, maybe, or seconds. He never looks back at whoever sent him."},{"name":"Whistle-Blown Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Message-runner forever mid-sprint toward the whistle","flavor":"Carries messages between shattered command posts at a dead sprint; the whistle that sends him over is always just about to blow again.","desc":"He comes at a flat sprint, chest heaving, one hand clamped over a satchel of dispatches that don't matter anymore. Somewhere behind him a whistle is always just finishing its note. He runs the same fifty yards over and over, and never arrives."},{"name":"Duckboard Vermin Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Fearless rat-swarm that owns the trench floor at night","flavor":"Fat and fearless on a diet no one wants named, they own the flooded duckboards after dark and don't scatter for the living anymore.","desc":"They move over the sunken boards in a single wet ripple, unbothered by boots, unbothered by torches. This ground was theirs before you got here and it'll be theirs after. Something crunches underfoot that you decide not to look at."},{"name":"Mustard Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"manes-vaporspawn","model":"manes-vaporspawn","summary":"Drifting toxic gas-cloud that hunts low ground blind","flavor":"A drifting yellow-green bank that used to be a chemical order given from far behind the lines; it rolls into low ground and doesn't care whose lungs it finds.","desc":"A low yellow-green bank rolls across the ground at knee height, unhurried, patient, following the dip of the land into every low place a man might hide. It doesn't chase. It just waits for the ground to funnel you toward it."},{"name":"Barbed Kill-Zone Tangle","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"gas-spore-fungus","model":"net-new: a thorned mass of coiled wire that snags a boot then pulls","summary":"Living wire-tangle that snags then reels men in","flavor":"Coiled wire gone wrong, grown thorned and hungry between the lines; it snags a boot first and pulls the rest of the man in after.","desc":"The wire here has grown thorns that weren't forged, only sharpened by something patient. A boot catches, and the whole tangle draws taut like a fist closing. It doesn't let go once it's caught what it wanted."},{"name":"Musket-Line Regular","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Volley-fire rifleman lost in permanent powder smoke","flavor":"Loads, presents, fires in volley by rote; the smoke never fully clears from a face that's forgotten peace.","desc":"He loads, presents, and fires in the same three motions he's fired a hundred times, smoke curling up past a face gone flat with repetition. The volley beside him thunders and he doesn't so much as blink. Peace, if he ever had a memory of it, is gone."},{"name":"Longship Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Beach-charging raider screaming a nameless war-cry","flavor":"Comes off the beach at a dead run, screaming a war-cry with no god's name left in it, only the noise.","desc":"He comes off the beach at a dead sprint, mouth open on a war-cry that lost its god's name generations back — just noise now, just momentum. Sand kicks up behind bare feet. He hits the line before the line finishes forming."},{"name":"Jungle Ambusher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"scout","summary":"Silent canopy-and-mud ambusher, gone before you see him","flavor":"Fights from the canopy and the mud both, silent until the moment he isn't; the vines remember where he waited.","desc":"He's part of the mud until the second he isn't, rising soundless out of ground-level cover with a blade already moving. Vines still hang off one shoulder. By the time you register motion, he's already somewhere else."},{"name":"Siege-Line Sapper","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Tunnel-digger laying the charge that breaches the wall","flavor":"Digs toward the wall under fire, laying the charge that will open it; talks about the tunnel like it's a person he's killing slowly.","desc":"He digs toward the wall on his knees, one ear pressed to the earth, listening for the counter-tunnel that might already be listening back. He talks to the tunnel like it's something he's killing slowly, patiently, on purpose. The charge he's laying is only the last part of a much longer conversation."},{"name":"Barbed-Wire Horror","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Wire-impaled corpse that never fell, still reaching","flavor":"A body the wire never let fall, stitched upright by rust and old rage; it still reaches for the men who left it there.","desc":"The wire never let it fall, and it never really has since — rust-stitched upright, arms still reaching the direction the charge was going. Old rage keeps its joints moving long after the tendons should have failed. It doesn't remember why it's reaching, only that it hasn't stopped."},{"name":"The Unkillable Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"NCO who won't stay dead, keeps ordering the charge","flavor":"Shot, gassed, and buried three times over the objection of his own men, he gets back up cursing and orders the charge again anyway.","desc":"Shot, gassed, and buried three separate times over his own men's loud objections, he climbs back out cursing at a volume that carries the length of the trench. He gives the same order he always gives. Nobody's found a way yet to make it stick."},{"name":"Hedgerow Tank-Killer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"tough-boss","summary":"Bocage ambusher waiting to drop a war-machine cold","flavor":"Waits in the bocage with a tube on his shoulder for a machine bigger than any dragon he's heard of in stories; one shot, one silence.","desc":"He waits flat in the bocage hedge with a tube braced on one shoulder, patient past what should be reasonable, watching a shape bigger than anything in his own war's mythology grind closer. One shot. Then a silence that swallows whatever noise the machine was making."},{"name":"Longship Warlord","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"ettin","model":"hill-giant","summary":"Giant raider-chief armored in three lines' worth of plate","flavor":"Twice the size a man should be, armored in captured plates from three different lines; the beach is his only law.","desc":"He stands twice the size a man ought to be, armored in captured plates scavenged off three separate battle-lines that never fought each other before he made them. The beach answers to him and nothing else does. He doesn't raise his voice — the size does that for him."},{"name":"Trench Ghast","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"No-man's-land feeder that mimics the whistle to lure prey","flavor":"Feeds in no-man's-land where nobody goes to collect the dead; it has learned to imitate the whistle to lure the living out.","desc":"It feeds where nobody goes to collect the dead, patient in the space between the lines, and it has learned to shape its throat around the exact pitch of the whistle. When it blows that note, boots start moving before anyone decides to listen. It's very good at getting men to come to it."},{"name":"Jungle Beast-Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Handler who marches a chained horror as a living breacher","flavor":"Marches a chained horror ahead of his own line as a breach-weapon; the leash is the only thing keeping the front intact.","desc":"He marches a chained horror a full length ahead of his own line, leash wrapped twice around one fist, using it the way another man might use a shield. The beast strains against him with every step. The leash is the only thing between the front line and whatever's on the other end of it."},{"name":"Iron Crawler War-Machine","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Treaded armored hull grinding across the wire alone","flavor":"A rivet-scarred hull dragging itself across the wire on tracks it wasn't built to have; the crew inside stopped answering the hatch a long time ago.","desc":"A rivet-scarred hull drags itself across the wire on tracks that were clearly never meant to survive this ground, engine note grinding low and wrong. The hatch on top hasn't opened in longer than anyone's willing to guess. Whoever answers from inside it doesn't answer anymore."},{"name":"Legion Standard-Breaker","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"Flag-devoted killer who believes in nothing but the fight","flavor":"Fights for the flag more than the cause, and the flag has no name anyone will say out loud; kills beautifully, believes in nothing.","desc":"He fights for the flag more than any cause it's supposed to stand for, and the flag itself has stopped meaning anything anyone will say out loud. His strikes are clean, almost beautiful. He believes in the fight and nothing underneath it."},{"name":"Musket-Line Cavalry Officer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Officer charging cannon-fire on horseback for the order alone","flavor":"Charges a line of guns on horseback because the order came down and orders are the only faith he has left.","desc":"He rides at a measured trot straight toward a line of leveled guns, sword raised, because the order came down and orders are the only faith he has left. Smoke swallows him and the horse both for a moment. When it clears he's still coming."},{"name":"The Line That Held","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Animate trench-line that simply refuses to yield ground","flavor":"A stretch of trench itself, animated by every soldier who swore to hold it and did, until holding was all that was left; it does not attack so much as refuse to move.","desc":"A whole stretch of trench itself seems to be standing its ground, animated by every soldier who swore to hold it and did, right up until holding was the only thing left of them. It doesn't lash out so much as simply refuse to move. Ground given up to it doesn't come back easily."},{"name":"Longship Draugr-Captain","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"wraith","summary":"Drowned captain still commanding his dead crew ashore","flavor":"Drowned with his crew and rose commanding them still; the tide brings his ship back to shores that no longer remember his war.","desc":"He came up drowned with his whole crew behind him and never stopped giving them orders, seawater still running steady from his sleeves. The tide brings his ship back to shores that don't know his war anymore. He commands the dead the same way he once commanded the living — without raising his voice."},{"name":"Jungle War-Engine","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Feral jungle war-machine still firing a stale coordinate","flavor":"A siege-machine gone feral in the canopy, vines grown through its plating, still firing on a target coordinate decades stale.","desc":"Vines have grown clean through its plating and it still fires on a coordinate that stopped mattering decades ago, servos grinding against root and rust both. Birds nest in its cannon housing. It doesn't seem to register that the war it's fighting ended without it."},{"name":"Legion Praetor-Revenant","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Dead commander who still drills a legion by discipline alone","flavor":"Commands a legion of the dead the way he commanded the living, by discipline alone; his oath outlived his empire and his name both.","desc":"He drills the dead the same way he drilled the living, by discipline and nothing softer, and a legion falls into formation behind him without being asked twice. His voice carries the same flat authority it always did. His oath outlived the empire it was sworn to."},{"name":"The Whistle","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"The sound of the order itself, given bone and rank","flavor":"Not a person anymore — the sound itself, given a shape of officers' bones and borrowed rank insignia, that sends men over the top forever; every era's war has heard it.","desc":"It isn't a person, hasn't been for longer than anyone can say — just the sound itself wearing officers' bones and borrowed rank, hovering above the field on nothing at all. Every era's war has heard that same note and gone over the top for it. It doesn't speak. It only blows.","traits":{"note": "It is the sound of the order, wearing officers' bones. Its rays are notes, not beams — each shriek a different command given force.", "actions": [{"name": "Over the Top (replaces one Eye Ray)", "text": "Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature that can hear the Whistle within 120 feet. Failure: the target immediately moves up to its speed toward the nearest enemy or hazard of the Whistle's choice, and takes 22 (4d10) Psychic damage."}]}},{"name":"No-Man's Bloom","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Plant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"War-soaked ground grown into a thorned, remembering forest","flavor":"Grew from ground so soaked in war it stopped being ground; a forest of barbed thorn and bone-white flowers that remembers every line that ever broke on it, and answers with all of them at once.","desc":"Barbed thorn and bone-white flowers rise out of ground too soaked in war to still be called ground, a forest that remembers every line that ever broke across it. It doesn't grow so much as accumulate. When it answers, it answers with all of them at once.","traits":{"note": "Gargantuan and rooted across the whole field — the fight is with the ground itself. Wire-thorn and bone-white blossom for a hundred yards in every direction.", "actions": [{"name": "The Lines That Broke (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranks of barbed thorn erupt in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 20. Failure: 20 (3d8 + 7) Piercing damage and the target has the Restrained condition (escape DC 20). Success: half damage only."}]}},{"name":"Trench Rat Cloud","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Carrion rats swarming abandoned trenches and packs","flavor":"Bloated on no-man's-land carrion, it swarms boots and packs before anyone can shoot it.","desc":"A carpet of fur and tails boiling up out of a flooded dugout, red eyes catching whatever light there is. They don't scatter at a shout anymore — they've learned the shout doesn't mean much here. The smell arrives half a second before they do."},{"name":"Conscript Straggler","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Green conscript, flinches and breaks under fire","flavor":"Handed a rifle a week ago, he still flinches at his own shots and breaks the instant his squad does.","desc":"Uniform too big, rifle held wrong, he flinches at the report of his own shot before it's finished. His eyes dart to where his squad used to be standing. He'll fight, badly, until the man beside him runs — then he runs too."},{"name":"Wire-Snagged Corpse","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Barbed-wire corpse still lurching toward the line","flavor":"Caught on the barbed wire mid-charge, it never fell — it just kept twitching forward, one strand at a time.","desc":"It hangs half-upright in the wire where it died, uniform rotted to threads, one boot still lodged in the mud below. It twitches forward an inch at a time, barbs tearing deeper with every pull. It has never once managed to get free."},{"name":"Powder Monkey Cutthroat","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Small shipboard runner, finishes off fallen boarders","flavor":"Small enough to run the guns below deck, mean enough to finish off boarders with a marlinspike.","desc":"Small enough to duck below the gunwale, quick enough to be underfoot before anyone notices, he carries a marlinspike slick with someone else's blood. He grins at boarders already on their knees. He finishes what the cannons started."},{"name":"Musket Skirmisher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"kobold-inventor","model":"net-new: a loose-order rifleman crouched and reloading in drifting smoke","summary":"Loose-order skirmisher, fires and vanishes into smoke","flavor":"Fires from cover in loose order, reloading in the smoke while the line volleys behind him.","desc":"He kneels in drifting smoke, ramrod working fast, eyes on the treeline instead of the drill-line. A shot cracks out from somewhere near him and he's already moved before the echo answers. Loose order suits him; he was never built for the volley."},{"name":"Longship Thrall","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"troglodyte","model":"net-new: a chained oarsman handed an axe at the beachhead","summary":"Chained oarsman turned axe-fighter at the beachhead","flavor":"Chained to the oar until the ship beaches, then handed an axe and pointed at the shore.","desc":"Oar-calluses thick as bark, ankle still ringed raw from the chain, he's handed an axe the moment the keel scrapes sand and shoved toward the shore. He doesn't know the men beside him. He only knows the ship behind him is worse."},{"name":"Jungle Leech-Thing","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"net-new: a canopy-dwelling leech creature dropping onto exposed necks","summary":"Canopy leech-creature that drops and drains blood","flavor":"Drops from canopy vines onto exposed necks; the bite numbs before it drains.","desc":"It drops from the canopy without a sound, a wet dark comma landing on the back of a neck. The bite doesn't hurt going in — that's the trouble. By the time it does, it's already fat and letting go."},{"name":"Siege Camp Looter","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Corpse-looter trailing behind the siege lines","flavor":"Follows the siege lines picking corpses clean before the burial details arrive.","desc":"He moves low between the dead with a sack and a knife, working fast fingers over pockets and boot-tops. He's careful not to look at faces. The burial detail's cart is already creaking closer down the line."},{"name":"Shell-Shocked Wanderer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"net-new: a hollow-eyed survivor wandering no-man's-land muttering old orders","summary":"Shell-shocked survivor wandering, immune to fear","flavor":"Walks no-man's-land muttering old orders, immune to fear because there's nothing left to lose.","desc":"He walks the open ground upright, unhurried, muttering an order that stopped meaning anything a long time ago. Shellfire doesn't make him flinch anymore — nothing left in him rises to it. He steps around craters like he still remembers where they are."},{"name":"Gas-Mask Sentry","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Masked sentry holding post through gas alarms","flavor":"Stands post in a rubber mask through every gas alarm, trusting the seal more than his own eyes.","desc":"He stands his post behind a rubber snout and round dark lenses, breath rasping through the filter loud in the quiet. An alarm bell somewhere down the trench keeps ringing and he doesn't move. He trusts the seal on his mask more than he trusts his own eyes."},{"name":"Draft-Horse Casualty","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"Dead draft horse still hauling its rotted harness","flavor":"A supply-train animal that died in harness and kept pulling, wagon and all, long after the wagon rotted away.","desc":"Ribs showing through rotted harness-leather, it hauls a wagon that fell apart years ago, hooves finding the same ruts by memory. The trace-chains drag empty air behind it. It has never once noticed the wagon is gone."},{"name":"Cavalry Lancer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Mounted lancer charging ahead of modern fire","flavor":"Charges in a wedge before the machine-gun era caught up with the horse.","desc":"He rides in a tight wedge, lance couched, hooves throwing up clods of torn field ahead of a charge the wrong century caught up to. He doesn't slow at the first crack of modern fire. The horse under him doesn't either."},{"name":"Musket-Line Drummer Boy","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"performer","model":"net-new: a young drummer keeping march step through the volleys","summary":"Drummer keeping march step, breaking his death shatters morale","flavor":"Keeps the march step through the volleys; killing him breaks the formation's nerve as much as any officer.","desc":"Small hands keep perfect time on a drumhead scarred by shrapnel, the beat steady through smoke that swallows the rest of the line. He doesn't look old enough for any of this. If he falls, the step around him falters before the shooting does."},{"name":"No-Man's-Land Crawler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Battlefield ghoul scavenging the unburied at night","flavor":"Feeds on the unburied between the lines, too cowardly to rise until the shelling stops.","desc":"It moves low between the shell-holes on all fours, only surfacing once the guns fall quiet, dragging a stink of rot ahead of it. It picks at what the burial parties missed. It won't rise while there's still light enough to be seen by."},{"name":"Jungle Ambush Sniper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Canopy-lashed sniper waiting days for one shot","flavor":"Lashed into the high canopy for days at a time, waiting for one clean shot.","desc":"Lashed high into the canopy, still as bark, he's been waiting since before dawn for a single clean angle. Nothing about him moves except one eye and, eventually, one finger. He'll wait through tomorrow too if he has to."},{"name":"Longship Shieldmaiden","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Flank shield-wall fighter screaming the ship's name","flavor":"Holds the shield-wall's flank and screams the ship's name until her voice gives out.","desc":"She braces the flank of the shield-wall with both boots dug in, voice gone ragged from screaming a ship's name over and over. Her shield rings under blow after blow. She doesn't step back — the wall doesn't get to break on her end."},{"name":"Trench Wire Golem","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Salvaged-armor construct patrolling the wire on its own","flavor":"Salvaged plate and barbed coils lashed into a shape that shambles the wire-line on patrol.","desc":"Salvaged plate lashed together with rusted coils, it shambles the wire-line at its own patrol pace, joints grinding wet with mud. Barbs trail off it like a tattered coat. It doesn't need orders to keep walking the same stretch."},{"name":"Musket Volley Ghost","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"net-new: a spectral rank of soldiers standing shoulder to shoulder in smoke","summary":"Volley-killed rank of soldiers standing in smoke","flavor":"A whole rank that died in one volley, still standing shoulder to shoulder in the smoke.","desc":"A whole rank stands shoulder to shoulder in drifting powder-smoke, muskets still raised at the angle that killed them. They fire in perfect unison, over and over, the same volley that ended them. The smoke never quite clears around their boots."},{"name":"Jungle War-Dog","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"net-new: a scent-trained war-dog running point ahead of the patrol","summary":"Scent-trained war-dog running point on patrol","flavor":"Trained to track by sweat and fear, it runs the point ahead of the patrol.","desc":"It runs the point low and fast, nose working the air ahead of the patrol, trained past fear to track by sweat alone. Its handler is somewhere behind, forgotten. It only stops when it's found something worth stopping for."},{"name":"Siege Sapper's Mole","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"ankheg","model":"ankheg","summary":"Tunneling beast bred to dig under siege walls","flavor":"Bred and directed to chew siege tunnels under walls, indifferent to the men riding its back.","desc":"It chews through packed earth in steady, mechanical bites, indifferent to the men riding its wide back down into the dark. Dirt sprays behind it in a fine constant rain. It was bred for exactly this and nothing else."},{"name":"Mustard Fog Sprite","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"net-new: a low-rolling pocket of living gas hunting by sound","summary":"Living gas-cloud that hunts by coughing sounds","flavor":"A living pocket of gas that rolls low across the wire, hunting by the sound of coughing.","desc":"A thin, low pocket of gas curls along the ground, hunting by the wet sound of coughing more than by sight. It rolls into dugouts uninvited. Where it stops, breathing stops being easy."},{"name":"Longship Berserker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"net-new: a wild-eyed berserker chewing ritual root before the beach charge","summary":"Beach-landing berserker numb to wounds mid-charge","flavor":"Chews the ritual root before the beach landing and doesn't feel the axe wounds until the tide turns red.","desc":"He's chewed the ritual root before the beach even comes into view, eyes gone glassy-wide, axe swinging before his boots find sand. Wounds open on him and he doesn't register them yet. By the time he does, the tide nearby has gone red."},{"name":"Colonial Trench Medic","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"net-new: a medic crawling between craters under fire, satchel in hand","summary":"Under-fire medic, priority target to break morale","flavor":"Crawls between craters under fire, more dangerous to leave alive than most riflemen.","desc":"He crawls crater to crater under fire, satchel dragging in the mud, more careful with bandages than any rifleman is with a shot. He's calm in a way that unsettles the men he's dragging back. Someone always seems to want him dead first."},{"name":"Jungle Pit-Trap Warden","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"thri-kreen-marauder","model":"net-new: a guerrilla warden crouched among staked pits and deadfalls","summary":"Guerrilla warden herding patrols into staked pits","flavor":"Lives among staked pits and deadfalls of his own building, herding patrols into them.","desc":"He lives among stakes and deadfalls of his own patient building, a shape barely distinguishable from the undergrowth until it moves. He doesn't fight so much as herd. The ground itself seems to be doing the work for him."},{"name":"Duckboard Trench Fiend","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"dretch","model":"dretch","summary":"Mud-spawned fiend climbing up through duckboards","flavor":"Something answered the mud's hunger and started climbing up through the duckboards at night.","desc":"Something climbs up between the slats of the duckboard floor, small and wrong and grinning, mud running off it like it just finished being born. It answers a hunger that isn't its own. It doesn't understand why it's here, only that it's hungry."},{"name":"Machine-Gun Nest Crew","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"Two-man gun crew that ends charges outright","flavor":"Two men and a tripod that can end a whole charge in the time it takes to reload once.","desc":"Two men crouch behind a tripod, one feeding the belt, one riding the traverse, both moving with the same clipped economy of long practice. The gun doesn't pause to reload so much as breathe. A whole charge can end in the time it takes them to swap a barrel."},{"name":"Storm-Trooper Breach Squad","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Fast breach specialists clearing trench sections","flavor":"Trained to cross the open ground fast and clear a trench section room by room before the rest arrive.","desc":"They cross open ground in short controlled rushes, grenades first, clearing a trench section corner by corner before the rest of the line even reaches the wire. No wasted motion, no shouting. They're gone from one bay before you know they were in it."},{"name":"Longship Skald-Reaver","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"net-new: a raider singing the saga while swinging an axe","summary":"Singing raider whose saga-verses embolden the crew","flavor":"Sings the raid's saga even as he fights, and the crew fights harder for being sung about.","desc":"He fights and sings in the same breath, verses of the raid keeping time with his axe-strokes, and the crew around him fights harder for being sung about. His voice doesn't crack even when his knuckles do. The saga matters more to him than the outcome."},{"name":"Jungle Pit Viper Ambush","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-constrictor-snake","model":"giant-constrictor-snake","summary":"Treeline ambush snake striking bunched patrols","flavor":"Strikes from the treeline the moment a patrol bunches up on the trail.","desc":"It waits coiled at the treeline until the patrol bunches shoulder to shoulder on the narrow trail, then it's simply already among them. Scales catch what little light gets through the canopy. It only needs the one mistake."},{"name":"Cavalry Saber Charge","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Full-gallop saber cavalry betting on the first pass","flavor":"Rides the flank at full gallop, saber down, betting everything on the first pass.","desc":"He rides the flank at a flat-out gallop, saber low and level, betting the whole engagement on a single pass. Hooves throw mud in sheets. He doesn't check the horse until the line in front of him is already broken or he is."},{"name":"Field Gun Battery","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"net-new: a cannon crew fighting on grimly at their fallen posts","summary":"Cannon crew fighting as one machine past death","flavor":"A cannon crew that fights on as one grim machine after the horses bolt and the gunners die at their posts.","desc":"The horses bolted and the gunners fell where they stood, but the gun keeps firing, worked now by whatever's left of the crew moving in one grim, wordless rhythm. Barrels glow faint in the smoke. It reloads itself the same way corpses shouldn't."},{"name":"The Wire-Cutter Colossus","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Wire-clipping walker built to open assault lanes","flavor":"Built to walk the wire ahead of the assault, clipping lanes through with rotating shears.","desc":"It strides ahead of the assault on legs built for exactly this ground, rotating shears at each forearm chewing lanes through the wire in long unhurried passes. Coils spring loose and whip past its shoulders. It doesn't slow for what's caught in them."},{"name":"Longship Hull-Breaker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"Raiding-crew brute thrown at hulls and gates","flavor":"A raiding crew's brute, thrown at ship hulls and gates alike with the same swing.","desc":"He's thrown at whatever's in the way — hull, gate, shield-wall — with the same overhand swing every time, and whatever's in the way generally gives first. Splinters or bone, he doesn't seem to notice the difference. He's already turning toward the next thing."},{"name":"Jungle Beast-Cage Handler","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lizardfolk-sovereign","model":"net-new: a handler flinging open bamboo cages at the ambush horn","summary":"Handler releasing caged war-beasts on the ambush horn","flavor":"Releases the war-beasts from bamboo cages the instant the ambush horn sounds.","desc":"He crouches beside stacked bamboo cages, hand resting on the latch, waiting on a horn only he seems to be listening for. When it sounds, the cages come open all at once. He steps back and lets whatever's inside do the rest."},{"name":"Gas Cloud Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"steam-mephit","model":"net-new: a roiling, undissipated gas cloud with a hunting will of its own","summary":"Sentient, undissipated gas barrage with a will","flavor":"A whole gas barrage that never dissipated, grown a hunger and a will of its own.","desc":"A whole barrage that should have thinned out and dispersed instead rolls low and thick across the field, deliberate now, hunting. It curls around cover instead of drifting past it. Something in the way it moves suggests it's choosing."},{"name":"Trench Raid Bayonet Line","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Silent bayonet line going over the top on the whistle","flavor":"Goes over the top in a fixed line, bayonets first, silent until the whistle blows.","desc":"They come up over the parapet in a fixed silent line, bayonets forward, boots finding the same broken ground without looking down. No one shouts until the whistle does. The line doesn't waver even where it's thinnest."},{"name":"Musket-Line Artillery Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"tough-boss","summary":"Voice-correcting gun sergeant walking under fire","flavor":"Walks the gun line under fire, correcting aim by voice alone.","desc":"He walks the gun line upright while everyone else keeps low, correcting elevation by voice alone between concussions that would drop a lesser man to his knees. Powder streaks his face black. The guns fire truer with him standing there than they would otherwise."},{"name":"Siege Tower Crew","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"net-new: a rolling wooden siege tower crewed by fighters at its top","summary":"Rolling siege tower crewed under falling arrows","flavor":"A rolling wooden tower crewed by soldiers who fight from its top even as arrows take the timbers apart.","desc":"The tower groans forward on log rollers, timbers already splintering under arrow-fire, men fighting from platforms near its top as it climbs the last yards to the wall. Ladders unfold with a crack. Nobody up there looks down to see how close the base is to giving out."},{"name":"Longship War-Wolf Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Raider running a leashed wolf-pack ahead of the men","flavor":"Runs with a leashed pack of raiding wolves that hit the shore ahead of the men.","desc":"He runs with a leashed pack straining ahead of him, wolves hitting the shoreline before the raiders' boots do. He lets the lead out in short savage bursts. The pack doesn't need him to point at anything twice."},{"name":"Jungle War-Elephant Driver","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"elephant","model":"net-new: a barded war-elephant carrying its mahout through the chaos","summary":"Barded war-elephant carrying its driver into chaos","flavor":"A trained war-beast in barded plate, its mahout riding the howdah through the chaos.","desc":"Barded plate creaks over a hide already scarred pale, the mahout riding high in a howdah that sways with every furious step. The ground shakes before the beast is even visible through the trees. He doesn't steer so much as suggest a direction."},{"name":"Trench Flame-Lance Team","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"salamander-fire-snake","model":"net-new: two soldiers hauling an oil-fire tank with a long lance-nozzle","summary":"Flame-tank team clearing bunkers in one breath","flavor":"Two men and a tank of oil-fire that clear a bunker in one long, screaming breath.","desc":"Two men haul a tank of oil-fire between them, one bracing the weight, one on the long lance-nozzle, and a bunker clears out in one continuous screaming breath of flame. Heat shimmers the mud around their boots. They don't linger to watch it finish."},{"name":"Deserter-Thing","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Executed deserter risen wrong, hunting its executioners","flavor":"Shot for running from the line, it came back wrong and now hunts whoever ordered the execution.","desc":"Shot against a post for running, it came back from the ground wrong, uniform still stripped of its markings, eyes fixed on the direction the firing squad stood. It doesn't chase anyone else. It only wants the men who gave the order."},{"name":"Musket-Line Grenadier","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"net-new: a tall-hatted grenadier carrying a satchel of black powder","summary":"Fearless grenadier carrying door-opening black powder","flavor":"Tall-hatted, fearless, and carrying enough black powder to open any door he's pointed at.","desc":"Tall hat, steady hands, he carries enough black powder slung at his hip to open any door he's pointed toward. He doesn't flinch lighting the fuse close to his own face. Whatever's behind that door stops being a problem shortly after."},{"name":"Longship Ghost Fleet Crewman","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Century-dead rower still believing the raid continues","flavor":"Rows a ship that beached a hundred years ago and never stopped believing the raid is still on.","desc":"He rows a ship that beached a century ago, oar dipping into water that isn't there anymore, expression fixed on a raid he still believes hasn't ended. Salt-rot clings to what's left of his tunic. He doesn't look up when you pass."},{"name":"Siege Ballista Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"net-new: a gate-punching ballista crewed by soldiers who never rest","summary":"Gate-punching war-machine crewed around the clock","flavor":"A war-machine built to punch through castle gates, reloaded by a crew that never sleeps.","desc":"The war-machine's crew reload without rest, arms moving in shifts that never seem to end, the great bolt-thrower groaning back to full draw again and again. It's built to punch gates, and it's punched more than most gates could survive. No one at the winches has slept in longer than anyone wants to say."},{"name":"Jungle Tiger-Rider Scout","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"tiger","model":"net-new: a scout riding a trained tiger along canopy trails","summary":"Trained big-cat rider scouting the canopy trails","flavor":"Rides a trained big cat through the canopy trails faster than any patrol can track.","desc":"He rides low along a canopy trail no patrol could follow, the big cat beneath him silent on padded feet, ears already turned toward something ahead. Leaves barely rustle where they pass. By the time you'd hear them, they've already gone."},{"name":"Trench Officer's Ghost-Whistle","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"net-new: a spectral officer still blowing a whistle for the charge","summary":"Dead officer whose whistle still calls the charge","flavor":"An officer who blew the whistle for the final charge and never stopped hearing it answered.","desc":"It doesn't have a face left worth describing, only a whistle still gripped between what used to be teeth, and the sound it makes is the same order it gave the night it died. Every man who hears it feels his boots start moving before he decides to. It has never once stopped believing the charge worked."},{"name":"Musket-Line Field Marshal's Honor Guard","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"net-new: an honor guard standing fast around a battle standard","summary":"Standard-guard sworn to die before it falls","flavor":"Sworn to die before the standard falls, and mean about proving it.","desc":"They stand fast in a tight ring around a battle standard, bayonets out, faces set, sworn to die before the fabric touches the ground. Fire crackles around them and none of them step back. They're not being brave so much as certain."},{"name":"Cavalry Death-Rider","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"net-new: a dead cavalry officer and warhorse still mid-charge","summary":"Dead cavalry officer and horse still mid-charge","flavor":"A cavalry officer and his warhorse, both killed in the same charge, still riding it out.","desc":"Both officer and warhorse died the same instant of the same charge, and neither seems to have noticed — hooves still drumming, sword still raised at the same angle it fell. Cold radiates off them before they're even close. The charge that killed them has never once finished."},{"name":"Longship Berserker-King's Champion","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"centaur-warden","model":"net-new: a bare-chested champion fighting at the longship's prow","summary":"Bare-chested prow-fighter daring the shore to resist","flavor":"Fights bare-chested at the prow, daring the enemy shore to try and stop the landing.","desc":"He fights bare-chested at the longship's prow, daring the whole shoreline to try and stop the landing, laughing through wounds that would drop three other men. Salt spray soaks him and he doesn't seem to notice the cold. Nobody near him wants to be the one who proves him wrong."},{"name":"Jungle Ambush War-Priest","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"oni","model":"net-new: a war-priest swinging a ritual club after blessing the ambush","summary":"Ritual-blessing war-priest wading into the ambush","flavor":"Blesses the ambush with old rites before the horn sounds, then wades in swinging a ritual club.","desc":"He mutters old rites over the ambush line before the horn sounds, ritual club already resting against one shoulder, eyes half-closed in something like prayer. When the horn comes, the prayer stops mid-word. He wades in like the blessing already did the hard part."},{"name":"Siege-Line Trebuchet Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-giant","model":"net-new: a hulking trebuchet that aims and looses itself","summary":"Self-aiming trebuchet that no longer waits for orders","flavor":"A siege engine grown a crude will, it aims itself now and doesn't wait for the order to loose.","desc":"It aims itself now, arm creaking back on its own without anyone giving the order, and looses the moment it decides the angle's right. Stone and timber groan under its own draw-tension. It stopped needing a crew a long time before anyone noticed."},{"name":"Musket-Line Cannon Golem","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"net-new: a field gun bolted onto a lumbering walking chassis","summary":"Walking field-gun chassis built to replace dead crews","flavor":"A field gun bolted to a walking chassis, built when someone realized the crew kept dying.","desc":"A field gun bolted onto a lumbering iron chassis rolls forward on legs built after too many crews died at their posts, the barrel swinging level with unnerving smoothness. Its footsteps land heavier than the recoil does. It doesn't need a gun-line standing behind it anymore."},{"name":"Trench Wraith of the Wire","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"net-new: a fused mass of soldiers hunting by remembered muzzle-flash","summary":"Company-wide death-wraith hunting by muzzle-flash memory","flavor":"A whole company lost to one machine gun, fused by grief and mud into something that hunts by muzzle-flash memory.","desc":"A whole company lost to one gun position fused together by grief and mud into a single drifting shape, hunting the field by the ghost of a muzzle-flash it remembers. It doesn't have individual faces anymore, just an outline where a hundred did. It moves toward wherever the flash used to be.","traits":{"note": "Moves through wire, mud, and revetment without hindrance, and always moves toward the last muzzle-flash it saw.", "actions": [{"name": "Wire-Drag (replaces Bite)", "text": "Loops of remembered wire whip out. Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage, and a Medium or smaller target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15) as the wire coils tight."}]}},{"name":"Longship Draugr-Fleet Captain","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"wraith","summary":"Drowned fleet-captain whose sunk ships still answer","flavor":"Commands a crew of the drowned, and every ship he's ever sunk still answers his horn.","desc":"He commands a crew of the drowned from a deck that shouldn't still float, and every ship he's ever sent to the bottom answers when he sounds the horn. Water pools steadily around his boots without ever draining away. The sea, wherever he sails it, still seems to owe him something."},{"name":"Jungle Colossus-Beast","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"net-new: a tamed prehistoric beast used as a living battering ram","summary":"Tamed prehistoric survivor used as a living ram","flavor":"A prehistoric survivor pressed into service as a living battering ram by whoever tamed it first.","desc":"A prehistoric survivor bigger than anything that should still be walking gets pressed into service as a living battering ram, hide scarred pale under barding lashed on in a hurry. Trees splinter ahead of it before the war-cry behind it even finishes. It doesn't know it's a weapon. It just knows to charge."},{"name":"Trench Butcher Golem","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a grim close-quarters clearing machine built for the wire","summary":"Close-quarters clearing machine built for the unstomachable work","flavor":"Built for the close-quarters clearing work no living soldier could stomach doing twice.","desc":"It was built for the close-quarters clearing work no living soldier could make himself do twice, moving through a trench section with an economy that has nothing to do with mercy. It doesn't hesitate at corners the way a person would. That's rather the point of it."},{"name":"Musket-Line Ghost Regiment","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","model":"net-new: a spectral regiment marching in perfect dead formation","summary":"Regiment lost in one charge, still marching in formation","flavor":"A whole regiment lost in one disastrous volley-charge, still marching in perfect dead formation.","desc":"An entire regiment lost in one disastrous volley-charge still marches in perfect dead formation across ground that no longer needs taking. Boots strike the earth in unison with no sound following. They don't seem to know the charge already failed — they're still marching toward the order that sent them.","traits":{"hp": 130, "ac": 14, "note": "A regiment fighting as one swarm-formation (scaled far past the crawling-claw chassis, CR 9): it can occupy other creatures' spaces, and its volley weakens once the formation is Bloodied.", "actions": [{"name": "Dead Men's Volley", "text": "The whole line presents and fires. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 16, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Failure: 22 (4d10) Necrotic damage, or 11 (2d10) if the Regiment is Bloodied. Success: half damage."}]}},{"name":"Siege Wall-Breaker Titan","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"fire-giant","model":"net-new: a hulking titan swinging a tree-trunk ram at a gate","summary":"Ram-wielding siege titan that doesn't stop swinging","flavor":"Swings a ram the size of a tree trunk and doesn't stop until the gate or its arm gives first.","desc":"He swings a ram the size of a felled tree in a slow relentless arc, again and again, gate-timbers splintering a little further with each hit. Sweat and mud run off him in equal measure. He doesn't stop until the gate gives or his own arm does, and he seems entirely at peace with either outcome."},{"name":"Longship Sea-Wyrm Figurehead","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"wyvern","model":"wyvern","summary":"Cursed living figurehead diving from fog onto ships","flavor":"A carved prow come alive with raider curses, it dives on enemy ships from the fog.","desc":"A carved prow comes alive out of the fog with a raider's dying curse still animating the wood, diving on unsuspecting hulls from an angle no lookout expects. Salt-slick timber gleams where scales should be. It surfaces again somewhere else before the wreckage even finishes settling.","traits":{"hp": 170, "ac": 16, "note": "Carved oak under salt-iron sheathing (scaled past the wyvern chassis, CR 10) — it is timber, not flesh: immune to Poison, and its tail is a rudder, not a sting.", "actions": [{"name": "Prow-Dive", "text": "It falls out of the fog like a ship coming down. If the figurehead moves at least 30 feet straight toward a target while flying and then hits it with a Bite attack, the target takes an extra 13 (2d12) Piercing damage and has the Prone condition."}]}},{"name":"Jungle War-Machine of Rusted Vines","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Root-swallowed ancient war-engine, still fully armed","flavor":"An engine of war swallowed by the jungle for decades, now grown through with roots and still armed.","desc":"An engine of war has been swallowed by the jungle for decades, roots grown thick through every seam in its plating, and it's still fully armed underneath all that green. Birds nest where a gunport used to matter. It doesn't seem to know the war it was built for is long finished."},{"name":"The Field Marshal's Undying Aide","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Undying aide delivering the same dead order nightly","flavor":"Delivers the same order at the same hour every night, a century after the marshal died reading it.","desc":"He delivers the same dispatch at the same hour every single night, a century after the marshal he serves died reading the first copy of it. His uniform hasn't faded so much as gone the color of dust. He waits for a reply he stopped expecting decades ago and delivers the order anyway."},{"name":"Trench Legion Revenant Colonel","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: a revenant colonel rallying every corpse in earshot","summary":"War-denying revenant rallying every nearby corpse","flavor":"Refuses to accept the war is over, and rallies every corpse in earshot to prove it.","desc":"He refuses, flatly, to accept that the war is over, and every corpse within earshot of his voice rises to help him prove it. His medals have tarnished black. He rallies the dead the same way he once rallied the living — by simply assuming they'll follow."},{"name":"Longship Storm-Caller Reaver","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"net-new: a reaver standing at the helm, storm crackling around him","summary":"Storm-bargaining reaver whose weather still owes him","flavor":"Bargained the sea itself into raiding for him, and the storm still owes him one more shore.","desc":"He bargained the sea itself into raiding on his behalf once, and the storm still seems to think it owes him one more shore. Lightning walks the mast behind him without ever quite touching it. He stands at the helm like a man collecting on a very old debt.","traits":{"note": "Not a genie — a mortal reaver the weather obeys, grudgingly. Kill him and the storm he bargained with does not stop; it just stops taking orders.", "actions": [{"name": "Call In the Debt (Recharge 6)", "text": "He points, and the storm pays what it owes. Lightning falls on a point he can see within 120 feet. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere on that point. Failure: 27 (6d8) Lightning damage and the target can't take reactions until the start of its next turn. Success: half damage only."}]}},{"name":"Jungle Chimera-Beast of War","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Warlord-bred chimera leading otherwise unsurvivable charges","flavor":"Bred by a warlord's beast-tenders to lead a charge no single animal could survive alone.","desc":"A warlord's beast-tenders bred three animals into one to lead a charge no single creature could have survived alone, and the three heads still argue faintly even mid-stride. It doesn't slow to settle the disagreement. Whatever it's charging toward, all three of it want the same thing."},{"name":"Musket-Line Field Marshal-Revenant","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"net-new: a spectral marshal frozen mid-order at a headquarters table","summary":"Century-dead marshal still finishing his last order","flavor":"Died at his own headquarters table mid-order and has been finishing that sentence for a hundred years.","desc":"He died at his own headquarters table in the middle of dictating an order and has spent a century since finishing that same sentence. Candle wax has puddled and re-hardened a hundred times around him. The order never quite gets to the end.","traits":{"note": "No bite, no blood — the unfinished order is what sustains him. He cannot be turned aside from his headquarters table for long; he always returns to it.", "actions": [{"name": "The Last Order (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "He finally finishes the sentence. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, each enemy within 30 feet that can hear him. Failure: 21 (6d6) Psychic damage, and the target obeys one word of the order — it can't take reactions until the end of its next turn. Success: half damage only."}]}},{"name":"Trench Colossus of Bone and Wire","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"rakshasa","model":"net-new: a titan built from the unburied dead, bone and barbed wire","summary":"Self-built ossuary titan from an unnamed battle's dead","flavor":"Built itself from the unburied dead of a battle no one survived to name.","desc":"It built itself, slowly, out of the unburied dead of a battle nobody survived to name, bone knitted through with rusted barbed wire like tendon. It doesn't remember whose side it fought for. It only remembers that the ground kept giving it more material.","traits":{"ac": 18, "note": "Huge, mindless of the rakshasa chassis's cunning — no spells, no disguise. Just mass, wire, and the patience of the unburied.", "actions": [{"name": "Ossuary Slam (replaces Cursed Touch)", "text": "A fist of fused ribcages. Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 19 (3d12) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Take Up the Dead", "text": "The colossus drags one corpse within 10 feet of it into its own mass and regains 19 (3d12) Hit Points."}]}},{"name":"No-Man's-Land Warlord's Ghost","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"General's ghost eternally watching his own fatal order","flavor":"The general who ordered the crater assault still watches it from above, unable to look away from his own order.","desc":"He still watches the crater from above, unable to look away from the assault he ordered into it, replaying the same few seconds without end. His hands are clasped the way they were when he gave the command. He has never once managed to take his eyes off the result.","traits":{"note": "Incorporeal — it drifts above the crater and passes through wire, wall, and rampart without hindrance. It cannot leave sight of the crater it made.", "actions": [{"name": "The Order, Again (replaces one Eye Ray)", "text": "The ghost repeats the order that killed them all. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature within 120 feet. Failure: the target must use its reaction, if available, to move up to its speed toward the crater's center."}]}},{"name":"The Ironclad Reaver-Queen","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a longship's hull fused with its captain into one war-machine","summary":"Ship-hull-and-captain war-machine that never comes ashore","flavor":"A longship's hull fused with its captain by a dying storm-oath, now a war-machine that never beaches.","desc":"A longship's hull fused with its captain in the last seconds of a dying storm-oath, and the result never quite beaches anywhere again. Barnacled plate groans where a keel should be silent. It patrols coastlines the way its captain once did, only now the ship and the woman are the same argument.","traits":{"note": "Hull and captain are one body. She never comes ashore — she fights from water deep enough to float her keel, and the shallows are her surrender line.", "actions": [{"name": "Carronade (replaces Fiery Bolt)", "text": "A hull-gun runs out and fires. Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 300 ft. Hit: 36 (8d8) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature it is pushed 10 feet straight away."}]}},{"name":"Legion Undying Praetorian Host","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Never-broken honor-guard formation, undying for centuries","flavor":"An entire honor-guard that swore to never break formation, and hasn't, in any century since.","desc":"An entire honor-guard swore, once, to never break formation, and it hasn't in any century since, ranks locked shoulder to shield exactly as drilled. Dust settles on them between the rare moments they move. Nobody currently alive gave them that oath, and it doesn't matter to them at all.","traits":{"hp": 260, "note": "A formation, not a man — one Large block of locked shields that fights as a single creature. While it has more than half its hit points, ranged attacks against it have Disadvantage (the shield-roof holds).", "actions": [{"name": "Pila Volley (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The front rank throws as one. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 18, each creature in a 30-foot Cone. Failure: 27 (6d8) Piercing damage. Success: half damage."}]}},{"name":"The Gas-King of the Salient","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"Sentient gas-cloud amalgam that owns the salient's ground","flavor":"Every gas attack ever loosed on the salient pooled into one thinking, hating cloud that owns the ground now.","desc":"Every gas barrage ever loosed across this stretch of ground has pooled together into one thinking, hating cloud that now simply owns the ground it used to just poison. It doesn't roll with the wind anymore — it decides. The salient belongs to it the way land belongs to whoever's still standing on it.","traits":{"ac": 14, "note": "A drifting, thinking cloud — blades and shot pass through it; strong wind and open flame are what it actually fears. It holds the low ground and lets you come to it.", "actions": [{"name": "Green Drift (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The cloud pours itself over a 30-foot Cube within 30 feet. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 20. Failure: 42 (12d6) Poison damage and the Poisoned condition until the end of the target's next turn. Success: half damage only."}]}},{"name":"The Siege That Never Lifted","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"Fused siege-line horror still failing to take the city","flavor":"A siege line's worth of engines, crews, and dead fused into one wall-breaking horror that still hasn't taken the city.","desc":"A whole siege line's worth of engines, crews, and dead have fused into a single wall-breaking horror that, after all this time, still hasn't taken the city in front of it. It keeps trying anyway, patient past any reasonable definition of patience. The walls it's failed against are older than most of what built it.","traits":{"hp": 350, "ac": 21, "note": "A colossus scaled to the siege it still fights (CR 17, not the full chassis) — the dead crews inside still load, aim, and correct their fire.", "actions": [{"name": "Breach Volley (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Every engine fused into it fires at once along a 120-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 21. Failure: 45 (10d8) Bludgeoning damage and the target has the Prone condition. Success: half damage only."}]}},{"name":"The Trench Ghost","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"shell-shocked revenant infantryman on eternal patrol","flavor":"A soldier who never left the line, rifle still slung, gas-hood rotted to rags; it keeps walking a patrol route that ended lifetimes ago.","desc":"Rifle still slung the way regulation demanded, gas-hood rotted down to rags at his collar, he walks a patrol route that finished being relevant lifetimes ago. His boots find the same ruts every time. He doesn't notice there's no trench left to patrol.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic WWI-lensed infantry archetype (no named nation/unit)"},{"name":"The Legion Wall","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"lone shield-and-spear legionary, drilled to a fault","flavor":"One tile of a wall that used to be a hundred men wide; it still steps in formation even with no one left on either flank.","desc":"He holds one tile of a shield-wall that used to run a hundred men wide, stepping in perfect formation with nobody left on either flank. Rust has fused the shield to the arm underneath it. He doesn't break rank even standing entirely alone.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"classical-era shield-line legionary archetype"},{"name":"The Musket Line","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"standing volley-drill musketeer, drilled past reason","flavor":"Loads, kneels, fires, reloads — the whole drill even when there's no second rank behind him and no order left to give.","desc":"He goes through the whole drill — load, kneel, present, fire, reload — with no second rank behind him and no order left worth giving. Smoke curls off a barrel that's fired for no one to see. His hands still know the sequence better than his eyes know the field is empty.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic 18th/19th-c. volley-fire infantry archetype"},{"name":"The Longship Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"hobgoblin-soldier","summary":"axe-and-round-shield sea raider, stranded in the war","flavor":"Came ashore for plunder and glory and got neither — just the theater's endless tide instead of home.","desc":"He came ashore chasing plunder and glory and found neither, only this theater's endless grinding tide instead of anything like home. His axe is nicked past use and he keeps swinging it anyway. He stopped expecting to make it back to a ship a long time ago.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"Norse-lensed raider archetype (not a specific saga figure)"},{"name":"The Jungle Scout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"camo-draped recon scout gone half-feral in the green","flavor":"Camouflage gone to lichen, machete more rust than edge — still moves like the canopy is watching him back.","desc":"Camouflage gone to actual lichen, machete more rust than edge, he still moves like the canopy above him is keeping watch. Insects have made a home in his gear straps. He hasn't stopped believing the jungle is on his side, even now.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic mid-century jungle-warfare scout archetype (no named conflict)"},{"name":"The Siege Sapper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"tunnel-digging siege engineer, still mining toward a wall","flavor":"Digs toward the wall by memory, pick over one shoulder, satchel of black powder over the other, humming a tune no living ear would know.","desc":"He digs toward a wall by memory alone, pick over one shoulder, a satchel of black powder swinging off the other, humming something no living ear would place. Dirt falls steady past his boots into the dark behind him. He doesn't remember which wall, only that there's always one.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"medieval siege-engineer archetype"},{"name":"The Berserker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"battle-trance warrior who fights past fear and flesh","flavor":"Fights bare-armed and bear-shirted, past fear, past pain, past the point where the theater's rules of engagement still apply to him.","desc":"He fights bare-armed, bear-shirted, past the reach of fear and past most of what should be pain, somewhere the rest of the field's rules of engagement stop applying to him. Blood doesn't seem to slow him the way it slows anyone else. Whatever's driving him isn't tactics.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse saga/legend berserkr tradition (public domain; no modern media design)"},{"name":"The Draugr Captain","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"mound-risen undead officer still holding a dead line","flavor":"Guards a rank that was overrun centuries ago as if the order to hold still stands; corpse-cold hands still know the grip of a sword-hilt.","desc":"He guards a rank that was overrun centuries back as though the order to hold is still current, corpse-cold hand closing on a sword-hilt like the grip never stopped meaning something. Mound-dirt still clings under his nails. He isn't waiting for relief — he's just still holding.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse folklore draugr — the mound-dwelling undead warrior of the sagas"},{"name":"The Machine-Gun Nest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"fused gun-and-gunner emplacement, animate and traversing","flavor":"Not one soldier but the whole emplacement fused together — tripod legs, traversing arms, a barrel where a face should be.","desc":"It isn't one soldier but the whole emplacement fused into a single traversing shape — tripod legs, articulated arms, a barrel where a face belongs. It swings its aim in one smooth motion, unhurried, mechanical. Nothing about it needs to breathe between bursts.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic entrenched-crew-served-weapon archetype"},{"name":"The Storm-Trooper Cadre","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"grenade-and-trench-knife shock infantryman","flavor":"Moves in twos and threes between the shell-holes, grenade-first, never in the open longer than a breath.","desc":"They move in twos and threes between the shell-holes, grenade-first, never lingering in the open longer than a single breath allows. No one calls out orders — they don't need to. They're already gone from one crater before you register they were ever in it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic elite-shock-infantry archetype (WWI stosstruppen-style, no named force)"},{"name":"The Valkyrie","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"empyrean-iota","model":"empyrean-iota","summary":"battlefield psychopomp choosing which dead the war keeps","flavor":"Walks the field after the guns fall quiet, marking which of the fallen the theater will keep and which it lets go home.","desc":"She walks the field once the guns have gone quiet, unhurried, studying the fallen with an attention that has nothing to do with mercy. Her hand hovers over some and passes others by without explaining the difference. She decides which of them the theater keeps.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse myth — chooser of the slain (public domain figure, our own visual take)"},{"name":"The Iron Cavalry","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gorgon","summary":"armor-plated war-beast standing in for every era's tank","flavor":"Half horse, half hull-plate — the theater's answer to any age's need for something that doesn't tire and doesn't feel the wire.","desc":"Half warhorse, half hull-plate, it moves at a grinding trot that doesn't tire and doesn't feel the wire tearing at its legs. Sparks strike off it where it clips the wrong ground. Whatever era it's fighting in, it's always the answer to the same problem.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic armored-cavalry/tank archetype, era-blurred"},{"name":"The Siege Tower","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"animate siege-tower, self-propelled toward the wall","flavor":"Rolls forward on its own dead momentum, ladders unfurling like wings, arrow-slits blinking where windows should be.","desc":"It rolls forward on its own dead momentum, ladders unfurling from its sides like slow wings, dark slits along its face blinking where windows ought to be. Arrows stick in its timber flanks like a bristling coat. It doesn't stop climbing toward the wall for anything short of collapse.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"medieval siege-engine archetype"},{"name":"The Trench Wight","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"revenant trench-officer still blowing the whistle to advance","flavor":"Commands a company that's mostly mud and memory now, whistle still around its neck, ready to blow the advance no one will survive.","desc":"Whistle still hung around a neck gone the color of old rope, he commands a company that's mostly mud and memory now, ready to sound the advance no one will survive. His voice carries even without much breath behind it. The men who'd have to follow that whistle stopped existing years ago, and he still expects them.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"WWI-lensed mass-grave revenant archetype (not any single named ghost)"},{"name":"The War Elephant","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"mammoth","model":"mammoth","summary":"armored siege-beast that shrugs off volleys and keeps coming","flavor":"Armored howdah still smoking from the last volley it shrugged off; it doesn't rout, it doesn't stop, it just keeps coming through the line.","desc":"Its armored howdah is still faintly smoking from the last volley it simply absorbed, and it doesn't slow, doesn't rout, doesn't do anything but keep coming through whatever line is in front of it. Each footfall lands like a small collapsing building. Nothing about its pace has ever changed.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"ancient/classical siege-beast archetype"},{"name":"The Gorgon Standard","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"gorgon-faced standard-bearer, a banner that petrifies stares","flavor":"A standard-bearer whose face the theater blurs on purpose — look at her banner too long and you understand exactly why armies used to carry her likeness into battle.","desc":"She carries a banner the theater keeps deliberately blurred at the edges, her own face turned just enough away that you understand, without being told twice, why armies used to march behind her likeness instead of beside her. Her grip on the standard-pole never wavers. Looking too long at the fabric feels like a mistake you already made.","traits":{"note": "The petrifying gaze lives in the banner she carries, not her face — and it keeps working after she falls, so long as the standard stands.", "actions": [{"name": "Raise the Standard (replaces Snake Hair)", "text": "She plants the pole and unfurls it. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 13, each creature within 30 feet that can see the banner. Failure: the target has the Restrained condition as it begins turning to stone, and repeats the save at the end of its next turn — Petrified on a second failure, free on a success."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Medusa/Gorgon, invoked here as a war-banner icon rather than the individual myth figure"},{"name":"The Flying Squadron","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"griffon","model":"griffon","summary":"aerial strafing beast standing in for the first air war","flavor":"Half war-bird, half war-machine, strafing the line from an altitude the trenches can only pray at.","desc":"Half war-bird, half war-machine, it banks low over the line and strafes a strip of churned ground the trenches can only flinch beneath. Its shadow crosses before the sound does. It climbs away before anyone below has finished ducking.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic early-aviation/biplane dogfighter archetype"},{"name":"The Ironclad Leviathan","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"roc","summary":"gargantuan warship-beast that dominates the theater's horizon","flavor":"It doesn't fly the theater's skies so much as displace them, guns run out along a hull too vast to have ever been launched from any yard.","desc":"It doesn't so much sail the theater's waters as displace them, a hull too vast to have ever been launched from any yard, guns run out along a flank that seems to go on past where the eye wants to stop. Its wake alone could swamp a longship. It doesn't change course for anything smaller than itself.","traits":{"ac": 18, "note": "The roc chassis wears an armored hull — shot rings off the plating. It does not land; it stations itself overhead like weather.", "actions": [{"name": "Gun-Deck Salvo (replaces one Beak attack)", "text": "The hull guns fire down the line of its shadow. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 60-foot Cone beneath it. Failure: 28 (8d6) Piercing damage. Success: half damage."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic armored-warship archetype, era-blurred (age-of-sail through dreadnought)"},{"name":"The War-Wyrm","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"chained siege-dragon deployed like a living artillery piece","flavor":"Chained to a war chariot bigger than most houses, it's less a monster than a munitions budget with wings and a grudge.","desc":"Chained to a war-chariot bigger than most houses, it strains against iron that was clearly built to hold something more reasonable, wings beating in short furious arcs it isn't allowed to finish. Its handlers ride well back from the reach of its chain. It's less a dragon anymore than a weapon someone decided to keep leashed.","traits":{"note": "Chained to its war-chariot — it flies only to the end of a 60-foot leash-arc and is hauled back. Deployed and fired like a battery piece, not fought like a dragon.", "actions": [{"name": "Ranging Shot (uses Fire Breath's recharge)", "text": "Its handlers walk the shot in. The wyrm arcs its fire at a point it can see within 300 feet. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere on that point. Failure: 28 (8d6) Fire damage. Success: half damage."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic siege-dragon archetype used as the theater's ultimate weapon, not tied to any named dragon myth"},{"name":"The Death Knight of No Nation","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"undead commander claimed by every faction, loyal to none","flavor":"Every side in every war in this theater has, at one time, sworn he was fighting for them; he has stopped correcting anyone.","desc":"Every faction in every war this theater has ever staged has, at some point, claimed him as theirs, and he has stopped bothering to correct any of them. His black armor carries no insignia that means anything specific. He fights with the same flat competence no matter whose line he's standing in.","traits":{"note": "At the first sound of battle he declares one side his own — no one, including him, knows which until he moves. His Dread Blade deals an extra 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage against anyone bearing the colors of the side he has disowned."},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic black-armored undead-commander archetype (fantasy stock type, no franchise ties)"},{"name":"The Siege of the World","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"ice-devil","model":"ice-devil","summary":"war given a body, wearing every era's uniform at once","flavor":"Wears every era's uniform at once and none convincingly; the theater's honest answer to what War would look like if it ever had to show its face.","desc":"It wears every era's uniform at once, and none of them convincingly, buckles and plate and drab canvas layered over each other in a shape that shouldn't hold together and does anyway. Smoke seems to follow it regardless of which century's weapons are firing nearby. It doesn't announce itself — it's simply already the reason the theater exists.","traits":{"hp": 290, "ac": 19, "note": "Not a devil of ice — a fiend of war. Its weapons change era mid-swing; the cold it deals is the cold of the field the morning after.", "actions": [{"name": "Every War at Once (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Every uniform it wears speaks a different dying order. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 19, each enemy in a 30-foot Emanation. Failure: 36 (8d8) Psychic damage and the Frightened condition until the end of the target's next turn. Success: half damage only."}]},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"original apex — the theater's totalizing embodiment of endless war, an original composite figure, not a myth or franchise reskin"}],
 "high-seas":[{"name":"Press-Ganged Deckhand","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Unwilling conscript swinging a cutlass under threat","flavor":"Taken off a dock at knifepoint three ports back; fights because the alternative is the lash, not because he wants your blood.","desc":"A cutlass wobbles in his grip like he's still learning which end is which. His shirt is someone else's, three sizes too big, and there's a rope-burn collar around his neck from being dragged aboard. He glances over his shoulder more than at you — checking who's watching him fight."},{"name":"Bilge Rat Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Chittering vermin tide pouring from the hold","flavor":"They ate the last cook's boots and are working on his replacement's; every hold has them and every hold pretends not to.","desc":"The deck seems to move before the rats do — a carpet of fur and pink tails boiling up through a hatch. The smell hits first, wet and ammonia-sharp, then the chittering, then a hundred small teeth all at once."},{"name":"Rope-Scar Cutthroat","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Cutlass-and-flintlock buccaneer swarming the rail","flavor":"Owes the crew's articles more than he'll ever earn; boards ships to buy back a little of his own name.","desc":"Rope has left white lines across both palms, permanent as tattoos. A flintlock hangs loaded but not yet drawn, and the cutlass comes up loose, almost lazy, like violence is just another chore before supper."},{"name":"Chum-Slick Reef Shark","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"reef-shark","model":"reef-shark","summary":"Blood-trail shark circling a wounded hull","flavor":"Follows any ship that's been bleeding into its wake — a bad sign the crew reads correctly and ignores anyway.","desc":"A dorsal fin cuts the surface in slow, unhurried figure-eights, following a thread of blood no one else can see yet. When it finally breaches for the strike, the water goes white before the teeth ever show."},{"name":"Waterlogged Deckwalker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Drowned crewman shambling back up the chain","flavor":"Went over in a storm and came back up the anchor chain; still wears the duty rota pinned to a rotted coat.","desc":"It climbs over the rail dripping brine from a coat gone the color of wet ash, a rotted duty-rota still pinned crooked to the lapel. Its steps are slow, deliberate, chain-scrape and squelch, like it's still walking a watch nobody canceled."},{"name":"Rattling Bone-Crew Deckhand","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Cutlass-armed skeleton still standing its watch","flavor":"Picked clean by fish and time, still hauling the same rigging it died hauling; the rope never lets a bone crew rest.","desc":"Bone knocks against bone with every step, a dry percussion under the creak of rigging. It hauls on a line that isn't attached to anything anymore, cutlass strapped to a wrist with kelp-rotted cord, still working."},{"name":"Fin-Toothed Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Fish-fanged sea-devil boarding from below","flavor":"Rises over the gunwale in packs when a hull rides low and slow; drags what it takes back down before the alarm bell finishes ringing.","desc":"It comes up over the gunwale in one wet heave, gill-slits flaring, rows of needle teeth bared in something that isn't quite a smile. Scales glisten black-green in the lantern light, and it's already reaching for the nearest throat."},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Squidling","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-octopus","model":"giant-octopus","summary":"Trench-spawned tentacle-beast dragging sailors under","flavor":"A juvenile shed off something vastly larger down in the trench; still small enough to drag a man under one-handed.","desc":"A tentacle comes up out of the black water first, thick as a mast and studded with suckers that leave welts. The rest of it surfaces slow and boneless, ink already clouding the water dark before it's fully seen."},{"name":"Gull-Eyed Wreck Harpy","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Rock-nesting harpy luring ships onto reefs","flavor":"Nests in the rigging of ships too slow to outrun it, singing sailors toward the rocks it circles like a gull circles chum.","desc":"It perches on the highest spar, wings mangy and salt-crusted, head cocked at an angle too sharp for a bird. Then it opens its mouth and the sound that comes out is almost a woman's voice, almost a song, almost enough to make a sailor forget the rocks."},{"name":"Debt-Marked Bosun","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Ledger-keeping enforcer collecting the crew's debts","flavor":"Keeps the ledger of who owes the crew what, in coin or blood, and collects personally when a name comes due.","desc":"A ledger is strapped shut at his hip with a leather cord gone soft from handling. He reads names off it before he swings, flat and businesslike, like collections is just another watch to stand."},{"name":"Deep-Fang Sea-Devil Priest","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Sea-devil war-priest chanting a raiding pack to frenzy","flavor":"Chants the raiding packs into a blood-frenzy from the wave-tops, offering the drowned to something older than the trench.","desc":"It stands at the wave-tops on legs that shouldn't hold weight on land, arms raised, chanting in clicks and glottal barks that don't sound like they were made for a human throat to answer. The raiding pack around it moves faster with every syllable.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Frenzy Chant", "text": "Nearby sahuagin allies gain advantage on their next attack roll."}]}},{"name":"Quartermaster of the Broken Articles","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Shadow-captain running the ship by fear alone","flavor":"Runs discipline on a ship whose captain hasn't been seen topside in weeks; the crew fears him more than any storm.","desc":"He counts coin without looking at it, eyes fixed on you instead, a smile that never once touches the rest of his face. The crew behind him goes quiet when he speaks — not respect, something closer to flinching."},{"name":"Chain-Dragging Drowned Sailor","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Anchor-chained revenant press-ganging the living","flavor":"Went down chained to the very anchor he was ordered not to release; surfaces to recruit a crew that never mutinies twice.","desc":"Rusted anchor-chain drags behind it across the deck, gouging the planks, fathoms of it looped and tangled around a bloated torso. Its eyes are the milk-white of something that drowned looking up at a surface it never reached.","traits":{"note": "presses conscripts — a grappled victim who dies rises as a thrall within the hour"}},{"name":"Mutinous First Mate","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Blade-drawn mate who murdered his way to command","flavor":"Slit the old captain's throat over a fair split and never looked back; the crew that followed him into it now wonders whose throat is next.","desc":"His coat still bears the old captain's braid, sewn crooked because he took it off a corpse in a hurry. The blade never leaves his hand, and there's a specific way he watches his own crew now — like counting who's next."},{"name":"Fogbank Siren","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"Fog-shrouded siren-witch bartering safe passage","flavor":"Sells safe passage through her fog for a name, a memory, or a firstborn — and always collects in a currency the crew didn't expect.","desc":"She emerges from fog thick enough to swallow a mast, green-skinned and smiling with too many teeth, one hand already extended like she's offering something instead of demanding it. Her voice, when it comes, is warm — that's the part that should worry you."},{"name":"Lantern-Eyed Ghost Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Translucent captain still haunting his own quarterdeck","flavor":"Still walks his own quarterdeck on the night the fog rolls thick, hailing living ships for a berth he'll never fill twice.","desc":"He stands the quarterdeck of a ship that isn't there, translucent as smoke, lantern-light bleeding straight through his ribs. He hails you formally, correctly, as if a berth still exists to offer."},{"name":"Riptide Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"Living riptide dragging a wreck's leftovers under","flavor":"A standing current with a temper, summoned or born where a ship went down wrong; drags cargo and crew alike to the same grave.","desc":"The water doesn't rise so much as decide to stand — a column of churning current, debris and driftwood spinning inside it like a held breath. It doesn't roar. It just pulls, patient and total."},{"name":"Deep-Baron of the Drowning Grounds","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"sahuagin-baron","model":"sahuagin-baron","summary":"Reef-ruling sea-devil warlord commanding raid packs","flavor":"Rules a reef of wrecks and the things that raid from them; ships that fish his water pay a toll in hulls.","desc":"It rises massive from the reef-shallows, crowned in barnacle and broken coral, a court of lesser sea-devils flanking it on every side. When it speaks the words come out as a demand for toll, not a greeting.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "commands nearby sahuagin, granting them advantage while it's conscious"}},{"name":"Plague-Hulk Zombie Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Fused mass of drowned dead still crewing the hulk","flavor":"A three-decker's worth of drowned dead fused by rot and current into one groaning, many-armed mass still trying to crew the ship.","desc":"Too many arms move at once from one bloated, fused mass of rotted flesh and torn uniform cloth. It still tries to crew the ship it died on — hauling ropes that lead nowhere, in a rhythm that used to mean something."},{"name":"Storm-Caller of the Drowned Choir","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"Voice-traded witch who calls storms on command","flavor":"Traded her voice to something under the swells for weather on command; the crew loves her and never quite meets her eyes.","desc":"She stands at the rail with her mouth working soundlessly, throat scarred where a voice used to be. The sky answers her anyway — clouds knotting overhead in a shape that has nothing to do with weather."},{"name":"The Admiral of Nowhere","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Undead fleet-admiral commanding a century-scuttled navy","flavor":"Commands a fleet that was scuttled a hundred years ago and never noticed; still promotes the drowned, still courts-martial the disloyal.","desc":"He stands on a quarterdeck a century gone to rot, epaulets tarnished black, and still gives orders to a fleet that sank around him without ever telling him it had. His eyes, when they finally fix on you, remember exactly how to court-martial the disloyal.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Muster the Drowned", "text": "Summons ghostly sailors from nearby wreckage to fight at his order."}]}},{"name":"The Keelbreaker","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Many-headed sea-brute older than the shipping lanes","flavor":"Many-headed and older than the shipping lanes; every captain who's fought it and lived describes a different number of heads.","desc":"Heads rise from the swell one after another, more than any sailor can count twice the same way, scarred hides overlapping like a wall of muscle and bone. The water around it churns before it even attacks, like the sea itself is bracing.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Regrowing Heads", "text": "A severed head is replaced by two new ones unless the stump is seared."}]}},{"name":"The Ghost Ship Herself","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"behir","model":"net-new: a sail-shredded derelict with a translucent hull, sailing herself","summary":"Self-sailing derelict crewed by its own drowned dead","flavor":"No living hand touches her wheel; she tacks into any wind, runs down any ship that spots her, and every soul she's ever taken still crews her rigging.","desc":"She comes on with sails shredded to lace, hull gone translucent as fogged glass, running against a wind that shouldn't be able to push her. Every plank groans with a voice, and every voice belongs to someone she's already taken.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Crewed by the Drowned", "text": "The ship fights back with ghostly crew manning cannon and rigging even with no living hand at the wheel."}]}},{"name":"The Fathom-Crowned Leviathan","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"The keel-sunk horror sailors swear by and dread","flavor":"The keel-sunk horror every sailor's oath invokes without meaning it; wakes when a ship's debts to the sea itself finally come due.","desc":"The sea doesn't ripple before it surfaces — it lifts, an entire swell of water sliding off a back the size of a keel. Tentacles unfurl slow as sails, and somewhere below the mass of it, the debt finally comes due.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"The Horizon's Own Reckoning","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"net-new: a burning derelict captain wreathed in storm-fire, chained to a wheel of drowned hands","summary":"Storm-fire captain who sailed past the edge of the charts","flavor":"The line where the horizon keeps its own counsel made flesh — a captain who sailed too far past the edge of the charts and came back wrong, wearing a crown of storm-fire and unpaid debts.","desc":"He stands at a burning wheel chained to his own wrists, storm-fire crowning a face no longer entirely human, drowned hands gripping the spokes alongside his. He sailed past where charts end, and came back as the edge itself.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Storm-Fire Wake", "text": "Leaves a trail of burning saltwater that ignites anything flammable it touches."}]}},{"name":"Salt-Cracked Deck Sweeper","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"Low-rank deckhand enforcer, no say in the voyage","flavor":"A ship's boy grown into a shipboard bruiser, all rope-burn hands and no say in where the vessel sails.","desc":"His knuckles are rope-scarred and his stance is all shoulders, built for shoving a smaller man out of the way rather than fighting fair. He doesn't ask where the ship's headed — he just enforces whatever the answer is."},{"name":"Powder Monkey Turned Cutthroat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Former powder-boy now knife-quick and patience-thin","flavor":"Started the crossing hauling shot to the gun deck; ended it with a knife of his own and no patience left.","desc":"Small and quick, he moves low along the deck the way he used to move hauling shot to the guns, except now the thing in his hand is a knife and his patience for talk is gone entirely."},{"name":"Barnacle-Crusted Beachcomber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Wreck-looting beachcomber, quick to rob the living","flavor":"Picks a wreck's bones clean before the tide can, and isn't shy about who else gets picked clean too.","desc":"Salt has cracked his skin into something like driftwood, and his pockets bulge with things pried off a wreck that isn't cold yet. He looks at you the same way he looks at cargo."},{"name":"Marooned Castaway","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Island-marooned mutineer's scapegoat, come back wrong","flavor":"Left on a spit of sand to die for a mutiny that wasn't his; came back off the island wrong and hungry.","desc":"Sunburn has peeled to leather across every inch of exposed skin, and there's a hunger in the eyes that isn't just for food. He was left on a spit of sand to die quietly. He didn't."},{"name":"Gull-Picked Corpse Crab","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-crab","model":"giant-crab","summary":"Scavenging tideline crab drawn to the recently dead","flavor":"Scuttles the tideline in loose scavenging clusters, drawn to anything that used to breathe.","desc":"It scuttles sideways along the tideline in loose, restless clusters, claws clicking, drawn by a smell of rot that hasn't reached your nose yet. When it finds something that used to breathe, the whole cluster converges at once."},{"name":"Chain-Rattling Bilge Zombie","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Drowned bilge-worker who never noticed the sinking","flavor":"Drowned in the hold when the pumps failed and never noticed the ship went down around it.","desc":"It rises dripping from the hold, chain looped loose around one rotted ankle, eyes fixed on nothing in particular. It never noticed the ship went down around it, and it still doesn't seem to notice now."},{"name":"Wreck-Wood Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Reef-floor skeleton reassembled by tide-logic","flavor":"Picked clean by fish and reassembled by whatever tide-logic runs the ocean floor's oldest graveyards.","desc":"Bone stands up off the seafloor in the wrong order, reassembled by current and time into something that walks anyway. Barnacles cling to the ribs like they grew there on purpose."},{"name":"Grog-Mad Deckhand","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"Becalmed sailor gone rum-mad and swinging","flavor":"Three weeks becalmed and a cracked rum cask turned an ordinary sailor into a swinging liability.","desc":"His eyes are bloodshot rings and his breath could strip paint, three weeks of dead calm and cracked rum boiled down into one swinging fist. He doesn't aim so much as flail in your general direction."},{"name":"Coral-Fanged Moray Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-piranhas","model":"swarm-of-piranhas","summary":"Territorial eel-knot nesting inside a breached hull","flavor":"A boiling knot of eels nesting in a hull-breach, territorial past all reason.","desc":"A hull-breach seethes with motion — dozens of eel-bodies knotted together, fangs bared, territorial past any reason a fish should have. The knot uncoils toward anything that gets too close to the gap."},{"name":"Flying-Fish Strafer Flock","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-ravens","model":"swarm-of-ravens","summary":"Oversized gliding fish-flock that shreds exposed skin","flavor":"An unnaturally large school that glides clean over the gunwale and shreds an exposed hand or face.","desc":"Silver bodies break the surface all at once, gliding low and fast over the gunwale in a shimmering, buzzing line. Each pass leaves a shallow slice across whatever skin was exposed."},{"name":"Bilge-Bloated Corpse Floater","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie-plague-carrier","summary":"Bloated floating corpse that only moves when approached","flavor":"Bobs face-down until something living gets close, then it isn't face-down anymore.","desc":"It bobs face-down in the swell, bloated and still, exactly the way a corpse should look — until something living gets close enough, and it isn't face-down anymore."},{"name":"Rope-and-Rum Buccaneer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Fair-weather buccaneer who renegotiates loyalty mid-fight","flavor":"Signed the articles for the split, not the cause, and will renegotiate both mid-boarding.","desc":"He's grinning before the first blow lands, already talking terms, cutlass loose in a hand that's clearly done this dozens of times and switched sides at least twice. Loyalty here has a price and it changes mid-fight."},{"name":"Tide-Warped Sahuagin Scout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sea-devil scout that tests hulls before the pod attacks","flavor":"Runs ahead of the raiding pod to test a hull's weak seams before the pack commits.","desc":"It hugs the waterline, only eyes and the ridge of a fin breaking the surface, testing the hull's seams with a webbed claw before the rest of the pod ever shows itself."},{"name":"Driftwood Effigy Watcher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Wreck-spar effigy that patrols the reef it was built to ward","flavor":"Lashed together from wreck-spars by superstitious crews to ward the reef; wards it by walking the tideline itself now.","desc":"Lashed spars and salvaged rope have been bound into a rough humanoid shape, warding-sigils carved crooked into the wood. It doesn't move like something that should move — until it takes its next slow, patrolling step."},{"name":"Reef-Crawling Giant Crab","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-crab","model":"giant-crab","summary":"Wreck-territorial crab that clamps and never releases","flavor":"Territorial over a wreck's cargo hold, clamps and doesn't let go until something breaks.","desc":"One claw is scarred and oversized from years of clamping onto cargo that fought back. It doesn't let go once it bites — the only way to end it is to make something break first."},{"name":"Fogbound Lookout Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Dead lookout still calling sightings to a vanished crew","flavor":"Still stands the watch it died at, calling sightings to a crew that scattered a century ago.","desc":"It stands at a crow's-nest post that rotted away a century ago, calling out sightings in a thin, carrying voice to a crew that scattered long before you were born. It doesn't seem to know no one's listening."},{"name":"Anchor-Chain Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Chain-tangled ghoul dragging fathoms of rusted iron","flavor":"Went down tangled in the anchor chain and rose still wrapped in it, dragging fathoms of rusted iron.","desc":"It drags fathoms of rusted chain across the deck, wrapped tight around a torso gone the color of drowned meat, claws already curling toward exposed skin. The chain never seems to slow it down."},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Tentacle Horror","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"Small deep-thing juvenile that boards and strikes throats","flavor":"A juvenile deep-thing washed inshore, small enough to board but old enough to know exactly where the throat is.","desc":"Small enough to board unnoticed, it slips over the rail with a wet, boneless economy of motion, tentacle-mouth already oriented toward the nearest throat with unnerving precision."},{"name":"Sea-Devil Net-Thrower","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sahuagin netter that drags swimmers under first","flavor":"Drags swimmers under with weighted netting before the rest of the raid ever surfaces.","desc":"A weighted net spins out from webbed claws before it even fully breaches, tangling around ankles and dragging feet out from under anyone standing too near the rail."},{"name":"Salvage-Diver Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"Drowned salvager-ghoul that won't surface without its box","flavor":"Died prying a strongbox from a sunken hold and still won't surface without it.","desc":"It clutches a rusted strongbox to its ribs even as it claws its way up the hull, refusing to surface without it, eyes fixed and hungry despite everything else about it being long dead."},{"name":"Hardtack Cannibal Crewman","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Lifeboat survivor turned desperate, quiet cannibal","flavor":"What's left of a lifeboat crew that ran out of hardtack long before they ran out of each other.","desc":"His cheeks are hollow and his eyes track you the way a starving man tracks the last biscuit. He doesn't announce what happened in the lifeboat. He just doesn't need to explain the knife."},{"name":"Shrieking Storm Petrel Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"Storm-heralding bird swarm that screeches the ship's name","flavor":"Precedes every gale that matters, screaming the ship's name back at the crew before the wind does.","desc":"A dark cloud of birds wheels overhead, screeching something that sounds unsettlingly close to the ship's own name, right before the wind picks up and confirms it."},{"name":"Barrel-Bomb Mutineer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Mutineer wielding a lit powder keg as leverage","flavor":"Carries a lit powder keg into a boarding fight like it's a threat and a bargaining chip both.","desc":"He carries a lit powder keg cradled against one hip like it's a baby, fuse hissing shorter by the second, grinning like the threat and the bargain are the exact same thing."},{"name":"Wreck-Grown Rust Louse Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"Hull-nesting vermin that rusts weapons to flakes","flavor":"Nests in derelict hulls and strips a boarding party's cutlasses to orange flakes before the fight even starts.","desc":"A rippling carpet of small, hard-shelled vermin pours out from a hull-breach, and everywhere it crawls, metal blooms rust and flakes to orange dust in seconds."},{"name":"Doldrums-Drunk Deserter","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"Starvation-mad deserter, dangerous to would-be rescuers","flavor":"Jumped ship in the doldrums rather than starve slow, and regrets it in a way that makes him dangerous to rescuers.","desc":"His ribs show through a torn shirt, and his eyes have the flat, glassy focus of someone who jumped ship rather than starve. He doesn't recognize rescue when it's offered — only threat."},{"name":"Barnacle Golem","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"net-new: a hull-plate golem crusted floor to helm in barnacles","summary":"Reef-grown armor golem woken by a scuttled hull","flavor":"Salvaged armor left lashed to a scuttled hull long enough for the reef to grow through the rivets and wake it up.","desc":"Salvaged armor plate creaks upright, crusted floor to helm in barnacle and dripping weed, joints grinding with the grit of a reef grown through every rivet. It moves like something that forgot it used to be worn by a man."},{"name":"Sea-Devil Priest's Acolyte","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Junior sea-devil chanter half a beat behind the priest","flavor":"Chants the drowning-litany half a beat behind the priest, close enough to matter.","desc":"It chants half a beat behind someone else's cadence, clumsy but earnest, eyes darting sideways for approval it clearly hasn't earned yet."},{"name":"Debt-Marked Purser","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Ship's purser running two ledgers, one true and one lie","flavor":"Keeps the true ledger of who owes the captain what, and the false one for the crew.","desc":"Two ledgers sit in two different pockets, and the way he shifts his weight when you get too close to either one tells you which is the lie."},{"name":"Reef-Devil Trapper","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sea-devil that lures hulls onto reefs with false lanterns","flavor":"Lures hulls onto shoal-teeth with false lantern-signals, then finishes what the reef starts.","desc":"It crouches at the reef's edge holding a lantern rigged to swing like a ship's true signal, patient as the tide, waiting for a hull to take the bait it's offering."},{"name":"Hollow-Eyed Lantern Ghost","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Drowned signalman's ghost-light, warning and luring both","flavor":"A drowned signalman's light, still swinging the warning nobody heeded, luring the unwary same as it once tried to save them.","desc":"A pale light swings low over the water on its own, no hand holding it, the shape of a drowned signalman visible only when the glow catches him at the wrong angle. It still swings the old warning — it just doesn't mean it as a warning anymore."},{"name":"Rope-Trick Rigging Spider","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"giant-spider","model":"giant-spider","summary":"Rigging-nesting spider that snares sail-climbers with silk","flavor":"Nests high in a ghost ship's rigging, dropping silk lines to snare anyone who climbs to reef the sails.","desc":"It hangs upside-down high in the rigging, legs longer than a man is tall, silk already spooling loose toward anyone climbing to reef a sail."},{"name":"Rock-Skulking Bilge Ooze","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Bilgewater ooze that corrodes hull-plate and boot leather alike","flavor":"Grew fat in a scuttled hold's standing bilgewater, corroding hull-plate and boot leather with equal patience.","desc":"A gray, formless mass seeps along the bilge boards, dissolving rivets and boot-leather with the same patient hiss, leaving a corroded sheen wherever it's passed."},{"name":"Quartermaster's Shakedown Man","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Articles-enforcer who finds loopholes when it profits him","flavor":"Enforces the Articles to the letter when it profits him and finds loopholes when it doesn't.","desc":"He recites the Articles from memory, word for word, and somehow the words always land in his favor. When they don't, he finds a clause that does."},{"name":"Coral Golem Guardian","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"net-new: a jagged reef-coral colossus shaped like a boarding pike, alive with darting cleaner-fish","summary":"Patient coral colossus guarding a sunken treasure gallery","flavor":"Grown by something patient to guard a sunken treasure gallery, indifferent to the centuries it's taken.","desc":"A colossus of jagged reef-coral rises from the sea floor, shaped roughly like a boarding pike, cleaner-fish darting in and out of its joints. It has clearly guarded this gallery for longer than any living captain has been alive.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"Storm-Wracked Harpy Matriarch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"Wreck-nesting harpy matriarch that sings ships to their ruin","flavor":"Nests her brood on a wreck-reef and sings ships onto the rocks to feed them.","desc":"She perches above a brood nested into a wreck's broken ribs, feathers matted with salt-spray, and when she sings the melody is unmistakably beautiful — right up until the rocks make sense of it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ruinous Lure Song", "text": "Nearby creatures who fail a save move toward the harpy's chosen hazard on their turn."}]}},{"name":"Bone-Naga of the Drowned Vault","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-naga","model":"bone-naga","summary":"Ancient bone-naga coiled around a sunken vault's treasure","flavor":"Coiled around a sunken hold's strongbox for two hundred years, patient past any living captain's greed.","desc":"It coils around a strongbox two centuries old, bone gone the color of old ivory, patient in a way nothing that still needs to breathe could ever manage."},{"name":"Fen-Tide Merrow Raider","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"merrow","summary":"Skiff-overturning merrow raider, plunder is an afterthought","flavor":"Overturns skiffs for the sport of it before it ever gets around to the plunder.","desc":"It surges up from beneath a capsized skiff, all muscle and green-gray hide, overturning what's left just for the sport of hearing sailors hit the water."},{"name":"Wreck-Diver Doppelganger","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Shape-stealing killer that answers to its last victim's name","flavor":"Wears the face of whichever sailor it drowned last, and answers to that name at the next port.","desc":"It wears a drowned sailor's face perfectly — down to the scar, down to the way he used to stand — and it answers to that dead man's name without a flicker of hesitation."},{"name":"Rigging-Runner Assassin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"Above-boarding assassin who drops garrote-first onto helmsmen","flavor":"Boards from above, garrote-first, dropping from the mainmast onto whoever's steering.","desc":"It drops from the mainmast in total silence, garrote already looped, aimed at whoever's hands are on the wheel before anyone below even hears the creak of the line it used to descend."},{"name":"Brine-Cursed Werebear Bosun","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werebear","model":"net-new: a hulking, salt-matted bear-shape bosun's coat still buttoned over the fur","summary":"Cursed bosun who becomes a bear-thing under full moon","flavor":"Cursed by a witch-doctor for flogging the wrong sailor, and now the whole crew fears the full moon more than the storms.","desc":"His bosun's coat is still buttoned tight over a frame that's grown too large and too furred for it, salt-matted and hulking, a curse laid on him for flogging the wrong sailor finally coming due.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "reverts to human form when reduced below half HP or at will"}},{"name":"Powder-Keg Berserker Boarder","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"First-wave boarding-axe berserker screaming a death-oath","flavor":"Leads the first wave over the gunwale swinging a boarding axe and screaming the crew's death-oath.","desc":"He comes over the gunwale first in the boarding wave, boarding axe already swinging, screaming an oath the whole crew swore together and only he still means."},{"name":"Fogbank Siren's Herald","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"sea-hag","summary":"Fog-wreathed hag singing harmony to lure ships ashore","flavor":"Sings the low harmony under the Siren's melody, close enough inshore that the fog never quite lifts.","desc":"She sings the low harmony underneath a stronger voice somewhere off in the mist, close enough inshore that the fog never quite lifts around her."},{"name":"Sunken Chapel Revenant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Drowned chaplain still preaching from a sunken pulpit","flavor":"A ship's chaplain who kept preaching as the water rose past the pulpit, and hasn't stopped since.","desc":"He stands at a pulpit half-submerged, robes waterlogged and translucent, still delivering a sermon that started rising with the tide and never stopped."},{"name":"Drowned Choir Cantor","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"Storm-hymn cantor who calls weather nobody sane wants","flavor":"Leads the storm-hymn from the quarterdeck, calling weather nobody sane would ask for twice.","desc":"She raises both hands at the quarterdeck rail, leading a hymn in a language that sounds liturgical and wrong at the same time, and clouds start answering before she's finished the first verse."},{"name":"Iron-Hulled Corsair Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"pirate-captain","summary":"Three-ship corsair captain, sinker of every bounty-navy sent","flavor":"Runs a fleet of three under false flags, and has personally sunk every navy sent to collect the bounty.","desc":"He stands at the wheel of a ship flying colors that change port to port, three more hulls visible on the horizon behind him, utterly unbothered by the navy flag flying on yours.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"Reef Titan Anemone","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Anemone colony that mimics drowning victims to lure rescuers","flavor":"A hull-sized anemone colony that's learned the shape of a drowning man and mimics it to draw rescuers in.","desc":"A hull-sized bloom of tendrils sways gently in the current, and somewhere in the mass a shape resolves — arms reaching up, a drowning man's silhouette — right before the tendrils close around whoever swam in to help."},{"name":"Gale-Bound Air Elemental Squallwright","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"air-elemental","model":"air-elemental","summary":"Bottled storm-elemental shaken loose in the worst weather","flavor":"Bound into a captain's storm-bottle generations back, and finally shaken loose in the worst possible weather.","desc":"Wind gathers into a visible, spinning shape torn loose of whatever bottle held it for generations, howling loud enough to drown out the storm it arrived inside of."},{"name":"Drowned Duelist Wraith","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Duel-drowned officer's ghost, still gripping his rapier","flavor":"Lost the duel over prize-shares and went over the rail still holding his rapier; he's kept the grip.","desc":"It still grips a rapier in a translucent hand, blade held in perfect dueling form, the grudge over a prize-share never once loosening its fingers even after death."},{"name":"Sahuagin War-Priestess","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Tide-timing sea-devil priestess who calls the surge to war","flavor":"Calls the tide itself into a raid, timing the assault to a surge no surface captain can predict.","desc":"She raises a webbed hand toward the moon, timing an assault to a tidal surge no surface captain could ever predict, chanting the raid into motion syllable by syllable."},{"name":"Boarding-Pike Skeleton Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Disciplined drowned skeleton unit, still holds formation","flavor":"A drilled, disciplined unit of the drowned that still holds formation better than most living marines.","desc":"Ranks of bone hold formation with a discipline that outlasts most living marines, pikes leveled in unison, advancing in lockstep across rotted planking."},{"name":"Waterlogged Chimeric Hulk-Beast","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three drowned sailors fused into one furious hulk","flavor":"Three drowned crewmen fused by whatever curse sank the ship, now sharing one waterlogged, furious body.","desc":"Three drowned crewmen have fused into one bloated, furious body, too many limbs thrashing in a rhythm that doesn't match itself, water sloughing off with every lurch forward."},{"name":"Deep-Baron's Shark-Bonded Enforcer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"sahuagin-baron","model":"sahuagin-baron","summary":"Sea-devil baron who rides a bonded shark into every raid","flavor":"Rides a bonded reef shark into every raid and has never once had to swim himself.","desc":"It rides a bonded reef shark straight over the reef line, one clawed hand fisted in a dorsal fin, and it's never once had to swim on its own."},{"name":"Hurricane-Voiced Storm Herald","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"Unseen wind-scout that finds a ship's weakest rigging first","flavor":"An unseen wind-thing that rides ahead of a hurricane, testing a ship's rigging for the weak point the storm will use.","desc":"Nothing is visible except the wind bending in a shape that shouldn't be possible, testing the rigging line by line for the weak point a hurricane will use an hour later."},{"name":"Cursed Doubloon Wight-Captain","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Gold-cursed wight-captain who conscripts anyone who takes a coin","flavor":"Cursed by the very gold he stole to guard it forever, raising every sailor who touches a coin as his crew.","desc":"Gold coin is stitched into his coat like scale-mail, and his eyes track anyone who so much as glances at a doubloon on the deck. Touch one and you belong to his crew now.","traits":{"note": "any creature that picks up a cursed coin must save or become dominated"}},{"name":"Foundered Frigate's Ghast Bosun","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Foundered frigate's undead disciplinarian, punishment unending","flavor":"Still runs the flogging line on a foundered frigate's ghost-deck, and the punishment never actually ends.","desc":"It paces a flogging line on a ghost-deck that never quite finished sinking, whip-scarred hand raised, still administering a punishment that never technically ends."},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Broodguard","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Half-grown deep-thing guarding a brood-nest, already boat-sized","flavor":"Half-grown but already big enough to take a longboat down whole, guarding the nest for whatever birthed it.","desc":"Half-grown and already the length of a longboat, it coils protectively around a nest none of you can see clearly, tentacles testing the water for anything that gets too close."},{"name":"Drowned Fleet Admiral's Ghost","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Ghost admiral commanding an invisible spectral squadron","flavor":"Still commands a spectral squadron that only he can see, and still expects every ship on the horizon to salute.","desc":"He salutes an empty horizon crisply, expecting every passing ship to answer in kind, commanding a spectral squadron that's visible only to him.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Phantom Broadside", "text": "Calls an invisible spectral ship to fire a ghostly volley at a chosen target."}]}},{"name":"Reef-Cracker Hydra","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Cave-denned hydra scarred by three failed charting attempts","flavor":"Denned in a sea-cave that's swallowed three ships trying to chart it, each head a different scar from the attempts.","desc":"It fills the mouth of a sea-cave that's swallowed three charting expeditions whole, each of its many heads scarred differently by whatever those failed attempts managed to land.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Regrowing Heads", "text": "A severed head is replaced by two new ones unless the stump is seared."}]}},{"name":"Boarding-Fiend Bone Devil","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"bone-devil","summary":"Contracted boarding-fiend, payment terms deliberately vague","flavor":"Contracted by a desperate captain for one impossible raid, and never bothered reading the fine print about payment.","desc":"It clatters over the rail on a barbed tail, contract-bound and clearly annoyed about the terms, sizing up the crew like collateral it never got paid for."},{"name":"Storm-Bound Efreeti Corsair","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"net-new: a fire-wreathed genie bound into a captain's figurehead, steam hissing where flame meets sea-spray","summary":"Figurehead-bound fire-genie granting speed for an unpaid price","flavor":"Bound into a corsair ship's figurehead by a desperate deal, and grants the crew impossible speed for an unpaid price.","desc":"Fire wreathes a genie bound into the ship's own figurehead, steam hissing where flame meets sea-spray, granting the hull a speed no honest ship should manage.","traits":{"note": "the bound ship gains a speed bonus while the efreeti remains fused to the figurehead"}},{"name":"Undertow Terror of the Shoals","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Shoal-burrowing terror that swallows hulls whole from beneath","flavor":"Burrows through sandbars and shoal-mud the way its cousins burrow through snow, swallowing hulls whole from below.","desc":"Sand and shoal-mud churn and collapse without warning, a hull-sized shape moving beneath the surface the way its cousins move through snow, right before something takes the ship's keel from below.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"Pale Fathom Wight-Lord","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Generational wreck-revenant that drags its whole crew back up","flavor":"Rises from a specific wreck-site once a generation, always dragging the whole doomed crew back up with him.","desc":"It rises once a generation from a specific wreck-site, gargantuan and pale as drowned coral, dragging an entire doomed crew back up behind it in a chain of bloated, silent bodies.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "rises with a retinue of lesser wight sailors"}},{"name":"Coral Throne Basilisk-Queen","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Reef-throne guardian that petrifies looters of a drowned crown","flavor":"Coils a sunken palace's reef-throne, petrifying anything that tries to loot the drowned crown beside her.","desc":"She coils across a sunken palace's reef-throne, scaled hide crusted with coral growth, gaze fixed and patient beside a drowned crown that nothing has managed to steal.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"Death-Knight of the Broken Articles","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Blood-oathed undead enforcer of pirate-code violations","flavor":"Signed the Articles in his own blood and died enforcing every clause; still hunts crews who break the code.","desc":"Blood-signed pages are sewn into his pauldron, armor black with rust and salt, and he hunts crews who break the code he died enforcing with the same cold discipline he had in life."},{"name":"Sunken Archmage of the Drowned Spire","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"archmage","summary":"Two-centuries-drowned archmage still mid-spell in his tower","flavor":"Went down with his tower-ship still casting, and hasn't noticed two centuries pass underwater.","desc":"He still stands mid-gesture in a drowned tower, robes drifting weightless around him, a spell frozen half-cast two centuries after the water should have stopped him."},{"name":"Nightbringer of the Drowned Fleet","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Shipboard vampire quietly turning a becalmed fleet's crew","flavor":"Turned in his own cabin during a becalmed crossing, and has been quietly recruiting the fleet ever since.","desc":"He moves through a becalmed fleet's decks unseen by moonlight, cape settled, teeth just visible when he smiles at a crewman he's already decided to visit tonight."},{"name":"The Bilge-Born Horror","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"Hold-grown horror that sees through the deck planks above","flavor":"Grew in the dark of a cursed hold on a diet of drowned stowaways, and sees every deck above it through the planks.","desc":"A single vast eye opens somewhere in the dark of a cursed hold, and the deck planks above seem thinner suddenly, like it can see straight through them to whoever's standing there.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"The Drowned Doge","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"net-new: a bloated, crown-wearing merchant-lord corpse enthroned on a barnacled chair of fused coin","summary":"Drowned merchant-lord enthroned over the port he sank","flavor":"Bankrolled the fleet that sank an entire rival port, and now presides drowned over the wreckage he bought.","desc":"Bloated and crowned, he sits enthroned on a chair of fused coin in the wreckage of the very port his fleet sank, water sloughing endlessly off silk robes that never dry.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Drowned Court", "text": "Commands nearby undead crew as an extension of his enthroned will."}]}},{"name":"The Ninth Wave Herald","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Huge","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"net-new: a churning wall-wave given a face, lightning threading through its curling crest like veins","summary":"Sentient storm-wave that is the reason the ninth wave is worst","flavor":"Sailors swear the ninth wave in any storm is always the worst; this is why, and it knows the superstition is true.","desc":"A wall of water rises higher than any wave before it, lightning threading its curling crest like veins, and it knows exactly why sailors always fear the ninth one worst.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"The Deathless Mutiny","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"dracolich","model":"net-new: a fused mass of mutineers' corpses forming one many-armed horror","summary":"Fused mass of every drowned mutiny, wearing a stolen captain's coat","flavor":"Every crew that ever turned on its captain and drowned for it feeds this thing; it wears whichever coat the nearest mutiny needs.","desc":"Dozens of mutineers' corpses have fused into one many-armed horror, wearing whichever stolen captain's coat the nearest doomed crew still needs, hands still reaching for a wheel none of them ever earned.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"The Sunken Cathedral's Choir Eternal","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"lich","model":"net-new: a coral-crowned lich enthroned in a drowned cathedral nave","summary":"Lich-chaplain still preaching to a two-century-drowned congregation","flavor":"A ship's chaplain who lichified himself to keep preaching to a congregation that drowned two centuries ago and never left.","desc":"A coral crown sits on a lich enthroned in a drowned cathedral's nave, still preaching to pews of the dead that never left, voice carrying through water like it was air.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Undying Sermon", "text": "Nearby undead gain resistance while the lich continues its unbroken sermon."}]}},{"name":"The Maw That Charts No Course","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Chartless leviathan that swallows convoys from no fixed direction","flavor":"Surfaces on no chart and no schedule, swallowing whole convoys, and every survivor swears a different direction it came from.","desc":"The sea splits open with no warning and no pattern, a gargantuan maw surfacing to swallow a convoy whole, and every survivor who lives to tell it swears it came from a different direction.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"}},{"name":"the Drowned Captain","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"pirate-captain","summary":"undead ship's-master, obsessed and unable to stop commanding","flavor":"Lashed to a wheel that rotted out from under him decades ago, he still barks headings to a crew that stopped answering. Cross his wake and he'll press every soul aboard into one more hunt.","desc":"Lashed to a wheel that rotted through decades ago, he still barks headings into the fog, jaw working around orders a crew stopped answering long before you were born. His eyes fix on your ship's wake like it owes him a debt.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Press the Crew", "text": "A creature slain within reach rises to serve him for the rest of the encounter."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"generic mad-captain figure in the vein of Melville's Ahab (1851, PD) — our own obsessive, not Ahab himself"},{"name":"Bosun Wormwood","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"rank-and-file cutlass pirate, first over the rail","flavor":"Every crew needs someone to swing first and count the take later. He's not smart, he's not brave, but there's always another one behind him.","desc":"He's already halfway over the rail before the others, cutlass swinging wide and careless, grinning like the take's already counted. He isn't smart and he isn't brave — he's just first, and there's always another one behind him.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock cutthroat-pirate-mook archetype (uncopyrightable stock type)"},{"name":"the Bone Quartermaster","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton","summary":"undead crewman, ledger-obsessed and cutlass-armed","flavor":"He still keeps the manifest, tallying cargo that turned to silt a hundred years back. Argue with his math and he'll settle it with a cutlass.","desc":"He balances a waterlogged manifest on one bony forearm, tallying cargo that turned to silt a hundred years back in a voice like grinding shell. Argue the numbers and the cutlass at his hip does the correcting.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"undead-crew archetype built on the ghost-ship stock trope"},{"name":"the Kraken","cr":23,"role":"apex","type":"aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"the mythic apex sea-titan, rarely surfaces, never forgotten","flavor":"Sailors call it a myth right up until the sea stands up around their ship. It doesn't hunt for food anymore — it hunts because something that old resents being disturbed.","desc":"The sea doesn't part so much as stand up — an arm thicker than a mast breaking the surface, then another, then the water itself seeming to rise around the ship like a wall closing in. It isn't hunting for food. Something that old is simply done being disturbed.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Crushing Grasp", "text": "Multiple tentacle attacks can grapple and constrict a ship's hull simultaneously."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse/Scandinavian sea-monster legend, pre-modern folklore (also the Alfred Tennyson sonnet, 1830, PD)"},{"name":"Moby, the White Whale","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"beast","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"dragon-turtle","summary":"the pale, unkillable whale that turns and fights back","flavor":"Pale as bone and scarred by a hundred failed harpoons, it doesn't flee ships — it turns and comes back for them. Some captains hunt it for the bounty. Others hunt it because they can't stop.","desc":"Pale as bone against the dark water, its hide is a map of old harpoon scars, and it doesn't flee the way whales are supposed to — it turns, slow and deliberate, and comes straight back at whoever struck first.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Melville, Moby-Dick (1851, PD) — the whale itself, not any adaptation's design"},{"name":"a Siren","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"reef-perched singer whose song offers exhausted sailors relief","flavor":"The song doesn't promise treasure or lust — it promises rest, which is worse, because half the crew actually wants that. She only has to be patient; the rocks do the rest.","desc":"She sits on a reef-rock combing her hair, voice pitched low and warm, and the song isn't promising treasure or lust — it's promising rest. That's the part that gets half the crew to lean toward the rocks without meaning to.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Song of Rest", "text": "Creatures who fail a save move toward the siren, ignoring the danger of the rocks."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — the Sirens (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"a Siren-Flock Screecher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"young siren, screeches and dives rather than enchants","flavor":"Not every siren has the voice for the killing song — the young ones just shriek and dive-bomb, hoping to knock a sailor loose from the rigging while their elders finish the job.","desc":"It doesn't have the killing song yet — it just shrieks and dive-bombs the rigging, wings beating hard enough to knock a climbing sailor loose while the elders finish what it started.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — the Sirens, junior/flock member"},{"name":"Scylla","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"strait-bound many-headed horror, takes a toll from every passing hull","flavor":"She doesn't chase ships — she waits in the same strait she's waited in since before anyone's grandmother, and takes exactly one sailor from every hull that passes too close to her side.","desc":"Six heads rear up from the strait's rock-face all at once, jaws snapping in different directions, patient in a way that says she's done this exactly the same way since before anyone's grandmother sailed here. She only ever takes one.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "each head can make a separate attack against a different target in reach"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Scylla, the six-headed strait-monster (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"the Charybdis Maw","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"living whirlpool that swallows the strait on a rhythm","flavor":"Not a creature so much as an appetite the sea itself grew — three times a day the strait empties into her throat and nothing caught in the pull ever argues its way back out.","desc":"The strait doesn't just have a current — it has an appetite, water spiraling down into a throat that opens on its own rhythm three times a day, and anything caught in the pull doesn't get the chance to argue.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "the whirlpool's pull intensifies on a fixed cycle rather than at will"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Charybdis, the whirlpool-monster paired with Scylla (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"the Flying Dutchman's Wheelman","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"the cursed ghost-ship itself, animate and hunting for crew","flavor":"Doomed to round the same cape forever, the ship's own helm has become a creature of splintered wood and drowned will — it doesn't want passengers, it wants company in the doom.","desc":"The ship itself has become the creature — splintered wood knit into something like a hull-shaped body, the wheel fused into where a chest should be. It doesn't want passengers. It wants company in a doom it's rounding the same cape to keep.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Flying Dutchman — Cape maritime legend, pre-modern folklore (first written accounts 18th c.)"},{"name":"a Dutchman Deckhand","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"waterlogged member of the cursed eternal crew","flavor":"Soaked through and past caring, they still haul the same lines they died hauling. Boarding one ship is the same as boarding the next, to them — the work never ends.","desc":"It hauls the same line it died hauling, soaked through past caring, and boarding your ship registers to it exactly the same as boarding the next one would. The work never ends and it stopped minding a long time ago.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Flying Dutchman legend — the doomed crew, pre-modern folklore"},{"name":"Davy Jones's Chain-Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"drowned-sailor ghoul climbing up from the seabed locker","flavor":"Every drowned sailor goes to the Locker eventually, the old saying goes — and some of them claw back up the anchor chain first, still hungry for one more meal above the waterline.","desc":"It claws up an anchor chain out of black water, locker-pale and still hungry, dragging itself hand over hand toward the waterline like the old sailors' saying about the Locker is something it's personally trying to disprove.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Davy Jones's Locker — sailors' folk-idiom for the seabed afterlife, maritime folklore (not a specific character design)"},{"name":"the Locker-Warden","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"marid","model":"marid","summary":"the folkloric seabed afterlife given a keeper, vast and patient","flavor":"Every sailor swears the Locker has a keeper who counts the dead as they settle. Whether that's true or just something sailors tell each other in a storm, something down there is definitely counting.","desc":"It waits in the dark below where the sailors' stories say the dead settle, vast and patient, and whether the counting is a myth or not, something down there is unmistakably keeping tally.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Davy Jones's Locker folk-idiom, personified as its own keeper — our invention on the folklore, not a claimed character"},{"name":"a Sea Hag of the Shoals","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"sea-hag","summary":"reef-dwelling hag who barters weather for confessions","flavor":"She trades storms for secrets and secrets for storms, and never tells you which one you actually bought. Sailors leave offerings on the reef so she'll look the other way.","desc":"She crouches at the reef line surrounded by small offerings left by sailors hoping she'll look away, and her bargain is always the same shape — a storm for a secret, though she never says which one you actually paid for.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"folk sea-hag figure, generic maritime witch-crone (not tied to any single copyrighted work)"},{"name":"a Sahuagin Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"reef-raiding fish-humanoid, opportunistic wreck-stripper","flavor":"They rise off the reef in packs when a hull rides too low and too slow, stripping a wreck bare before the survivors even reach the boats.","desc":"It rises off the reef in a loose pack formation, webbed claws already reaching for whatever's loose on deck, stripping a wreck bare before the survivors even reach the boats.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic fish-humanoid raider archetype (own deep-water raider framing, no external IP)"},{"name":"a Sahuagin Depth-Priest","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"deep cult priest who blesses reef-raids with dread invocations","flavor":"He blesses the raids in a tongue that predates any surface language, and the raiders fight harder for it — not out of faith exactly, more like fear of what he'd do if they didn't.","desc":"It chants in a tongue older than any surface language, low and guttural, and the raiders around it fight harder — not devotion exactly, more the particular fear of what happens if they don't.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic fish-humanoid priest archetype, own deep-sea cult framing"},{"name":"a Merrow Wrecker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"merrow","summary":"brutish sea-ogre that swarms wrecks for the meal, not the loot","flavor":"Not clever, just strong and hungry and drawn to the sound of splintering hulls. A merrow doesn't wreck ships for treasure — treasure's just what's left after it eats.","desc":"It surges up hungry and brutish, drawn by the sound of splintering wood, muscle rippling under green-gray hide. Treasure is just what's left over after it eats — it isn't clever enough to want it first.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic ogre-of-the-sea archetype (folkloric merrow stock type, no specific IP)"},{"name":"the Bosun's Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"haunting ship's-officer whose whistle warns (or curses) the crew","flavor":"He still walks his rounds belowdecks, and any living sailor who hears his whistle in the dark knows to brace for something going badly wrong topside within the hour.","desc":"A thin whistle carries through the dark below-decks before anything else does, and any sailor who's heard it before knows to brace — because within the hour, something topside always goes badly wrong.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic maritime-haunting archetype — the officer who died on duty and can't leave it"},{"name":"a Corsair Deckhand","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"nimble boarding-raider, cuts lines before the main assault","flavor":"Fast over the rigging and faster with a knife, these are the ones sent ahead to cut lines and douse lanterns before the boarding party even shows itself.","desc":"Fast over the rigging and faster with a knife, it's already cutting lines and dousing lanterns before the rest of the boarding party has even shown its face.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic historical-corsair mook archetype — long-dead seafaring raider figure, not any named individual"},{"name":"the Storm-Bound Djinn","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"djinni","summary":"elemental genie fused into a waterspout, capricious and huge","flavor":"Bound into a waterspout centuries ago by a captain who never wrote down how, it now answers to no one and drags whole ships skyward just to watch them fall.","desc":"A waterspout twists upright out of calm water, a genie's shape barely visible inside the spinning wall, and it drags whole ships skyward on a whim just to watch them fall.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"elemental sea-storm archetype drawn from the broad genie/elemental stock type of maritime legend"},{"name":"the Wrecking Reef-Wraith","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"drowned wrecker's ghost, still luring ships onto the rocks","flavor":"In life it lit false beacon-fires to lure ships onto the rocks for salvage. In death it just lights the fires — there's no cargo left to want, only the habit.","desc":"A pale light bobs along the shoals where a beacon-fire used to burn, drowned and translucent now, still lighting the same false signal it once used to lure ships onto rocks — there's no cargo left to want, only the habit.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic ghost-of-the-shoals archetype — the drowned wrecker who lured ships onto rocks in life"}],
 "lost-world":[{"name":"Sand-Choked Sentry","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"classic bone guardian, forever walking its post","flavor":"A picked-clean guard still standing post at a gate nobody uses, sand pouring from its ribs.","desc":"Sand pours from between its ribs when it turns, a thin dry hiss like a held breath let out. It carries a spear worn to a splinter and stands its post at a gate that opens onto nothing but more ruin. The joints grind with each step, patient as erosion."},{"name":"Glyph-Warded Scarab Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"tomb-curse insect swarm guarding a sealed door","flavor":"A living seal poured into a doorway generations ago; disturb the lintel and the carpet of beetles rises.","desc":"The threshold looks paved until it moves — a shifting carpet of black shells clicking against each other in the dark. Lift your torch and the whole floor lifts with it, a wet chitinous roar rising off the stone. It was poured into that doorway on purpose, generations ago, and it has never once stopped guarding it."},{"name":"Sun-Fat Ridgeback","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"oversized lizard basking among fallen ruins","flavor":"A sun-fat lizard the size of a hound, sunning on toppled cornices until your shadow crosses it.","desc":"It suns itself on a toppled cornice, scaled hide gone the color of the surrounding dust, gorged and slow to move. Only the flick of a lidless eye tracks you crossing its patch of shade. When it finally rouses, it's with the unhurried confidence of something that has never had to hurry."},{"name":"Linen-Wrapped Shambler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"rot-wrapped shambler retracing a dead ritual","flavor":"A pilgrim mummified mid-step by the dry wind, still shuffling a processional route no one remembers.","desc":"Dry wind mummified it mid-stride, and mid-stride is how it still moves — a stiff, marching shuffle down a processional route no living thing remembers the destination of. Linen wrappings have gone the color of the sand it walks through. It does not look at you; it has somewhere to be."},{"name":"Blind Archive-Gnawer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"blind vermin swarm infesting the buried archive","flavor":"Pale, sightless rat-things nesting in the archive halls for a thousand years, chewing scrolls no one will miss.","desc":"Pale, sightless shapes boil out from between shelves of scroll-cases at the first vibration of a footstep, whiskers twitching toward sound instead of sight. A thousand years underground has bleached them the color of old parchment. They've eaten most of the archive already, and they are not picky about what comes next."},{"name":"Cracked Watch-Idol","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"animated stone idol stuck on an endless patrol","flavor":"A hollow votive statue jerking through a guard pattern it can no longer complete without falling over.","desc":"Stone limbs jerk through half a guard pattern before the motion runs out and it has to start over, joints grinding rock dust with every restart. A crack runs the length of its once-painted face. It has forgotten every step of the drill except that there is one."},{"name":"Vine-Choked Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-wolf-spider","model":"giant-wolf-spider","summary":"venomous ambush-spider lurking in overgrown ruins","flavor":"Something fat and patient in the vines strangling the ornamental garden; it strikes from beneath the flowers.","desc":"The ornamental garden has gone to seed and something fat and patient lives in what it became, hidden beneath a carpet of dead blossoms. Silk lines run taut between the broken trellises, invisible until they aren't. It waits for the flowers to move on their own."},{"name":"Bone-Orchard Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"scavenger jackal pack circling grave robbers","flavor":"Pack scavenger that has learned tomb-robbers mean an easy meal; it circles at the treeline, waiting for the digging to stop.","desc":"They keep to the treeline in loose, watchful knots, ribs showing, ears pricked toward the sound of digging. Generations of easy meals have taught the pack that grave robbers mean an open larder. They don't attack first — they wait for you to stop shoveling."},{"name":"Curse-Bound Grave Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"paralyzing ghoul, once a fellow tomb-raider","flavor":"Someone who broke the same seal you're about to break, and never made it back out.","desc":"It crouches over what's left of the last person who broke this seal, knuckles dragging, jaw unhinged wider than a living jaw should go. Torn cloth still clings to it — someone's expedition gear, cut for someone your size. Its eyes track you with recognition it shouldn't have."},{"name":"Snake-Cult Zealot","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-infiltrator","model":"cultist","summary":"fanged serpent-cultist guarding forbidden rites","flavor":"A serpent-blooded devotee who kept the old faith alive underground long after the empire fell, fangs bared under a ceremonial mask.","desc":"A ceremonial mask hides everything but the mouth, and the mouth is full of filed, fanged teeth bared beneath painted lips. It keeps the old rites alive down here long after the empire that banned them crumbled. It hisses the invocation before it draws steel, like it still expects an audience."},{"name":"Wall-Set Spear-Guard","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"bandaged vizier still guarding an empty throne","flavor":"The last vizier, wound in the same linens as the dead-tongue king it still serves, delivering proclamations to an empty throne room.","desc":"Bandages the color of the throne room's dust wrap a vizier still delivering proclamations no one is left to hear, spear held at present-arms before an empty seat. Its voice, when it speaks at all, comes out in the dead tongue of a court that has been gone for centuries. It will not move from its post while the throne remains unoccupied."},{"name":"Plinth-Fused Sentinel","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"stone temple guardian bound to bar the sanctum","flavor":"A carved guardian fused to its plinth, sworn to never let the inner sanctum see a second dawn of daylight.","desc":"Its lower half has fused into the plinth it was carved to stand on, stone grown into stone across the centuries. What was meant to be a statue with a duty has become a duty with a statue's patience. It swings its arms free of the plinth only when the sanctum door is disturbed — and only that far."},{"name":"Riddle-Keeper of the Threshold","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-secrets","model":"sphinx-of-lore","summary":"riddling sphinx guarding the tomb's final gate","flavor":"A stone-eyed watcher at the last unbroken gate, bound to test any who'd pass with a question the builders thought unanswerable.","desc":"Stone eyes track you the length of the last unbroken gate, a question already forming on lips that have asked it a thousand times before. The builders thought the riddle unanswerable and built the whole tomb around that confidence. It has all the time in the world for you to be wrong."},{"name":"Raptor of the Ruined Plaza","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"allosaurus","model":"allosaurus","summary":"pack-hunting raptor stalking the ruined plaza","flavor":"A lean pack-hunter that has ruled the crumbled plaza for generations, using fallen colonnades as blinds.","desc":"It uses the fallen colonnades as blinds, feathers dust-grey against the broken stone, moving in short low-shouldered bursts between cover. Claw marks score every column at throat height. This plaza has been its hunting ground for generations, and it knows every sightline better than you ever will."},{"name":"Living Armor-Back","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"ankylosaurus","model":"ankylosaurus","summary":"club-tailed armored dinosaur, unstoppable and slow","flavor":"A slow tank of a beast that has worn a path through the sacred road for so long its footprints are mistaken for paving.","desc":"Its shell has worn its own trail across the sacred road, a groove deep enough that travelers mistake the footprints for paving stones. The club-tail drags a furrow behind it, slow and unstoppable as a tide going out. Nothing here has found a way to make it hurry."},{"name":"Horned Terror of the Sacred Road","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"triceratops","summary":"three-horned dinosaur charging trespassers on sight","flavor":"A three-horned bull of a beast that charges anything crossing its stretch of the ceremonial highway.","desc":"Three horns lower the instant your shadow crosses its stretch of the ceremonial highway, a warning it gives exactly once. Old scars crisscross its frill from previous trespassers who didn't heed it. When it charges, the ground answers before the sound does."},{"name":"The Weeping Cistern","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"corrosive ooze filling a flooded sacred bath","flavor":"Ceremonial water gone wrong across centuries of stagnation and old magic, filling the sunken bath-hall.","desc":"What was once holy water sits black and thick in the sunken bath-hall, centuries of stagnation and old rites curdled into something that moves against its own currents. A film on the surface parts wherever it reaches upward. The ripples reach the edges of the pool long before anything else does."},{"name":"Marching Colossus of the Processional","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"towering stone statue still marching a dead parade","flavor":"A processional statue built to march the ceremonial road once a generation; the ceremony stopped, but nobody told the statue.","desc":"It was built to walk the ceremonial road once a generation, and the ceremony has been dead for longer than anyone remembers — but the statue was never informed. Its enormous stone feet strike the flagstones in a rhythm centuries out of step with any living calendar. It marches whether or not there's a road left to march."},{"name":"Basalt Gaze of the Garden","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"snake-haired guardian posing as garden statuary","flavor":"Cursed by the same magic that petrified the garden's statuary, she has become one more monument in a courtyard full of them — until she moves.","desc":"She stands among the courtyard's other statuary so convincingly that you'll walk past her twice before the third glance catches a tremor in stone that shouldn't move. Snake-hair coils slow against her shoulders, testing the air. The same curse that petrified the garden made her one more monument in it — until she turns to look at you."},{"name":"Coiled Warden of the Inner Vault","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"guardian-naga","model":"guardian-naga","summary":"giant guardian serpent coiled around the vault door","flavor":"A serpentine spirit bound by the builders to guard the innermost vault, ancient and imperturbably patient with intruders.","desc":"Its coils fill the passage in front of the vault door, ancient scales dulled to the color of old bronze, head raised at exactly the height of your eyes. The builders bound it here to outlast them, and it has. It watches you with the imperturbable patience of something that has never once needed to move first."},{"name":"Throne-Ape of the Fallen Grove","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-ape","model":"giant-ape","summary":"worshipped ape-god ruling the collapsed temple grove","flavor":"A colossal ape the ruin's people once worshipped as a living god; it still holds court over the collapsed temple grove, and it still expects tribute.","desc":"It holds court on a pile of collapsed masonry that used to be a temple, still expecting the tribute its worshippers stopped bringing generations ago. Its knuckles are the size of your skull and it drums them idly on stone whenever it's displeased. This was its grove before it was anyone's ruin, and it plans to keep it that way."},{"name":"Ever-Marching Automaton King","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"golem king still guarding a throne that's empty","flavor":"A war-engine built in the last king's image to defend the throne room forever; its coronation speech still loops, garbled, from a mouth that was never meant to speak this long.","desc":"A garbled coronation speech loops from a mouth that was never built to speak this long, syllables worn down to static by centuries of repetition. It was cast in the last king's image to defend a throne room that has nothing left to defend. Its clay joints have cracked and been patched with clay again, over and over, for longer than any dynasty lasted."},{"name":"Apex Titan-Lizard","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"tyrannosaurus-rex","model":"tyrannosaurus-rex","summary":"apex tyrant-lizard ruling the collapsed dome","flavor":"The garden's true owner now — a saurian titan that has claimed the collapsed dome as its den, indifferent to the empire whose bones it sleeps on.","desc":"It has claimed the collapsed dome as a den, sleeping across the bones of an empire it has no notion ever existed. Broken columns crack under its shifting weight like kindling. It doesn't rule here out of ambition — it simply never met anything that told it no."},{"name":"The Unread King","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"the mummified god-king, cursed and finally waking","flavor":"The god-king himself, entombed with a dead language carved into his sarcophagus so no living mouth could ever again pronounce his true name — and no living hand could ever again wake him. Someone always finds a way.","desc":"The sarcophagus lid is carved in a dead script no living mouth could pronounce — that was the whole point, once. Now the seals are broken and the wrappings stir on their own, and something ancient and patient is remembering how to breathe. It rises the way stone settles: slow, certain, and past the point where anyone can stop it."},{"name":"The Standing Monument","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"gargantuan stone colossus that never stopped watching","flavor":"The greatest work of the vanished builders — a titan raised to watch the horizon until the world ended, animated by a will so patient it has outlasted every empire since, including the one that made it.","desc":"It was raised to watch the horizon until the world ended, and the world has tried several times since without managing it. Gargantuan and eroded, it still turns — one degree a decade, one degree a season, however fast its patience allows — toward whatever disturbs it. Every empire that built temples in its shadow is gone; the shadow remains."},{"name":"Sun-Baked Scrap Raptor","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"Small pack raptor darting between ruined stones","flavor":"A pack-hunting lizard the size of a hound, quick to swarm anything that stumbles.","desc":"Small enough to hide behind a single fallen block, quick enough that you never see more than one at a time — until the rest call in from the ruins around you. Sun-bleached feathers blend into the rubble almost perfectly. It hunts in numbers it never lets you count."},{"name":"Feathered Sickle-Claw","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"axe-beak","model":"axe-beak","summary":"Feathered raptor slashing with a hooked hind claw","flavor":"A quick-footed hunter with a slashing rear claw, common in the temple scrub.","desc":"It holds one clawed foot cocked back off the ground as it stalks the temple scrub, saving the hooked hind talon for the killing stroke. Dust-colored feathers ripple along its spine when it tenses. The strike, when it lands, comes low and fast and from an angle you didn't expect."},{"name":"Sickle-Toed Ambush Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"net-new: a pair of raptors flanking prey between broken columns","summary":"Coordinated raptor pair flanking around fallen columns","flavor":"Coordinated raptors that flank prey between broken columns.","desc":"They come from both sides of the broken colonnade at once, flanking without a sound signal passing between them — pure instinct, honed over generations of driving prey between fallen pillars. One drives, one waits. You rarely see the second until it's already committed."},{"name":"Withered Grave-Servant","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Shuffling tomb-slave still walking its funeral circuit","flavor":"A tomb-slave animated by lingering funerary rites, shuffling in endless circuits.","desc":"Its funeral circuit takes it past the same three tomb-doors, over and over, a duty its body remembers though the rites that bound it ended lifetimes ago. Grave wrappings hang in tatters from limbs gone the color of old rope. It doesn't attack so much as collide, indifferent to whether you're in its path."},{"name":"Salt-Cured Husk","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Salt-cured husk shambling with brittle relentlessness","flavor":"Preserved by desert salts rather than proper rites, brittle but relentless.","desc":"Desert salts did the preserving work no priest was left to perform, curing the corpse brittle instead of whole. Its skin has crystallized in patches that catch torchlight like broken glass. It moves in short, jerking lurches, and every one of them is stronger than it looks."},{"name":"Rattling Ossuary Ward","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Wire-bound bones standing eternal watch over bones","flavor":"Bones bound with copper wire to stand eternal watch over an ossuary door.","desc":"Copper wire binds its bones tight enough that it rattles a full second before it moves, a warning bell built right into its joints. It stands eternal watch over an ossuary door stacked floor to ceiling with the dead it's meant to guard. The wire has gone green with age, but it hasn't loosened."},{"name":"Loose-Jointed Tomb Archer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"net-new: a rattling bone-guard still loosing arrows down a processional hall","summary":"Bone-guard still loosing arrows down the hall","flavor":"Old bone-guards still loosing arrows down processional halls.","desc":"Its bow-arm still draws and looses down the processional hall on a rhythm set into its bones generations ago, arrows nocked from a quiver that never quite empties. Joints clatter loose with each shot, held together by will more than sinew. It doesn't aim so much as fire along the line it was set to guard, and anything standing in that line is the target."},{"name":"Dune-Coiled Fang Serpent","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"net-new: a coiled venomous serpent nesting in a cracked idol plinth","summary":"Venomous serpent nesting in a cracked plinth","flavor":"Nests in cracked idol plinths, strikes at intruding feet.","desc":"It nests coiled inside a cracked idol plinth, scales the exact color of the surrounding sand, invisible until the strike. Venom beads visibly at its fangs even at rest. Disturb the plinth and you'll feel it before you see it."},{"name":"Constrictor of the Choked Aqueduct","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"constrictor-snake","model":"net-new: a heavy-bodied serpent coiled against wet aqueduct stone","summary":"Heavy serpent squeezing prey against wet stone","flavor":"A heavy-bodied snake that squeezes prey against aqueduct stone.","desc":"It hangs coiled against wet stone where the aqueduct still weeps groundwater, scales slick and dark against the mineral streaks. The whole passage smells faintly of standing water and something dead nearby. It doesn't strike so much as fall, and then it doesn't let go."},{"name":"Sun-Cult Acolyte","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Robed acolyte chanting to unanswering old gods","flavor":"A robed devotee chanting to gods the ruins no longer answer.","desc":"A robed figure kneels before a sun-disk that hasn't answered a prayer in centuries, chanting anyway in a voice gone hoarse from repetition. The paint on the disk has flaked to bare stone. Faith, down here, has long since stopped requiring evidence."},{"name":"Dead-Tongue Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"net-new: a gaunt initiate muttering an extinct liturgical language","summary":"Initiate half-mad from an extinct liturgical tongue","flavor":"Trains in the extinct liturgical language, half-mad from isolation.","desc":"He mutters the liturgical language under his breath constantly now, even between rites, half-mad from years of isolated study in a tongue no one else living speaks. His eyes track motion but rarely seem to register what it means. He'll answer questions only in a language you can't understand."},{"name":"Scaled Temple-Guard","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Hardened spear-guard sworn to a dead dynasty","flavor":"A hardened spear-bearer sworn to a dynasty centuries gone.","desc":"He's sworn an oath to a dynasty that ended before his grandfather was born, and he hasn't been told the vow expired. His spear is well-maintained despite the ruin of everything around him. He guards a door that leads to nothing now but rubble, and he takes the job seriously anyway."},{"name":"Feather-Cloaked Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"hobgoblin-soldier","summary":"Plumed sentinel marching the crumbling outer wall","flavor":"Marches the outer wall in molting ceremonial plumage.","desc":"Ceremonial plumage molts from his shoulders as he marches the crumbling outer wall in a pattern that once had honor guards flanking him and now has none. His boots follow a groove worn into the stone by decades of the same route. He salutes fallen colonnades as if someone were still watching."},{"name":"Idol-Cracked Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"jackal","model":"net-new: a scavenger jackal denning beneath a toppled idol","summary":"Scavenger jackal denning beneath a toppled idol","flavor":"A scavenger pack that dens beneath toppled idols.","desc":"The pack dens beneath a toppled idol's outstretched arm, using the stone as shade and shelter both. They're smaller than the plaza jackals, quicker to scatter, quicker to circle back. A low growl rises from the shadow under the idol before you see a single one of them."},{"name":"Grave-Wasp Nest Cluster","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-wasp","model":"net-new: a wasp nest cluster swarming out of a hollow sarcophagus","summary":"Wasp nest swarming from a hollow sarcophagus","flavor":"Nests inside hollow sarcophagi, swarming any disturbance.","desc":"The hollow sarcophagus hums before it's disturbed — a low papery vibration that means the nest inside has already noticed you. Break the seal and the swarm boils out in a column thick enough to blot the torchlight. They don't stop at the lid; they follow."},{"name":"Chittering Reliquary Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"net-new: a scarab swarm boiling out of a cracked reliquary","summary":"Scarab swarm boiling from a cracked reliquary","flavor":"Scarabs boiling out of a cracked reliquary at the first footstep.","desc":"The reliquary's crack widens with a dry chittering sound just before the scarabs pour out, a black tide across the floor and up the walls both. It's a tomb-curse poured into a vessel generations ago, still doing its one job. It rises at the first footstep and doesn't stop until you're gone or it's satisfied you are."},{"name":"Rope-Fanged Pit Viper","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"venomous-snake","model":"net-new: a coiled viper hidden in a false-bottomed coffin","summary":"Coiled viper hidden in a false-bottomed coffin","flavor":"Coils in false-bottomed sarcophagi as a trap-maker's last defense.","desc":"The coffin's false bottom hides more than a trap-maker's final defense — it hides a coiled length of muscle and venom that strikes the instant the seal breaks. Its scales mimic the grain of old rope so closely you'll swear the coffin's binding just moved. One bite is all the trap needs to work."},{"name":"Choke-Vine Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"net-new: a creeping vine blight rooted in cracked temple flagstone","summary":"Creeping vine blight rooted in cracked flagstone","flavor":"A creeping blight rooted in cracked temple flagstone.","desc":"It has rooted itself in a crack running the length of the temple flagstone, vines the color of dried blood coiled tight against the seam. It doesn't move to find prey — it waits for prey to walk across its patch of floor. The first vine wraps an ankle before you notice the others are already moving."},{"name":"Spore-Choked Idol Fungus","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"shrieker-fungus","model":"net-new: a fungal growth on an idol that shrieks when disturbed","summary":"Idol fungus shrieking to summon every guardian","flavor":"Shrieks a warning when disturbed, drawing every guardian in earshot.","desc":"It grows straight out of an idol's open mouth, a pale bloom that looks decorative until something brushes it. The shriek that follows carries the length of the temple and draws every guardian within earshot. It doesn't attack; it just makes sure you're never alone in here for long."},{"name":"Loincloth Grave-Robber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Desperate local looting the same cursed tombs","flavor":"A local desperate enough to loot the same tombs the party is exploring.","desc":"He's dug his way in from a collapsed side-passage, canvas sack half-full of the same relics you came for. Desperation shows plainer than greed on his face — this is a meal, not a fortune, and he knows it. He'll fight for the sack before he'll run from you."},{"name":"Whisper-Idol Cultist Fanatic","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Fanatic convinced the silent idols still listen","flavor":"Speaks in the dead tongue and believes the idols still listen.","desc":"She speaks in the dead tongue with total conviction, certain the silent idols around her are still listening even after everyone else stopped believing that. Ritual scarring runs down both forearms in patterns matching the temple's carvings. Zealotry, not skill, is what makes her dangerous."},{"name":"Broken-Fang Wererat Tomb-Rat","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"net-new: a cursed grave-looter scurrying tomb tunnels as vermin","summary":"Cursed looter scurrying tunnels as vermin","flavor":"A cursed grave-looter who now scurries the tunnels as vermin by night.","desc":"By night it scurries the tunnels as vermin, and only the size gives it away — too big, too deliberate, too aware of where the traps are. It was a looter once, cursed for greed rather than trespass. It still remembers every passage it ever mapped, and it uses that against anyone following the same route."},{"name":"Stalking Sand-Ambusher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"net-new: a spider-shape slipping through desert heat-mirage to ambush","summary":"Ambusher slipping through heat-mirage to strike","flavor":"Slips between the desert's heat-mirage and the material world to strike.","desc":"The desert's heat-mirage shivers wrong just before it steps through, a spider-shape half-real slipping out of the shimmer to strike. It's gone again before the dust it kicked up finishes settling. You never quite see where it went, only where it was."},{"name":"Petrifying Serpent-Crowned Guardian","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"net-new: a stone-eyed guardian statue that petrifies with a glance","summary":"Stone-eyed guardian that petrifies with a glance","flavor":"A carved-looking beast said to have once been a living guard, now stone-eyed.","desc":"It looks carved, the way half the statuary down here looks carved, until its eye finds yours across the chamber. Locals say it was once a living guard, and something about the stillness of its posture makes that easy to believe. Don't look back."},{"name":"Vulture-Headed Carrion Priest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"net-new: a vulture-masked priest presiding over open-air excarnation rites","summary":"Vulture-masked priest presiding over excarnation rites","flavor":"Wears a vulture skull mask and presides over open-air excarnation rites.","desc":"A vulture skull mask hides his face as he presides over open-air excarnation rites atop a crumbling platform, ceremonial knife catching what little light reaches down here. The stink of the rite clings to everything around him. He doesn't stop the ceremony for intruders — he just adds them to it."},{"name":"Sarcophagus-Bound Wight Steward","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Undead steward still enforcing dead household order","flavor":"Once the mummy-king's chief steward, still enforcing an outdated household order.","desc":"He still enforces an outdated household order — proper distance from the sarcophagi, proper silence in the antechamber, proper deference to a household that's been dust for centuries. His voice carries the clipped formality of a servant who never once questioned his post. He corrects your posture before he attacks."},{"name":"Blazing Ember-Skull Oracle","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"flameskull","model":"net-new: a burning severed skull muttering fire-lit prophecy","summary":"Astrologer's burning skull still muttering prophecy","flavor":"The severed head of a court astrologer, still muttering prophecy in fire.","desc":"A severed skull hovers wreathed in low blue flame, muttering fragments of prophecy between crackling pops of burning bone. It was a court astrologer once, and it still reads omens in the fire it's made of. The mutter never fully stops, even mid-fight."},{"name":"Broken Wing Terror-Bird","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-axe-beak","model":"giant-axe-beak","summary":"Flightless apex hunter ruling terraced garden ruins","flavor":"A flightless apex predator that once ruled the temple's terraced gardens.","desc":"It can't fly anymore — hasn't been able to for generations — but the terraced gardens it once ruled from above, it now rules from the ground with a stride longer than a man is tall. Its beak alone could open a shield. It moves at a speed the broken wings never suggest."},{"name":"Vault-Sworn Ettin Doorkeeper","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"net-new: a two-headed brute chained to guard a single vault door","summary":"Two-headed brute oath-bound to guard one door","flavor":"Two-headed brute chained by old oath to guard a single vault door.","desc":"Two heads argue in low tones about whether you're worth the effort, chained by an old oath neither of them remembers agreeing to. The chain has rusted into the stone floor around a single vault door. Whatever's inside, it's guarded by something that has had centuries to get tired of guarding it and hasn't."},{"name":"Weretiger Jungle-Stalker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"weretiger","model":"net-new: a cursed hunter prowling the jungle canopy above the ruin","summary":"Cursed hunter prowling the ruin's jungle canopy","flavor":"A cursed hunter who prowls the jungle canopy above the ruin.","desc":"Something moves through the canopy that's grown up above the ruin, silent between branches that shouldn't bear that much weight. Stripes flicker between shadow and sun in a rhythm that's almost hypnotic to track. It prowls the high growth the way it once prowled a jungle that predates the ruin itself."},{"name":"Cracked-Idol Gargoyle Watcher","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Stone guardian animated by residual sun-magic","flavor":"A stone temple guardian animated by residual sun-god magic.","desc":"Residual sun-god magic keeps it moving long after the temple that made it lost its priests, stone wings folded tight against a cracked back. It perches motionless for hours, indistinguishable from decoration, until the light shifts and it doesn't. Dust sifts from the crack whenever it stretches."},{"name":"Ash-Grey Ochre Seep","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"ochre-jelly","model":"net-new: a corrosive ooze seeping through burial-chamber floor cracks","summary":"Corrosive ooze seeping through burial-chamber cracks","flavor":"Seeps through cracks in the burial chamber floor, dissolving the careless.","desc":"It seeps through hairline cracks in the burial chamber floor before you notice the floor has cracks at all, a slow grey advance that dissolves anything careless enough to stand still. The smell is mineral, almost sweet. By the time you see the sheen on the stone, it's already closer than it looks."},{"name":"Hollow-Coffer Gelatinous Vault","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"net-new: a cube-shaped ooze absorbing a tomb corridor's grave goods","summary":"Cube-shaped ooze absorbing centuries of grave goods","flavor":"Fills an entire tomb corridor, absorbing centuries of grave goods.","desc":"It fills the entire corridor wall to wall, translucent and patient, centuries of grave goods suspended inside it like specimens in murky glass. Coins and bone fragments drift past each other in its gut. It doesn't hunt so much as occupy — and the corridor was never wide enough to go around it."},{"name":"Chain-Bound Barrow Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"net-new: a ravenous ghast in rotted chains once served the king's table","summary":"Ravenous ghast once serving the king's table","flavor":"A ravenous grave-thing that once served the mummy-king's table.","desc":"Rotted chains still hang from wrists that once served at the mummy-king's table, dragging with every ravenous lunge. Whatever manners it had in life are long gone, replaced by an appetite that recognizes no rank. It moves faster than the chains suggest it should be able to."},{"name":"Bandaged Falconry Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"net-new: a bandaged ghast tending the tomb's mummified hunting birds","summary":"Ghast tending the tomb's mummified hunting birds","flavor":"Handles the tomb's mummified hunting birds with rotted, careful hands.","desc":"It tends the tomb's mummified hunting birds with a careful, rotted gentleness at odds with everything else about it, arranging feathers on creatures that will never fly again. The birds' glass eyes seem to track alongside its own. Interrupt the ritual and the gentleness disappears entirely."},{"name":"Toppled Minotaur Skeleton Guard","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-skeleton","model":"net-new: a skeletal minotaur guard still pacing its ruined maze","summary":"Skeletal labyrinth-guardian still pacing its maze","flavor":"The bones of a labyrinth-guardian, still pacing its maze in death.","desc":"Bone horns scrape the low ceiling as it paces a maze that collapsed generations before its flesh did, tracing the same dead-end turns from memory alone. It doesn't seem to notice the walls are gone. It still knows every corner of a labyrinth that no longer exists."},{"name":"Grave-Silk Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"net-new: a shrouded poltergeist hurling funerary urns at intruders","summary":"Poltergeist hurling urns at silence-breakers","flavor":"Hurls funerary urns and shrouds at anyone who breaks tomb silence.","desc":"Funerary urns lift off their shelves on their own and fly the moment tomb silence breaks, shrouds snapping like sails in a wind that isn't there. Nothing solid throws them — just an angry absence in the room's cold air. It escalates fast, and it doesn't tire."},{"name":"Zombie-Herd Elephant Carrier","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-zombie","model":"net-new: a shambling zombie elephant still hauling grave-cart chains","summary":"Shambling zombie beast still hauling grave-cart chains","flavor":"A shambling beast of burden still hauling grave-cart chains.","desc":"Grave-cart chains still drag from a rotted harness as the great beast hauls a cart that lost its wheels centuries ago, driven by nothing but habit written into dead muscle. Its hide has gone the grey of ash. It doesn't notice obstacles; it simply keeps pulling through them."},{"name":"Snake-Cult Priest of the Hollow Coil","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"net-new: a chanting priest summoning serpents up from the foundations","summary":"Priest whose chants summon serpents from below","flavor":"Leads chants that draw serpents up from the temple's foundations.","desc":"His chant draws a slow hiss up from cracks in the temple foundation, and the hiss keeps getting closer the longer he's allowed to keep speaking. Scale-patterned tattoos run the length of both arms. Silence him fast, or the foundation stops being empty."},{"name":"Sacrificial Blind Prophet","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-blind-prophet","model":"net-new: a blind prophet claiming to speak for a buried god","summary":"Blind prophet claiming to speak for a buried god","flavor":"Claims to speak for a god buried under the plaza; sometimes right.","desc":"He claims a god lies buried beneath the plaza and speaks with the total certainty of someone who has never once been proven wrong about it. Milk-white eyes track sound rather than shape. Sometimes, uncomfortably, he's right."},{"name":"Wrapped Gladiator of the Sun Pit","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"net-new: a bandage-wrapped undying gladiator dueling an empty arena","summary":"Undying champion still dueling a vanished crowd","flavor":"An undying champion still fighting exhibition duels for a vanished crowd.","desc":"He still fights exhibition duels in an arena with no crowd left to watch, bandaged limbs moving with a showman's flourish that centuries of solitude never wore down. Old chains of office rattle at his wrists between strikes. He salutes an empty box before every bout, including this one."},{"name":"Bog-Sunk Umber Digger","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"umber-hulk","model":"umber-hulk","summary":"Tunneling digger whose gaze cracks minds below","flavor":"Tunnels beneath the temple, its gaze cracking minds through cracked floors.","desc":"Tunnels open in the temple floor without warning, and the thing that made them looks up through the new gap with eyes that crack minds through the crack alone. Chitinous claws the size of shovels have carved half the passages beneath this ruin. Don't meet its gaze; look at your feet instead."},{"name":"Rot-Feathered Bulette Ambusher","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"Burrowing ambusher erupting under temple courtyards","flavor":"Erupts from beneath temple courtyards, scattering worshippers and looters alike.","desc":"The courtyard erupts without a sound of warning — no burrow-scrape, no shifting dust, just stone giving way and a maw the width of a cart underneath it. Worshippers and looters alike learned to walk the courtyard's edges the hard way. It surfaces once and dives again before you can plant your feet."},{"name":"Sun-Forged Earth Colossus Fragment","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"earth-elemental","model":"earth-elemental","summary":"Animate wall-shard powered by buried sun-forges","flavor":"A shard of an ancient wall given animus by buried sun-forges.","desc":"A single shard of an ancient wall has taken on a will of its own, powered by forge-heat still banked somewhere in the foundations below. It moves in slow, grinding lurches, mortar cracking loose with every step. It was part of a building once, and it still thinks like one — immovable, until it isn't."},{"name":"Cinder-Font Fire Warden","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"Warden guarding the mummy-king's eternal brazier","flavor":"Guards the eternal brazier said to keep the mummy-king's tomb warm.","desc":"It guards a brazier said to keep the mummy-king's tomb warm through every century of his sleep, flame-limbs flickering low and steady around the coals. Heat rolls off it in visible waves that warp the passage air. It has never once let the fire go out, and it won't start with you."},{"name":"Rope-Trap Roper of the Deep Shaft","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"roper","model":"roper","summary":"Stalactite-mimic lurking a deep excavation shaft","flavor":"Mimics a stalactite in the temple's deepest excavation shaft.","desc":"It hangs from the excavation shaft's ceiling looking exactly like a stalactite, mineral-streaked and utterly still, until a rope-thin tendril lashes out faster than the eye follows. By the time you notice the texture is wrong, it's already reeling something in. The shaft goes quiet again the instant it's fed."},{"name":"Bloated Refuse-Idol Otyugh","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Refuse-fed horror lurking a forgotten temple well","flavor":"Feeds on centuries of temple refuse dumped down a forgotten well.","desc":"Centuries of temple refuse have been dumped down this forgotten well, and something down there has grown fat and patient on all of it. The smell alone announces it before the tentacles do. It doesn't chase — it simply waits for the well to be disturbed again."},{"name":"Shambling Garden Overgrowth","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Plant","size":"Large","frame":"shambling-mound","model":"net-new: a sentient tangle of vines reclaiming a hanging garden","summary":"Sentient overgrowth reclaiming a hanging garden","flavor":"A reclaimed hanging garden, fully sentient and territorial now.","desc":"The hanging garden reclaimed itself so completely it became something else — fully sentient now, territorial about every inch of the terrace it used to just decorate. Vines the thickness of a man's arm test the air like feelers. It moves slowly enough to seem harmless right up until it doesn't."},{"name":"Ashen Vampire-Spawn Handmaiden","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"net-new: a pale undead handmaiden tending a long-empty throne","summary":"Undead handmaiden still tending an empty throne","flavor":"A royal handmaiden turned undead, still tending an empty throne.","desc":"She still tends an empty throne with the same quiet devotion she gave it in life, dusting a seat no one has sat in for generations, pale and unhurried in the tomb's cold air. Her fingers linger on the armrest a beat too long. She turns from the throne only when something disturbs the room's silence."},{"name":"Wight-Lord of the Processional Guard","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"net-new: an armored wight-lord commanding the marching dead guard","summary":"Undead lord commanding the marching dead guard","flavor":"Commands the lesser dead who still march the ceremonial road.","desc":"He commands the lesser dead who still march the ceremonial road, voice carrying the same clipped authority it held in life, armor rattling with each barked order. The marching dead don't need the orders anymore, but he gives them anyway. Command, it turns out, outlasts the need for it."},{"name":"Sky-Talon Wyvern of the Ziggurat","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"wyvern","model":"wyvern","summary":"Wyvern roosting atop the tallest step-pyramid","flavor":"Roosts atop the tallest step-pyramid, territorial over the whole valley.","desc":"It roosts atop the tallest step-pyramid, territorial over the whole valley below, wings mantled against the wind at the summit. Its shadow crosses the ruins below long before its cry does. Nothing nests this high without a reason to defend the view."},{"name":"Idol-Warped Chimera of Three Gods","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Grafted horror built from three patron-beast idols","flavor":"A grafted horror built from the temple's three patron-beast idols.","desc":"It was grafted from the temple's three patron-beast idols by magic no one fully understood even then, three mismatched heads arguing in three different animal registers. Scorch marks scar the stone around wherever it's fought before. It doesn't move like any one animal — it moves like a compromise none of the three wanted."},{"name":"Eight-Legged Web-Warden of the Vault","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"drider","model":"drider","summary":"Half-cursed drider webbing shut the treasure vault","flavor":"Half-cursed guardian left to web shut the innermost treasure vault.","desc":"Half-cursed and left behind on purpose, it has spent generations webbing the innermost treasure vault shut layer by layer. Silk thick as rope crisscrosses the passage in patterns only it can navigate cleanly. It doesn't guard the treasure so much as bury it under an ever-thickening cocoon."},{"name":"Storm-Song Satyr Revelmaster of Ruins","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"satyr-revelmaster","model":"net-new: a fey satyr holding a feral revel among fallen columns","summary":"Fey revelmaster luring travelers to ruin-feasts","flavor":"Holds feral revels among the fallen columns, luring the reckless in.","desc":"Music drifts from among the fallen columns before you see the source — a wild, half-mad revel with no living guests, held for centuries by something that never noticed the party ended. He beckons travelers in with a grin that promises more than it delivers. The reckless who join him rarely leave in the same shape."},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Vrock Carrion-Caller","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"vrock","model":"net-new: a vulture-headed demon bound to guard forbidden grave-magic","summary":"Summoned scavenger-demon guarding forbidden grave-magic","flavor":"A summoned scavenger-demon bound to guard forbidden grave-magic.","desc":"It was summoned and bound generations ago to guard forbidden grave-magic no one living remembers the purpose of, vulture head cocked at an unnatural angle, tracking scent more than sight. A carrion stink follows it that has nothing to do with anything it's killed recently. It calls out in a register that makes the air itself feel wrong."},{"name":"Serpent-Sworn Lamia of the Oasis Court","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"lamia","model":"net-new: a serpent-bodied lamia charming travelers at a hidden oasis","summary":"Charming oasis fiend feeding on stolen years","flavor":"Charms travelers at a hidden oasis before feeding on their years.","desc":"She holds court at a hidden oasis, serpent coils where her legs should be, charming every traveler who stumbles onto the water before feeding on the years she's charmed out of them. The oasis is real and the water is sweet — that's most of the trick. By the time you notice you've aged, it's already spent."},{"name":"Basalt-Skinned Gorgon of the Sun Gate","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"net-new: a bull-shaped stone construct breathing petrifying dust at a gate","summary":"Bull construct petrifying intruders at the sun gate","flavor":"A bull-shaped construct whose breath turns intruders to stone at the gate.","desc":"Bull-shaped and built of the same stone as the gate it guards, it breathes a fine grey dust that turns intruders to statuary matching the rest of the courtyard. Its hooves strike sparks off the flagstones with every step. The gate has never needed a second line of defense."},{"name":"Nine-Serpent Basalt Hydra Spawn","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Cistern hydra whose heads regrow when severed","flavor":"Guards the temple's central cistern, heads regrowing with each severed strike.","desc":"It guards the temple's central cistern, and every head you take is replaced before the water finishes rippling from the blow. Its many throats hiss in a chorus that never quite synchronizes. The cistern has stayed full for centuries because nothing has ever gotten past it to drain it."},{"name":"Petrified Roc of the High Terraces","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"net-new: a colossal roc nesting atop a crumbling stone terrace","summary":"Colossal roc nesting on the crumbling terrace","flavor":"A colossal bird that nests atop the crumbling highest terrace tier.","desc":"It nests atop the crumbling highest terrace tier, wingspan wide enough to blot out the ruin below when it circles. The stone up here has cracked under the weight of a nest built from broken columns instead of branches. It doesn't dive at trespassers below — it drops boulders instead."},{"name":"Fossil-Chained Behir of the Under-Passage","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Lightning serpent-beast patrolling flooded passages","flavor":"A lightning-scaled serpent-beast that patrols the flooded under-passages.","desc":"It patrols the flooded under-passages with a low electric hum crackling along lightning-scaled flanks, water displacing in slow ripples ahead of its coils. The passage floods deeper wherever it's passed recently. You hear the hum before you see the shape making it."},{"name":"Dune-Sunk Purple Devourer","cr":15,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Colossal worm tunneling beneath the whole valley","flavor":"Tunnels beneath the whole valley, swallowing pilgrims and pillars alike.","desc":"The whole valley trembles faintly whenever it turns beneath the sand, a colossal worm that has swallowed pilgrims and pillars with equal indifference for longer than the ruin has had a name. Dunes shift and collapse into fresh sinkholes without warning. You feel it coming up through your boots before you ever see the sand crack open."},{"name":"Efreeti Bound to the Eternal Forge-Idol","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"efreeti","model":"net-new: a flame-wreathed efreeti chained to stoke an idol-forge","summary":"Bound efreeti stoking the temple's idol forge","flavor":"Bound by old contract to stoke the forge that casts the temple's idols.","desc":"Old contract binds it to stoke the forge that casts the temple's idols, flame-wreathed and visibly resentful of terms it can't break. Molten slag pools where its feet should leave footprints. It works the forge with total competence and zero enthusiasm, and it will absolutely take that resentment out on you instead."},{"name":"Cyclops Oracle of the Buried Eye","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"net-new: a blinded one-eyed giant reading omens in collapsing stone","summary":"Blinded giant seer reading omens in ruined stone","flavor":"A blinded seer-giant who reads omens in the ruins' collapsing stone.","desc":"Blinded on purpose long ago, it reads omens now in the sound and shift of the ruins' collapsing stone, head cocked to catch vibrations you can't feel yet. Its remaining scars run deep across both temples. It'll tell you what's about to happen before it happens — usually too late to matter."},{"name":"Marble-Veined Storm Giant Excavator","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"storm-giant","model":"net-new: a marble-veined giant standing guard over a quarry pit","summary":"Giant quarry-guard who once cut the temple's stones","flavor":"Once quarried the temple's founding stones; still guards the quarry pit.","desc":"It once quarried the very stones this temple was built from, and it still guards the quarry pit those stones came out of, marble veins running visibly under weathered grey skin. Thunder gathers audibly whenever it's provoked. It remembers exactly how many blocks it cut, and it counts them still standing."},{"name":"Death-Cultist Herald of the Buried Sun","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"net-new: a robed cultist preaching that the sun itself lies entombed","summary":"Cultist preaching the sun is entombed, awaiting blood rite","flavor":"Preaches that the sun itself is entombed and can be freed by blood rite.","desc":"He preaches with total conviction that the sun itself lies entombed somewhere below, freeable only by blood spilled at the right hour. Robes stained dark at the hem suggest he's already tried more than once. He doesn't flinch from a fight — he treats it as an offering."},{"name":"Archpriest of the Dead Liturgy","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"net-new: an aged archpriest, last living speaker of a dead tongue","summary":"Last living speaker of the temple's dead liturgy","flavor":"The last living speaker of the temple's true dead language, and its final judge.","desc":"He is the last living speaker of the temple's true dead language, and he has appointed himself its final judge as well as its final voice. Every word he says in the old tongue sounds like both a blessing and a verdict. He judges you before you've said a thing worth judging."},{"name":"Bone-Crowned Death Knight of the Ziggurat","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: a bone-crowned death knight commanding a legion long gone","summary":"Entombed general commanding a legion long gone","flavor":"An entombed general still commanding a legion that no longer exists.","desc":"He still commands a legion that stopped existing generations ago, barking orders into an empty processional yard with total conviction that ranks will form. Bone shards crown a helm gone black with age. The legion he commands may be gone, but the authority in his voice hasn't noticed."},{"name":"Vault-Sealed Naga of the Bone Archive","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-naga","model":"net-new: a serpent-sage naga coiled guarding an archive of the dead","summary":"Serpent-sage guarding the archive of the dead's names","flavor":"A serpent-sage bound to guard the archive of dead names.","desc":"It coils around an archive stacked floor to ceiling with the names of the dead, serpent-sage eyes tracking every scroll case as much as every intruder. It speaks in slow, deliberate syllables, weighing each word like it costs something. The archive has never once lost a name on its watch."},{"name":"Frost-Cracked Abominable Cave-Beast","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Anomalous cold-beast denning in a frost-slick cave","flavor":"An anomalous cold-thing that dens in the temple's deepest, frost-slick cave.","desc":"Cold that has no business existing this deep in a desert ruin radiates off a hulking white shape denning in the temple's lowest, frost-slick cave. Its breath fogs thick in air that shouldn't be cold enough to fog. Nobody built it here, and nobody knows how long it's actually been."},{"name":"Rakshasa Vizier of the Broken Court","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"Fiendish vizier still whispering from the throne's shadow","flavor":"The mummy-king's old advisor, still whispering counsel from the shadows of the throne.","desc":"He still whispers counsel from the shadows behind the throne, the same seat he advised in life, voice smooth and reasonable and entirely untrustworthy. Tiger-striped hands fold politely at his sleeves. He offers you a deal before he offers you a fight, and the deal is worse."},{"name":"The Undying Ape-Colossus of the Sacred Grove","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"net-new: a titanic stone ape-idol animated to punish desecrators","summary":"Titanic ape-idol punishing desecrators of the grove","flavor":"A titanic idol carved in the shape of the ape-god, animated to punish the grove's desecrators.","desc":"Carved titanic in the shape of the grove's ape-god and animated to punish anyone who desecrates it, its shadow alone covers half the fallen temple floor. Moss and vine have grown into the joints without slowing it down. It doesn't ask what you touched — it already knows, and it's already moving."},{"name":"Dragon-Turtle of the Drowned Necropolis","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"net-new: a shelled leviathan wearing a swallowed necropolis like armor","summary":"Shelled leviathan wearing a swallowed necropolis","flavor":"A shelled leviathan that swallowed a lesser necropolis whole and now wears it like armor.","desc":"It swallowed a lesser necropolis whole at some point and now wears the wreckage across its shell like armor, drowned spires jutting at odd angles from between its scutes. Water sheets off it in waterfalls when it surfaces. Tombs still visible on its back suggest this has happened more than once."},{"name":"The First Priest-King, Undying","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"demilich","model":"net-new: a jeweled, dreaming skull, all that remains of a founder-king","summary":"Founder-king's jeweled skull still dreaming empire","flavor":"All that remains of the dynasty's founder, a jeweled skull that still dreams of empire.","desc":"All that's left of the dynasty's founder is a jeweled skull, and the skull still dreams — out loud, in a language that predates the empire it built. Gemstones socketed where eyes should be catch light without needing a source. It speaks of an empire that ended so long ago even the ruins have forgotten its name."},{"name":"Emperor Wyrm of the Sunken Ziggurat","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"dracolich","model":"net-new: a great serpent-dragon corpse bound to its own ziggurat","summary":"Serpent-dragon bound in death to its own ziggurat","flavor":"A great serpent-dragon bound in death to the ziggurat it once terrorized alive.","desc":"A great serpent-dragon corpse, bound in death to the very ziggurat it once terrorized while alive, coils motionless until the wards holding it are disturbed. Scales have gone the color of wet ash, but the size hasn't diminished with the centuries. Whatever killed it clearly didn't trust it to stay dead on its own."},{"name":"The Ever-Watching Sphinx of Final Judgment","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Celestial","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-valor","model":"sphinx-of-valor","summary":"Threshold sphinx judging souls by riddle or blade","flavor":"Judges every soul that crosses the temple threshold, riddle or blade in equal measure.","desc":"She judges every soul that crosses the temple threshold, riddle in one breath and blade in the next, equally prepared to use either. Wings fold with the deliberate patience of something that has judged more souls than the ruin has stones. She has never once needed to hurry a verdict."},{"name":"Medusa","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"snake-haired gaze-petrify guardian of a forbidden shrine","flavor":"A cursed priestess left to guard a ruin no one else will enter; she doesn't hunt, she waits for you to look.","desc":"She waits rather than hunts, a cursed priestess left to guard a ruin no one else will enter, coiled hair testing the air with quiet, restless motion. Statuary in her chamber isn't decoration — it's a record of everyone who looked too soon. She doesn't chase you; she simply waits for the moment you forget not to look.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Perseus cycle)"},{"name":"the Minotaur","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","model":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","summary":"bull-headed labyrinth-warden, gores anything that gets turned around","flavor":"Bred as a punishment and grown into a king of his own maze — the walls moved to keep him, so now he moves them to keep you.","desc":"Bred as a punishment and grown, over years underground, into king of his own maze, he tracks by scent and sound through walls that shift specifically to keep him in and everyone else lost. Horns scrape stone at every turn he takes at a dead run. The labyrinth moved to keep him once; now he moves it to keep you.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Theseus / Cretan labyrinth)"},{"name":"the Hydra","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"regenerating many-headed swamp apex predator","flavor":"Every wound you land is a negotiation it wins later — cut deep enough, fast enough, or it simply outlasts you with one more mouth.","desc":"Every head that goes still is a temporary condition — sever one and two more crowd up out of the wound before the blood finishes running. Steam rises off multiple throats hissing in ragged unison. It doesn't need to win a fight quickly; it just needs to still be here when you're not.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Labors of Herakles)"},{"name":"the Cyclops","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-sentry","model":"cyclops-sentry","summary":"one-eyed shepherd-giant sentry, brutal in close quarters","flavor":"He counts his flock by touch, one eye or none, and either way he's never once lost track of an intruder.","desc":"He counts intruders the way he counts sheep, by touch and sound rather than sight alone, and he has never once lost track of one in the dark. A single vast eye tracks motion with unnerving precision for something so simple-seeming. Close quarters favor him more than they favor you.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Homer's Odyssey, Polyphemus)"},{"name":"the Oracle Cyclops","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"cyclops-oracle","summary":"blind seer-giant, prophetic elite variant of the sentry","flavor":"Blinded on purpose, so the story goes, in trade for seeing further — he'll tell you your death before he deals it.","desc":"Blinded on purpose, so the story goes, in exchange for seeing further than sight ever could, he speaks your death before he deals it — calmly, like a weather report. Milk-pale sockets face you without needing to. He has all the patience of someone who already knows how this ends.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Cyclopes as forge-kin of Hephaestus / seer tradition"},{"name":"the Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"lion/goat/serpent composite, breathes fire mid-roar","flavor":"Three heads, three different opinions about how you should die — the goat screams first so the lion and the dragon don't have to.","desc":"Three heads hold three different opinions about how you should die, and none of the three are in a hurry to agree. The goat-head screams a warning the lion and the serpent don't bother giving. Fire gathers at the back of one throat before you've even decided which head to watch.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Iliad; Bellerophon cycle)"},{"name":"the Harpy","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"filth-winged bird-woman raider, hunts in screaming flocks","flavor":"They don't so much attack as infest — a shrieking cloud that strips a camp of food and morale in the same pass.","desc":"They don't so much attack as infest, a shrieking cloud descending on a camp and stripping it of food and morale in the same pass. Filth-matted wings beat a rhythm meant to disorient before a single talon ever connects. By the time you've counted them, they've already doubled back for a second pass.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Argonautica; Aeneid)"},{"name":"the Harpy Matriarch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"harpy brood-leader, coordinates the swarm's dive attacks","flavor":"Older, meaner, and smart enough to use her flock as bait — she circles while they soften you up.","desc":"Older, meaner, and smarter than her flock, she circles above the fight while the others soften you up, diving only when the outcome's no longer in doubt. Scarring across one wing marks a fight she survived and they didn't. She uses her brood as bait without a flicker of hesitation.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — harpy tradition, elevated to a brood-leader"},{"name":"the Sphinx-Warden","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"manticore","model":"net-new: lion-bodied, human-faced, feathered-winged riddler perched on a ruined threshold","summary":"riddling lion-bodied guardian barring a sealed passage","flavor":"She'll let you pass if you answer well — and she is in absolutely no hurry, because she has outlived every wrong answer she's ever heard.","desc":"She perches on a ruined threshold with the unhurried air of something that has outlived every wrong answer it's ever heard, feathered wings mantled, human face utterly still. She'll let you pass if you answer well — and she is in absolutely no hurry either way. Silence, to her, is just another kind of answer.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek/Egyptian myth (riddle-guardian tradition, Oedipus cycle)"},{"name":"Anubis's Jackal-Priest","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"net-new: jackal-masked embalmer-priest in funerary wrappings, ceremonial flail","summary":"jackal-masked tomb-priest, judges intruders before it fights them","flavor":"He was a man once, before the mask stopped coming off — now he weighs every heart that walks into his tomb, including his own.","desc":"He was a man once, before the jackal mask stopped coming off, and now he weighs every heart that crosses into his tomb on scales only he can see. Funerary wrappings move stiffly beneath ceremonial armor. He judges before he fights, and he includes his own heart in every weighing.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Egyptian myth/religion (Anubis, funerary tradition) — treated as a masked mortal priesthood, not the god"},{"name":"the Mummy","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"bandage-wrapped rot-cursed guardian of a sealed tomb","flavor":"Wrapped, sealed, and cursed on purpose — it was meant to stay down here forever, and it resents every second you've made that not true.","desc":"It was wrapped, sealed, and cursed on purpose — meant to stay down here forever — and it resents every second you've spent proving that wrong. Bandages have gone the color of the surrounding dust, stiff with age but far from fragile. It moves slow enough to seem harmless right up until its grip finds you.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Egyptian funerary myth/folklore (pre-1929 literary tradition, e.g. Stoker's Jewel of Seven Stars)"},{"name":"Gilgamesh's Shade","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"net-new: a once-great king's armored shade, bull-horned crown, still swinging for immortality","summary":"legendary king's undying shade, apex melee boss","flavor":"He tore down Humbaba, refused his own death twice, and still lost the one fight that mattered — now he re-fights every stranger like they might be that fight.","desc":"He tore down a forest guardian and refused his own death twice, and he still lost the one fight that ever mattered — so now he re-fights every stranger on the chance they might be that fight come back around. A bull-horned crown sits crooked on an armored, translucent brow. He swings for immortality every single time, and he has never once landed it.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Epic of Gilgamesh (Mesopotamian, ancient/public domain)"},{"name":"Humbaba","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"fomorian","model":"net-new: bark-skinned forest titan, roaring face of coiled intestine-like features per the epic's description","summary":"monstrous forest-guardian giant, terrifying roar attack","flavor":"He was posted here to keep the cedar forest safe from people exactly like you, and he has never once been relieved of that duty.","desc":"He was posted here to keep the cedar forest safe from people exactly like you, and no one has ever formally relieved him of that duty. His roar alone splinters low branches before he's taken a single step. He still treats the post as sacred, long after everyone who assigned it is gone.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Epic of Gilgamesh — forest guardian set by the gods"},{"name":"Grendel","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"net-new: hulking marsh-born raider, iron-resistant hide, drags prey back to the fen","summary":"iron-immune marsh-raider, hunts camps at night","flavor":"He doesn't want your gold and doesn't want your land — he wants the noise you make to stop, permanently.","desc":"He doesn't want your gold and doesn't want your land — he wants the noise you make to stop, permanently, and he's willing to drag you back to the fen to guarantee it. Iron scars mark old wounds that never slowed him for long. He hunts camps at night specifically because that's when the noise is worst.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Beowulf (Old English epic, public domain)"},{"name":"Grendel's Mother","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"net-new: a mere-dwelling avenger, drags the fight underwater to fight on her terms","summary":"underwater ambush-avenger, drags foes into her mere","flavor":"She only comes up out of the mere when someone's killed one of hers — and by then the math has already stopped being in your favor.","desc":"She surfaces from the mere only when someone's killed one of hers, and by the time she's above the waterline the math has already stopped favoring you. She drags fights back under with her on purpose, fighting on terms only she's practiced. The water closes over both of you before you've finished drawing breath.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Beowulf — the mere-wife, avenging kin"},{"name":"Raptor Pack-Hunter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"net-new: feathered pack-hunting dromaeosaur, quick and coordinated","summary":"quick feathered pack-hunter, always comes in threes","flavor":"One alone is a nuisance; hearing three more calling back from the treeline is the actual threat.","desc":"One alone is a nuisance, quick and feathered and easily driven off — it's the three more calling back from the treeline that turn this into a real problem. They coordinate without a sound passing visibly between them. By the time you've dealt with the first, the others have already flanked.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact (dromaeosaurid dinosaur), no IP owner"},{"name":"Pteranodon Screecher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"pteranodon","model":"pteranodon","summary":"cliff-nesting flying scavenger, snatches and flees","flavor":"It doesn't want a fight, it wants your lunch — but it'll take a finger to get it.","desc":"It doesn't want a fight, it wants your lunch, and it'll take a finger or an ear to get it if you don't drop the bag fast enough. Cliffside nests give it a straight, fast dive at any exposed food or shiny gear. It's gone again before you've finished cursing at it.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact (pterosaur), no IP owner"},{"name":"Allosaurus","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"allosaurus","model":"allosaurus","summary":"mid-sized ambush predator, fast and relentless","flavor":"Not the biggest thing in the valley, just the fastest thing willing to test that against you.","desc":"Not the biggest thing in the valley, just the fastest thing willing to test that claim against you, low-slung and quick through the underbrush. Scarring along its flank marks fights against bigger things it walked away from. It relies on speed doing the work size usually does.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"},{"name":"Triceratops","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"triceratops","summary":"armored horned grazer, devastating charge when cornered","flavor":"It would honestly rather be left alone grazing the fern-flats — it just won't be told to move twice.","desc":"It would honestly rather be left alone grazing the fern-flats, three horns lowered only as a last warning before the charge. Its frill carries old scoring from disputes it's already won. It won't be told to move twice.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"},{"name":"Tyrannosaurus Rex","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"tyrannosaurus-rex","model":"tyrannosaurus-rex","summary":"the valley's apex predator, ends most fights in one bite","flavor":"The valley has a food chain and one name at the top of it — everything else here is just working out how to be somewhere else when it walks by.","desc":"The valley has a food chain and exactly one name at the top of it, and everything else down here has already worked out how to be somewhere else when it walks by. Ground trembles a full second before the shape clears the treeline. Most fights with it end in one bite — the rest end in you being smart enough to not have one.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"}],
 "gloom":[{"name":"Threshold Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Vermin omen fleeing whatever else lives here","flavor":"Ordinary vermin that nest only in houses where something else already lives; they scatter from the cellar door the instant it's ajar, and never go back in.","desc":"A wave of small bodies breaks for the cellar door the second it swings open, claws skittering on stone, tails whipping past your ankles. Their fur is matted and their eyes catch no light at all. They do not come back once they're out, no matter how you call the room."},{"name":"Guttered Wick","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Drifting corpse-light that steals your shadow","flavor":"A candle-flame that should have died in the draft an hour ago; it drifts room to room looking for the wick it lost. Touch its light and your own shadow forgets to follow you for a minute.","desc":"A candle-flame no bigger than a thumbnail drifts at eye height, sourceless and slow, guttering in a wind that isn't there. It bobs from doorway to doorway like it's checking each room for something it lost. Where its light crosses you, your shadow lags a half-step behind, and doesn't catch up for a long minute after."},{"name":"Grinning Poppet","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword: a small porcelain doll skittering upright on cracked joints","summary":"The haunted doll that creeps when unwatched","flavor":"Left on the nursery shelf for three generations, it only moves when no one is looking directly at it, and it is always exactly one shelf closer than it was.","desc":"A porcelain doll sits on the shelf with its head lolled sideways, seams cracked white at every joint, its painted smile too wide for its face. Look away and listen — a dry little click of ceramic against wood. Look back and it's one shelf closer, smile unchanged."},{"name":"Pallid Newcomer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Fresh-buried neighbor still walking its route","flavor":"Someone who died recently enough that the neighbors still wave. It walks the same route to the same house every night and knocks exactly three times.","desc":"He walks the same lane at the same hour, grey around the mouth, clothes buttoned wrong, and lifts a hand to neighbors who no longer wave back. He climbs the same porch steps and knocks three times, waits exactly as long as he used to, and shuffles on when no one answers."},{"name":"Bone-Rattle Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Reassembled grave-bones, a cult's patient tool","flavor":"Grave-robbed bones reassembled by something patient; it clicks when it walks, a metronome counting down to whatever the cult needs it for.","desc":"Bones wired and bolted into a rough man-shape shuffle forward in a dry clatter, joints clicking in an even rhythm, like a clock counting something down. Torchlight passes right through the empty ribs. It doesn't hesitate, doesn't flinch — it moves like it's been told exactly what to do and has done it before."},{"name":"Zealous Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Robed true-believer running the ritual anyway","flavor":"A true believer in plain robes, still capable of guilt, still capable of running the ritual anyway. Answers to the coven without question.","desc":"A figure in plain grey robes stands at the ritual's edge, chanting the words with a slight tremor in the voice — not fear of you, fear of stopping. Their hands shake around the knife, but they don't lower it. Somewhere under the certainty, their eyes are still asking for permission to feel bad about this."},{"name":"Static Reflection","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"Mirror-double, one second behind, draining you","flavor":"A mirror-image one full second behind, that finally catches up and steps out of the glass. It drains you the way a slow leak drains a tire — you don't notice until you're on the ground.","desc":"Your reflection in the window glass is a full second behind every move you make — a beat too late to raise a hand, a beat too late to turn away. Then it catches up all at once and steps out of the glass toward you, and the room goes a little colder where it walks."},{"name":"Rot-Handed Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Grave-eater whose bite paralyzes the mourner","flavor":"Once a mourner who ate what it was supposed to bury; its paralytic bite is the reason funerals in the gloom are held at noon, never dusk.","desc":"It crouches low over freshly turned earth, fingers black and swollen, working a bite of something it shouldn't eat between grey teeth. The smell of it arrives before it does — wet soil, and worse. Its bite doesn't just hurt; the numbness spreads slow, and you feel your own limbs stop answering you."},{"name":"Moonshackled Cur","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"dire-wolf","model":"dire-wolf","summary":"Half-turned wolf-thing running with the pack","flavor":"Runs in the pack that follows the werewolf's howl, half-turned and losing more of itself with every full moon it survives.","desc":"It runs low and wrong at the edge of the pack, more limbs than a wolf ought to move on, hide patched with something not quite fur. It howls a half-second off from the others, like it's still learning the note. Every full moon it loses a little more of what used to be a dog."},{"name":"Household Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Decades-long tantrum that throws the furniture","flavor":"Not a haunting — a tantrum, ongoing, decades long. It throws whatever's closest and has strong opinions about who's allowed in its kitchen.","desc":"A chair skids across the floor on its own and slams into the wall, followed by a plate flung so hard it shatters at your feet. Cupboard doors bang open and shut in a fast, furious rhythm. Nothing here wants to talk — it's been throwing this same tantrum, alone, for decades."},{"name":"Cellar Warden","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"The cult's own guard now opening the door","flavor":"The cult leaves it down in the dark to keep the door shut from the inside — except lately it's been the one opening it.","desc":"It stands at the bottom of the cellar stairs with its back to the door, grey-skinned and patient, exactly where the coven left it to keep the dark in. Lately it's been the one turning the latch. Its cold touch doesn't just hurt — where it grips you, something in your arm goes stiff and slow to obey."},{"name":"Full-Moon Shepherd","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"The neighbor who wears a wolf's face at midnight","flavor":"Wears its human face at the market and its true face at midnight, and swears every time it will be the last. It never is.","desc":"By day it's the neighbor who waves from the fence line, mild and a little tired-looking. Under full moonlight the jaw stretches wrong, hands curl into something with claws in them, and the mild face is gone entirely. It swore, every time before, that this would be the last."},{"name":"Hollow-Robed Zealot","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"Self-mummified elder still preaching to no one","flavor":"A cult elder who finished the rite on himself; wrapped in the vestments he died in, still leading services nobody living attends.","desc":"Wrapped in the same funeral linens it finished the rite in, it stands at the front of an empty room and preaches to rows of dust-covered pews, voice dry as paper. It doesn't seem to notice no one's left to listen. Its bandaged hands still turn the pages of a book that's long since rotted through."},{"name":"Possessed Vessel","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"A person worn like a coat, blinking wrong","flavor":"Wears a person like a coat, imperfectly — the voice is right but the blinking is wrong. Whatever's inside it wants the body back once its work is finished.","desc":"It talks like the person you knew, uses their turns of phrase, wears their face without a wrinkle out of place — except the blink comes a beat too slow, and sometimes both eyes close a half-second apart. Whatever's driving that body is only borrowing it, and it's counting down to when the real work starts."},{"name":"The Slow Reflection","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Ghost one second behind, plotting to catch up","flavor":"Lives one mirror-second out of sync with the world; it has had a full lifetime alone in that lag to plan what it'll do the moment it catches up.","desc":"It steps free of a cracked mirror a full second behind your own motion, translucent, mouthing words you said a moment ago. It has spent what feels like a lifetime alone in that lag, watching you live just ahead of it. Something in the way it moves says it's done waiting to catch up."},{"name":"Grief-Fed Banshee","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Wailing widow owed a wake that never came","flavor":"Mourns in a key that shatters glass and eardrums both; she was promised a wake that never happened, and she's still owed it.","desc":"Her wail arrives before she's visible, a note that finds the glass in the windows and the fillings in your teeth at once. When she appears she's in mourning black gone the color of old rain, face raw with a grief that's had years to curdle. She was owed a wake nobody held, and she intends to collect."},{"name":"Coven Matriarch","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Coven matriarch trading in stolen sleep and souls","flavor":"The eldest of a coven of three, who trades in stolen sleep and worse; her sisters answer to her the way a storm answers to the moon.","desc":"The eldest of three sits closest to the hearth, hands folded, watching you with the calm of someone who has already decided how this ends. Her voice is warm, almost kind, right up until it isn't. Sleep taken from a hundred houses shows in the unnatural stillness of her face."},{"name":"Marrow Revenant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Undead thing that only wants its killer, unerringly","flavor":"Came back wrong and remembers exactly who wronged it. Walks in a straight line toward its killer through locked doors, walls, anything.","desc":"It came back grey and gaunt, joints held together by will more than sinew, and it walks in one direction only — toward whoever wronged it. Locked doors don't slow it. Walls barely do. It doesn't seem to notice you exist at all unless you're standing between it and its killer."},{"name":"Candlewax Doppelganger","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"Melting face that copies whoever stares longest","flavor":"A face that melts and re-sets itself into whoever last looked at it too long; meeting its eyes is how it decides which of you to become next.","desc":"Its face runs like hot tallow and re-sets a little differently every time you look away — cheekbones, jaw, the set of the eyes shifting toward whoever it studied last. Meeting its gaze for too long is how it decides. When it settles, it's wearing someone's face better than they do."},{"name":"Congregation Made Flesh","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"A coven's dozen bodies fused into one prayer","flavor":"What happens when a coven's devotion finally has somewhere to go — a dozen willing bodies fused at the altar into one thing that still, somehow, prays.","desc":"It rises out of the altar as one shuddering mass of limbs and half-formed faces, a dozen bodies folded into a single frame that still moves like it's kneeling. Every mouth on it murmurs the same prayer, slightly out of time with the others. It doesn't attack so much as embrace.","traits":{"note": "A dozen willing sacrifices fused at the altar; strikes as one but each limb still half-answers to a different will, occasionally fumbling in ways a normal aberration wouldn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Chorus of Selves", "text": "Once per turn, when it would take an action, it may instead speak with a dozen overlapping voices, forcing a creature within 30 ft that hears it to make a Wisdom save or be frightened until the end of its next turn."}]}},{"name":"Warden of the Cellar Door","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Vampire bound to the door that's never shut","flavor":"Bound to the one door in the house that's never fully closed; it has watched every family that ever lived there and outlasted all of them.","desc":"It waits just inside the one door in the house that never quite latches, still and courtly, watching the hallway the way a butler watches for a guest who's late. It has outlived every family that ever lived here and remembers each of their names. The door creaks the same amount whether it's opening or closing.","traits":{"note": "Bound to a single threshold; can't willingly move more than 60 ft from the cellar door chassis-normal otherwise.", "actions": [{"name": "Never Fully Shut", "text": "As a bonus action, it may attempt to open any door or window within 60 ft that isn't locked by more than a mundane latch, regardless of line of sight."}]}},{"name":"Bell-Tolling Revenant","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Bell-tower revenant tolling once per debt owed","flavor":"A funeral bell's worth of grief given shape and a bell-tower's worth of reach; it tolls once for every soul it's owed, and it keeps very careful count.","desc":"Somewhere above, a bell rings once, unbidden, in a tower with no bellringer. The sound rolls out low and enormous, and where it lands the air goes thick with old grief. It counts its debts by the toll — one for every soul it believes it's owed — and it is never wrong about the number.","traits":{"note": "Gargantuan scale grants extended reach/aura beyond the base chassis.", "actions": [{"name": "The Toll", "text": "Once per long rest, it may ring its bell as an action: all creatures within 120 ft who can hear it must succeed a Wisdom save or be frightened and have disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of their next turn."}]}},{"name":"The Second Face in the Glass","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Elder vampire kingpin living inside the mirrors","flavor":"An elder vampire kingpin who lives entirely inside reflective surfaces, one beat behind its prey, until the night it decides to be early instead.","desc":"It lives inside every mirror and dark window in the house, a beat behind your reflection, patient as rot. For a hundred years it's been content to stay one step slow. Tonight, for reasons only it knows, it steps out early — and the glass behind it doesn't crack so much as exhale.","traits":{"note": "Kingpin-tier vampire; the mirror-lag is fluff for its Misty Step-style repositioning, not a new mechanic.", "actions": [{"name": "Early", "text": "Once per combat, it may teleport to any reflective surface within 60 ft as a reaction, appearing a half-second 'ahead' of where it should be — before the triggering attack resolves."}]}},{"name":"The Uninvited","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Ancient thing that only ever needs one knock","flavor":"It always knocks first. Every house it has ever entered, it was let in — a guest, a mourner, a face someone half-remembered — and it has never once needed to knock twice.","desc":"It stands on the threshold, patient, hands folded, wearing the face of someone you half-remember from a funeral or a wedding you can't quite place. It has never had to knock twice. Every house that's ever let it in did so willingly, and it is in no hurry now that it's inside yours.","traits":{"note": "Apex mummy-lord; the 'always let in' fluff never overrides player agency at the door — it's atmosphere for its curse/fear kit, not a forced-entry mechanic.", "actions": [{"name": "One Knock", "text": "If a creature voluntarily opens a door for it, that creature has disadvantage on saving throws against its frightening presence for the rest of the encounter."}]}},{"name":"The Possession at the Root","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"A congregation's willing vessels burned to one shape","flavor":"Not a demon wearing a body — a congregation's worth of willing vessels burned down to one true and monstrous shape, still calling itself by the coven's oldest, most patient name.","desc":"The shape towers huge and burning at the bottom of the crypt stair, built from a congregation's worth of willing bodies burned down into one true and monstrous silhouette. It still answers, in a chorus of overlapping voices, to the coven's oldest name for itself. Ash falls from it like it's shedding a robe.","traits":{"note": "Apex balor-chassis; fluff-only voice work, no new mechanics beyond the SRD frame.", "actions": []}},{"name":"Crawlspace Widow","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"giant-wolf-spider","model":"giant-wolf-spider","summary":"Attic spider that drops on sleepers","flavor":"A bloated house-spider the size of a cat that drops from attic rafters onto sleeping throats.","desc":"Something the size of a housecat clings to the rafters, legs folded tight against a bloated abdomen, patient as dust. It drops without warning onto whatever's sleeping below, silent until the moment its fangs find a throat. The webs up there are thick enough to muffle a scream."},{"name":"Threadbare Scarecrow","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Straw effigy that walks after moonrise","flavor":"A field-post effigy stuffed with grave-dirt straw that unpins itself at moonrise.","desc":"Propped crooked over a dead field, straw leaking from a burlap seam, it hangs slack against its post all day like any other scarecrow. At moonrise the post creaks empty. It walks with a stiff, jerking gait, arms still splayed the way they were pinned."},{"name":"Ashen Widow's Cat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"cat","model":"cat","summary":"Unblinking cat that tracks the dead","flavor":"A funeral-black cat that never blinks and always knows which door hides the coffin.","desc":"A black cat sits very still on the stair, tail curled over its paws, and does not blink. Its eyes track you the way it might track a mouse, patient and total. It always seems to be facing the one door in the house you'd rather it didn't."},{"name":"Gutter Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Drowned grudge haunting the storm drains","flavor":"A drowned drunk's grudge, sluicing through storm drains looking for the one who left him there.","desc":"A grey shape rises out of the storm drain grate, dripping and half-formed, dragging the smell of standing water with it. It mutters the same accusation over and over, aimed at nobody in the room and everybody at once. Wherever it passes, the gutters run backward for a moment."},{"name":"Wick-Eyed Changeling Child","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"sprite","model":"sprite","summary":"Cradle-swapped child with a widening smile","flavor":"A too-quiet foundling left in a cradle, its smile widening only when no one is looking.","desc":"It sits too quietly in the cradle, small hands folded, watching the room with an attention no infant should have. The smile only widens when it thinks no one's looking — a fraction more teeth each time. It hasn't cried once since it arrived."},{"name":"Tallow Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"Candle-vigil ghoul dripping rendered fat","flavor":"A ghoul that drips rendered fat from a crypt-candle vigil that never ended.","desc":"It kneels beside a candle that's burned down to nothing, wax dripping thick and yellow off its own skin like the vigil never ended. Its nails are candle-black, its breath smells of tallow and grave-dirt. It doesn't look up from the flame until you're close enough to touch."},{"name":"Splintered Marionette","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"net-new: a puppet with its own cut strings, still bowing","summary":"Self-cut puppet bowing to an empty house","flavor":"A puppet-theater star whose strings were cut by its own hand, still bowing to an empty house.","desc":"Its own strings hang cut and curling from the crossbar overhead, and still it bows — low, formal, precise — to a house with no one left in the seats. Its joints clack in place of applause. It seems to be waiting for someone to throw a rose."},{"name":"Bog-Sunk Revenant","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Peat-bog hanged man risen with the noose","flavor":"A peat-preserved corpse hauled from the marsh, its noose still knotted at the throat.","desc":"Peat-black skin, a noose still cinched tight at the throat, it hauls itself up out of the marsh a step at a time, mud sluicing off in ropes. It moves like the ground still owns half of it. The rope creaks with each stride, though there's nothing left to hang from it."},{"name":"Pox-Marked Thrall","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Plague villager thralled to a whisper","flavor":"A plague-branded villager who traded a fever for a whisper that never stops.","desc":"Sores mark the skin along the jaw and throat, fresh enough that they should have killed by now. Something in the eyes says the fever broke, and something else moved in behind it. The villager mutters along to a whisper only they can hear, low and constant, like a hymn stuck on one line."},{"name":"Feral Barn Bat-Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"Bell-triggered swarm pouring from the rafters","flavor":"A rafters-thick cloud of bats that only stirs when the church bell cracks midnight.","desc":"The rafters look ordinary until the church bell cracks midnight — then the ceiling comes apart into a thousand small wings, a black tide pouring down in one shrieking mass. The sound of it fills the room before the bats do. It settles as fast as it rises, the instant the last bell-note dies."},{"name":"Rope-Burned Suicide","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Hanging-tree haunt re-living its last minute","flavor":"A hanging-tree haunt that re-lives its last minute on anyone who lingers beneath the branch.","desc":"Rope-burn rings the throat, feet dangling a few inches off ground that isn't there. Beneath the old hanging-tree, it relives the same last minute on a loop — the drop, the jerk, the stillness — and anyone who lingers gets pulled into the memory with it. Its eyes are the only part of it that still moves."},{"name":"Hollow Nursemaid","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Lullaby-humming absence in the nursery wall","flavor":"A governess-shaped absence that hums lullabies through the nursery wall long after the family fled.","desc":"A shape darker than the shadow it should cast moves along the nursery wall, humming a lullaby with no breath behind it. The tune is off by a few notes, over and over, patient as a metronome. The family fled this house generations ago; she never got the message."},{"name":"Cur of the Black Barn","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"Loyal farm dog that starved and rose wrong","flavor":"A farm dog that starved loyal beside its master's grave and rose wrong.","desc":"It waited by the grave until its ribs showed through the hide, loyal past any reasonable end, and something answered that loyalty wrong. Now it circles the barn on legs that bend at angles a dog's shouldn't, growling low at nothing, still watching the spot where it used to sleep."},{"name":"Rat-King Knot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Tail-fused rats forming one furious knot","flavor":"Dozens of sewer rats fused tail-to-tail into one furious, many-headed knot.","desc":"Dozens of rats writhe together in the corner, tails knotted into one impossible braid, a single furious mass of fur and teeth trying to move in a dozen directions at once. It doesn't so much attack as thrash, and everything within reach of that thrashing gets bitten."},{"name":"Choir-Loft Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Organist's fury slamming hymnals and bellropes","flavor":"An organist's fury, still slamming hymnal pages and yanking bellropes no hand can hold.","desc":"Hymnal pages flip themselves violently in the choir loft, and the bell-rope down in the nave snaps taut on its own, yanking the bell into a furious, uneven clang. No hand is on either. Whatever's left of the organist up there is still furious about something long past fixing."},{"name":"Gravecloth Zombie","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Shroud-stitched exhumee lurching by grave-light","flavor":"A shroud-wrapped exhumee, still stitched into its burial linens, lurching by grave-light.","desc":"Wound tight in burial linens gone grey and stiff, it moves by grave-light with the shroud still cinched at wrist and ankle, restricting every step to a shuffle. Where the wrappings have torn, the skin beneath is the color of old candle wax. It doesn't seem to notice the cloth at all."},{"name":"Fen Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Crypt-nesting ghoul with silt-slick claws","flavor":"A ghoul that nests in flooded family crypts, its claws slick with graveyard silt.","desc":"It nests in flooded family crypts, half-submerged, silt-slicked claws dragging along stone as it pulls itself up out of the water. The smell of standing swamp-rot arrives with it. It moves faster in the water than it has any right to on land."},{"name":"Beast of the Full Moon Runt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Freshly bitten victim terrified of itself","flavor":"A fresh-bitten victim mid-transformation, more terrified of itself than of you.","desc":"Fur is only halfway in on this one — patches of human skin still show between the tufts, and the transformation looks like it hurts. It flinches at its own reflection in puddles. More than anything, it seems terrified of what it's about to become, and that terror makes it dangerously unpredictable."},{"name":"Wax-Sealed Familiar","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"raven","model":"raven","summary":"Coven crow with a beak sewn shut","flavor":"A coven's carrier-crow, its beak sewn shut around a secret it will die before dropping.","desc":"A crow perches just out of easy reach, beak sealed shut with a dark wax that's cracked but never fully broken. It watches with one unblinking eye at a time, turning its head slow. Whatever message it's carrying, it will die with its beak sewn shut before it drops it."},{"name":"Sackcloth Effigy","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"Hair-stitched poppet animated by a pinned name","flavor":"A burnt-corn poppet stitched with a stranger's hair, animated by whoever's name is pinned to its chest.","desc":"Burnt corn husks stitched into a rough manlike shape, a stranger's hair sewn along the scalp seam, it stands motionless until a name pinned to its chest gives it somewhere to walk. It moves stiff and jerking, straw rasping at every joint, obeying whoever holds the pin."},{"name":"Ossuary Skitterling","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"crawling-claw","model":"crawling-claw","summary":"Severed charnel-wall hand scrabbling homeward","flavor":"A single severed hand from the charnel wall, still scrabbling toward its own coffin.","desc":"A single severed hand drags itself across the floor on its fingertips, knucklebones clicking against stone. It's headed somewhere specific — toward a coffin it half-remembers being part of. It doesn't seem to register anything else in the room until something blocks its path."},{"name":"Lantern-Jawed Corpse Candle","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Grave-light that feeds on following mourners","flavor":"A death-light that hovers over fresh graves, feeding on the grief of mourners who follow it.","desc":"A pale light hovers low over a fresh grave, warm and inviting the way a lantern in a window is inviting. Anyone who follows it feels a little of their grief drain away with each step closer — which is exactly what it's feeding on. It never leads anywhere good."},{"name":"Widow's Veil Shade","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"Mirror-shed silhouette that grieves at funerals","flavor":"A mourning-dress silhouette that peels off mirrors during funerals to grieve alongside the living.","desc":"It peels itself free of a mirror's surface the moment mourning bells start ringing somewhere nearby, a silhouette in a funeral veil with no face beneath it. It drifts to stand among the grieving, head bowed, indistinguishable from a real mourner until someone reaches to comfort it."},{"name":"Feasting Cellar Grub","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"Pale centipede fattened on deeper offerings","flavor":"A pale root-cellar centipede fattened on offerings left for something worse living deeper down.","desc":"Pale and segmented, thick as a forearm, it coils in the dark corner of the root cellar where offerings are left for something deeper down. It's grown fat on food that was never meant for it. When it moves, dozens of small legs ripple in a wave along its length."},{"name":"Rusalka's Drowned Bride","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Jilted drowned bride walking out dripping","flavor":"A jilted bride who walked into the millpond in her gown and now walks out of it, dripping.","desc":"She walks up out of the millpond in a wedding gown gone the color of pond-scum, water sheeting off her in constant runnels that never stop. Her veil clings wet to a face still arranged for a ceremony that never happened. She doesn't seem to notice she's dripping onto dry floor."},{"name":"Fanged Chorister","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Hymn-voiced ghoul luring the faithful closer","flavor":"A choir-loft ghoul whose hymn-perfect voice lures the faithful within reach of its talons.","desc":"A voice drifts down from the choir loft, perfect and aching, pulling you a step closer before you've decided to move. What's making that sound has a face built more for tearing than singing, and talons where the hymnal should be. It only stops singing once you're within reach."},{"name":"Marrow Beetle Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"swarm-of-insects","summary":"Grave-beetle carpet that strips corpses clean","flavor":"A carpet of grave-beetles that strips a corpse to clean bone in a single feeding.","desc":"A dark carpet of beetles moves across the floor in one rippling sheet, drawn to whatever's freshly dead — or freshly wounded. In seconds a corpse left in their path is bone. The sound of that many small shells clicking together fills the room before you see them."},{"name":"Bell-Jar Wraith","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Failed experiment reaching for its notes","flavor":"A physician's failed experiment, trapped between a bell jar and the grave, still reaching for its notes.","desc":"It hangs half-formed between a shattered bell jar and the floor, reaching with translucent fingers for notes that scattered years ago. Chemical residue still clings to what's left of its coat. It repeats the same failed gesture, over and over, never quite grasping the paper."},{"name":"Attic-Bound Revenant","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Locked-away relative still pacing six feet","flavor":"A locked-away relative the family pretended never existed, still pacing the same six feet.","desc":"Something paces the same six feet of attic floorboard, over and over, footsteps landing in exactly the same spots each pass. The family who locked it up here pretended for years it didn't exist. It still wears whatever they buried it in, and the door still won't open from outside."},{"name":"Coven Apprentice","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Hedge-witch initiate half in love with the dark","flavor":"A hedge-witch initiate memorizing the coven's book by candle-stub, half in love with the dark it teaches.","desc":"She sits hunched over a book by a candle stub, copying passages in a hand that shakes only a little now. There's a hunger in the way she reads — half fear, half something closer to love. She looks up at intruders like they've interrupted a lesson she was finally starting to enjoy."},{"name":"Reliquary Ghast","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Stolen saint's corpse gone hungry in vestments","flavor":"A saint's stolen corpse gone hungry, still wearing the vestments it was buried in.","desc":"Vestments hang rotted but recognizable off a frame that used to be a saint, or was buried as one. It moves with a clergy stoop, hands folded in front like it's still blessing something. The smell that comes off it is incense gone badly wrong."},{"name":"Ossified Bell-Ringer","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Skeleton still ringing an unheard dusk bell","flavor":"A campanile skeleton that still climbs the tower stair each dusk, ringing a bell no one else hears.","desc":"Bone climbs the tower stair each dusk on schedule, hauling on a rope that no longer has a bell attached — or does, and nobody living can hear it anymore. It performs the same ritual with total conviction. Dust falls from the belfry each time it pulls."},{"name":"Charnel-Yard Skeleton Archer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"skeleton-archer","summary":"Crossbow skeleton still holding its cemetery post","flavor":"A crossbow-armed grave-guard skeleton that still holds its post along the cemetery wall.","desc":"It stands at its post along the cemetery wall, crossbow leveled, exactly where it was set generations ago. Vines have grown through the ribcage and around the stock of the weapon. It doesn't move until something crosses the boundary it was told to hold."},{"name":"Full-Moon Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Pack lieutenant hiding claws until convenient","flavor":"A pack lieutenant who hunts in human guise all week and only shows its claws at the coven's convenience.","desc":"He looks like ordinary muscle in human shape — until his knuckles crack wrong and the fingers lengthen, claws sliding free only once the coven gives the word. All week he hunts on two legs, patient and quiet. He seems to enjoy the waiting more than the change."},{"name":"Steeple Bloodkin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Choirmaster vampire leading hymns with stitched smile","flavor":"A choirmaster turned bloodsucker who still leads the hymn each Sunday, mouth stitched into a smile.","desc":"He still leads the hymn from the choir loft every Sunday, mouth stitched into a permanent smile that never quite reaches the eyes. His voice carries beautifully, if you don't look too closely at the stitches. Between verses, his gaze drifts to the congregation's throats."},{"name":"The Weeping Bride","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Jilted ghost bride whose scream shatters glass","flavor":"A ghost bride whose scream shatters glass at the mention of the groom who left her at the altar.","desc":"White lace, yellowed and torn at the hem, drags behind her as she walks the aisle of an empty chapel. Mention the groom who left her and the windows shudder — a scream that starts as grief and ends as something that shatters glass and eardrums both."},{"name":"Warden of the Drowning Pool","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Cursed executioner guarding the drowning pool","flavor":"A witch-trial executioner cursed to guard the millpond where he condemned the innocent.","desc":"He stands knee-deep at the edge of the millpond, cursed to guard the water where he once condemned the innocent. His executioner's hood is soaked black and clinging. He doesn't let anyone leave the water's edge until he's decided whether they deserve to."},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Ghast Priest","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Defrocked cleric who joined his flock's feast","flavor":"A defrocked cleric who fed his own flock to something in the crypt and joined the feast.","desc":"He wears a collar gone stiff with old blood, standing over what's left of a flock he fed to something in the crypt below. His voice still has a sermon's cadence, warm even now. He joined the feast himself, in the end, and hasn't stopped since."},{"name":"Coven Hexweaver","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"Coven's youngest sister, bargains cruelly","flavor":"A three-sister coven's youngest voice, still human enough to bargain, cruel enough to relish it.","desc":"The youngest sister of the coven looks almost ordinary — a little too pretty, a little too pleased with herself. She'll bargain fairly if it amuses her, and cruelly the moment it stops. Her hands never quite stop moving, weaving something out of the air between sentences."},{"name":"The Mirror-Bound Twin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Face-stealing reflection waiting in every mirror","flavor":"A reflection that stole its owner's face centuries ago and now waits in every polished surface.","desc":"Every polished surface in the house holds the same watching shape, waiting since it stole its owner's face centuries ago. It mimics your expressions a beat too perfectly, like it's practicing. When it finally steps free of the glass, it looks exactly like you expected — just wrong around the eyes."},{"name":"Rite-Scarred Zealot Captain","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Ritual leader scarred with a forbidden name","flavor":"A ritual leader whose scars spell the summoning name in a language the tongue was never meant for.","desc":"Scars run in careful lines across his face and forearms, spelling a name in a tongue no human throat was built to say. He commands the ritual with total certainty, voice raised over the chanting circle. The scars seem to catch what little light there is."},{"name":"Charnel-House Ogre Zombie","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-zombie","model":"ogre-zombie","summary":"Gravedigger's corpse raised by his own rite","flavor":"A gravedigger's own hulking corpse, reanimated by the very rite he used to raise others.","desc":"It was a gravedigger once, and huge even then — now it's huger, raised by the very rite it used to perform on others. Grave-dirt packs its wounds instead of blood. It swings a shovel still crusted with the mud of its own grave."},{"name":"The Second Groom","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Jilted suitor presiding over an eternal reception","flavor":"A jilted suitor who murdered the wedding party and now presides over an eternal, empty reception.","desc":"He presides at the head of an empty banquet table, plates set for guests who died at his hand decades ago. His wedding coat has rotted to lace. He still rises to greet new arrivals with the exact same toast, word for word, waiting for someone to finally say yes."},{"name":"Loomstitch Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Face-thief impersonating the beloved village elder","flavor":"A face-thief who replaced a beloved village elder months ago, and no one has noticed the seams yet.","desc":"The village elder greets you warmly, exactly as they always have — the voice is right, the mannerisms are right, and if you look closely at the hairline there's a seam that shouldn't be there. It's been wearing this face for months, and no one else has noticed."},{"name":"Gallows Wraith Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Hanged highwayman commanding lesser gibbet-spirits","flavor":"An executed highwayman who commands lesser hanged-spirits from the crossroads gibbet.","desc":"It hangs at the crossroads gibbet with the noose still around its neck, commanding a handful of lesser hanged-spirits with a raised, rotted hand. Its voice carries the flat authority of a man used to giving orders. The other gibbet-ghosts obey without hesitation."},{"name":"Vestry Revenant","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"graveyard-revenant","model":"graveyard-revenant","summary":"Swollen sexton digging until his killer's found","flavor":"A murdered sexton, swollen with grave-rot fury, who will not stop digging until his killer is found.","desc":"Enormous and swollen with grave-rot, it claws through the churchyard soil with hands too big for the shovel that used to fit them. It was a sexton once, murdered mid-dig, and it will not stop turning earth until it finds whoever did it. Dirt sprays with every furious motion."},{"name":"Cellar-Bound Bulette Grub","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"Burrowing horror surfacing through open graves","flavor":"A burrowing horror that tunneled up under a village graveyard and now surfaces through open plots.","desc":"The ground heaves and cracks before it surfaces — a horror built for tunneling, breaking up through an open grave in a spray of soil and splintered wood. It doesn't so much emerge as erupt. Nothing about its approach is subtle."},{"name":"Coven Matron's Cauldron-Kin","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Second matriarch trading in nightmares, not curses","flavor":"A second matriarch of the same coven, who trades in nightmares rather than curses.","desc":"A second matriarch, this one trading in nightmares instead of curses, stirs something dark and slow over a low fire. Her presence makes the shadows in the room lean toward her. She smiles the way someone smiles when they already know how your dreams tonight will go."},{"name":"Blood-Thrall Chevalier","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Centuries-loyal knight thrall, still starving","flavor":"A knight sworn to a vampire's service centuries past, still armored, still loyal, still starving.","desc":"He still wears his armor, dented and centuries out of fashion, sworn to a master he serves without question. His eyes are sunken with a hunger he's forbidden from satisfying himself. He stands at rigid attention outside the coffin door, starving in perfect discipline."},{"name":"Ashfall Mummy Curate","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"Punished elder mummified alive, still shepherding","flavor":"A sect elder mummified alive as punishment, now shepherding the congregation from inside its wrappings.","desc":"Wrapped alive as punishment by his own sect, he still shepherds a congregation that's long since stopped listening — voice muffled through the linen at his mouth. He moves with the slow, careful patience of someone who has nowhere left to be in a hurry."},{"name":"Marrow-Bound Wererat Broker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Sewer relic-fixer who bites debtors","flavor":"A black-market fixer who trades cursed relics from the sewers, and bites those who don't pay.","desc":"He works the sewer market in a long coat, laying cursed relics out on a blanket like they're ordinary wares. His smile shows a few too many teeth when a debtor's late on payment. The bite that follows isn't a warning — it's a bill collector's signature."},{"name":"Widow-Maker Banshee Elder","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Generations-old wail that claims every husband","flavor":"A generations-old keening spirit whose wail has claimed every man who married into her bloodline.","desc":"Her wail has claimed every man who married into this bloodline for generations, and she has no plans to stop now. She keens from somewhere just out of sight, the sound aging with each retelling of the family's grief. New husbands don't last the season."},{"name":"Coffin-Nail Wight Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Buried captain drilling reanimated ranks by night","flavor":"A militia captain buried with his men, now drilling their reanimated ranks in the churchyard at night.","desc":"Buried with the men he commanded, he now drills their reanimated ranks in the churchyard by night, barking the same orders in a voice gone dry as the ground he rose from. The ranks shamble into formation with a discipline that outlived them."},{"name":"Blood-Drunk Vampire Familiar Knight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-familiar","model":"vampire-familiar","summary":"Turned squire guarding the coffin, hunting by dusk","flavor":"A turned squire who serves his master's coffin by day and hunts travelers by dusk.","desc":"He guards his master's coffin by day, dutiful and silent, and by dusk he's out hunting travelers on the road with the same discipline. Turned young and kept that way, he still moves like a squire eager to prove himself — just with a different kind of service now."},{"name":"Seance Circle Medium","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"priest","summary":"Parlor medium who opened a door she can't close","flavor":"A parlor spiritualist who really did open a door, and now can't close it, or doesn't want to.","desc":"Her hands rest on the table, palms up, eyes rolled back to white while her voice comes out layered — hers, and something else's underneath. She really did open a door, once, in a parlor full of paying customers. She isn't sure anymore if she wants it closed."},{"name":"Effigy-Bound Flesh Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"Resurrectionist's patchwork sewn from village corpses","flavor":"A resurrectionist's stitched patchwork, sewn from a village's worth of the recently deceased.","desc":"Stitched from a village's worth of the recently deceased, it lumbers forward in patchwork skin the color of old bruises, seams visible at every joint. It moves without hurry, without hesitation, built by a resurrectionist who was never squeamish about the sourcing."},{"name":"The Uninherited Heir","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Disinherited ghost rewriting the will in blood","flavor":"A disinherited son who haunts the family estate, rewriting the will in blood on the study wall each night.","desc":"He haunts the family study, disinherited and furious, rewriting the will in dripping red script across the wallpaper each night. By morning the room reeks of iron and old paper. He erases it and starts over the moment anyone reads it aloud."},{"name":"Coven Familiar Alpha","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"winter-wolf","summary":"Coven-bound wolf whose howl carries a curse","flavor":"A frost-pale wolf bound to the coven's oldest hex, its howl carrying a curse instead of a warning.","desc":"Frost clings to its pelt even indoors, a wolf built along wrong lines, bound to the coven's oldest hex. Its howl doesn't carry a warning the way a wolf's should — it carries the curse itself, landing on whoever's close enough to hear the note change."},{"name":"Rot-Crowned Spirit Naga","cr":8,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"spirit-naga","summary":"Serpentine grave-idol worshipped as a saint","flavor":"A grave-cult idol given serpentine unlife, worshipped by the possessed congregation as a saint.","desc":"Coiled at the heart of the grave-cult's shrine, serpentine and glowing faintly with unlife, it's worshipped by a possessed congregation as something holy. It speaks in a voice too calm for what it is, offering wisdom laced with rot."},{"name":"The Chained Confessor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant-zombie","model":"eye-tyrant-zombie","summary":"Fused inquisition victims forced to confess","flavor":"An inquisitor's own victims fused into one shackled horror, forced to confess sins that were never theirs.","desc":"Fused victims of some long-dead inquisitor writhe together in one shackled mass, mouths forced open, forced to confess sins that were never theirs to begin with. The confessions overlap into a single unbearable murmur. Chains bite into flesh that's stopped bleeding a long time ago."},{"name":"Blood-Countess's First Spawn","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Ancient childe groomed to replace the matriarch","flavor":"The vampire matriarch's oldest childe, groomed for centuries to eventually replace her.","desc":"Groomed for centuries to one day replace the matriarch, he carries himself with the patient poise of someone playing a very long game. His fangs are immaculate, his manners perfect. He watches everyone in the room like he's already calculating their usefulness."},{"name":"Church-Broken Death Knight","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Crusader who slaughtered his flock, guards its grave","flavor":"A crusader who slaughtered his own congregation at the coven's whisper, and now guards their unmarked grave.","desc":"A crusader once, he slaughtered his own congregation at a whisper he still can't fully remember choosing to obey, and now he guards their unmarked grave in silence. His armor is scorched black at the joints. He does not want to talk about what he did."},{"name":"The Cellar Door's Real Keeper","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Generation-fed tunneling horror mistaken for legend","flavor":"A tunneling horror the covens have fed for generations, mistaken by the village for a mere legend.","desc":"The village calls it a legend — the thing the covens have fed for generations, tunneling somewhere below the cellar floor. When it finally breaks through, the smell of turned earth and old meat arrives first, then the scrape of something far too large for the space it's moving through."},{"name":"Matriarch of the Full Moon Pack","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Alpha whose bite founds a whole bloodline","flavor":"A were-beast alpha whose bite carries a curse potent enough to found an entire bloodline in one night.","desc":"She stands taller than any wolf has business standing, a bite in her jaw potent enough to found a bloodline in a single night. The pack defers to her with lowered heads. Her eyes hold something closer to ambition than hunger."},{"name":"The Archivist of Screams","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Librarian who became the sum of every scream","flavor":"A librarian who catalogued every scream in the manor's history and became the sum of them.","desc":"It was a librarian once, cataloguing every scream this manor ever produced, until it became the sum of all of them at once. It doesn't speak so much as replay — a hundred voices layered into one enormous, echoing wail that fills the halls it haunts."},{"name":"Blightmother's Chosen Vessel","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"yochlol","model":"yochlol","summary":"Cult conduit to something old beneath the church","flavor":"A cult's living conduit to something old and hungry beneath the church foundation.","desc":"The cult keeps it close to the church foundation, a conduit to something old and hungry underneath. Its shape barely holds still, edges smearing like wet ink whenever it moves. The congregation speaks of it in whispers even the cult leaders don't correct."},{"name":"The Reflection That Escaped","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Mirror-escaped vampire hunting its former family","flavor":"A vampire that shattered its own mirror-prison and now hunts the family it once served for a hundred years.","desc":"It shattered its own mirror-prison after a hundred years of quiet service to a family it fed on slowly and fondly. Now it hunts the descendants of that same house with a patience that used to be devotion and has curdled into something else entirely."},{"name":"Wax Cathedral Sentinel","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"Vigil-wax colossus animated by a century of grief","flavor":"A candle-wax colossus grown from a century of dripped vigil-tapers, animated by grief alone.","desc":"A century of dripped vigil-candles built this colossus one slow layer at a time, grief made solid and finally given shape. It moves with the heavy, deliberate weight of melted wax cooling mid-motion, trailing a faint smell of tallow and old smoke."},{"name":"The Possessed Cardinal","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"horned-devil","model":"horned-devil","summary":"Church official possessed, sermons not his own","flavor":"A high church official whose sermons now come from something else entirely, congregation unaware.","desc":"He delivers his sermon with total conviction, robes immaculate, voice carrying to the back pew — except the words underneath the words aren't his, and the congregation has no idea. Something behind his eyes watches the room like it's counting heads for later."},{"name":"Gravebound Necrohulk","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Plant","size":"Large","frame":"violet-fungus-necrohulk","model":"violet-fungus-necrohulk","summary":"Mass grave grown into a fungal flesh horror","flavor":"A mass grave that sprouted fungal flesh over centuries, wearing every buried skeleton at once.","desc":"A mass grave sprouted fungal flesh over centuries until it stood up wearing every skeleton buried in it at once, bone and pale mushroom-flesh fused into one lumbering horror. Spores drift off it with every step, and the ground underfoot feels soft in a way ground shouldn't."},{"name":"The Hollow Cardinal Enthroned","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Mummified saint-king ruling a dead congregation","flavor":"A saint-king mummified on his own cathedral throne, still ruling a congregation of the dead.","desc":"Mummified on the very throne he ruled from, he still holds court over a congregation of the dead who kneel in rows that never move. His voice, when it comes, sounds like it's speaking through the wrappings rather than around them.","traits":{"note": "Apex mummy-lord; congregation is set dressing, not summoned reinforcements beyond the SRD chassis.", "actions": []}},{"name":"The Bloodline's First Sin","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Founding ancestor enforcing the house's damning pact","flavor":"The founding ancestor of a cursed noble house, still enforcing the pact that damned every heir since.","desc":"He founded the house whose every heir has since been damned by the pact he struck, and he still enforces it from wherever the dead go to keep old promises. His armor bears a crest no living member of the family would recognize anymore.","traits":{"note": "Apex death-knight; fluff-only, standard SRD chassis.", "actions": []}},{"name":"The Rite Given Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"marilith","model":"marilith","summary":"Century-long ritual completed as living flesh","flavor":"A century-long summoning ritual finally completed, wearing the coven's collective sacrifice as a body.","desc":"A century of ritual chanting finally has somewhere to go — a body built from the coven's own collective sacrifice, six arms moving with a terrible, practiced grace. It doesn't remember being anything else. It only remembers being summoned, and it intends to stay.","traits":{"note": "Apex marilith-chassis; fluff-only, no new mechanics.", "actions": []}},{"name":"Grand Matriarch of the Blood Court","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"Vampire queen who transcended into lichdom","flavor":"A vampire queen who transcended even undeath through a lichdom pact, ruling both realms of the dead.","desc":"She was a vampire queen once, and found even that unlife too small — the lichdom pact she struck since lets her rule both the living dead and whatever waits past them. Frost follows her rather than blood. Her court kneels without needing to be told.","traits":{"note": "Apex lich-chassis reskinned as a transcended vampire queen; fluff-only.", "actions": []}},{"name":"The Everlasting Congregation","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Entire drowned parish fused into one singing mass","flavor":"An entire drowned parish fused by a cataclysmic ritual into one endless, singing, grasping mass.","desc":"An entire drowned parish fused by some cataclysmic rite into one endless, grasping mass, still singing the hymn that was playing when the water came in. Hundreds of mouths carry the same note. It moves like a tide rather than a body.","traits":{"note": "Apex; fluff-only reskin of the yuan-ti-abomination chassis, huge scale.", "actions": []}},{"name":"the Bloodless Bride","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"shuffling grave-bride, drawn to warmth and mourning","flavor":"A shambling grave-bride still in her rotted wedding linens, drawn to warmth and grief in equal measure; she doesn't hunt so much as attend, over and over, a wedding that ended badly.","desc":"She shuffles toward any warmth in the room, wedding linens gone the color of old rot, veil torn and dragging. She doesn't hunt so much as attend — the same ruined ceremony, over and over, and grief draws her in as surely as a pulse does.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"European folk-revenant/vampire folklore (pre-literary, no single owner)"},{"name":"Renfield's Kin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"insect-eating thrall serving something undead","flavor":"An asylum-thin thrall who traded sanity for a taste of borrowed immortality; catches flies, counts them, offers the count up like a prayer.","desc":"Thin as a coat rack, he crouches by the window catching flies between two fingers, counting each one aloud before he eats it like it's an offering. His eyes track something outside that isn't there. He talks about his master in the reverent hush of a man promising himself a reward that's coming any day now.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker, Dracula (1897, PD) — the Renfield archetype, generalized (not the named character)"},{"name":"the Carrion Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"beast (shapechanger)","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"grave-fed wolf edging toward the curse","flavor":"Not yet a full were-thing — just a wolf that has fed on the wrong grave and picked up a taste, and a little too much cunning, for it.","desc":"It looks like an ordinary wolf until it looks at you a beat too long, a little too aware of what it's deciding. It's fed on the wrong grave recently, and something in that meal is still working through it — not the full curse yet, just a taste, and a cunning it didn't used to have.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"generic European werewolf folklore (pre-literary tradition, not any specific IP)"},{"name":"Fog-Walker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-bat","model":"giant-bat","summary":"fog-bound phantom hound, harmless in clear air","flavor":"A pale hound-shape that only holds together inside fog; step into clear air and it's a stray dog again, confused and harmless.","desc":"A pale hound-shape paces just inside the treeline, only holding together as long as the fog does. Step past the mist-line and it's suddenly just a confused, ordinary stray, blinking like it doesn't know how it got there. Inside the fog, though, it moves like something built entirely out of it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-horror mist/fog-hound stock creature"},{"name":"the Somnambulist","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"a townsperson's cruel second self, out after dark","flavor":"A respectable townsperson by day; by dusk something narrower and meaner wears their face out into the streets. They remember none of it — the gloom remembers all of it.","desc":"By daylight they're perfectly respectable — a shopkeep, a clerk, someone you'd trust with your coin. After dusk something narrower and meaner takes the wheel, wearing the same face out into the dark streets. Come morning they remember nothing, though the gloom keeps a full account.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stevenson, Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (1886, PD) — the split-self archetype, generalized"},{"name":"Ashen Handmaiden","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"loyal ghost-servant, stuck in a burned house's routine","flavor":"Still dusting a house that burned down a century ago; she'll answer the door for guests who knocked before her own death, and mistake the party for them.","desc":"She dusts furniture that burned to ash a century ago, humming to herself in a house that's mostly char and moonlight. She'll answer the door for guests who knocked before she died, curtsy, and mistake you for them entirely, gesturing you toward a parlor that isn't there anymore.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-manor servant-ghost stock type"},{"name":"Innsmouth Hollow-Kin","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"gill-marked villager with an unspoken tide-hunger","flavor":"A villager whose family married the tide-line one generation too many; gill-slits under a high collar, and a hunger for the shallows nobody in town will name out loud.","desc":"A high collar doesn't quite hide the faint gill-slits along the throat, and the eyes have a damp, unblinking quality that the rest of the village pretends not to notice. There's a hunger in the way they look toward the shallows — one nobody in town will say out loud, including them.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic isolated-fishing-village/hybrid-folk stock type (not any specific IP's mythos)"},{"name":"the Wolf-Cursed","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid (shapechanger)","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"the classic moon-bound curse, mid-transformation","flavor":"Cursed at a crossroads or bitten in a churchyard — the story varies by village, but the moon doesn't care which version is true.","desc":"Whatever the crossroads or the churchyard did to them, the change comes on mid-word sometimes, jaw stretching wrong around a sentence that doesn't finish human. Every version of the story blames a different night. The moon isn't interested in which one's true.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"generic European werewolf/loup-garou folklore"},{"name":"the Steward of the House","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"eloquent, grieving, stitched-together giant","flavor":"Stitched together and abandoned by its maker, it reads philosophy it finds in ruined libraries and hates almost as eloquently as it grieves; cornered, it is devastating, and it knows exactly why it became this.","desc":"Stitched from parts that don't quite match and abandoned by the one who made him, he reads philosophy scavenged from ruined libraries in a low, articulate voice. He hates as eloquently as he grieves, and he knows exactly, precisely why he became this — which makes cornering him a mistake.","traits":{"note": "Elite flesh-golem chassis reskinned as an articulate, wounded intellect (Shelley's Creature, novel-accurate — not the mute-brute film version).", "actions": [{"name": "A Reasoned Grievance", "text": "Once per encounter, it may forgo an attack to deliver a devastating accusation at a creature within 30 ft that can hear it, forcing a Wisdom save or that creature has disadvantage on its next attack roll, shaken by the truth of it."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Shelley, Frankenstein (1818, PD) — the Creature, our own take, novel-version only (articulate, wounded, not a mute brute)"},{"name":"Lady of the Blood Countess's Line","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"patient, affectionate centuries-old blood-drinker","flavor":"Centuries of patient, intimate hunting have made her gentler than any predator has a right to be — she prefers a slow, doting courtship of her prey to a chase.","desc":"Centuries of patient, intimate hunting have made her gentler than any predator has business being — she prefers a long, doting courtship of her prey to anything so crude as a chase. Her affection is entirely genuine, which is somehow worse.","traits":{"note": "Elite night-hag chassis reskinned as Carmilla — affectionate, patient predator, not a hag-archetype villain.", "actions": []},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Le Fanu, Carmilla (1872, PD)"},{"name":"the Riderless Terror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"headless rider hunting a replacement skull, every autumn","flavor":"A cannonball took his head at some forgotten muster, and every autumn he rides out looking for a replacement — pumpkin, skull, or yours, he isn't particular.","desc":"A cannonball took his head at some forgotten muster, and every autumn since he rides out on a skeletal warhorse looking for a replacement. Pumpkin, skull, or yours — he genuinely isn't particular, so long as something rides home on his shoulders by dawn.","traits":{"note": "Elite; warhorse-skeleton chassis, fluff-only Headless Horseman reskin.", "actions": []},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Irving, The Legend of Sleepy Hollow (1820, PD) — the Headless Horseman"},{"name":"the Unseen Guest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"invisible chemist, tracked by breath and footprints","flavor":"Bandaged only when he wants to be seen; the rest of the time you track him by breath-fog on cold glass and the footprints that appear in spilled flour.","desc":"Bandages only appear when he wants to be seen; otherwise you track him by breath-fog on cold glass and footprints blooming suddenly in spilled flour. His voice comes from empty air, reasonable and a little delighted with himself, right up until it turns cruel.","traits":{"note": "Elite invisible-stalker chassis reskinned as Wells's Griffin — a chemist undone by his own formula, not a horror-film design.", "actions": []},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Wells, The Invisible Man (1897, PD) — the Griffin archetype, our own take (a chemist undone by his own formula, not a specific film design)"},{"name":"the Portrait's Truth","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"ageless beauty whose hidden portrait holds the rot","flavor":"Ageless and lovely to look at; somewhere in the house hangs the ledger of every cruelty, rotting so its owner never has to. Destroy the portrait and you destroy the deal.","desc":"Ageless and lovely to look at, unmarked by a single year of the cruelty in his history — because somewhere in the house hangs a portrait doing the aging and the rotting for him. Destroy that canvas and whatever he's owed comes due all at once.","traits":{"note": "Elite vampire-spawn chassis reskinned as Dorian Gray; portrait-destruction as a narrative kill-switch is a DM-adjudicated fiction hook, not a new mechanic — SRD stats otherwise.", "actions": []},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Wilde, The Picture of Dorian Gray (1890, PD)"},{"name":"the Baba Yaga","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"arch-hag","summary":"chicken-legged hut-witch who judges before she helps","flavor":"Her hut walks on chicken legs and judges visitors before she does; help without being asked and she rewards extravagantly, ask without helping and you become the next fence-post skull.","desc":"Her hut creaks past on legs like a chicken's, fence posts around it capped with skulls old and new. She judges visitors before she helps them — offer aid first and she rewards lavishly; ask first and you risk joining the fence line.","traits":{"note": "High-tier arch-hag chassis reskinned as Baba Yaga; judgment mechanic is DM-adjudicated narrative behavior (help-first vs ask-first), not a new combat rule.", "actions": []},"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Slavic folklore — Baba Yaga (settled, widely published legend figure, not a living closed tradition)"},{"name":"the Gorgon's Daughter","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"gaze-cursed gorgon, curating a garden of statues","flavor":"She keeps a garden of the men who looked, arranged by the year they made the mistake; she's stopped being angry about it and started being a curator.","desc":"She tends a garden of statues, each one a man who looked too long, arranged neatly by the year of his mistake. She's long past angry about any of it — these days she's more curator than monster, walking the rows with something like pride.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Medusa (ancient, no owner)"},{"name":"the Opera-House Phantom","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"masked genius-architect ruling from beneath the stage","flavor":"A genius disfigured and driven underground who built a kingdom of trapdoors and misdirection beneath the stage he was never allowed to stand on; he'll kill for the right voice as readily as he'd die for it.","desc":"A mask catches the gaslight below the stage he was never allowed to stand on, and beneath a labyrinth of trapdoors and false walls, a genius disfigured by the world plots his masterpiece. He'll kill for the right voice as readily as he'd die for it.","traits":{"note": "High-tier assassin chassis reskinned as the Phantom; fluff-only Leroux novel version.", "actions": []},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Leroux, The Phantom of the Opera (1910, PD)"},{"name":"the Impaler-Count","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"ancient, courtly count who owns the road home","flavor":"Old enough to have negotiated treaties in three dead empires; he doesn't need to chase you, because he already owns the roads, the weather, and the wolves between you and the border.","desc":"Old enough to have signed treaties in empires that no longer exist, he receives you with courtly warmth in a castle that owns the roads, the weather, and the wolves between you and the border. He has no need to chase you. He already has.","traits":{"note": "Apex vampire chassis reskinned as Dracula, novel-accurate courtly/commanding version.", "actions": [{"name": "Master of the Road", "text": "Once per long rest, as a bonus action, it may summon a pack of wolves (use standard wolf statistics, up to 4) to arrive from the surrounding terrain within 1 minute."}]},"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker, Dracula (1897, PD) — novel version (charismatic, ancient, commanding wolves/mist, not any film's fangs-and-cape design)"},{"name":"the Woeful Cry","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"keening death-omen spirit; herald, not killer","flavor":"She doesn't kill; she announces. Hearing her keen at your door is the gloom's way of telling you the paperwork on your death is already filed — what you do with the notice is still yours.","desc":"She keens from somewhere just out of sight at your door, a note that isn't meant to kill — only to announce. Hearing it is the gloom's way of telling you the paperwork on your death is already filed; what you do with that notice is still entirely yours.","source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Irish/Scottish folklore — the banshee (settled literary/folkloric figure, generalized, treated as an omen-spirit rather than flattened into a stock ghost)"},{"name":"the House That Remembers","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Huge","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"a haunted manor that rearranges itself to relive its dead","flavor":"Every family that ever died under this roof left a little of their worst moment behind, and the house learned to move the furniture with it; it doesn't want visitors, it wants witnesses.","desc":"Furniture slides on its own to recreate the worst moment of whoever last died under this roof, over and over, walls breathing faintly with old grief. It doesn't want visitors so much as witnesses — someone to see what happened here and finally believe it.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-haunted-house stock type (the manor-as-monster trope)"}],
 "bright-kingdom":[{"name":"Wind-Up Soldier","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"clockwork toy soldier, keeps marching until unwound","flavor":"A key juts from its back, ticking down; when it hits zero the toy soldier salutes and falls apart, spilling gears. Its bayonet-poke still draws real blood.","desc":"A key the size of a fist juts from its back, ticking down in tight little clicks as it marches — left, right, left — painted boots striking the ground in perfect time. Its face is a fixed smile, its bayonet a toy prop until it isn't. When the key stops turning it snaps to attention, salutes no one, and comes apart in a spray of gears that keep twitching on the ground."},{"name":"Plush Ripper","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"cuddly stuffed animal hiding a mouthful of hooks","flavor":"Button eyes, felt seams, a music-box giggle — and a mouth full of hooked steel teeth sewn in wrong. It cuddles up before it bites.","desc":"Button eyes, calico fur, a music-box hum that plays when you squeeze it — everything about it says hug me. The seams along its belly are stitched wrong, puckered where something was forced in sideways: a jaw's worth of fishhooks, curved and rusted, packed into stuffing that still smells like a nursery."},{"name":"Candy-Cane Golem","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"hard-candy construct, sweet shell hides razor shards","flavor":"A shambling column of hard-shell peppermint, sweet enough to lure children and sharp enough at the broken edges to open an artery.","desc":"It shambles upright as a striped pillar of hard candy, red and white swirled glass-slick in the light, sweet enough that the air around it smells like peppermint. Where it's cracked — shoulder, hip, the ragged stump of an arm — the edges catch and glint, each broken facet honed sharp enough to open a vein."},{"name":"Jack-in-the-Box Stalker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"boxed ambusher springs out mid-tune, already too close","flavor":"Crouches motionless inside a painted crate for hours, cranking out a tinny tune, until the lid bursts and it's already inside your guard.","desc":"A painted crate sits motionless at the edge of the room, cranking out the same eight notes over and over, patient as a held breath. The tune always seems to end one beat sooner than it should — because by then the lid has already burst and it's already inside your guard, grinning, close enough to touch."},{"name":"Laughing-Mask Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","model":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","summary":"swarm of grinning masks that clatter, snap, giggle","flavor":"A drift of hollow carnival masks, all fixed grins, clattering and snapping at ankles in a chorus of muffled giggling that never quite becomes words.","desc":"A drift of hollow carnival masks skitters low across the floor on invisible legs, papier-mâché grins all fixed the same wide curve, clattering together like wind chimes made of teeth. They giggle — not one voice but many, muffled behind painted mouths, a chorus that never resolves into words."},{"name":"Balloon-Skin Grub","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"squeaking balloon-hide grub that deflates when popped","flavor":"Squeaks like a dog toy with every bite; pop it and it deflates into a wet rubbery flap that still twitches.","desc":"It squeaks with every wet, looping inch it drags itself forward, a fat larval shape stretched tight and glossy like a balloon left too long in the sun. Puncture it anywhere and it doesn't die so much as deflate, sagging into a rubbery flap on the ground that keeps twitching long after the air's gone out."},{"name":"Carnival Tout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"grinning barker who herds marks toward the big tent","flavor":"Striped vest, painted grin, a barker's patter that never stops — 'Step right up!' — while it herds you toward the tent with a knife up its sleeve.","desc":"Striped vest, chalk-white grin, a barker's patter that never quite stops — step right up, don't be shy, the show's about to start. He keeps one hand out for your ticket and the other tucked behind his back, and the knife in that hand has heard every word of his pitch before."},{"name":"Static-Charge Kitten","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Tiny","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"sparking fey kitten, a pet that shocks you dead","flavor":"Fur standing on end, purring like a dying engine; every pet it gives back is a jolt that can stop a weak heart.","desc":"Fur standing on end, purring like an engine winding toward failure, it winds between your ankles wanting to be picked up. Scratch behind its ears and it leans in gratefully — and discharges everything it's been building, a jolt sharp enough to stop a weak heart mid-beat."},{"name":"Marching Peanut","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"grinning peanut-soldier in an endless parade conga line","flavor":"A grinning legume-soldier on toothpick legs, part of an endless conga line pouring out of a parade float. Salted, but never quite dead.","desc":"Grinning, salted, and strapped into a tiny soldier's coat, it goose-steps in an endless conga line that spills out of some parade float no one remembers starting. Pop one and the line behind it doesn't break stride — it just closes the gap and keeps marching over the shell."},{"name":"Piñata Brute","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"paper-hide brute that bursts into candy shrapnel","flavor":"Papier-mâché skin stretched taut over a swinging club-arm; crack it open in the right spot and it detonates candy shrapnel and stolen teeth.","desc":"Papier-mâché skin, bright crepe-paper fringe, a swinging club arm sized for a real fight rather than a birthday — it lumbers forward grinning through its painted seams. Crack it open in the wrong place at the wrong time and it doesn't spill candy so much as detonate it, shrapnel and stolen teeth alike.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Burst Open", "text": "on death, explodes in a burst of candy shrapnel dealing minor damage to anything adjacent — a death-burst layered on the ogre chassis"}]}},{"name":"Carousel Nightmare","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"carved carousel horse torn free, circling for blood","flavor":"A painted wooden charger torn loose from its pole, galloping in place no longer — gilt cracked, glass eyes rolling, hooves that never stop circling for the kill.","desc":"A painted wooden charger tears free of its pole mid-spin, gilt paint cracked along every seam, glass eyes rolling loose in their sockets. It doesn't need the carousel anymore — it gallops in place on nothing, hooves striking sparks off the air itself, circling tighter the longer you stand still."},{"name":"Sugar-Rush Harlequin","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"pixie-wonderbringer","summary":"jittering harlequin brawler, hopped up on rock candy","flavor":"Diamond-patched and cackling, it mainlines rock candy between blows, moving in jittery double-time no eye can quite track until the pratfall becomes a killing blow.","desc":"Diamond-patched and cackling, it mainlines fistfuls of rock candy straight from a pouch at its belt between every blow, jittering in a double-time no eye can quite track. One second it's mid-pratfall, arms flailing for balance — the next its foot's already connected, and the joke was never the point."},{"name":"Bubblegum Ooze","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"pink bubblegum ooze, engulfs and dissolves you slowly","flavor":"Bright pink, sickly-sweet-smelling, and stickier than any trap — it swallows whole and digests slow enough you can hear yourself dissolve.","desc":"Bright pink, glossy, and sickly sweet-smelling from across the room, it moves in a slow, stretching roll that looks almost playful. It swallows whole rather than strikes, and the digestion is slow enough — deliberately slow — that you can hear your own voice going soft and distant from somewhere inside it."},{"name":"Claw-Machine Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"arcade claw-machine on legs, rigged to never miss","flavor":"A coin-op cabinet on stilted legs, its steel claw always 'almost' catching you — until the game rigs itself to let the claw actually close.","desc":"A coin-op cabinet stands up on four stilted, spring-loaded legs, its glass front lit garish yellow, a steel claw dangling and swaying overhead. The claw drops for you again and again, 'almost' catching, teasing — until the machine decides the game's rigged enough in its favor, and the claw actually closes."},{"name":"Funhouse Double","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"mirror-warped double wearing your own stretched face","flavor":"Steps out of a warped mirror wearing your own face stretched a little too wide, mimicking your voice back at you a half-second behind.","desc":"It steps out of a warped funhouse mirror wearing your own face, stretched a fraction too wide at the mouth, the proportions just wrong enough to itch at the back of your skull. It mimics your voice back at you a half-second behind, testing the words in your mouth before it tries anything with its hands."},{"name":"Ferris-Wheel Horror","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gargoyle","summary":"rolling wheel-boned horror, its gaze turns you to stone","flavor":"Rusted gondolas for a ribcage, it rolls upright on its own broken wheel-rim, and anything that looks too long into its lantern-eyes seizes up stone-still.","desc":"Rusted gondola cars hang where ribs should be, and it rolls upright on the broken rim of its own wheel, groaning metal on stone with every rotation. Lanterns burn where its eyes should sit, and anything that stares too long into that light finds its joints locking, stone-still, mid-stride."},{"name":"Cotton-Candy Wraith","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"sugar-sweet drifting haze that feeds on happy memories","flavor":"A drifting pink haze that smells of childhood summer fairs, sweet right up until it's inside your lungs, unspooling your last happy memory as it feeds.","desc":"A drifting pink haze rolls low across the ground, smelling exactly like a childhood summer fair — sugar and dust and distant calliope music. It's sweet right up until it's inside your lungs, and only then do you feel it pulling at something warm and specific, unspooling your happiest memory thread by thread as it feeds."},{"name":"Arcade Sentinel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"glitching screen-boss, bolts skip you straight to wounded","flavor":"Pixelated and buzzing, it flickers between screen and floor, hurling glitching bolts that skip frames of your body straight past the pain and into the wound.","desc":"Pixelated at the edges, buzzing where it should be solid, it flickers between the screen's glow and the floor like a loading bar that never finishes. The bolts it hurls don't burn or cut so much as skip — your body jumps frames straight past the pain and lands, already, in the wound."},{"name":"Mascot-Suit Puppeteer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"grell","summary":"hollow mascot suit worn by tendrils wearing your smile","flavor":"The beloved mascot costume is empty air on the inside — a knot of grasping tendrils wearing the plush like a second skin, waving for the children with someone else's hand.","desc":"The beloved mascot costume waves cheerfully from its post at the gate, plush and huge and welcoming — but the inside of that suit is empty air where a body should be. A knot of grasping tendrils wears the plush like a second skin, and the wave it gives the children is worked by someone else's hand."},{"name":"Firework Effigy","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"living fireworks display, still building to a finale","flavor":"Built for the finale and never told the show is over, it keeps blooming into new colors overhead, each burst a little closer to the crowd.","desc":"Built for one grand finale and never told the show ended, it keeps blooming overhead in fresh colors — gold, then violet, then a red that lingers too long. Each burst climbs a little lower than the last, the sparks drifting closer to the upturned faces below, still waiting for its cue to stop."},{"name":"The Ringmaster","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"top-hatted ringmaster who commands the whole show","flavor":"Top hat, painted smile, a whip that cracks louder than thunder — every act in the tent performs for him, willing or not, and the show never ends until he says so.","desc":"Top hat cocked just so, painted smile fixed under the brim, he cracks a whip that snaps louder than real thunder over the ring. Every act under this tent performs for him — willing or not — and the show does not end, cannot end, until he decides to say so.","traits":{"note": "a compulsion caster — the whip-crack forces movement/action into 'the act' rather than dealing direct harm", "actions": [{"name": "Command Performance", "text": "cracks the whip to force a target into a scripted action of the Ringmaster's choosing on its next turn"}]}},{"name":"The Overwound Nutcracker","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"giant nutcracker soldier, jaw snaps clean through bone","flavor":"Painted uniform, oversized jaw hinged to crack more than nuts — every strike is a full-body snap of that grinning mouth, splintering whatever's fed to it.","desc":"Painted uniform buttons gleam under the lights, and its oversized jaw hinges open on a spring built for cracking more than nuts. Every strike is a full-body snap of that grinning mouth, hinge and teeth together, splintering whatever gets fed into it with a sound like a tree going down."},{"name":"Vending-Machine Colossus","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"coin-slot golem, dispenses violence for your last coin","flavor":"Rows of snack-slots for a chest, it dispenses whatever you 'paid' for — usually a fist — and jams itself deliberately so you keep feeding it coins.","desc":"Rows of snack-slots line its chest like ribs, coin slot glowing faintly at its sternum, and it dispenses exactly what you 'paid' for — which is usually a fist. It jams itself on purpose after every payout, rattling and grinding, because it wants you to keep feeding it coins."},{"name":"The Birthday King","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"planetar","summary":"crowned rigger of the game no one is meant to win","flavor":"Crowned in melted candles, he presides over the game you cannot win — the wheel is rigged, the dice are his teeth, and every prize you claim costs you a year of your life.","desc":"Crowned in a ring of melted, dripping candle wax, he presides over a game rigged from the first roll of the dice — his own teeth. Every prize claimed at his table comes billed in years, and he collects with the same delighted, patient smile he wears for the birthday song.","traits":{"note": "the rigged-game boss — every action he takes is framed as a 'fair' game the table already lost", "actions": [{"name": "Rig the Wheel", "text": "forces a reroll against a target it already knows the outcome of, then narrates the loss as if luck decided it"}]}},{"name":"The Grinning Prize","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"kraken","summary":"top-shelf plush titan, a dozen button-eyes snap open","flavor":"The top shelf's biggest stuffed monster, too big for any booth, its dozen glass-button eyes all open at once the moment you finally win it.","desc":"It hangs from the top shelf of the biggest booth in the midway, too large for any prize rack, stitched fur worn soft from decades of longing stares. The moment someone finally wins it down, all dozen of its glass button-eyes snap open at once, and none of them blink."},{"name":"Tin Drummer Boy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"drumming tin toy that locks your heartbeat to its beat","flavor":"Beats an unbreakable march rhythm that syncs enemy hearts to its tempo until they seize up mid-stride.","desc":"It beats an unbreakable, driving march on a tin drum strapped across its chest, the rhythm never wavering, never speeding, never stopping. Listen too long and your own pulse starts falling in step with the beat — right up until the tempo locks your heart mid-stride."},{"name":"Rag Doll Skulker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"limp rag doll that scuttles the second you look away","flavor":"Limp and lifeless until your back is turned, then it scuttles on button-thread joints, needle fingers first.","desc":"It hangs limp over a shelf or a windowsill, button eyes half-lidded, utterly lifeless — for as long as you're looking. The instant your back turns, it scuttles forward on thread-thin joints, needle-fingers reaching first, faster than a thing stuffed with cotton has any right to move."},{"name":"Gumdrop Sprite","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Tiny","frame":"pixie","model":"pixie","summary":"sugar-shard pixie giggling above dog-whistle pitch","flavor":"A candy-coated pixie that pelts foes with hardened sugar shrapnel, giggling in a register only dogs and the dying can hear.","desc":"A candy-coated pixie no bigger than a hand, it hovers in a shimmer of sugar dust, giggling in a pitch that climbs past what most ears can follow. It pelts with fistfuls of hardened sugar shrapnel, each shard glinting rainbow before it draws blood, still giggling the whole time."},{"name":"Squeak-Toy Hound","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"rubber toy dog whose bite-squeak gets louder with damage","flavor":"Every bite compresses its rubber chest into a cheerful squeak that somehow gets louder the deeper the wound.","desc":"A rubber toy dog trots forward on stiff little legs, every bite compressing its chest into a cheerful, high-pitched squeak. The wound doesn't quiet the sound — somehow the squeak gets louder with each deeper bite, cheerful and awful in equal measure."},{"name":"Confetti Wisp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"glitter-storm elemental made of razor-edged party confetti","flavor":"A cloud of shredded paper and glitter that swirls into a blinding storm, each fleck razor-cut at the edge.","desc":"A cloud of shredded paper and glitter swirls at head height, catching the light in flickers of gold and red, harmless-looking as a party favor gone loose. It tightens into a blinding storm on approach, and every fleck in that glittering cloud is cut razor-sharp at the edge."},{"name":"Marionette Cutpurse","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"string-puppet thief worked by an unseen hand overhead","flavor":"Jointed limbs jerk on visible strings that lead up into empty air; something above is definitely still pulling.","desc":"Its jointed limbs jerk in stiff, unnatural arcs, strings trailing up from wrist and shoulder into open air with nothing visibly holding the other end. It picks pockets with a puppet's clumsy precision, and whatever's pulling those strings is patient, deliberate, and still up there somewhere."},{"name":"Pop-Gun Grenadier","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"toy-soldier grenadier lobbing shrapnel-cored party favors","flavor":"Fires corked party-favor rounds that detonate on impact with genuine shrapnel hidden under the cork.","desc":"Dressed in a toy soldier's bright piping, it lobs corked rounds from a party-favor gun with a cheerful little pop and a trailing streamer. The cork is a lie — packed shrapnel rides under it, and the party favor detonates on impact like it means it."},{"name":"Licorice Whip-Vine","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"vine-blight","summary":"sticky black candy-vine that lashes and constricts","flavor":"Sticky black ropes of edible-looking vine lash out and constrict, tasting faintly of anise and old blood.","desc":"Sticky black ropes coil up out of the ground, glossy and candy-slick, smelling faintly of anise from a distance. Up close that smell curdles into something coppery, and the vine lashes and constricts with a strength no piece of candy should have."},{"name":"Kite-String Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"paper kite dragging a bone-child on garrote-taut string","flavor":"A torn paper kite drags a skeletal child's shape behind it on razor-taut string, forever chasing an updraft that never comes.","desc":"A torn paper kite dips and jerks against a sky with no wind, dragging a small skeletal shape behind it on taut, razor-thin string. It's forever chasing an updraft that never comes, and the bone-child at the end of its line reaches for anyone who gets too near the line's path."},{"name":"Snow-Globe Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"ice-mephit","model":"ice-mephit","summary":"trapped globe-spirit that shakes itself into a blizzard","flavor":"Trapped forever inside a floating glass sphere, it shakes itself into a blinding blizzard when threatened.","desc":"Trapped forever inside a floating glass sphere no bigger than a fist, a tiny pale shape drifts in slow, endless circles through painted snow. Threaten it and the whole globe shakes violently, the gentle flurry inside erupting into a blinding, freezing blizzard that spills out past the glass."},{"name":"Puppet-Show Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"hand-puppet corpse twitching to an absent puppeteer","flavor":"A hand-puppet corpse with a painted grin sewn permanently open, fingers still twitching to an absent puppeteer's cues.","desc":"A hand-puppet corpse lies slumped in its little painted booth, felt mouth stitched into a permanent, cheerful grin. Its fingers twitch on unseen cues even with no hand inside it, jerking through a performance for a puppeteer that isn't — visibly — there."},{"name":"Ticket-Booth Imp","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Small","frame":"imp","model":"imp","summary":"toll-imp who brands hands and demands blood admission","flavor":"Demands admission in blood before letting anyone leave the fairgrounds, stamping hands with a brand that never fades.","desc":"It leans out from a chipped ticket window, small and grinning, and demands admission before anyone's allowed to leave the fairgrounds. The toll is blood, always blood, and the brand it stamps on the back of your hand doesn't fade no matter how hard you scrub."},{"name":"Streamer Serpent","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"giant-venomous-snake","summary":"crepe-scaled snake whose sweet venom masks as punch","flavor":"Crepe-paper scales trail like party streamers as it strikes, its venom sweet enough to be mistaken for punch.","desc":"Crepe-paper scales trail behind it like party streamers caught in a breeze, rustling with every fluid, sinuous strike. Its venom tastes sweet on the way in — sweet enough to be mistaken for punch — right up until it isn't."},{"name":"Popcorn Blight","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"kernel-husk plant that bursts in scalding shrapnel steam","flavor":"Clusters of white kernel-husks burst apart in a shower of blinding steam and hooked husk-shrapnel.","desc":"Clustered white kernel-husks sway together on a single stalk, gently rattling, looking for all the world like an oversized snack display. Get close and they burst apart at once in a shower of blinding steam and hooked husk-shrapnel, popping like a string of firecrackers."},{"name":"Domino Sentinel","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"toppling domino construct that chain-falls in a crushing line","flavor":"Stands rigid in a row until one falls; then the whole line topples in a cascading, crushing avalanche.","desc":"It stands rigid in a long, silent row alongside its fellows, painted pips facing outward, waiting. The instant one falls — pushed, struck, or simply tired of standing — the whole line topples in a cascading, crushing avalanche down its length.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chain Fall", "text": "when one Domino Sentinel is knocked prone or destroyed, every other Domino Sentinel adjacent to it in the line falls too, each dealing its normal slam to whatever's beneath"}]}},{"name":"Wooden Nutcracker Cadet","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"shell-cracking nutcracker jaw that prefers fingers now","flavor":"Painted teeth clamp with a jaw built for cracking shells, now finding fingers just as satisfying.","desc":"Painted teeth clamp shut with a crisp, mechanical snap, a jaw built and hinged specifically for cracking shells. It's found fingers just as satisfying as walnuts, and it doesn't seem to notice the difference anymore."},{"name":"Yo-Yo Stringer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"street performer garroting foes with a weighted yo-yo","flavor":"Whips a weighted yo-yo on garrote-strength string that returns to hand freighted with whatever it wraps.","desc":"A street performer flicks a weighted yo-yo out in a lazy, showy arc, garrote-taut string singing as it spins. It always returns to hand — freighted, on the way back, with whatever got wrapped up in its loop."},{"name":"Fun-Fair Goblin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"goblin-warrior","model":"goblin-warrior","summary":"rigged carnival-game goblin who charges fingers, not coins","flavor":"Small, gaudy, and vicious, it hawks rigged ring-toss games where losing costs a finger, not a coin.","desc":"Small, gaudy, and grinning under a striped awning, it hawks a rigged ring-toss game with a carnival barker's practiced charm. Losing costs more than the entry fee — the goblin's price for a bad throw is a finger, taken with the same cheerful patter as the pitch."},{"name":"Prize-Claw Scuttler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"detached claw-machine grabber skittering on cable legs","flavor":"A detached claw-machine grabber skitters on cable legs, forever hunting something small enough to clamp and lift.","desc":"A detached claw-machine grabber skitters low across the ground on thin cable legs, three steel prongs opening and closing, testing the air. It hunts for anything small enough to clamp and lift, dragging its catch back toward a glass box that isn't there anymore."},{"name":"Whack-a-Mole Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-badger","model":"giant-badger","summary":"burrowing mole-toy that pops up to bite, then vanishes","flavor":"Pops from hidden holes to bite before vanishing back down, rewarding the quick with only a bruised knuckle.","desc":"It pops from a hidden hole with a cheerful little chime, bites once, and vanishes back underground before a hand can follow. The quick get nothing worse than a bruised knuckle for their trouble; the slow don't get a second chance to swing."},{"name":"Fortune Machine Familiar","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"fortune-teller automaton whose cards come horribly true","flavor":"A mechanical gypsy bust dispenses cursed fortune cards that come cheerfully, horribly true.","desc":"A mechanical fortune-teller's bust sits behind curtained glass, painted eyes glowing faintly, one hand hovering over a slot. The cards it dispenses read cheerful nonsense in looping print — and every single one of them comes true, horribly, exactly as written."},{"name":"Bumper-Car Brawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"stripped bumper-car chassis that charges and never stops grinning","flavor":"A stripped-down bumper car chassis charges anything in its lane, crumpling on impact and grinning wider each hit.","desc":"A stripped-down bumper car chassis rattles forward on bare wheels, sparking where the roof used to be, painted grin scorched onto its front bumper. It charges anything in its lane, crumples satisfyingly on impact, and grins a little wider with every hit it takes."},{"name":"Peppermint Stalker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"caroling candy-striped goblinoid dragging prey to sugar vats","flavor":"A candy-cane-striped homunculus with a hook-shaped hand, humming carols while it drags foes toward the sugar vats.","desc":"Candy-cane stripes wind up its small frame, one hand curled into a permanent hook, humming a carol under its breath as it moves. The tune never stops, not even while it drags something struggling toward the sugar vats steaming somewhere out of sight."},{"name":"Merry-Go-Round Foal","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse","model":"warhorse","summary":"carousel horse torn free of its pole, still bobbing as it tramples","flavor":"A gilded carousel horse tears free of its pole mid-spin, still bobbing up and down as it tramples the crowd.","desc":"A gilded carousel horse tears free of its brass pole mid-spin, paint chipping, still bobbing rhythmically up and down as it moves. It tramples with the same up-down gait it always had on the ride, indifferent to the difference between a painted platform and flesh."},{"name":"Face-Paint Marauder","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"grease-painted brawler laughing through every clubbing swing","flavor":"Grease-paint smeared into a permanent scream-grin, it laughs through every swing of its balloon-animal club.","desc":"Grease paint smears its face into a permanent scream-grin, garish red and white running where sweat's cut through it. It laughs the whole way through every swing of its balloon-animal club, delighted by its own violence like a birthday party trick that got out of hand."},{"name":"Toy-Chest Mimic","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"toy-chest mimic whose lid is lined with teeth","flavor":"Looks like the best toy box in the playroom until the lid's teeth close on the hand that reaches in.","desc":"It sits invitingly open at the edge of the nursery, the best-looking toy chest in the room, lid propped just so. Reach in for whatever's glinting inside and the lid's hidden row of teeth closes tight around the offering wrist.","traits":{"note": "straight mimic-chassis reskin — lid-bite replaces the pseudopod slam, disguise-as-object unchanged"}},{"name":"Two-Faced Jester","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"jester whose two painted faces switch mid-attack, unpredictably","flavor":"One painted face grins, the other weeps; it switches mid-sentence and mid-swing, and you never learn which is the lie.","desc":"One painted face grins ear to ear; the other, worn on the back of the same head, weeps black greasepaint tears. It switches mid-sentence and mid-swing between the two, and you never quite learn in time which face was telling the truth."},{"name":"Marionette Master","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"puppeteer who yanks strings to animate a squad mid-fight","flavor":"Works a cross of tangled strings that yank a squad of animate puppets into sudden, borrowed violence.","desc":"A cross of tangled strings hangs from both raised hands, each thread running taut to a slack-limbed puppet somewhere in the crowd. A single practiced yank animates the whole squad at once, borrowed limbs jerking into sudden, coordinated violence."},{"name":"Whirligig Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gorgon","summary":"spinning rotor-ride whose scythe gondolas scatter red confetti","flavor":"A carnival ride's rotor arms spin faster than sight, each seat a scythe-edged gondola scattering the crowd in red confetti.","desc":"A carnival ride's rotor arms spin faster than the eye can follow, each seat swapped out for a curved, scythe-edged gondola. It scatters the crowd in a spray of shredded red confetti with every full rotation, never once slowing its pace."},{"name":"Sawdust Strongman","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"ettin","summary":"two-headed circus strongman crushing while both heads lie","flavor":"A two-headed circus strongman act, each head shouting a different crowd-pleasing lie while the shared arms crush the truth out of you.","desc":"Two heads sit atop one broad circus-strongman's frame, each shouting a different crowd-pleasing lie over the other's voice. The shared arms crush regardless of which head is winning the argument, squeezing the truth — and everything else — out of whatever they've grabbed."},{"name":"Balloon-Animal Chimera","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"cockatrice-regent","model":"cockatrice-regent","summary":"twisted-latex chimera that pops apart and re-knots itself","flavor":"Twisted latex shapes into a dog-headed, snake-necked menagerie that pops apart and re-knots itself around a wound.","desc":"Twisted latex forms itself into a dog-headed, snake-necked menagerie, squeaking faintly at every joint as it moves. Struck hard enough, it pops apart into loose twisted shapes — and simply re-knots itself back together around the wound a moment later."},{"name":"Cotton-Candy Spinner Witch","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"sugar-floss witch whose spun webs harden into glass thread","flavor":"Spins sugar-floss webs from a rusted machine-heart, luring children close before the floss hardens to glass thread.","desc":"A rusted machine-heart spins sugar-floss into long, drifting webs, sweet-smelling and pink, luring children close with the promise of a treat. The floss goes rigid the instant it's touched, hardening into threads of glass sharp enough to hold and to cut."},{"name":"Painted Pony Revenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"ghost carousel horse trampling an endless six-foot loop","flavor":"A carousel horse's ghost gallops the same six feet of track forever, trampling anyone standing where the pole once was.","desc":"A carousel horse's translucent ghost gallops the same six feet of empty track it always did, forever circling a brass pole that isn't there anymore. It tramples anyone foolish enough to stand where that pole used to be, blind to anything outside its old loop."},{"name":"Rubber-Duck Leviathan","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-crocodile","model":"giant-crocodile","summary":"cheerful bath-toy giant with a jaw unhinging past its grin","flavor":"An oversized bath toy bobs cheerfully atop the fairground's dunk-tank pool, jaw unhinging wider than its floating grin should allow.","desc":"An oversized bath toy bobs cheerfully atop the dunk-tank's dark water, rubber squeaking faintly with each gentle rise and fall. Its jaw unhinges far wider than its painted, floating grin should allow, opening a mouth built for something much bigger than a bathtub."},{"name":"Static Shock Clown","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"azer-pyromancer","model":"azer-pyromancer","summary":"crackling clown discharging balloon-rubbed static arcs","flavor":"Rubber-soled and crackling, it rubs a balloon against its own painted hide until arcs of blue static leap for the crowd.","desc":"Rubber-soled and crackling faintly at the fingertips, it rubs a balloon slowly against its own painted hide, building charge with obvious relish. Arcs of blue static leap for the nearest crowd the second it's built up enough, crackling like tiny lightning between fairground lights."},{"name":"Fun House Mirror-Stalker","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"mirror-dweller that stretches your reflection's arm to grab you","flavor":"Lives in the warped glass of every funhouse mirror, stretching your reflection's arm long enough to reach through and grab.","desc":"It lives in the warped glass of every funhouse mirror in the hall, watching your reflection lag a half-second behind your real movements. Given the chance, it stretches that reflected arm impossibly long, reaching straight through the glass to grab the real one."},{"name":"Bearded Sideshow Prophet","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"tent prophet whose tarot readings land as curses","flavor":"A tent-show oddity who reads futures off a deck of tarot-carnival cards, each prediction a curse dressed as a prize.","desc":"A tent-show oddity in a threadbare robe lays out a deck of tarot-carnival cards with slow, theatrical ceremony. Every prediction lands true and every prediction is a curse dressed up as a prize, delivered with the same warm, welcoming smile."},{"name":"Cymbal-Monkey Swarm","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-stirges","model":"swarm-of-stirges","summary":"clashing wind-up monkey troop that shatters focus and eardrums","flavor":"A skittering troop of wind-up cymbal monkeys clashes brass in a deafening rhythm that shatters concentration and eardrums alike.","desc":"A skittering troop of wind-up cymbal monkeys clashes brass together in a deafening, arrhythmic din, key-wound arms never tiring. The noise alone shatters concentration and eardrums both, drowning out any warning of the bite that follows."},{"name":"Puppet Theater Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"stage-ghost that casts bystanders into its unheard endless play","flavor":"Haunts a collapsed proscenium stage, casting itself as every character in a play only it can hear, dragging watchers into the script.","desc":"It haunts a collapsed proscenium stage, casting itself in every role of a play only it can hear, muttering lines to an empty house. Watch too long and you find yourself pulled into the script, a bystander suddenly given lines you never agreed to speak."},{"name":"Shooting-Gallery Marksman","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"gallery marksman who swapped tin ducks for screaming real ones","flavor":"Never misses a moving target; his rifle's tin ducks have been replaced with real, screaming ones for practice.","desc":"He tracks every moving target along the gallery's rail with a rifle that never misses, squinting down the sight with a carnival worker's easy grin. The tin ducks on his stand have all been swapped out for something that screams when it's hit."},{"name":"Cackling Music-Box Horror","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"ballerina automaton whose backward lullaby ages listeners down","flavor":"A brass ballerina spins atop a box that plays a lullaby backward, and every reversed note peels a year off whoever listens.","desc":"A brass ballerina spins atop an ornate box, arms frozen in a pirouette, playing a lullaby run backward note by note. Every reversed chime peels a year off whoever's still listening, the tune getting sweeter as its audience gets younger and smaller."},{"name":"The Understudy Doppel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"mask-cycling mimic wearing the faces of the fair's dead","flavor":"Wears the faces of everyone who's ever died at the fair, cycling masks mid-conversation until you can't remember who you were talking to.","desc":"It wears the borrowed faces of everyone who's ever died at the fair, cycling through them mid-conversation without warning. One moment it's speaking with a voice you recognize; the next it's someone else entirely, and you've lost track of who you were talking to."},{"name":"Pinwheel Djinn","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"pinwheel-bound genie whose wishes twist gaudy and cruel","flavor":"Bound into a spinning pinwheel toy, it grants wishes that always twist back gaudy and cruel, true to the letter and never the spirit.","desc":"Bound into a spinning pinwheel toy, its shape blurs into a smear of color with every gust, genie features flickering in and out of the spin. It grants wishes gladly and grants them exactly as spoken — twisted gaudy and cruel, true to the letter and never once to the spirit."},{"name":"Toy Soldier Colonel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"clockwork colonel drilling a squad of key-wound infantry","flavor":"Commands a squad of wind-up infantry with parade-ground precision, keys still turning in every subordinate's back.","desc":"It drills a squad of wind-up infantry with crisp, parade-ground precision, barking orders in a tinny, amplified voice. Keys still turn slowly in every subordinate's back as they march, and the Colonel's own key never seems to run down."},{"name":"Bell-Tower Puppet","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"clock-tower automaton whose hourly strike finds softer targets","flavor":"A cathedral-clock automaton strikes the hour on the crowd below, its bronze mallet finding softer targets than the bell.","desc":"A cathedral-clock automaton looms at the top of its tower, bronze mallet raised, gears ticking down toward the hour. When it strikes, the mallet swings down onto the crowd below rather than the bell, finding softer targets than bronze."},{"name":"Rictus Ringleader","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"whip-cracking sideshow boss whose grin is stitched shut","flavor":"A whip-cracking sideshow boss whose smile is stitched, not painted, and whose acts always end with someone missing.","desc":"A whip-cracking sideshow boss struts the ring in a tattered ringmaster's coat, smile stitched permanently into place rather than painted on. Every act it runs ends the same way — with someone from the crowd missing by the time the lights come back up."},{"name":"Sugar-Spun Basilisk","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"basilisk","summary":"candy-eyed basilisk that crystallizes prey into hard candy","flavor":"Gazes at foes with candy-glass eyes, and whatever it stares at slowly crystallizes into a life-size hard-candy statue.","desc":"Candy-glass eyes catch the fairground lights in a hard, glittering stare, its scaled hide the exact hue of hard-shell candy. Whatever it looks at long enough stops moving, slowly crystallizing into a life-size sugar statue, sweet and brittle and still."},{"name":"Popcorn Machine Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"overheated popcorn-machine golem hailing scalding kernels","flavor":"Overheated kernels burst from its chest cavity in a scalding, blinding hail while its stitched apron soaks up the mess.","desc":"Overheated kernels burst from a cavity in its chest in a scalding, blinding hail, steam venting from every stitched seam of its apron. It doesn't seem to notice the mess it makes, popping and hissing louder the angrier it gets."},{"name":"Wax Figure Doppelganger","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"wax-museum figure that melts into a dozen grasping arms","flavor":"Stands frozen among a wax museum's other figures until a hand brushes too close, then melts into a dozen grasping arms.","desc":"It stands frozen among a museum's other waxwork figures, posture perfect, expression serene, indistinguishable at a glance from the rest. The instant a hand brushes too close, the wax runs and reshapes into a dozen grasping, half-melted arms."},{"name":"Grand Prize Chimera","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"three-headed stuffed-prize chimera, each head still tagged","flavor":"Stitched from three unclaimed stuffed-animal prizes, each head still wears its raffle tag and its own hunger.","desc":"Three unclaimed stuffed-animal prizes have fused into one lurching, stitched-together body, and each head still wears its own faded raffle tag. Every head hungers separately, and all three seem to agree on exactly one thing: it wants you closer."},{"name":"Runaway Roller-Coaster Wyrm","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"derailed coaster track turned serpent, cars clacking as teeth","flavor":"A derailed coaster track has grown a serpentine mind of its own, its cars now teeth clacking down an endless, screaming loop.","desc":"A derailed length of coaster track has coiled itself into a long, serpentine body, rusted cars still bolted along its spine like segmented plates. Those cars have become its teeth, clacking down an endless loop with a scream of metal that never quite stops echoing.","traits":{"note": "reach-heavy chassis reflavor — the 'breath' becomes a forward track-lurch that covers ground instead of an elemental cone"}},{"name":"Grand Guignol Actor","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"undead stage actor whose prop dagger's blood is now real","flavor":"Died mid-performance and never left the stage, reciting the same monologue while the blood in his prop dagger turns real.","desc":"He died mid-monologue and never left the stage, reciting the same lines night after night to a house long since emptied. The prop dagger in his hand was always meant to be fake — but the blood welling from his co-star's chest now is unmistakably real."},{"name":"Hedge-Maze Minotaur","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","model":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","summary":"topiary-bull minotaur that reshapes the maze to trap guests","flavor":"Grown from hedge-clippings into a living topiary bull, it reshapes the maze walls behind guests so no path leads back out.","desc":"Clipped hedge-leaves and woody bull horns make up its shifting green bulk, twigs cracking softly with every heavy step through the maze. It reshapes the hedge walls behind anyone foolish enough to enter, closing off the path back the way they came."},{"name":"The Barker's Voice","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"omnipresent barker-voice hiding a tentacled body in speaker horns","flavor":"A disembodied, amplified voice that fills the fairground from every direction, its tentacled true body hidden inside the speaker horns.","desc":"An amplified voice fills the whole fairground at once, warm and welcoming, seeming to come from every direction and none. Its true body — a knot of tentacles — hides folded inside the speaker horns mounted overhead, waiting for the crowd to gather close enough."},{"name":"Wheel-of-Fortune Oracle","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"rigged fortune-wheel witch who collects on every fated spin","flavor":"Spins a rigged wheel that decides not prizes but fates, and every guest who plays owes her whatever the wheel names.","desc":"She spins a garish, rigged wheel with a showman's flourish, painted wedges promising prizes that never quite come up. The wheel doesn't decide winnings — it decides fates, and every guest who plays owes her whatever name lands under the pointer."},{"name":"Tilt-a-Whirl Horror","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"cloaker","model":"cloaker","summary":"spinning ride-maw that disorients riders while digesting them","flavor":"Folds its riders into a spinning cup-shaped maw, disorientation and gravity doing half the digesting for it.","desc":"Its body folds and unfolds like a spinning ride car, cup-shaped and hollow, whirling faster the longer a victim struggles inside it. Disorientation does half the work for it, digestion following close behind as the spin never lets up."},{"name":"Effigy of the Midway","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"towering lost-and-found effigy animated by collected grudges","flavor":"A towering scarecrow-king built from every unclaimed prize and lost mitten, animated by the fair's collected grudges.","desc":"A towering scarecrow-king shape rises from a heap of every unclaimed prize and lost mitten the fair's ever collected, straw limbs bulging with old grudges. It moves with the slow, deliberate weight of something that's been building for years, finally standing up."},{"name":"Puppet King's Herald","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"satyr-revelmaster","model":"satyr-revelmaster","summary":"herald whose compelling fanfare herds crowds toward danger","flavor":"Announces the Ringmaster's arrivals with a fanfare that compels the crowd to applaud even as it herds them toward the tents.","desc":"A herald in gaudy court colors raises a brass horn and announces the Ringmaster's arrival with a fanfare that swells louder than it should. The crowd applauds despite themselves, compelled forward, cheering their own steps toward the waiting tents."},{"name":"Hall of Mirrors Horror","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"hive-minded shattered mirror-hall, every shard a coordinated attacker","flavor":"A shattered fun-house hallway given a hive mind, each shard-reflection a separate, coordinated attacker.","desc":"A shattered fun-house hallway lines both walls in broken glass, every fragment catching a slightly different angle of the room. Each shard-reflection moves and strikes on its own, all of them coordinated by a single mind that shares none of your blind spots.","traits":{"note": "hive-mind flavor over the base chassis's telepathic link — no flanking blind spot exists against it since every shard sees a different angle"}},{"name":"Grandfather Clock Devourer","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"antique clock-golem whose chime ages victims to dust","flavor":"An antique carnival clock swallows time itself, its pendulum swing aging anyone caught in its chime to dust.","desc":"An antique carnival clock stands taller than a door, pendulum swinging in slow, patient arcs, hands frozen at the wrong hour. Anyone caught inside its chime feels time itself pour off them, skin and years both wearing away toward dust with every ring.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "The Hour Strikes", "text": "once per encounter, chimes the hour: everyone within the tolling range takes aging-flavored necrotic damage as the golem's normal slam, no separate save track added"}]}},{"name":"The Understudy King","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"backstage understudy rehearsing to seize the Birthday King's crown","flavor":"Waits backstage to replace the Birthday King the instant he falters, rehearsing the crown's cruelty in an empty dressing room mirror.","desc":"He waits backstage in an empty dressing room, rehearsing the Birthday King's cruelty line by line in a cracked mirror, ready the instant the crown falters. Every gesture is a copy refined a hundred times over, waiting only for its cue."},{"name":"Roulette Devil","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"cursed casino-tent devil who collects bets in stolen years","flavor":"Runs the fairground's cursed gaming tent, and every bet placed against him pays out in years of the loser's life.","desc":"He runs the fair's cursed gaming tent from behind a spinning wheel of red and black, smiling with too many teeth at every new bet placed. Every wager lost against him pays out not in coin but in years, peeled straight from the loser's life."},{"name":"The Grand Carousel Titan","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"storm-giant","model":"storm-giant","summary":"whole carousel fused into a lurching titan of bobbing wooden limbs","flavor":"An entire carousel has fused into one lurching gilded titan, its wooden animals now limbs still bobbing on their poles.","desc":"An entire carousel has fused into one lurching, gilded titan, its carved wooden animals now serving as limbs still bobbing gently on their original poles. It moves with the slow, groaning creak of old brass and rot-softened wood, each stride a small parade of its own.","traits":{"hp": "above-chassis (Huge, fused-mount frame)", "actions": [{"name": "Bobbing Limbs", "text": "each of its carved-animal limbs can strike a separate target in the same turn, up and down in the ride's old rhythm"}]}},{"name":"The Confetti Cannon Colossus","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"frost-giant","model":"frost-giant","summary":"siege-toy cannon launching cheerful bursts of glass confetti","flavor":"A fairground siege-toy that once fired harmless streamers now launches shrapnel-glass confetti in cheerful, deadly bursts.","desc":"A fairground siege-toy that once fired harmless paper streamers now booms with a deeper report, barrel glowing faintly at the mouth. What launches out in cheerful, colorful bursts is shrapnel-glass confetti, glittering prettily on the way down."},{"name":"Matriarch of the Sideshow","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"ancient sideshow exhibit whose curse feeds on being watched","flavor":"The oldest exhibit in the tent, kept alive by decades of gawking stares, her curse now feeds on being watched, not touched.","desc":"The oldest exhibit under the tent sits enthroned behind faded velvet rope, kept alive for decades by nothing but the crowd's gawking stares. Her curse has changed with her hunger — it no longer needs a touch, only to be watched, and watched, and watched.","traits":{"note": "petrification-adjacent gaze reworked as attention-based rather than eye-contact based — being watched by her counts, not just watching her", "actions": [{"name": "Fed by the Crowd", "text": "any creature that has observed her for a full round without looking away begins to stiffen, slowing before it stills"}]}},{"name":"The Perpetual Winner","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"undying champion whose losing challengers become living trophies","flavor":"Has won every game at the fair a thousand times over and cannot stop; challengers who lose join his trophy case, still breathing.","desc":"He's won every game on the midway a thousand times over and physically cannot stop, moving from booth to booth with a champion's easy grin. Every challenger who loses to him joins his trophy case afterward — mounted, displayed, and still, somehow, breathing.","traits":{"note": "a downed-and-mounted state instead of a normal death for creatures it defeats — narrative hook for the trophy case, not extra mechanics on the PC"}},{"name":"The Calliope Behemoth","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"dracolich","model":"dracolich","summary":"steam-organ dragon whose cheerful hymn liquefies listeners' bones","flavor":"A steam organ grew a serpent's spine and dragon's wind, and its cheerful hymn liquefies bone in anyone who can still hear it.","desc":"A steam organ has grown a serpent's coiling spine and a dragon's furnace-breath, brass pipes gleaming where scales should be. Its cheerful, tuneless hymn rolls out across the fairgrounds, and every note that reaches an ear liquefies the bone beneath it.","traits":{"note": "breath weapon reflavored as a sonic hymn-cone rather than fire/acid — same chassis math, different sensory delivery"}},{"name":"Warden of the Big Top","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"vast tent-eye that conscripts failed performers as new attractions","flavor":"The tent's peak is one vast, veiled eye that watches every act performed beneath it, and every failed performer becomes its next attraction.","desc":"The peak of the tent is not canvas but one vast, veiled eye, watching every act performed on the ring below without blinking. Any performer who fails under its gaze doesn't get carried off — it conscripts them on the spot, folding them into its next attraction.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Conscript the Fallen", "text": "a creature dropped to 0 HP beneath the Warden's gaze can be reanimated as a new minor attraction-thrall instead of dying outright"}]}},{"name":"The Sold-Out Show","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"eternal demon-headliner whose lights burn brighter per soul billed","flavor":"A demon booked eternally for one final performance, its stage lights burning brighter with every soul added to the marquee.","desc":"A demon stands eternally booked for one final performance, marquee lights strung across its shoulders like a headliner's name in neon. Those lights burn brighter with every soul added to the bill, and the show, by design, never actually closes.","traits":{"note": "escalating-brightness stacking condition — narrated as the marquee getting louder/brighter per kill in the encounter, mechanics riding the balor chassis's existing escalation"}},{"name":"The Never-Ending Attraction","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"arch-hag","summary":"court rival running an endless ride that loops joy into captivity","flavor":"A rival to the Birthday King's court, she runs the ride that never lets guests off, looping the same three minutes of joy into decades of captivity.","desc":"A rival to the Birthday King's own court, she runs a ride that never quite lets its passengers off, looping the same three minutes on repeat. Each loop feels like pure joy the first time through — it's only the hundredth time that reveals it as captivity.","traits":{"note": "a repeating-round hazard-lock (charm/restrain flavor) rather than a straight damage-dealer; the loop is the threat, not the hit"}},{"name":"Marching Band Automaton","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"brass-skeleton whose off-key blare shatters concentration","flavor":"A brass-instrument skeleton blares off-key notes that rattle armor loose and shatter concentration mid-spell.","desc":"A brass-instrument skeleton stomps forward in a marching band's stiff cadence, valves and slides clattering where muscle should be. It blares deliberately off-key notes that rattle loose rivets and armor plating alike, the discord alone enough to shatter a caster's concentration."},{"name":"Rubber Ball Bouncer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"grinning rubber ball bouncing faster with every bone-jarring hit","flavor":"A red rubber ball with a painted smiling face bounces at increasing speed, each impact a bone-jarring thud.","desc":"A red rubber ball with a painted smiling face bounces across the floor in slow, deliberate arcs, gaining speed with every landing. Each impact lands with a bone-jarring thud far heavier than its size suggests, faster and harder the longer the chase goes on."},{"name":"Strongman Hammer Golem","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"high-striker golem whose swing is meant for skulls, not bells","flavor":"Rings the high-striker bell with a swing meant for skulls, its painted grin never dimming no matter how loud the crack.","desc":"It grips an oversized mallet at the base of a high-striker game, swinging with a strongman's showmanship at anything that gets close. The bell at the top rings clean and loud with every hit that connects with a skull instead, its painted grin never dimming."},{"name":"Petting-Zoo Horror","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-goat","model":"giant-goat","summary":"once-gentle petting-zoo animal grown too many teeth","flavor":"Once a gentle attraction, its wool now hides too many teeth, and it head-butts with a strength no child should have petted.","desc":"It was once a gentle attraction, woolly coat matted now from years of hands that shouldn't have been trusted with it. Underneath that wool is a mouth that's grown too many teeth, and a head-butt with a strength no petting-zoo animal should carry."},{"name":"Glow-Stick Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"bobbing glow-stick wisp that lures stragglers off the path","flavor":"A chemical-glow spirit lures children off the midway paths with a cheerful bobbing light, then snaps their glow out cold.","desc":"A chemical-glow spirit bobs cheerfully along the midway's darker paths, its light a soft, inviting green that seems to promise safety. It leads children and stragglers off the trail with that same gentle bob — then snaps its own glow out cold the moment they're alone."},{"name":"Cake-Topper Golem","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"fused bride-groom cake figure, frosting-slick, still smiling","flavor":"A porcelain bride-and-groom figurine fused into one lurching shape, frosting-slick and still smiling for a wedding long over.","desc":"A porcelain bride-and-groom figurine has fused into one lurching shape, frosting-slick along every seam, faces still turned toward each other in a fixed, permanent smile. It moves with a wedding-day stiffness, sugar dripping from its joints, still dressed for a ceremony long over."},{"name":"the Playing-Card Guard","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-duodrone","model":"clockwork-law-construct-duodrone","summary":"flat card-soldier, obeys any shouted rank","flavor":"Flat, hinged, and utterly loyal to a rank it can't read — it swings a spade-halberd edge-on so it nearly vanishes, then face-on so it looms.","desc":"Flat and hinged at every joint, it swings a spade-tipped halberd edge-on so the blade nearly vanishes from sight, then face-on so the whole card looms wide and sudden. It obeys any shouted rank without question, loyal to an authority it can't even read.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the Queen of Hearts' card-soldiers who paint the roses red"},{"name":"the Tin Soldier's Hollow Cousin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-monodrone","model":"clockwork-law-construct-monodrone","summary":"wind-up soldier, marches until unwound","flavor":"Painted smile, key still turning in its back; it marches in whatever direction it was last wound, even off a table's edge.","desc":"Painted smile fixed under a tin shako, its key still turns slowly in its back with every step it takes. It marches in whatever direction it was last wound to face, indifferent to walls, stairs, or the edge of a table.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock nursery-toy-come-to-life archetype (generic wind-up soldier, not any single IP's toy line)"},{"name":"the March Hare","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-badger","model":"net-new: lanky twitching hare in a waistcoat of fur, teacup always in one paw","summary":"tea-mad hare, hostile to clocks and cutlery","flavor":"It never stops setting the table and never stops smashing it; ours argues with the furniture between bites.","desc":"It never stops laying out the tea things, and it never stops smashing them either, cutlery flying with every irritable swipe. Ours argues loudly with the furniture between bites, chair legs and teapots taking the worst of a temper that never settles.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the tea-party Hare, mad from too much March"},{"name":"a Wicked Witch's Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"storybook wolf, mimics a soft voice before attacking","flavor":"Chalk-dust still clings to its throat from swallowing a voice that wasn't its own; it talks before it bites, and the talking is the worse part.","desc":"Chalk dust still clings faintly to its throat, residue from swallowing a voice that was never its own to begin with. It talks in a soft, borrowed cadence before it attacks, and somehow the talking is worse than the teeth that follow.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Grimm fairy-tale wolves (Little Red Riding Hood / the Wolf and the Seven Young Kids, PD folk tradition)"},{"name":"Geppetto's Runaway Marionette","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"lying puppet, nose-hinge lengthens with each lie","flavor":"Its nose is a broken hinge that keeps lengthening whenever it insists it means no harm; the strings dangling from its wrists still twitch toward a hand that isn't there.","desc":"Its nose is a broken wooden hinge, and that hinge keeps lengthening every time it insists — sincerely, wide-eyed — that it means no harm at all. Loose strings dangle from both wrists, twitching now and then toward a hand that isn't there anymore.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Collodi, Le avventure di Pinocchio (1883, PD) — a puppet who lied its way out of its strings"},{"name":"the Piper's Rat","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"tune-compelled rat, swarms toward any melody","flavor":"It can't help following music, even music it invents by chewing on pipes; a column of them will drown a room before the tune even lands.","desc":"It can't help but follow music, even the tuneless clatter it makes itself gnawing on hollow pipes as it scurries forward. Alone it's nothing; a column of them pouring through a doorway will drown a room in fur and teeth before the melody even finishes.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Pied Piper of Hamelin legend (medieval German folk legend, PD)"},{"name":"the Mouse King's Sentry","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-hyena","model":"net-new: scrawny multi-headed mouse-courtier in a torn paper crown","summary":"multi-headed mouse-courtier, argues with itself mid-fight","flavor":"Extra heads, extra crowns, extra grudges — it snaps at whichever slight it remembers most that second.","desc":"Extra heads sprout in a ragged crown atop one small, armored body, each wearing its own tiny paper coronet and its own private grudge. It snaps and lunges toward whichever slight it's currently stewing over, the heads rarely agreeing on a single target.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Hoffmann, Nussknacker und Mausekönig (1816, PD) — the Mouse King's seven-headed court"},{"name":"the Nutcracker Grenadier","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"wooden grenadier, jaw-hinge crushing bite","flavor":"Jaw hinged to crack more than nuts; painted eyes track motion better than most flesh does.","desc":"Its jaw hinges wide on a spring built for cracking more than walnuts, painted uniform buttons gleaming under whatever light finds them. Glassy painted eyes track motion with an unsettling precision that most flesh-and-blood soldiers never manage.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic wooden-soldier toy archetype (the Nutcracker's rank-and-file, not the named prince)"},{"name":"the Cheshire Grin","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"net-new: striped cat dissolving into mist, grin the last visible feature","summary":"fading cat, taunts and phases out mid-combat","flavor":"It answers every question with a worse one and vanishes exactly when a hit should land; the grin is the last thing to go, and the first thing to come back.","desc":"It answers every question with a worse one, tail curling lazily in the air as its outline starts to blur at the edges. It vanishes exactly when a killing blow should land, leaving the grin hanging a beat longer than the rest of it — the last thing to go, and always the first thing back.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the cat that fades to only its smile"},{"name":"the Winged Monkey Raider","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-owl","model":"giant-owl","summary":"cap-bound flying monkey, resents its own orders","flavor":"It hates every second of the compulsion and takes it out on whoever's closest; free one mid-fight and it simply leaves.","desc":"Bound wings beat hard and resentful, wide eyes flicking toward whoever's holding its leash rather than its target. It clearly hates every second of the compulsion driving it and takes that hatred out on whoever's nearest — free it mid-fight and it simply flies off.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD, novel version) — the Wicked Witch of the West's flying monkey soldiers, bound by the Golden Cap"},{"name":"the Goblin Toymaker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"green-hag","model":"net-new: hunched goblin tinker hung with keys, spare parts, and a whistle","summary":"toy-peddling goblin, remote-commands nearby constructs","flavor":"Every toy it's ever sold is still listening for its whistle; it fights by recalling its merchandise, not by swinging anything itself.","desc":"Small, gaudy, and cheerful in a shopfront apron, it never swings a weapon of its own — it doesn't need to. Every toy it's ever sold is still listening for its whistle, and it fights entirely by recalling its merchandise from wherever it's been carried.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock malevolent-toymaker/goblin-tinkerer archetype drawing on Grimm-style goblin/gnome tradition (PD folk motif, not any branded IP)"},{"name":"the Queen of Hearts","cr":4,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"net-new: imperious card-court queen, oversized ruffed gown, axe she never swings herself","summary":"tyrant queen, commands the battlefield instead of fighting it","flavor":"She never actually swings the axe — she just declares a sentence and the room's own furniture carries it out; the tantrum is the spell.","desc":"She never actually raises the axe herself — she simply declares a sentence in a voice that cracks the air, and the room's own furniture carries the verdict out. The tantrum that follows a denied whim is, itself, the spell.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — 'Off with their heads!'"},{"name":"the Grimm Woodland Witch","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"cannibal-witch, lures and force-feeds before the kill","flavor":"She fattens what she can't yet eat and eats what she's already fattened; the oven is a door she keeps ajar just to hear you consider it.","desc":"She fattens whatever she can't yet eat and eats whatever she's already fattened, humming contentedly over a simmering pot the whole while. The oven door stays cracked open, not from carelessness, but because she wants you to consider it, at length, before she decides.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Grimm fairy-tale witches (Hansel and Gretel's gingerbread-house witch; PD folk tradition, our own original description — no film likeness)"},{"name":"the Wicked Witch of the West","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"net-new: one-eyed witch wrapped in dust-colored robes, umbrella-staff, no green skin","summary":"beast-commanding witch, dissolves rather than dies clean","flavor":"Ours is a hoarder of borrowed servants, not a green face — she never fights fair and she never fights dry-eyed once the bucket comes out.","desc":"Ours is no green-skinned face cackling alone — she's a hoarder of borrowed servants, sending others in first and staying dry behind them. She never fights fair, and she never fights with dry eyes once a bucket of water enters the room.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD novel version) — melts to water, commands wolves/crows/bees/monkeys, not any film's green-skin design"},{"name":"the Mouse King","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"seven-headed rat-king, regenerates through internal rivalry","flavor":"Seven heads mean seven opinions about how you should die; killing one crown just promotes the angriest survivor.","desc":"Seven crowned heads rise from one hulking rat body, and every head has its own opinion about exactly how you ought to die. Cut down the loudest one and the killing blow only serves to promote whichever surviving head was already the angriest.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Hoffmann, Nussknacker und Mausekönig (1816, PD) — the seven-crowned rival of the Nutcracker Prince"},{"name":"the Automaton in the Wicker Man's Skin","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"straw guardian-construct, patrols a fixed boundary forever","flavor":"Straw where a heart should sit and a painted grin that never once needed the muscles to hold it; it guards the toybox border like it remembers being told to.","desc":"Straw fills the space where a heart should beat, and a painted grin sits fixed on its woven face, needing no muscle at all to hold its shape. It patrols the same fixed boundary over and over, guarding the toybox's edge like it still remembers being told to.","source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scarecrow-come-to-life archetype (generic animated-guardian toybox motif, not any branded character)"},{"name":"the Wonderland Jabberwock","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"nonsense-dragon, telegraphs doom in verse before it strikes","flavor":"It doesn't so much attack as arrive — burbling, whiffling, eyes of flame — and the vorpal answer is always a blade someone else forged.","desc":"It doesn't so much attack as simply arrive — burbling low in its throat, whiffling through the underbrush, eyes lit like twin coals catching flame. Whatever verse it recites on the way in always ends the same: with a vorpal blade someone else was left to forge.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Through the Looking-Glass (1871, PD) — 'the jaws that bite, the claws that catch'"},{"name":"the Tin Woodman, Rusted Wrong","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"hollow tin giant, mourns while it swings the axe","flavor":"Somewhere under the seams is the man who kept chopping even after every piece of him was replaced; he still oils his own joints mid-fight, out of habit, not need.","desc":"Somewhere under all the replaced, rust-streaked seams is still the shape of a man who kept swinging his axe even after every piece of him got swapped out. He oils his own joints mid-fight out of pure habit, not need, mourning quietly the whole time he chops.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD novel version) — the woodman who traded his flesh limb by limb for tin"},{"name":"the Hamelin Piper","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"net-new: gaunt piper in motley, pipe always at his lips, never draws a blade","summary":"compulsion piper, turns the battlefield's own mooks against it","flavor":"He never raises a weapon; he raises a tune, and the toybox itself gets up to dance for him, one compelled soldier at a time.","desc":"He never once raises a weapon of his own; he raises a tune instead, fingers dancing lightly over pipe-holes worn smooth with age. The toybox itself gets up to dance for him at that sound, one compelled soldier at a time, joining his side against its own will.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Pied Piper of Hamelin legend (medieval German folk legend, PD) — paid in rats, repaid in children"},{"name":"the Wonderland Executioner-Court","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-lemures","model":"net-new: a whirling mass of card-guards rising as a single verdict","summary":"card-mob swarm, group-verdict area attacks","flavor":"A deck's worth of guards rising as one verdict; it doesn't think, it convicts, and it convicts everyone in reach at once.","desc":"A deck's worth of card-guards rise together as one single, seething mass, suits and numbers blurring into a wall of moving paper and blade. It doesn't think or deliberate — it convicts, and it convicts everyone standing within reach all at once.","source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the trial of the Knave of Hearts, the mob of cards"}]
};
